  "12-jyotirlinga-tour-package": {
    "overview": "There are countless temples in India. However, Jyotirlingas hold a place of their own! Deemed as the ultimate pilgrimage, See More\n\nthe trip to these holy temples is considered highly sacred for it promises Moksha \u2013 liberation from the cycle of birth and death! The Jyotirlingas are distributed across the country \u2013 from Somnath in Gujarat to Rameshwaram in Tamil Nadu! Although this is a challenging journey, our 12 Jyotirlinga Tour Package takes you to all these special shrines of Lord Shiva across the entire nation.\nSo think no more! Book this package now, and be the recipient of the abundant blessings that will fall your way once you complete this trip. To get a quote and know more, simply give us a call and we\u2019ll get back to you shortly!\nWhy Visit the 12 Jyotirlingas?\nThe 12 Jyotirlingas are considered highly sacred, and visiting them is a must for every Lord Shiva devotee. It\u2019s believed that these temples manifest from the very energy of him when he was in the form of an infinite cosmic light pillar.\nAs per the Shiva Purana, once Lord Shiva appeared in the form of this bright light in order to exert his supremacy over Lord Vishnu and Lord Brahma. And now, each Jyotirlinga is a representation of his divine energy, and is considered to be a self-manifested lingam! Also, it\u2019s believed that taking this sacred spiritual tour of Lord Shiva temples cleanses one\u2019s sins and grants them Moksha, in turn.\nMoreover, if you go to these holy temples, you can enjoy the culture and traditions of different places that you get to visit while being on this holy journey. Also, many devotees combine this trip with other tours such as Char Dham Yatra or Shaktipeeth visits, to make this a truly mega pilgrimage!\nBook My Quick Trippers\u2019s Jyotirlinga Darshan package and take an easy-peasy comfortable trip to India's most sacred shrines!\nSignificance of 12 Jyotirlingas\nHere\u2019s a quick guide to all twelve shrines covered in the 12 Jyotirlinga Tour Package:\n\nSomnath: This was one of the very first Jyotirlingas! This sea-facing temple symbolizes eternal faith. Devotes simply love the evening light and sound show here.\nMallikarjuna: Also known as the \u201cKailash of the South\u201d, this temple is associated with Parvati as Mallika and Shiva as Arjuna.\nMahakaleshwar: This is the only south-facing Jyotirlinga you\u2019ll find. It\u2019s famous for its holy Bhasma Aarti, where Lord Shiva is offered the sacred ash.\nOmkareshwar: The specialty of this Jyotirlinga is that it is located on an island that is shaped like the OM symbol. It\u2019s believed that coming here fulfills your wishes.\nKedarnath: This temple has a huge significance associated with it. Not only is it a Jyotirlinga, it\u2019s also a part of the Chhota Dham circuit. It\u2019s also the highest Jyotirlinga in altitude.\nBhimashankar: Surrounded by dense forests, this temple is linked to the mythology about the demon Tripurasura being defeated by Lord Shiva.\nKashi Vishwanath: Located in the \u2018spiritual capital of India\u2019, Varanasi, this temple promises Moksha if someone dies here of natural causes.\nTrimbakeshwar: This is a unique Jyotirlinga that has 3 lingams, representing Brahma, Vishnu, and Shiva. This temple is popular for its Narayan Nagbali Puja rituals.\nVaidyanath: This temple sees a load of pilgrim traffic in the Shravan month, that is, when Kanwariyas visit this temple. Lord Shiva is worshipped here as the supreme healer, a Vaidya that is.\nNageshwar: This Jyotirlinga houses a tall Shiva statue, and it\u2019s associated with the demon Daruka.\nRamanathaswamy: This temple has a very old Ramayana link. It\u2019s believed that Lord Rama worshipped Lord Shiva here before he went to the Lanka war. There are also 22 sacred wells inside the temple where one can take a ritual bath.\nGrishneshwar: This is the smallest Jyotirlinga, located very close to the Ajanta-Ellora caves. You can enjoy the rich carvings on temple walls here and the ever-present peaceful atmosphere.\n\nTo enjoy a smooth trip, simply opt for our Jyotirlinga Yatra booking and travel in comfort!\n12 Jyotirlinga Tour Package by Train and Flight\nMy Quick Trippers also offers you combo 12 Jyotirlinga Tour Packages by Train and Flight, where you get to travel by both railways and plane. This combined trip makes the journey easier and far smoother. With the comfort & high speed of air travel, along with the traditional experience of the train journey, you get to enjoy the best of both worlds.\nOn this hybrid route, we would cover segments like Mumbai to Madurai and Hyderabad to Deoghar by flight. This is the most suitable way, as these are located far from each other and flying there considerably reduces the travel time. And for the shorter segments like Omkareshwar to Ujjain or Nashik to Bhimashankar, we can go for the scenic train journey. \nWith this train and flight Jyotirlinga Yatra package, devotees reach the Jyotirlingas in the most optimal time and also reduce fatigue. In general, this fight and train to Jyotirlingas tour is the best way to complete Darshan of all 12 Jyotirlingas (takes about 12-18 days). Book now or call us to know more about this combo package! \nBest Time for the 12 Jyotirlinga Tour\nThe best time to go on this sacred Jyotirlinga tour differs from region to region, as the sacred shrines are distributed all across India. However, for most shrines, you can consider the season of autumn (September \u2013 November) for taking this sacred tour. The weather in this window is pleasant for the most part, and therefore can be considered for the holy trip.\nMoreover, this is also ideal for the tour to Kedarnath, which gets closed in November, and stays so until April. Also, this window is great for visiting the temple in the south (Rameswaram and Srisailam) as well.\nTravel Tips for Devotees\nHere is some travel advice that you might find useful on this Jyotirlinga Yatra Package:\n\nEven before you step out for this sacred tour, make a Sankalp in front of Lord Shiva\u2019s idol in your home or a nearby temple, asking for the success of this tour.\nBook your 12 Jyotirlinga Travel Package in advance \u2013 at least 3-6 months. The slots get quickly filled up, especially if you\u2019re planning to travel during special occasions, such as Shravan, Navratri, and Maha Shivaratri.\nIf you\u2019re a senior citizen, then consider going by train or plane, as this will help you reduce the physical strain and exhaustion caused by road travel.\nIf you plan to take the helicopter services, then make sure you have your ID proof and medical certificate ready.\nTry to make your trip even more fulfilling by combining your Jyotirlinga tour with nearby major sightseeing attractions, like Dwarkadhish Temple (in Dwarka), Ellora Caves (in Aurangabad), and Rameswaram beaches (in Rameswaram).\nTry to group your Jyotirlinga tour in a region-wise cluster. For example, combine your temple trips in West India, South India, Central India, and North India. This organised tour will help you save time and reduce your fatigue significantly.\nThere\u2019s always a chance of delays. This could be due to weather and other unforeseeable factors. Therefore, always keep 1-2 days spare in your Jyotirlinga Yatra itinerary.\nThroughout your trip, stay hydrated. Always carry a water bottle with you. Also, eat easily digestible, light food to aid digestion.\nAlways follow the temple etiquette. Some common practices include removing your shoes before entering the temple, wearing modest clothes, and not carrying leather items inside the shrine.\n\nDistance and Location of 12 Jyotirlingas\nThinking of getting a Jyotirlinga Yatra Package and want to see what your trip will look like? Then, here\u2019s a quick guide to the location and the distances of the holy shrines from the nearest hub:\n\n\n\n\nJyotirlinga Temple\nLocation (State)\nNearest City\nDistance from the Nearest City\n\n\n\n\nSomnath Jyotirlinga\nPrabhas Patan, Gujarat\nVeraval / Rajkot\nVeraval \u2013 7 km, Rajkot \u2013 200 km\n\n\nMallikarjuna Jyotirlinga\nSrisailam, Andhra Pradesh\nHyderabad\n215 km\n\n\nMahakaleshwar Jyotirlinga\nUjjain, Madhya Pradesh\nIndore\n55 km\n\n\nOmkareshwar Jyotirlinga\nKhandwa district, Madhya Pradesh\nIndore\n80 km\n\n\nKedarnath Jyotirlinga\nRudraprayag, Uttarakhand\nRishikesh / Dehradun\nRishikesh \u2013 210 km + 16 km trek from Gaurikund\n\n\nBhimashankar Jyotirlinga\nPune district, Maharashtra\nPune\n110 km\n\n\nKashi Vishwanath Jyotirlinga\nVaranasi, Uttar Pradesh\nVaranasi\nWithin city (20 km from airport)\n\n\nTrimbakeshwar Jyotirlinga\nNashik, Maharashtra\nNashik\n28 km\n\n\nVaidyanath (Baidyanath) Jyotirlinga\nDeoghar, Jharkhand\nJasidih Railway Station\n7 km\n\n\nNageshwar Jyotirlinga\nDwarka, Gujarat\nDwarka\n16 km\n\n\nRamanathaswamy Jyotirlinga\nRameswaram, Tamil Nadu\nMadurai / Rameswaram\nMadurai \u2013 170 km, Rameswaram Railway \u2013 2 km\n\n\nGrishneshwar Jyotirlinga\nEllora, Maharashtra\nAurangabad\n30 km\n\n\n\n\n12 Jyotirlinga Route Map\nThe Jyotirlinga are spread all across the nation, and that is why it\u2019s best to cover them in clusters. That is, if you\u2019re in the west India, it\u2019s best to visit all the temples in this region first, before moving on to the other region. Here\u2019s a Jyotirlinga Route Map for your guidance:\n\nGujarat (Nageshwar \u2192 Somnath)\nMadhya Pradesh (Omkareshwar \u2192 Mahakaleshwar)\nNorth India (Kashi Vishwanath \u2192 Vaidyanath \u2192 Kedarnath)\nMaharashtra (Trimbakeshwar \u2192 Bhimashankar \u2192 Grishneshwar)\nSouth India (Mallikarjuna \u2192 Rameswaram)\n\nBook the Best 12 Jyotirlinga Yatra Package!\nDon\u2019t take this 12 Jyotirlinga Tour Package as just a religious journey, for it takes you to the various corners of India, giving you a glimpse of the rich heritage. More than just a journey of faith, this holy pilgrimage is meant to have you discover the culture, resilience, and divine power of the very country. Book My Quick Trippers\u2019s complete Jyotirlinga pilgrimage plan and enjoy a trip pan-India like never before! Remember, we\u2019re just a call away!",
    "highlights": [
      "Sacred Darshan of all the 12 Jyotirlingas",
      "Experience the mesmerizing Ganga Aarti at Haridwar\u2019s Har Ki Pauri and Varanasi\u2019s Dasaswamedh Ghat",
      "Combined visit to Shakti Peetha and Jyotirlinga with Mallikarjuna Temple Darshan",
      "Marvel at the magnificent architecture of Meenakshi Amman Temple and Srisailam",
      "Trek to Kedarnath temple amidst snow-capped peaks and Himalayan valleys",
      "Cultural visit to Shirdi and Shani Shingnapur",
      "Experience the unique rituals like the Bhasma Aarti at Mahakaleshwar",
      "Explore the heritage sites like Nashik, Dwarka, and Madurai",
      "Pan-India Pilgrimage Experience",
      "Well-crafted itinerary and friendly staff"
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1: : Arrival in Mumbai and Journey to Rajkot",
        "description": "Once you reach Mumbai, our travel representatives will greet you with a warm welcome.\nNow, it\u2019s time to catch the overnight train to Rajkot, Gujarat. You\u2019ll get full assistance in boarding from our side.\nEnjoy an overnight stay on the train. We recommend packing some light snacks and water for this train journey."
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 2: Trip to Dwarkadhish and Nageshwar Jyotirlinga",
        "description": "By early morning, you\u2019ll arrive in Rajkot.\nDeboard the train, and now you\u2019ll be driven to Dwarka. This holy city is one of the Char Dhams and also a Sapta Puri.\nNow, check into your pre-booked hotel and freshen up!\nLater, you\u2019ll be taken to the Dwarkadhish Temple first. It is dedicated to Lord Krishna, where he\u2019s worshipped in his royal form as the King of Dwarka!\nNext, you\u2019ll be driven to the very first Jyotirlinga of this tour, that is, Nageshwar Jyotirlinga. Lord Shiva is worshipped here as the protector against poison.\nAfter your Darshan and Poojan, return to your hotel for dinner in the evening.\nGet a restful night of sleep at your hotel.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 3 \u2013 Somnath Jyotirlinga Darshan",
        "description": "Have breakfast and then check out of your hotel.\nNow, you\u2019ll be transferred to Somnath near Veraval. Once you arrive in this city, check into your hotel and take rest for a while.\nAfterwards, you'll be taken to Somnath Jyotirlinga Temple, a shrine that enjoys a glorious history. According to the Hindu mythology, it\u2019s believed that the temple was originally built by Chandra Dev in order to please Lord Shiva. Over centuries, this temple has been destroyed and rebuilt 17 times, and now stands as a metaphorical symbol of faith and resilience!\nAlso, attend the evening Aarti at the temple.\nThen, come back to the hotel for an overnight stay.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 4 \u2013 Somnath to Ujjain transfer (Overnight Train Journey)",
        "description": "Wake up early and attend the morning Aarti at Somnath temple.\nNow, check out of your hotel and head to the railway station and catch a train to Ujjain in Madhya Pradesh.\nThis will be an overnight journey by train. We recommend carrying a light shawl or blanket with you as the nights can get a little chilly."
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 5 \u2013 Arrival in Ujjain and Visit to Omkareshwar Temple",
        "description": "You\u2019ll arrive in Ujjain early in the morning. Upon arrival, check into your hotel and take a little rest for a while.\nNow, you\u2019ll be taken to the Omkareshwar Jyotirlinga, which is situated on an island surrounded by the Narmada River. There\u2019s another specialty of this island, which is that it is shaped like an \u2018OM\u2019 symbol. You can also choose to circumambulate the island, as many devotees do.\nAfterwards, return to your hotel for an overnight stay.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 6 \u2013 Ujjain (Mahakaleshwar Darshan) and Train to Haridwar",
        "description": "Get up early in the morning and proceed for the Darshan and Poojan at the Mahakaleshwar Jyotirlinga. This is one of the most revered shrines of Lord Shiv, where he\u2019s worshiped as the destroyer of time itself.\nIf you reach there early, you can also witness the Bhasma Aarti, which takes place from 4 AM to 6 AM. In this sacred ritual, Lord Shiva is offered the sacred ash.\nLater, enjoy a trip to the popular temples like Harsiddhi Mata Temple and Kal Bhairav Temple. Both of these temples have a strong background in the rich Tantric traditions of India.\nIn the evening, you\u2019ll be driven to the railway station, where you\u2019ll board the train to Haridwar.\nEnjoy an overnight stay on the train.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 7 \u2013 Arrival in Haridwar (Ganga Aarti Experience)",
        "description": "You\u2019ll reach Haridwar in the morning. From the railway station, you'll be transferred to your hotel, where you can check in. Take some time to relax and freshen up. The rest of the day is free!\nIn the evening, drop by the Har ki Pauri and witness the mesmerizing Ganga Aarti. Watch as the thousands of Diyas float by on the Ganga River.\nReturn to the hotel for an overnight stay.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 8 \u2013 Transfer to Guptkashi and Visit to Ardhanarishvara Temple",
        "description": "Have breakfast in the morning.\nNow, begin a scenic drive towards Guptkashi. Once you get there, check into your pre-booked hotel.\nNow, you\u2019ll be taken to the Ardhanarishvara Temple. This temple holds a great deal of significance as it symbolizes Lord Shiva and Goddess Parvati\u2019s unity.\nReturn to the hotel for dinner and overnight stay.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 9 \u2013 Trek to Kedarnath Temple",
        "description": "In the morning, we\u2019ll depart from Sonprayag to start the trek to the Kedarnath temple.\nBegin your 16 km trek via Gaurikund. You can also hire a pony/Palki service to reach the Kedarnath Dham.\nOnce you reach the temple, engage in the Darshan and Poojan ritual. The views all around are gorgeous, providing you with a backdrop of snow-capped peaks.\nWait till the sun goes down, when you can attend the evening Aarti, which is a soul-stirring experience, to say the least.\nYour dinner and overnight stay will be arranged in Kedarnath only.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 10 \u2013 Morning Aarti at Kedarnath and Transfer to Rudraprayag",
        "description": "Wake up early before sunrise and attend the morning Aarti at Kedarnath temple.\nNow trek back to Sonprayag. From there, you\u2019ll be taken to Rudraprayag.\nCheck into your hotel there and enjoy an overnight stay."
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 11 \u2013 Overnight Train to Varanasi",
        "description": "Have a hearty breakfast.\nNow, you\u2019ll be driven back to Haridwar.\nOnce you reach there, board the overnight train for Varanasi. Your lunch and dinner will be served on the train itself."
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 12 \u2013 Evening Ganga Aarti at Varanasi",
        "description": "Welcome to Varanasi! This is one of the world\u2019s oldest cities, and is quite dear to Lord Shiva.\nNow check into your hotel and rest for a while.\nVisit the Dasaswamedh Ghat in the evening, where you can witness the grand Ganga Aarti live. Take in the whole experience of chants, bells, and floating lamps!\nCome back to your hotel in the evening for an overnight stay.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 13 \u2013 Kashi Vishwanath Jyotirlinga and Transfer to Deoghar",
        "description": "Wake up early to go for a morning Darshan at the Kashi Vishwanath Jyotirlinga. Perform Poojan to your heart\u2019s content.\nNext, we\u2019ll take you to the Sankat Mochan Hanuman Temple.\nAfter that, board a train to Jasidih. Once you get there, you\u2019ll take a short drive towards Deoghar, Jharkhand.\nEnjoy an overnight stay in your hotel at Deoghar.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 14 \u2013 Baba Baidyanath Jyotirlinga and Train to Chennai",
        "description": "Wake up early in the morning and get ready for Darshan at the Baba Baidyanath Jyotirlinga. This temple is special since here Lord Shiva is worshipped as a healer (Vaidya).\nPerform your Abhishek Puja & Darshan and soak in the calming atmosphere of the shrine. It is believed that Ravana himself worshipped Lord Shiva here by offering his heads as a sacrifice.\nNext, board a train to Kolkata from here. Once you reach Howrah station, take a connecting train to Chennai.\nEnjoy an overnight stay on the train.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 15 \u2013 Arrival in Chennai and Train to Rameswaram",
        "description": "You\u2019ll arrive in Chennai in the morning.\nTake some time to freshen up and relax in the station waiting room.\nLater, board the train to Rameswaram, one of the most holy pilgrimage towns in India!\nEnjoy an overnight stay on the train."
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 16 \u2013 Arrival at Rameswaram (Leisure Day)",
        "description": "Once you reach Rameswaram, get to your hotel and check in.\nThe rest of the day is purposefully made free of any sightseeing. You can take this leisure time to rest or travel on your own around the area. If you go out, do indulge in the local Tamil vegetarian cuisine, which is simply delicious.\nAt night, enjoy dinner and get a restful night of sleep."
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 17 \u2013 Rameswaram Darshan and Drive to Madurai",
        "description": "We\u2019ll visit the Ramanathaswamy Temple early in the morning. This temple houses the very Rameshwaram Jyotirlinga that Lord Rama worshipped after he went to war with Ravana.\nAfterwards, you\u2019ll be taken for a drive to Madurai.\nIn the evening, visit the majestic Meenakshi Amman Temple, which is dedicated to Goddess Parvati. Enjoy the masterpiece of Dravidian architecture that this temple is!\nSpend the night in your Madurai hotel.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 18 \u2013 Train to Pune",
        "description": "Treat yourself to a delicious breakfast.\nNow, you\u2019ll be transferred to Madurai railway station, where you can board the train to Pune.\nEnjoy an overnight journey on the train."
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 19 \u2013 Arrival at Pune (Leisure Day)",
        "description": "Once you arrive in Pune, check into your hotel.\nThe rest of the day is free. You can utilize it by either resting or going sightseeing/shopping on your own.\nEnjoy the overnight stay at your hotel in Pune."
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 20 \u2013 Visit to Bhimashankar and Trimbakeshwar",
        "description": "Have breakfast and then get ready for the Jyotirlinga tour.\nToday, you\u2019ll be taken to the Bhimashankar Temple, which is located in the lush Sahyadri Hills. It's also considered to be the source of the river Bhima.\nIn the latter part of the day, we\u2019ll visit yet another Jyotirlinga, that is Trimbakeshwar Temple, which is located in Nashik.\nAt night, return to the hotel and get a restful night of sleep.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 21 \u2013 Trimbakeshwar Darshan, Nashik Sightseeing, and Trip to Shirdi",
        "description": "In the morning, set out again for the Darshan at the Trimbakeshwar Jyotirlinga.\nAfterwards, you\u2019ll indulge in a sightseeing tour of Nashik, where you\u2019ll be visiting:\nSita Gufa (This is where Sita stayed during exile)\nKapileshwar Temple\nKala Ram Temple\nPanchavati and Godavari River\nLater in the day, drive towards Shirdi and check into your hotel for an overnight stay.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 22 \u2013 Shirdi Sai Baba Darshan",
        "description": "After breakfast, get ready for Darshan of Shri Sai Baba at the famous Shirdi temple.\nSpend ample time here to perform Pooja, Aarti, and pay homage to Baba.\nEnjoy lunch and some free time for shopping at the local market for Sai Baba souvenirs.\nReturn to your hotel for overnight stay.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 23 \u2013 Transfer to Aurangabad",
        "description": "After breakfast, check out of the hotel and proceed towards Aurangabad.\nCheck into your Aurangabad hotel and enjoy a relaxed evening. Overnight stay at Aurangabad.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 24 \u2013 Ajanta-Ellora Caves Sightseeing",
        "description": "After breakfast, proceed for sightseeing of Ajanta and Ellora Caves. Ajanta caves are famous for their ancient Buddhist rock-cut architecture and murals.\nEllora caves are known for their Buddhist, Hindu, and Jain rock-cut temples, representing India\u2019s religious harmony.\nReturn to Aurangabad hotel in the evening and enjoy dinner and overnight stay."
      }
    ],
    "faqs": []
  },
  "2-days-ayodhya-tour-package": {
    "overview": "Get the best 2 days Ayodhya Tour package deals to see some of the most famous spiritual and cultural places and take part in spiritual rituals with My Quick Trippers. See More\n\nWe offer expert guides, comfort, best price and personalized services.\nWe, My Quick Trippers are one of the best tour operators, approved by trusting local authorities with verified customer reviews. We offer value for money, safety and comfort to our travellers.\n\nCall us Now \nand Get a free quote from our travel Expert, \n[Book Now]\n\nKey Highlights\nWhy Does Ayodhya Matter for a Hindu Devotee?\n\n\nAyodhya is a sacred abode of Lord Rama, Maryada Purushottam. The name Ayodhya comes from Sanskrit which means the city where no war can be fought against. \u2018A\u2019 means not and Ayodhya means war, so, it's a place where no war can be fought against. In the name Ayodhya, it hints at its eternal strength, harmony and peace as it is the birthplace of Lord Rama.\n\n\nVisit Ram Janmabhoomi Temple. It is the original birthplace of Lord Rama. After a long held wait of many years, the temple was consecrated on Jan 22nd, 2024.\n\n\nEnjoy numerous festivals related to Lord Rama like Ram Navami, Dussehra and experience the city\u2019s sacred charm.\n\n\nThere are many places in Ayodhya like Kanak Bhawan, Dashrath Mahal which will take you back in the time of Treta Yuga.\n\n\nKey Highlights of 2 Day Ayodhya Tour\n\nYou will get hassle free pick up and drop service within Ayodhya. Our driver will take care of all the routes while you enjoy your trip with the loved ones.\nAccording to the chosen Tour package, you will get comfortable and centrally located hotels & guesthouses to relax after spiritual tours.\nVIP and Guided Darshan of Ram Janmabhoomi, Hanuman Garhi, Kanak Bhawan, and Treta Ke Thakur.\nWe offer Family-friendly, group, and senior citizen-friendly tour packages at best price.\n\nWhat are the Places Covered in the 2 Day Ayodhya Tour?\n\n\n\n\nAyodhya Famous Places\nDetails\n\n\n\n\nRam Janmabhoomi\nScared Birthplace of Lord Rama\n\n\nKanak Bhawan\nA sacred gift to Lord Rama and Devi Sita by Keikei just after their marriage\n\n\nHanuman Garhi\nDivine abode of the protector of Ayodhya\n\n\nSaryu River Aarti and Ram Ki Paidi\nSacred places where all the sins dissolve and devotees embrace eternal peace\n\n\nDashrath Mahal\nAbode of King Dasharatha, Father of Lord Rama\n\n\nValmiki Ramayana Bhawan (Optional)\nDedicated to the creator of the divine Ramayana, Valmiki.\n\n\nTreta Ke Thakur (Optional)\nA place where Lord Rama performed Ashwamedha Yagya\n\n\n\n\nHow Much Does a 2 Day Ayodhya Tour package Cost?\nAyodhya Tour Package Options\n\n\n\n\nPackage\nCost\nInclusion\n\n\n\n\nStandard Ayodhya Tour Package\nStarts @ INR 18, 900\nHotels, Meals, Transfers, Darshan Assistance, Guide\n\n\nLuxury Ayodhya Tour Package\nStarts @ INR 38,500\nLuxury Hotels, Private Car, VIP Darshan Assistance, Tour Guide\n\n\n\n\n\nThe exact price of the Ayodhya Tour package depends on the category of hotel chosen, \ntravel duration, group size, transportation needs etc. We have categorized our Tour \nPackages for different types of travel style and budget needs. To simplify your planning, \ncheck our different budget Ayodhya Tour Packages-\n\n\n\nSpecial Senior Citizen Packages for Ayodhya Tour (with extra assistance)- In this type of package, we will take care of all the travel needs with extra care for your elder ones.\n\n\nFamily-Friendly Yatra Packages- If you have kids then this type of tour package will suit your needs. We will offer best guides and 24/7 assistance throughout your journey.\n\n\nGroup Tours (Corporate, Societies, NGOs)- If you are travelling in a group, this package will cater to your needs to enjoy Ayodhya Tour. We offer best deals and discounts for large groups.\n\n\nCustom Date Departures for NRIs & International Devotees- If you are a foreigner, this package will cater to all your hotel, transportation needs including transfers, VIP Darshan and expert guide.\n\n\nBudget Yatra Packages for Students & Young Travelers- It is a perfect deal for students or young travelers who are spiritually inclined and looking for a budget deal. We offer best deals for advance booking. This package includes hotel, transport, meals and guided tours.\n\n\nWhen is the Best Time to Book Ayodhya Tour?\nPeak Season- October to March is the best time to enjoy the Ayodhya tour with family. It\u2019s the best time to have a soul soothing experience of the spiritual wealth of Ayodhya. During this time the weather remains pleasant for sightseeing and strolling in Ghats for hours. You will also be able to enjoy some of the most prominent festivals like Dussehra, Navratri, Diwali, Ram Mandir Pran Pratishtha ceremony (22nd Jan). It's the peak season of Ayodhya Tourism so book your hotels and flight/train tickets in advance to enjoy a hassle-free trip.\nWhen Not to Visit Ayodhya?\nSummer (April- June)\nThis is not a peak tourism season in Ayodhya so you can visit here if you are a budget conscious traveller. During this time the flights/ train tickets and hotel price drop down. But if you really want to enjoy the Ayodhya tour comfortably then try not to visit during this time. The extreme heat will make the journey physically draining especially for senior citizens and kids. Waiting in long queues and long walks to reach the temple premises during this time can be frustrating. The temperature may also rise up to 40 degrees Celsius.\nPeak Monsoon (July- August)\nDuring this time, heavy rains might disrupt your travel plans for exploring famous temples and boat ride plans at Saryu River.\nBased on your 2024-25 weather records and the official Uttar Pradesh Tourism\u2019s festival calendar, these months are the best for a soul-pleasing Ayodhya Tour for devotees of Lord Rama.\n\n\n\n\nSeason\nMonths\nWeather\nPros\nCons\n\n\n\n\nBest Time\nOctober - March\nPleasant weather to enjoy Sightseeing\nIdeal for exploring Ayodhya (Festive months)\nHigher prices of hotels and flight / train tickets, crowded\n\n\nShoulder Season\nFebruary - March\nModerate (can enjoy)\nEnjoy the festival of Vasant Panchami, Holi, Still pleasant to enjoy Ayodhya Tour\nThe temperature rises in the month of March\n\n\nOff Season\nApril- June\nVery Hot (Not favorable)\nBest for budget conscious travellers\nNot ideal to enjoy wholeheartedly for kids and senior citizens\n\n\nMonsoon\nJuly- September\nRainy and Humid (Not Favorable)\nLush greenery, refreshing vibes\nRains can disrupt travel plans.\n\n\n\n\nIs the Ayodhya Tour perfect for senior citizens and families?\nYes, absolutely, Ayodhya Tour is perfect for senior citizens and families with kids. For the citizens who cannot walk, we offer Palki services, cycle rickshaw and other necessary arrangements on request to make the journey full of comforts. My Quick Trippers\u2019s tailor-made itineraries are suitable for every traveller whether its families with kids or senior citizens. Moreover, Ayodhya\u2019s famous temples are senior citizen and kid friendly. There are proper pathways, ramps and escalators in some of the most famous temples.\nAre Group Tours and Custom Itineraries Available?\nYes, My Quick Trippers offers a group tour for Ayodhya with fixed departure. Our tour packages are very cost effective and full of comforts. From guided tours, to proper transportation, meals, VIP Darshans and hotel stays we offer best services to the travellers at best price.\nHow Do I Book the Ayodhya Tour?\nIn our Ayodhya Tour, you will get good transportation, meals, guided tours, VIP Darshans and stay facilities. There would be no hurry, you will travel at your own pace. Our tailor-made itineraries are customizable according to your need and budget. We have made the booking process simple for you to avoid confusion. Follow these simple steps-\n\nPlease send us an inquiry about the Ayodhya Tour. Choose your travel date.\nYou will get your itinerary and quotation prepared by our travel representatives.\nDiscuss your preferences and customize your Ayodhya itinerary.\nConfirm the Tour and make payment. Payment can be made by UPI, by Cheque / Demand Draft/ money transfer (RTGS & NEFT), Google Pay, Paytm, PhonePe or any other wallet app, PayPal, via bank transfer, Debit card/ Credit Card (3% Bank charges).\nGet your invoice and tour confirmation voucher.\n\nKindly fill out this Booking form to book your Tour\n\nIf you want to book your Ayodhya Tour through Mobile, you can send us the tour details, and we will get back to you within 24 hours.\n\nDownload our Android Mobile app- My Quick Trippers or iOS app- My Quick Trippers to book Ayodhya tour packages in one click and get the best offers.\nWhat Safety Neasures are followed on the Ayodhya tour?\nAt My Quick Tripperss we ensure safety and comfort to all our travellers booking Ayodhya Trip with their family with us. We offer\n\nLicensed vehicle providers with trained drivers\nWe offer verified multi-lingual tour guides\nHotels that are well sanitized in a safe location\n24/7 Support to solve any unforeseen situations\nWe offer secure payment gateways and proper invoices\nClear terms and conditions on refunds, cancellations and overall pricing.\n\nSee Less",
    "highlights": [
      "Ayodhya is a sacred abode of Lord Rama, Maryada Purushottam. The name Ayodhya comes from Sanskrit which means the city where no war can be fought against. \u2018A\u2019 means not and Ayodhya means war, so, it's a place where no war can be fought against. In the name Ayodhya, it hints at its eternal strength, harmony and peace as it is the birthplace of Lord Rama.",
      "Visit Ram Janmabhoomi Temple. It is the original birthplace of Lord Rama. After a long held wait of many years, the temple was consecrated on Jan 22nd, 2024.",
      "Enjoy numerous festivals related to Lord Rama like Ram Navami, Dussehra and experience the city\u2019s sacred charm.",
      "There are many places in Ayodhya like Kanak Bhawan, Dashrath Mahal which will take you back in the time of Treta Yuga."
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1: Arriving in Ayodhya - Feel the divine presence of Lord Rama",
        "description": "On the first day, our tour representative will pick you up from your designated location (station/airport) and transfer you to your pre-booked hotel. After some relaxation, you will enjoy a guided Ayodhya Tour. We will explore the following places-\nRam Janmabhoomi-\nRam Janmabhoomi is a landmark temple as it is the birthplace of Lord Rama. devotees from all across the world visit here to get the divine blessings of Lord Rama. After a long held wait of many years, the sacred consecration of the temple took place on Jan22nd 2024.\nKanak Bhawan Temple-\nKanak Bhavan has kept the stories of Treta Yuga. This sacred temple was a gift to Lord Rama and Goddess Sita just after their wedding by Kaikeyi. It used to be their personal residence.\nDashrath Mahal -\nIt is a popular Siddha Peetha, and divine abode of King Dasharatha, (father of Lord Rama). You will see the beautiful idols of Lord Rama, Devi Sita, Lakshman, Shatrughan and Bharat here.\nHanuman Garhi-\nHanuman Garhi is dedicated to Lord Hanuman who is considered as a protector of Ayodhya. It is said that Lord Hanuman resides in a cave and watches over the entire city of Ayodhya to protect them from all the evils.\nEvening Tour-\nEmbracing Bhakti, culture and peace wholeheartedly\nThe divine Aarti at Saryu River in Naya Ghat is something which will take your breath away.\nWitness the living spiritual heritage of Ayodhya as you stroll along the serene Saryu River Ghats.\nOvernight stay-\nAfter the sightseeing Ayodhya Tour with your loved ones, the day ends on a happy note. We will return to our hotel room for an overnight stay.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 2: Cultural and spiritual escape in the city of Legends",
        "description": "After breakfast in the morning, we will explore the Saryu River to take a holy dip for spiritual purification and enjoy a scenic boat ride.\nWe will also witness the sacred\nRam ki Paidi-\nIt's a beautiful series of Ghats built on the banks of the Saryu River. It\u2019s a place where devotees take holy dip to dissolve their sins.\nNageshwarnath Temple-\nIt is a must not miss place when you are on Ayodhya Tour. We will visit here for sure. It\u2019s a temple dedicated to Lord Shiva, built by Kush ( son of Lord Rama).\nIf time allows, we will explore,\nValmiki Ramayana Bhawan\u2013\nThe sacred Bhawan is dedicated to Sage Valmiki (Creator of Ramayana). Its lush greenery and peaceful vibe are a perfect spot for meditation and relaxation.\nTreta Ke Thakur-\nTreta Ke Thakur is a very popular sacred spot in Ayodhya. It\u2019s the same place where Lord Rama performed Ashwamedha Yagya. There are many statues in this temple made of Blackstone and belonging to the era of Vikramaditya.\nEvening-\nAyodhya is a place where you will discover your soul and be nourished by the eternal heritage of faith. After sightseeing, we will depart from Ayodhya with the divine blessings of Lord Rama, Mata Sita and Lord Hanuman. We will drop you at your selected location and the trip to Ayodhya will end on a happy note.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      }
    ],
    "faqs": []
  },
