  "2-days-khajuraho-tour": {
    "overview": "Visit Khajuraho, which wraps spirituality and artistry in one tour! See More\n\nSee temples that are dedicated to ancient gods, carvings that drew inspiration from life itself, and exquisite architecture that baffles even today\u2019s great minds! To enjoy a seamless tour here, book our Khajuraho tour package that will take care of all the travel logistics for you so that you can enjoy your trip peacefully, as it\u2019s supposed to be.This two-day Khajuraho trip gives you a glimpse of yesteryear\u2019s culture like no other. And with our services, you can comfortably live the whole experience. Book now to go on an unforgettable adventure of your life!See Less\n\nSee temples that are dedicated to ancient gods, carvings that drew inspiration from life itself, and exquisite architecture that baffles even today\u2019s great minds! To enjoy a seamless tour here, book our Khajuraho tour package that will take care of all the travel logistics for you so that you can enjoy your trip peacefully, as it\u2019s supposed to be.\n\nThis two-day Khajuraho trip gives you a glimpse of yesteryear\u2019s culture like no other. And with our services, you can comfortably live the whole experience. Book now to go on an unforgettable adventure of your life!\n\nTour GalleryTour NameKhajuraho 2 Day Sightseeing TourTour Duration02 Days / 01 NightMealsBreakfastVehicle TypeSedan / SUVStarting & Ending PointKhajurahoDestination CoveredKhajuraho - TKandariya Mahadev Temple - Parshvanatha TemplePickup TimeDepend on your Flight Timing Tour BenefitsBest price & enjoyable travel guarantee",
    "highlights": [
      "Explore UNESCO World Heritage Khajuraho Temples known for stunning carvings & architecture",
      "Visit the Western Group:Kandariya Mahadev Temple \u2013 Grandest masterpieceLakshmana Temple \u2013 Rich mythological carvingsVishwanath Temple \u2013 Shiva temple with NandiJagdambi Temple \u2013 Elegant artistic detailing",
      "Kandariya Mahadev Temple \u2013 Grandest masterpiece",
      "Lakshmana Temple \u2013 Rich mythological carvings",
      "Vishwanath Temple \u2013 Shiva temple with Nandi",
      "Jagdambi Temple \u2013 Elegant artistic detailing",
      "Eastern Jain Temples \u2013 Parsvanath, Adinath & Shantinath Enjoy the Sound & Light Show and traditional dance performanceCultural storytelling sessions about Chandela historyTrip to the scenic Raneh FallsPeaceful heritage walks through gardens & pathwaysVisit the Archaeological Museum",
      "Enjoy the Sound & Light Show and traditional dance performance",
      "Cultural storytelling sessions about Chandela history",
      "Trip to the scenic Raneh Falls",
      "Peaceful heritage walks through gardens & pathways",
      "Visit the Archaeological Museum",
      "See More"
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1: Sightseeing at Western Group of Temples",
        "description": "After your arrival at Khajuraho, you\u2019ll be transferred to your hotel by our team representative. Drop your bags and freshen up!\nNow, get ready for sightseeing at the Western Group of Temples! Explore Kandariya Mahadev Temple, Lakshman Temple, Chausath Yogini Temple, and more.\nIn the evening, you can enjoy the cultural Light & Sound Show as well as a local dance performance that is held there regularly.\nCome back to the hotel and have a restful night of sleep.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 2: Visit to Eastern Group of Temples and Departure",
        "description": "Relish a hearty breakfast in the morning.\nToday, you\u2019ll explore the Eastern and Southern Group of Temples. See sculptures and statues at Parshvanatha Temple, Adinath Temple, Ghantai Temple, etc.! Enjoy artistic depictions of Apsaras, human emotions, stages of life, and much more!\nIf time permits, you\u2019ll be taken to watch the majestic Raneh Falls, where you can enjoy photography, too.\nLater, you\u2019ll be transferred back to the Khajuraho Airport/ Railway station from where you can cover your further journey. Your trip here concludes with us!\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      }
    ],
    "faqs": []
  },
  "2nights-3days-orissa-tour-package": {
    "overview": "Odisha is a beautiful state, known as the soul of India, located near the Bay of Bengal on the eastern coast.  See More\n\nIt has a wide range of tourist attractions because this place is blessed with a vibrant culture, natural beauty, and impressive monuments. Nature lovers can also enjoy its scenic beaches and green forests\nVisitors should explore Odisha\u2019s famous Jagannath Temple, especially during the popular Rath Yatra festival. Apart from this, Sun temple is also a perfect place to see its beautiful architecture. \nThis trip covers four places in Odisha, such as Bhubaneswar, Konark, Puri, and Pipli. It is a 3-day Odisha trip, where you can choose between an affordable holiday tour or a luxury vacation. This tour package is also customizable and includes meals, hotels, and transportation. Book now for this unforgettable trip to see the beauty of Odisha. \nSee Less\n\nIt has a wide range of tourist attractions because this place is blessed with a vibrant culture, natural beauty, and impressive monuments. Nature lovers can also enjoy its scenic beaches and green forests\n\nVisitors should explore Odisha\u2019s famous Jagannath Temple, especially during the popular Rath Yatra festival. Apart from this, Sun temple is also a perfect place to see its beautiful architecture.\n\nThis trip covers four places in Odisha, such as Bhubaneswar, Konark, Puri, and Pipli. It is a 3-day Odisha trip, where you can choose between an affordable holiday tour or a luxury vacation. This tour package is also customizable and includes meals, hotels, and transportation. Book now for this unforgettable trip to see the beauty of Odisha.",
    "highlights": [
      "Full day Bhubaneswar sightseeing",
      "Konark sun temple darshan",
      "Darshan and visit to Jagannath temple",
      "Satapada exploration",
      "Chilka lake visit with boat ride"
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1: Arrival at Bhubaneswar (the capital of Odisha)",
        "description": "When you reach Bhubaneswar Airport or Railway Station, our representative will welcome you and take you to the hotel. Next you will visit the twin hills of Khandagiri and Udayagiri, where you can explore Jain Temple and Elephanta Caves, including the Lion Cave and Queen Cave from the first century BC. Bhubaneswar is famous for its temples built from the 7th to the 13th centuries. In this temple city, you can see the temples like Lingaraj, Mukteshwar, Kedargouri, Parashurameshvara Mandir, and Bindusagar.\nNote:\nNandankanan, the State Museum, and the Tribal Museum are closed on Mondays and state holidays.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 2: Bhubaneswar - Dhauli - Pipli - Konark - Puri",
        "description": "After breakfast, drive to Konark and stop to explore Dhauli (a Buddhist Stupa and peace pagoda) and Pipli (a popular village for its decorative work). When you reach Konark, visit the famous Konark Sun Temple. It was constructed in the 13th century by King Narasimha. Now, proceed to Puri, and on the way, visit Chandrabhaga Beach, which has amazing clean sands, and ramachandi Temple. Then, go to Puri and check into the hotel. In the evening, explore Puri and visit Shri Jagannath Temple, this temple is important in Odisha\u2019s culture and religion. Over the years, many kings, religious leaders, worshippers, and devotees come to visit. It is famous around the world. Next, stay overnight at a hotel.\nNote:\nTravelers cannot visit the Jagannath Temple during the \u201cAnavasara\u2019\u2019 period, from the Krishna Paksha of Ashada month until the Jagannath Rath Yatra begins.\nDate -\n27 June 2025\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 3: Depart from Puri to Bhubaneshwar (60 kms /2 hours)",
        "description": "After breakfast, end your \u2018Puri Konark Tour\u2019. Return to Bhubaneswar, on the way stop at Raghurajpur, a village popular for its Pattachitra paintings, palm leaf art, wooden toys and more. You will also pass through Pipli and Dhauli. The trip ends at Bhubaneswar railway station.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      }
    ],
    "faqs": []
  },
