  "3-days-madurai-rameshwaram-tour": {
    "overview": "With our 3 Days Madurai Rameshwaram Tour Package you can explore the real charm of South India in just 3 days. It is a perfect choice for those who have limited time but still want to see everything - famous temples, local culture and calm beaches in a short trip.See More\n\nThis journey starts in Madurai, a beautiful city surrounded by peaceful hills. This town is full of old temples and the most famous one is Meenakshi Amman Temple. Its excellent architecture attracts everyone, even visitors from other countries. Apart from this, if you get a chance, try Madurai's famous drink, Jigarthanda, which is loved all over India.\nThe journey also includes Rameshwaram, a wonderful place that needs no introduction. It is where Lord Rama and his army built a bridge to reach Sri Lanka. You'll see many interesting places here so plan your Madurai to Rameshwaram Trip to explore even more!\nSee Less\n\nThis journey starts in Madurai, a beautiful city surrounded by peaceful hills. This town is full of old temples and the most famous one is Meenakshi Amman Temple. Its excellent architecture attracts everyone, even visitors from other countries. Apart from this, if you get a chance, try Madurai's famous drink, Jigarthanda, which is loved all over India.\n\nThe journey also includes Rameshwaram, a wonderful place that needs no introduction. It is where Lord Rama and his army built a bridge to reach Sri Lanka. You'll see many interesting places here so plan your Madurai to Rameshwaram Trip to explore even more!",
    "highlights": [
      "Explore Madurai and Rameshwaram, two famous spiritual cities known for ancient temples and peaceful surroundings.",
      "Visit Ramanathaswamy Temple, Agni Theertham, Dhanushkodi and the Pamban Bridge.",
      "See Madurai's charm with Meenakshi Amman Temple and taste the local drink, Jigarthanda.",
      "Pick-up and drop-off service included.",
      "See More"
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 01- Madurai - Rameshwaram (173 km/ 3-4 hrs)",
        "description": "The Madurai tour begins as you are picked up from your selected point - Airport, Railway Station, or your chosen location in Madurai. Our\nMy Quick Trippers\nteam will welcome you and take you to Rameshwaram. If you choose a guide, he will join the driver and help you whole day.\nOn arrival, check into the hotel and later visit-\nRamanathaswamy Temple-\nIt is one of\nthe 12 Jyotirlingas\n, located near the ocean, where the sea waves and scenic views make the place even more beautiful.\nAgnitheertham\nRamjharoka Temple-\nThe temple is famous for Lord Rama's footprints, and many tourists often share that they feel very relaxed here due to the cool wind and peaceful surroundings.\nAfter exploring the main attractions in Rameshwaram, return to the hotel for an overnight stay.\nNote-\nRamanathaswamy Temple timings are from\n5:00 AM\nto 1:00 PM and\n3:00 PM\nto 9:00 PM.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 02- In Rameswaram",
        "description": "Early in the morning, around\n5:00 AM\n, proceed for a holy bath at\nAgni Theertham (Sea Bath).\nNow visit the\nSphatik Lingam (Mani Darshan).\nIt is believed that praying here with a pure heart brings good fortune and happiness.\nAfter this, bathe in the\n22 sacred wells\ninside the Ramanathaswamy Temple, known as\nTheerth Snanam.\nAfter the holy bath and Darshan, return to the hotel for breakfast.\nAfter breakfast, start your\nRameshwaram\nsightseeing tour. Visit the\nFive-faced Hanuman Temple, Ramar Patham, Kothandaramaswamy Temple, Gandamadana Parvatham, Rama Setu or Adam's Bridge, Dr. A. P. J. Abdul Kalam's House and Dhanushkodi\n(a beautiful spot to enjoy sunset).\nAfter sightseeing, return to the hotel. Overnight stay at\nRameshwaram\n.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 03- Rameswaram - Madurai *Departure* (200 km/ 3-4 hrs)",
        "description": "Early in the morning, visit the Ramanathaswamy temple again or take a holy dip in the sea, known as\nSamudra Snanam\n. After that, drive back to Madurai.\nOn the way, stop at the\nPamban Bridge\nand\nPamban Rail Scissors Bridge\n, famous for their beautiful views (Don't forget to click pictures here).\nWhen you reach Madurai, visit the famous\nMeenakshi Amman Temple\n. Spread over\n14 acres\n, this temple will impress you with its size and beauty and there are more than\n33,000\nstone statues.\nThe\nRameshwaram Tour from Madurai\nends with wonderful memories as you will be dropped at Madurai Airport or Railway Station for your next journey.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      }
    ],
    "faqs": []
  },
