  "3-days-srisailam-mallikarjuna-jyotirlinga-tour": {
    "overview": "If you\u2019re not sure how to plan for the 3 Days Srisailam Mallikarjuna Jyotirlinga Darshan, this package helps with everything you need for a smooth journey. See More\n\nIt is located in Andhra Pradesh, surrounded by green forests and a peaceful atmosphere. This temple is very important in Hinduism as it is one of the 12 Jyotirlinga in India.Another interesting fact is that this temple is also a Shakti Peetha, where it is believed that Goddess Sati\u2019s neck fell. Apart from main temple, our guests will visit Srisailam Dam where the natural views and cool wind create a heavenly vibe!You will also visit Golconda Fort known for its beautiful architecture. If time allows don\u2019t miss the evening light show here - it\u2019s truly memorable. There\u2019s a lot to explore mentioned in our itinerary so plan your Srisailam Mallikarjuna trip and make the journey unforgettable.See Less\n\nIt is located in Andhra Pradesh, surrounded by green forests and a peaceful atmosphere. This temple is very important in Hinduism as it is one of the 12 Jyotirlinga in India.\n\nAnother interesting fact is that this temple is also a Shakti Peetha, where it is believed that Goddess Sati\u2019s neck fell. Apart from main temple, our guests will visit Srisailam Dam where the natural views and cool wind create a heavenly vibe!\n\nYou will also visit Golconda Fort known for its beautiful architecture. If time allows don\u2019t miss the evening light show here - it\u2019s truly memorable. There\u2019s a lot to explore mentioned in our itinerary so plan your Srisailam Mallikarjuna trip and make the journey unforgettable.",
    "highlights": [
      "Visit Srisailam Mallikarjuna Jyotirlinga, one of India\u2019s 12 Jyotirlingas and also a Shakti Peetha surrounded by peaceful forests.",
      "Explore Srisailam Dam, Pathala Ganga and Octopus Viewpoint for nature views, photography and boating experiences.",
      "Enjoy cultural spots like Bhramaramba Devi Temple, Sakshi Ganapathi Temple and Chenchu Lakshmi Tribal Museum for a spiritual and historical experience.",
      "End the trip with Hyderabad sightseeing, including Golconda Fort, Birla Mandir, Charminar and Salar Jung Museum for history, architecture, and local culture.",
      "See More"
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "DAY 01- Hyderabad - Srisailam (213 Kms / 4-5 Hours Drive)",
        "description": "Start your Srisailam Mallikarjuna Jyotirlinga Tour with a pick-up from your chosen location in Hyderabad, either from the airport or railway station. Our team from the\nMy Quick Trippers\nwill come to receive you, and then you will proceed to Srisailam.\nDuring the journey, visit-\nSrisailam Dam\nBhramaramba Devi Temple-\nBhramaramba is the goddess of black bees; many devotees believe that if you listen carefully inside the temple, you can hear a buzzing sound of bees; it is a divine power of Bhramaramba Devi.\nSakshi Ganapati Temple\nHatkeshwar Temple\nOctopus View Point-\nA beautiful viewpoint where the Krishna River flows between the hills, and the shape looks like an octopus (A great spot for photography).\nChenchu Lakshmi Tribal Museum\nPathala Ganga\nRopeway, Srisailam-\nEnjoy a cable car ride above the hills and forests, with a beautiful view of the valley.\nAfter reaching Srisailam, check in at the hotel. In the evening, visit the Mallikarjuna Temple for Darshan. Stay overnight in Srisailam.\nNote-\nMallikarjuna Temple timings are 4:30 AM to 3:00 PM and 6:00 PM to 9:00 PM.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 02- Srisailam - Hyderabad (214 Kms / 4-5 Hours Drive",
        "description": "Begin the morning with Pooja and Darshan at\nLord Mallikarjuna Swamy Temple\n.\nAfterward, visit\nSri Bhramaramba Ammavari Shakti Peeth Temple\n, then explore\nPaladara\nand\nPanchdara\n(Beautiful spots for hiking and nature adventure).\nClimb\nSikharam hill\nto see\nShikaresvara Temple\n, and continue to\nSakshi Ganapathi Temple\nand\nPathala Ganga\n. Don\u2019t miss boating on\nKrishna River\n.\nLater, drive to\nHyderabad\n. If time permits, visit the\nStatue of Equality\nnear Hyderabad Airport.\nEnjoy your overnight stay in\nHyderabad\n.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 03- Hyderabad Sightseeing Departure",
        "description": "Early in the morning, have breakfast, check out from the hotel, and proceed for sightseeing. Sightseeing for this day will depend on your departure time (optional).\nYou may visit\nBirla Mandir\n, built on a hill. The view from the top is really amazing and worth capturing!\nAfter that, continue your journey to\nGolconda Fort\n.\nLater, visit the\nSalar Jung Museum\n.\nNow, go to the famous\nCharminar\n. Around it is Laad Bazaar, known for bangles, pearls and traditional Hyderabad items.\nContinue your trip to\nHussain Sagar Lake\n, tourists enjoy spending time here. The lake view is truly beautiful, and the big Buddha statue in the center makes it even more special.\nNext, you\u2019ll go to\nLumbini Park\n.\nIf you have some extra time, visit\nNTR Gardens\nfor a relaxing walk with beautiful fountains, and stop near the Sudha Cars Museum to see some unique car designs.\nLater, you\u2019ll be dropped at\nHyderabad\nAirport or Railway Station for your next journey.\nNote-\nOn Fridays, you can\u2019t do city sightseeing in Hyderabad because many places are closed.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      }
    ],
    "faqs": []
  },
  "3-days-tripura-sundari-tour": {
    "overview": "Fancy a trip to North East India that is filled with culture, heritage, and omnipresent spirituality? See More\n\nThen book our Agartala Tripura Sundari tour package, which will treat you with pre-booked hotels, delicious meals, and local transfers. With our expert guides, you can travel the city with ease and comfort. Our well-designed itinerary makes sure you see the best that the city has to offer and enjoy these three days to the maximum!\nThere\u2019s really a lot to see in this cultural city. Whether it\u2019s the ever-so majestic Neermahal Water Palace or the sculpture that dates back to the 15th century, the city makes sure you get the perfect dose of the culture, no matter for how long you\u2019re here. Stroll through its colourful Bazaars, enjoy scenic boat rides, or visit ancient temples \u2013 the atmosphere here is completely different from what you get in your daily city life. Coming here is a must at least once! Give us a call now so that we can arrange this special trip to the east for you!\nSee Less\n\nThen book our Agartala Tripura Sundari tour package, which will treat you with pre-booked hotels, delicious meals, and local transfers. With our expert guides, you can travel the city with ease and comfort. Our well-designed itinerary makes sure you see the best that the city has to offer and enjoy these three days to the maximum!\n\nThere\u2019s really a lot to see in this cultural city. Whether it\u2019s the ever-so majestic Neermahal Water Palace or the sculpture that dates back to the 15th century, the city makes sure you get the perfect dose of the culture, no matter for how long you\u2019re here. Stroll through its colourful Bazaars, enjoy scenic boat rides, or visit ancient temples \u2013 the atmosphere here is completely different from what you get in your daily city life. Coming here is a must at least once! Give us a call now so that we can arrange this special trip to the east for you!",
    "highlights": [
      "Seek Darshan at the highly revered Shakti Peeth Tripura Sundari Temple",
      "Exploration of the Ujjayanta Palace, which is considered a symbol of Tripura\u2019s royal heritage",
      "Visit to the stunning Neermahal Water Palace",
      "A scenic boat ride at Chabimura",
      "Witness ancient rock-cut sculptures in Devtamura Hills",
      "Discover wildlife at Sepahijala Wildlife Sanctuary",
      "Watch the flag-lowering ceremony at the Indo-Bangla Border",
      "Souvenir shopping for bamboo handicrafts and handwoven textiles"
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1: Arrival and Agartala Sightseeing",
        "description": "Upon your arrival in Agartala, you\u2019ll be greeted by our travel team representative.\nAfterwards, you\u2019ll be taken to the hotel. Check in and relax for a while.\nNow proceed for sightseeing, where you\u2019ll get to visit:\nUjjayanta Palace\nJagannath Temple\nLaxminarayan Temple\nHeritage Park\nIn the evening, you'll be driven to the\nIndo-Bangla Border\n, where you can watch the glorious\nflag-lowering ceremony.\nIf time permits, you can engage in some\nshopping at local markets.\nReturn to the hotel for an overnight stay.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 2: Tripura Sundari Temple - Chabimura Exploration - Neermahal - Sepahijala Wildlife Sanctuary",
        "description": "Treat yourself to a delicious breakfast in the morning.\nNow, you\u2019ll be taken to Udaipur, where you can seek blessings at the\nTripura Sundari Temple\n, one of the 51 Shakti Peethas.\nAfterwards, get ready for\nChabimura Exploration\n! Go on a\nboat ride on the Gomati River\n, through which you can watch rock-cut sculptures on Devtamura Hills. Prominent among them are:\nDevi Chakrakma (Mahishasura Mardini Durga)\nPanels of Shiva, Vishnu, Kartikeya, and Ganesha\nQueen in a palanquin\nNow, you\u2019ll be taken for a tour of\nNeermahal Water Palace\nand\nSepahijala Wildlife Sanctuary\n.\nIn the evening, return to Agartala.\nVisit the\nPurbasha Handicrafts Emporium,\nwhere you can shop for souvenirs, such as bamboo, cane, and handwoven items.\nGo back to the hotel and enjoy a restful night of sleep.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 3: Sightseeing and Departure",
        "description": "Enjoy a hearty breakfast before checking out of the hotel.\nYou\u2019ll be taken to the scenic\nKamalasagar Lake\nand the age-old\nKasba Kali Temple\n.\nNow, you'll be transferred to the airport/railway station from where you can continue your further journey.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      }
    ],
    "faqs": []
