  "3-days-ujjain-omkareshwar-tour": {
    "overview": "Feel spiritually nurtured by undertaking a spiritual pilgrimage with our Indore- Ujjain - Omkareshwar Tour Package that will help you visit the holiest sites of Lord Shiva, See More\n\nwhich include Omkareshwar and Mahakaleshwar of Ujjain. The 3 days/2 nights travel gives you ample time to visit these holy shrines and be soaked within their divine energy. On the way, you may also visit some other important spiritual places and taste Indore with its cultural flavor, vibrant market, and famous sweets. Indore Ujjain Omkareshwar tour package comes with a comfortable hotel stay, tasty food, and convenient transport facilities so that your trip has no problems and it is worth your money. We take care of the travel arrangements while you give your best to your spiritual quest with our 24/7 support. So, why the wait? Check our thoughtfully curated 3 days Indore-Ujjain-Omkareshwar tour package today and book a relaxing and hassle-free pilgrimage like never before!\n\nwhich include Omkareshwar and Mahakaleshwar of Ujjain. The 3 days/2 nights travel gives you ample time to visit these holy shrines and be soaked within their divine energy. On the way, you may also visit some other important spiritual places and taste Indore with its cultural flavor, vibrant market, and famous sweets.\n\nIndore Ujjain Omkareshwar tour package comes with a comfortable hotel stay, tasty food, and convenient transport facilities so that your trip has no problems and it is worth your money. We take care of the travel arrangements while you give your best to your spiritual quest with our 24/7 support. So, why the wait? Check our thoughtfully curated 3 days Indore-Ujjain-Omkareshwar tour package today and book a relaxing and hassle-free pilgrimage like never before!",
    "highlights": [
      "Worship Lord Shiva at the Mahakaleshwar Temple and also attend evening aarti.",
      "Make a visit to the ISKCON temple, Omkareshwar Jyotirlinga, Shakti Peeth, Harsiddhi Temple, Sandipani Ashram, Bade Ganesh Ka Mandir, and Ram Ghat.",
      "Take a holy dip in the River Narmada.",
      "Witness the charm of the Statue of Oneness.",
      "Exploration of Rajwada and Lalbagh Palace.",
      "Tasting sweet and other special delicacies of Indore and Ujjain.",
      "See More"
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1: Arrival in Indore to Ujjain (60 kms / 2-2.5 hrs)",
        "description": "When you get down at the railway station or at the airport in Indore, you shall have to travel to Ujjain. As soon as you reach the city, you need to first check in and then rest. After lunch in the afternoon, you must commence with your sightseeing activities in Ujjain. Some of the places that you will visit today are, the\nMahakaleshwar Jyotirlinga, ISKCON temple, Shakti Peeth,Gadkalika Temple, and the Harsiddhi Temple, Sandipani Ashram, Bade Ganesh Ka Mandir, Mahakal Lok and Ram Ghat\n. Later take an evening aarti at Mahakaleshwar Temple and back to the hotel. Have a sound sleep followed by a healthy and sumptuous dinner.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 2: Ujjain to Omkareshwar Day (139 km / 3-4 hrs)",
        "description": "Once you have your light breakfast at the hotel, start your day by getting the darshan of\nOmkareshwar Jyotirlinga\n. Have a sacred bath in the\nRiver Narmada\nand pray to her to get a good life. Moreover, the city is also named after Lord Shiva, and its shape is rather close to Om (\u0950). Apart from this, with our Indore Ujjain Omkareshwar tour packages, you get to explore the hanging bridge over the River Narmada. This is one of the best selfie spots where you can make some amazing reels and expand your social media follower list.\nMoreover, this city is home to 68 Teerths (holding high religious significance) and has a cluster of 108 Shivlingas, making it a must-visit Shiva site. You should also visit the ancient Mamleshwar temple, established beautifully on the left bank of the Narmada. Furthermore, don\u2019t forget to make a visit to the Statue of Oneness (dedicated to Adi Shankaracharya). It is believed that the sacred inscriptions on the temple walls are dated to 1063 AD. Maharani Ahilyabai Holkar was known to be devoted and a patron of architecture, and gave her patronage to this temple, now a protected monument by the Archaeological Survey of India (ASI). Pay a visit to the temple, then take on the Narmada Parikrama, a sacred circular route around Omkar Hill, which is around 7 km.\nApart from this, the path that runs along the parikrama route is filled with many ancient temples, peaceful ashrams, and the meeting of two rivers, hence making the route quite beautiful and spiritual. One can also take a boat ride along the Narmada River (on a direct payment basis) to find the natural beauty and tranquility of the place.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 3: Omkareshwar temple - Indore (78-80 kms 2- 3 hrs)",
        "description": "Get up early in the morning and drive towards the sacred Omkareshwar Temple and witness the religious aura of the place. This is the time to say goodbye to the city and return to Indore. If time allows you then you can visit some of the prominent landmarks of the city, including the historic Rajwada Palace and the elegant Lal Bagh Palace.\nYour Indore Ujjain Omkareshwar tour ends here. Leave Indore and head toward home. We would like to thank you for spending your time with us.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      }
    ],
    "faqs": []
  },
