  "4-days-mahavatar-babaji-cave-tour": {
    "overview": "Have you ever wanted to visit a secret cave filled with peaceful surroundings, natural beauty and amazing stories? See More\n\nThis Mahavatar Babaji Tour Package takes you to sacred cave near Dwarahat, Uttarakhand where pilgrims enjoy unique experiences and feel close to nature. Few people know about this hidden gem.It is believed that Mahavatar Babaji taught Kriya Yoga to help people feel calm, avoid negative energy, and make their mind and body refreshed. If time allows, you can also visit Pandav Kholi, close to Babaji\u2019s cave where the Pandavas once lived. You\u2019ll then go to Kainchi Dham near the beautiful Kosi River, popular for Neem Karoli Baba Ashram, which is world-famous; many foreign travelers and celebrities arrived here for its spiritual importance.Next, journey takes you to Nainital for a boat ride on Naini Lake, where you can spot colorful fish in clear water. The area is surrounded by beautiful cafes, markets, and famous temples. There\u2019s even more to explore, all mentioned in our itinerary. This Mahavatar Babaji tour plan is perfect for families, friends, and solo travelers. So let\u2019s explore and enjoy!See Less\n\nThis Mahavatar Babaji Tour Package takes you to sacred cave near Dwarahat, Uttarakhand where pilgrims enjoy unique experiences and feel close to nature. Few people know about this hidden gem.\n\nIt is believed that Mahavatar Babaji taught Kriya Yoga to help people feel calm, avoid negative energy, and make their mind and body refreshed. If time allows, you can also visit Pandav Kholi, close to Babaji\u2019s cave where the Pandavas once lived. You\u2019ll then go to Kainchi Dham near the beautiful Kosi River, popular for Neem Karoli Baba Ashram, which is world-famous; many foreign travelers and celebrities arrived here for its spiritual importance.",
    "highlights": [
      "Go on a trek to Mahavatar Babaji\u2019s Cave, sit quietly and meditate in its calm surroundings.",
      "Visit Kainchi Dham Ashram and experience Neem Karoli Baba\u2019s ashram.",
      "Explore Nainital, go for a boat ride on Naini Lake and watch the nature all around.",
      "Visit Dunagiri Mata Mandir and explore nearby temples known for their old style architecture.",
      "See More"
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1: Pantnagar - Kainchi Dham (70-85 km / 3-4 hours)",
        "description": "Start your journey with a warm welcome at Pantnagar Airport or Kathgodam Railway Station by our\nMy Quick Trippers\nrepresentative. If you include a guide, they will come along with the driver to make sure you have support all day. From here, enjoy a scenic drive to Kainchi Dham. After reaching, check into your hotel and take some time to relax.\nAfter that, explore the following place-\nKainchi Dham -\nVisit Kainchi Dham Temple, enjoy its spiritual atmosphere, and take photos of the beautiful surroundings as the ashram glows with lights.\nAfter exploring stay overnight at a hotel in Kainchi Dham.\nNote -\nKainchi Dham Temple timings are 6:00 AM to 9:00 PM.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 2: Kainchi Dham - Nainital - Dwarahat (Total Approx. 110 km / 4-5 Hours Drive)",
        "description": "Wake up early and spend a calm morning at\nKainchi Dham Ashram\n. Pray, meditate, light a Diya, offer flowers, or join the Aarti.\nAfter the Darshan, return to the hotel for breakfast.\nAfter checking out from the hotel, proceed to\nDwarahat\n. On the way, stop at\nNaini Lake\nin Nainital. You can enjoy boating, walk around the lake, and click beautiful photos. Also, visit\nNaina Devi\nTemple to pray and enjoy the view of the hills. (Goddess Sati\u2019s eye is believed to have fallen here).\nAfter sightseeing, the journey continues towards Dwarahat.\nOnce you arrive, stay overnight at the hotel.\nNote-\nPhotography is not allowed inside Kainchi Dham.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 3: Dwarahat to Mahavatar Babaji Cave (25 km Drive / 50 minutes + 3 km Trek / 1-1.5 hours)",
        "description": "Start your morning with a healthy breakfast. Then, prepare for a trek to\nMahavatar Babaji\u2019s Cave.\n(This trekking spot is great for bird watching).\nVisit the holy cave of Mahavatar Babaji where you can meditate and experience the spiritual atmosphere. This place is best for inner peace and positivity.\nSpend time at the\nMeditation Hut of YSS\n, surrounded by nature where you can observe and learn about the different kinds of plants and rare flowers in the area.\nNext visit\nDunagiri Mata Mandir\n, an ancient temple over 1,000 years old, dedicated to Goddess Durga. It is believed that while Hanuman was carrying Sanjivani Booti some herbs fell here, which makes the temple special.\nVisit other nearby temples such as a local\nVishnu temple\nand\nGujjar Dev Temple\n, you can take photos of their beautiful architecture.\nTrek back to the main road where your vehicle will pick you up and return to the hotel.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 4: Dwarahat - Pantnagar (115 Kms/ Approx. 3 Hrs)",
        "description": "Morning after breakfast, depart for Pantnagar. Your\nMahavatar Babaji cave tour package\nends with happy memories as we drop you at Delhi airport."
      }
    ],
    "faqs": []
  },
  "4-days-odisha-tour-packages": {
    "overview": "",
    "highlights": [],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1: Arrival at Bhubaneswar",
        "description": "You will be welcomed by our representative when you reach Bhubaneswar Airport or railway station, they will take you to the hotel. Next, you will see the twin hills of Khandagiri and Udayagiri, where you can find the Jain Temple, Elephanta Caves, Lion Cave, and the Queen Cave. Bhubaneswar is known for its beautiful temples constructed from 7th to 13th centuries. You can also visit many temples like Lingaraj, Mukteshwar, Parshuram mandir, Kedargouri, and Bindusagar. Then, stay overnight in a hotel.\nNote:\nNandankanan, the State Museum, and the Tribal Museum are closed on Mondays and on state holidays.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 2: Bhubaneswar - Dhauli - Pipli - Konark - Puri",
        "description": "After breakfast, you will proceed to Konark by vehicle. On the way, visit Dhauli to see the Buddhist Stupa and peace pagoda, and stop to explore Pipli (famous for its decorative work). Once you reach Konark, you will visit the popular Sun Temple that was constructed by King Narasimha in the 13th century. Now, you will travel to Puri. On the way, visit Chandrabhaga Beach, known for its clean sand and peaceful surroundings. You will also visit Ramchandi Temple. Now, go to Puri and check into the hotel. In the evening, Visit its famous Jagannath Temple (oldest Hindu temple). Over the years, it has attracted many kings, devotees, pilgrims, and people from around the world. Now, rest in a hotel for an overnight stay.\nNote:\nTourists cannot go to the Jagannath Temple during the \u201cAnavasara\u2019\u2019 period, from the Krishna Paksha of Ashada month until the Jagannath Rath Yatra begins.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 3: Puri Exploration",
        "description": "Next day, (after breakfast) visit Chilika Lake, the largest brackish water body in Asia, where you can see many birds and sea creatures. Take a boat to the island to enjoy nature and visit Kalijai Temple on Kalijai Island (this is an extra cost).\nNow, return to the hotel and relax on Puri\u2019s golden beach in the evening. Then, stay overnight.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 4: Depart from Bhubaneswar",
        "description": "This concludes the tour with happy memories, now we will drop you to Bhubaneswar airport or railway station for your onward journey."
      }
    ],
    "faqs": []
  },
