  "allahabad-varanasi-tour": {
    "overview": "This 2 nights/ 3 days long package has been designed to explore the beauties of two ancient and holy cities in India- Varanasi, and Allahabad. These two divine places located in the state of Uttar Pradesh holds a great place in Hindu mythology and their importance has been mentioned in the holy Hindu texts.\n\nAlso, the presence of River Ganges takes the religious significance of these cities to the highest level where one can indulge in spiritual activities.\nVaranasi, a holy city settled on the riverbank of Ganga boasts myriads of beauties known for their mystical charms that keep the devotees engaged all throughout the trip. Temples fringing the river, Ghats, and ancient temples are the key attractions of this city. Devotees flock to the Ghats and take a dip in the river to get rid of the sins they have committed in their entire life and some come to immerse the ashes of their dear ones and the ancestors. You can find the markets and the Ghats flooded with pilgrims throughout the year and you also participate in the various religious rituals performed at the Ghats. If you want to gain an extraordinary spiritual experience then Varanasi must be your next visit.\nAllahabad, a city popular among tourists for both history and the modern outlook is located in Uttar Pradesh. According to Hindu mythology, Lord Brahma also called as the god of creation descended in this holy city only. However, the city is always flooded with a huge number of tourists but during the auspicious Magh Mela, Allahabad witnesses a heavy crowd. The city is also known as \u201ccity of Prime Ministers\u201d as the record states that various Prime Ministers hail from this place only. One can visit a number of ancient temples and other numerous sightseeing attractions in Allahabad.",
    "highlights": [
      "Visit to the well-known Bharat Mata Mandir",
      "Visit the Triveni Sangam at Prayagraj",
      "Visit to Anand Bhawan and the lying Hanuman Temple are a must",
      "Also explore divinity at Sitamarhi and Vindhyachal temples",
      "Enjoy the boat ride in the evening on river Ganges",
      "At Varanasi visit the Vishwanath Temple, Tulsi Manas Mandir, Durga Temple, Sarnath, and most importantly Banaras Hindu University",
      "Relish the delectable in the streets of Varanasi"
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1 :In Varanasi",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 2 :Varanasi \u2013 Allahabad",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 3 :In Varanasi",
        "description": ""
      }
    ],
    "faqs": []
  },
