  "amarnath-tour": {
    "overview": "Amarnath Yatra, an annual pilgrimage organized by the state government of Jammu and Kashmir is counted amongst some of the most challenging pilgrimages in India.\n\nThis holy cave of Baba Barfani is one of the most acclaimed pilgrimages in India where tourists from all across the world come to pay their offerings and to seek the life-changing blessings of Lord Shiva.\nBeing located on an extreme altitude, the pilgrimage and its surrounding areas are covered with thick sheets of snow throughout the year and are opened only during the summer season when the snow starts melting down. When the shrine gets opened, the pilgrimage witnesses a huge crowd coming from different corners of the globe.\nSimilar to other religious places in the country, Amarnath also holds mythological tales associated with its origin and the most popular and interesting one is the incident of revealing the secret of life and birth stated by Lord Shiva to Goddess Parvati. The shreds of evidence of this incident can be witnessed on your trip to Amarnath as you will come to explore several places en-route the holy cave where the naturally formed ice stalagmite is worshipped. Those places are mentioned in that mythology of revealing the truth of life and if you want to get practical knowledge then you must plan your Amarnath Yatra by Helicopter in any coming year.\nAs stated above that this sacred cave is located at an insane location so one needs to take care of their safety and health. There are certain things that one needs to keep in mind if they are planning to embark on this holy Yatra like which is the perfect route to follow for your trip, the best time to visit, and there are many more things to take care of.",
    "highlights": [
      "Pahalgam, and its mesmerizingly beautiful landscape.",
      "The mesmerizingly beautiful views of Kashmir\u2019s landscape from the skies upon helicopter journey.",
      "A holy visit to Amarnath Cave."
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1 :Arrival Srinagar - Pahalgam (90 kms/3 hrs)",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 2 :Pahalgam - Panjtarni - Amarnath Holy Cave",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 3 :Pahalgam - Srinagar",
        "description": ""
      }
    ],
    "faqs": []
  },
