  "amarnath-yatra-helicopter": {
    "overview": "Amarnath attracts millions of devotees from all over India and abroad. The most wondrous thing about this holy shrine is the ice lingam that renews itself each year, symbolising Lord Shiva's eternal presence. Traditionally, trekkers reach the cave at the end of the Lidder Valley after an arduous journey. However, the easiest and fastest way is to go by helicopter and complete the Amarnath Yatra package in just 2 nights and 3 days.\n\nWe, My Quick Trippers, have something special for you; like every year, we have organised the Amarnath Yatra by helicopter, which will not only save your time but also provide you with a lifetime opportunity to sit in a helicopter and view the scenic mountains around the rugged Baltal Valley, snow-capped Himalayan peaks, glaciers, and the winding Amar Ganga River below. from sky heights. \nAmarnath Yatra 2026 runs from July 3 to August 28 \u2014 a 56-day season confirmed by the Shri Amarnathji Shrine Board (SASB). Helicopter slots fill fast once booking opens in May-June. Register at jksasb.nic.in early and book your package in advance. \nPrice Details\n\n\n\nTour Name\nAmarnath Yatra Helicopter via Baltal (Neelgrath Helipad)\n\n\n\n\nDuration\n2 Nights / 3 Days\n\n\nDestinations\nSrinagar \u2192 Sonmarg \u2192 Baltal \u2192 Panchtarni \u2192 Amarnath\n\n\nTour Price\nRs. 25,000 per person (min. 2 pax) | Season: July 3 - August 28, 2026\n\n\n\nAmarnath Helicopter Ticket Fare 2026 (SASB Fixed Rates)\nThe helicopter charges below are fixed by SASB and are included in our package price:\n\n\n\nRoute\nOne-Way\nRound Trip\nFlight Time\n\n\n\n\nBaltal (Neelgrath Helipad) to Panjtarni\nRs. 2,800 per person\nRs. 5,500 per person\n8-10 minutes\n\n\nPahalgam to Panjtarni\nRs. 4,600 per person\nRs. 9,200 per person\n20-30 minutes\n\n\n\nNo helicopter service is available from Panjtarni directly to the Amarnath cave. From Panjtarni, pilgrims cover the remaining 6 km on foot or by pony/palki. Book helicopter tickets at jksasb.nic.in or through us.\nAbout Amarnath Cave & Yatra 2026\nThe Amarnath Cave is a natural limestone cave at 3,888 metres (12,756 ft) in Anantnag district, Jammu & Kashmir \u2014 approximately 141 km from Srinagar. A naturally-forming ice Shivling appears inside the cave each year, growing and shrinking with the lunar cycle. Alongside it are two smaller ice formations representing Mata Parvati and Lord Ganesha.\nThe cave is accessible via two routes: Baltal (helicopter to Panjtarni + 6 km trek) or Pahalgam (46 km traditional trek or helicopter to Panjtarni + 6 km trek). Both routes end at Panjtarni \u2014 the helicopter's final landing point.\n\n\n\nDetail\n2026 Information\n\n\n\n\nYatra Start Date\nJuly 3, 2026\n\n\nYatra End Date\nAugust 28, 2026 (56 days total)\n\n\nRegistration Portal\njksasb.nic.in | Fee: Rs. 150 per person\n\n\nCave Altitude\n3,888 m (12,756 ft)\n\n\nPanjtarni to Cave Distance\n6 km \u2014 no helicopter available. Trek or pony/palki.\n\n\nAge Eligibility\n13 to 70 years. Pregnant women not permitted.\n\n\nPanjtarni Return Cut-off\n3:00 PM daily \u2014 must report by 3 PM for return helicopter\n\n\n\nAmarnath Yatra Registration 2026\nRegistration is mandatory for every pilgrim including helicopter Yatra. Without valid registration, no one is permitted at any helipad or base camp checkpoint. Three types are available:\n\nIndividual registration: For solo travellers or groups of fewer than 10 persons\nGroup registration: For groups of 10 or more persons\nNRI registration: For non-resident Indians travelling from abroad\n\nRegister at jksasb.nic.in or at designated bank branches \u2014 Punjab National Bank, SBI, J&K Bank, Yes Bank. Fee: Rs. 150 per person.\nCompulsory Health Certificate (CHC): Every pilgrim must obtain a CHC from an SASB-authorized government doctor confirming fitness for the high-altitude Yatra. Helipads check CHC before boarding. Our team provides complete guidance for both registration and CHC as part of your booking.",
    "highlights": [
      "A scenic view of Sonmarg with Thajiwas glacier and the Sindhu River",
      "Thrilling helicopter ride from Baltal to Panchtarni (15-20 min)",
      "Darshan of ice Shivling in Amarnath cave with priority pass",
      "Peaceful Shikara ride on Dal Lake at sunset",
      "Explore Mughal gardens, Nishat Bagh, Shalimar Bagh, Chashma Shahi for 2 nights and 3 days Amarnath Yatra helicopter package with hotel/houseboat stays",
      "Visit Shankaracharya Temple \u2014 one of the oldest Shiva temples in Kashmir with panoramic views of Dal Lake"
    ],
