  "andaman-a-short-visit": {
    "overview": "Tour Itinerary (Subject to weather conditions the itinerary may be shuffled)\n\nThe group of Andaman and Nicobar Islands sit prettily in the Bay of Bengal caressed by the surf, warm breezes and the Sun. Epitomizing Nature at its best, these islands will refresh and charm you when you join NamasteIndiaTrip Andaman Short Tour for all of 3 nights and 4 days.\n\nAndaman Short Tour Itinerary Package\n\n\nDay 1 :Port Blair\n\n\nArrive in Port Blair to a warm welcome by our tour guide who escorts you to your hotel. Refresh yourself, have a relaxed lunch, and then join the group for a visit to Corbyn\u2019s Cove Beach about 9 km from Port Blair. The beauty of the palm-lined golden sands will grab your soul and you will love to laze about or go bathing in the crystal clear waters. From here we proceed to the Cellular Jail (once known as Kalapani) and then we are treated to a Light and Sound Show that brings alive the freedom struggle of India. Return to your hotel for the night. You can set out on your own to explore the beach by moonlight.\n\n\n\n\nDay 2 :Port Blair \u2013 Havelock \u2013 Port Blair\n\n\nBreakfast on local fare and set out by ferry to explore Havelock Island. The ride is delightful and the boat coasts along on the swells for 2.5 hours and you can relax on deck. On arriving at Havelock we go on a half day sightseeing to Radhanagar Beach, rated the finest in all of Asia. Go swimming, laze about or go scuba diving for a view of the breathtaking underwater life. Return in the evening to Port Blair for stay in your hotel.\n\n\n\n\nDay 3 :North Bay and Ross Island Excursion\n\n\nRise early, breakfast and join the group for a full day excursion to the marvelous North Bay and Ross Islands. The coral reef, beautiful underwater life and stretches of sands will charm you. Return to your hotel in the evening.\n\n\n\n\nDay 4 :Departure Port Blair\n\n\nBreakfast over, the tour comes to an end and our tour guide assists you to get to the airport for the return journey. You promise to return and join NamasteIndiaTrip extended Andaman tour sometime soon.",
    "highlights": [],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1 :Port Blair",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 2 :Port Blair \u2013 Havelock \u2013 Port Blair",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 3 :North Bay and Ross Island Excursion",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 4 :Departure Port Blair",
        "description": ""
      }
    ],
    "faqs": []
  },
  "andaman-beach-tour": {
    "overview": "Andaman has swaying palm trees, soft white sandy beaches, lovely mangroves, and enticing tropical rainforests. Andaman is an excellent beach tourism destination in India for unwinding and spending time in the many peaceful and unspoiled areas nearby.\n\nAndaman beaches are ideal vacation destinations for those who are tired of the constant and stressful hustle and bustle of city life.\nAndaman can help you relieve stress and spend time alone with nature and solitude during your beach vacation. As a result, this is an ideal remote destination where you can not only relax but also participate in water sports on Andaman beaches when the desire for adventure arises. The 4 days / 3 night tour will be the best stress relief trip for you.\n\nAndaman beaches are ideal vacation destinations for those who are tired of the constant and stressful hustle and bustle of city life.\n\nAndaman can help you relieve stress and spend time alone with nature and solitude during your beach vacation. As a result, this is an ideal remote destination where you can not only relax but also participate in water sports on Andaman beaches when the desire for adventure arises. The 4 days / 3 night tour will be the best stress relief trip for you.\n\nAndaman Beach Tour Itinerary Package\n\n\nDay 1 :Arrival at Port Blair and Sightseeing\n\n\nThe My Quick Trippers representative will welcome you at the Port Blair airport (Veer Savarkar) and take you safely to the pre-booked hotel for check-in. Rest for some time in the hotel after which you will go for sightseeing to the places cited below.\nSamudrika Museum: This place is under the supervision of the Indian Navy. The various sections in it dedicated to Marine Life, Geographical information, the local people and archaeology. It also has an impressive colorful fish, shells and corals collection.\nAnthropological Museum: This place was built between1975-76 and depicts the Negrito tribes of Andaman that include the Sentinels, the Jarawas, the Onges and the Great Andamanese along with the Mongoloid Nicobar tribes including the Shompens and the Nicobarese. This place describes the development of the people by stage and their present lifestyle. The display includes tools, handicrafts, weapons, photographs and other \u2018art and crafts\u2019.\nFisheries Museum: This place houses over 350 marine life species. These are all placed on display and belong mostly to the Indo- Pacific Ocean and the Bay of Bengal. It is located just next to the \u2018Rajiv Gandhi Water Sports Complex\u2019 in Port Blair.\nCellular Jail: This jail has a historical significance with its construction in the 19th century in the shape of a wheel that has 7 spokes. However, only 3 out of the 7 wings exist today.\nSound & Light Show: You can opt for a \u2018Sound and Light Show\u2019 at the \u2018National Memorial Cellular Jail\u2019 in which the freedom struggle movement of India is depicted using sound and light. The show is presented in both Hindi and English.\nReturn to the Hotel for Night Stay\n\n\n\n\nDay 2 :Port Blair \u2013 Havelock (57Km)\n\n\nEarly morning on day 2 you will be taken to the \u2018Phoenix Bay Harbour\u2019 for boarding either the \u2018MV Makruzz\u2019 (1.5 hours) or the \u2018Government Ferry\u2019 (2.5 hours) to reach the \u2018Havelock Island\u2019.\nHavelock Island: This Island has been named after some prominent British \u2018Army Officer\u2019. Havelock Island provides facilities for scuba diving and snorkeling. The place is well-known for the transparent waters and white sand.\nOnce you reach the island you will be assisted in finding a proper restaurant to have your breakfast (in case you decided to have it after the ride) post which you will be taken to the Radhanagar Beach that is considered the 7th most beautiful beach in Asia. You can opt for swimming here or simply wet your feet while absorbing the scenic beauty.\nAfterwards, you will check into a pre-booked hotel where you will be served dinner and will spend the night.\n\n\n\n\nDay 3 :At Neil Island\n\n\nOn day 4 you will have an early breakfast after which you will leave this island for boarding a ferry to the \u2018Neil Island\u2019.\nNeil Island: The Island is named after \u2018James George Smith Neil\u2019 who served in the British Army during the \u2018Sepoy Mutiny\u2019 of 1857. The island is also termed as \u2018Vegetable Bowl\u2019 as its produces high quality as well as the quantity of agricultural products. The only jetty is available at \u2018Bharatpur\u2019 serving as the lone \u2018entry-exit\u2019 point. This island is perfect for those interested in \u2018eco-tourism\u2019 as it provides a wide variety of marine creatures. The well-known beaches of this region include the \u2018Lakshmanpur\u2019 beach, the \u2018Sitapur\u2019 beach (popular for the \u2018red sand\u2019 here) and the Bharatpur Beach. These beaches remain unspoiled and purely natural. One other tourist attraction is the \u2018Howrah Bridge\u2019, a naturally formed bridge.\nAfter a full day on the beach you will return to Port Blair and enjoy the changing sky colour in the evening and the sea breeze on the way back. You may even chance upon the flying fish and dolphins swimming next to your boat. Take rest for the night at the hotel in Port Blair.\n\n\n\n\nDay 4 :Port Blair Departure\n\n\nOn the final day you will start with a hearty breakfast after which the Namaste India representative will take you safely to the Port Blair airport/ harbor for you to get back home with unforgettable memories.",
    "highlights": [
      "Visit to all the museums in Port Blair",
      "The history will be spoken through the Cellular jail visit",
      "Travel to the Havelock Island in MV Mackruzz",
      "Know more about the Neil Island",
      "Also the famous sound and light show at the Cellular Jail"
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1 :Arrival at Port Blair and Sightseeing",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 2 :Port Blair \u2013 Havelock (57Km)",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 3 :At Neil Island",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 4 :Port Blair Departure",
        "description": ""
      }
    ],
    "faqs": []
