  "badrinath-kedarnath-yatra-from-haridwar": {
    "overview": "Welcome to an absolutely wonderful and safe journey to the amazing high holy mountains of North India. People worldwide dream of visiting the beautiful temples of Lord Shiva and Lord Vishnu. Special Badrinath Kedarnath Yatra Package from Haridwar includes visiting these famous places easily. You travel safely in a personal car. You will get the best rooms and tasty food so you can relax fully. Just look at the high green hills and enjoy the fresh air.\n\nWhether you travel alone, with kids, or bring old parents, this Do Dham Yatra package from Haridwar suits your needs. Deep care must be taken for older people ensuring they never feel tired on steep roads. People call this the best Badrinath Kedarnath Yatra because it combines deep prayers with a relaxing holiday. So book this tour for a magical experience. Your deep heart will quickly feel true peace and your busy mind always becomes extremely calm and happy.\nHighlights of Badrinath Kedarnath Package\nHere are the main features of Uttarakhand Do Dham Yatra:\n\nYour holy trip begins directly from the quiet parts of Haridwar.\nFinish visiting both temples in a simple five-day travel plan.\nWe promise a completely guided Haridwar to Kedarnath Badrinath tour package.\nLook at shining rivers, green valleys, and white snow mountains.\nThis tour includes quick entry passes.\nSleep in carefully checked, safe, and super clean rooms every night.\nOur chosen drivers have years of driving experience on mountain roads.\nWe add special resting stops for senior citizens in this package.\nPlanners keep extra free hours just in case rain stops cars.\nThe daily schedule is highly flexible so you can easily stop.\nWe mix the hard walking part of Kedarnath with the simple Badrinath drive perfectly.\nWe select low-height places for night sleeping to keep breathing normal.\nFood and sleep are covered in your low Haridwar to Kedarnath Badrinath trip cost.\n\nKedarnath Trekking Guide\nRead these highly useful details before you start your mountain walk:\n\nTrek Start Point: The path starts from Gaurikund. First, ride a car to Sonprayag. Then, sit in a local jeep to reach Gaurikund gates.\nKedarnath Trek Distance: The walking road is exactly sixteen to eighteen kilometres to one side.\nAltitude of Kedarnath Temple: This beautiful stone temple sits very high. Its height is around 3,583 meters above sea waters.\nKedarnath Trek Difficulty: Walking up is not very simple. The path goes high. Fit people can walk it slowly. Old people or kids must hire a horse or palanquin to go up safely.\nKedarnath Trekking Time: If walking, you need nearly six to ten hours to finish one side.\nPermits Required: Yes, the government says you must carry a scanned biometric registration paper.\nFacilities: You easily find horse riders calling you. Small local mountain shops sell tasty hot noodles, sweet tea, and fresh water bottles everywhere.\nTrekking Route: You pass Gaurikund, Jungle Chatti, Bheembali, Linchauli, Kedarnath Base Camp, and finally Kedarnath Temple.\nSafety Tips for Kedarnath Pilgrimage: Do not eat a big meal before walking. Drink lots of plain water to stop headaches. Sleep at a lower town for one day to let lungs adjust. Wear thick, strong walking shoes. Try booking very early because millions arrive here every summer. In the last year, you will see that in the first two days after opening there were 55,000 pilgrims visiting Kedarnath. nollow\n\nComplete Badrinath Kedarnath Travel Guide\nKeep these great suggestions in mind for your Kedarnath Badrinath tour package from Haridwar:\n\nBest time for Do Dham Yatra: The greatest months to travel are May, June, September, and October. The sky looks clear during this time.\nDistance between Kedarnath and Badrinath: The driving length is roughly 240 kilometres. Your car takes around ten hours to safely move between these places.\nBadrinath Kedarnath Opening Dates 2026: Doors open during summer months. For 2026, temple committees will open Kedarnath around April 22 and Badrinath around April 23.\nRoad Conditions for Badrinath Kedarnath Yatra: Driving paths from Haridwar towards Sonprayag look fine with some mud patches. The highway towards Badrinath is built strongly. Still, stay awake near thin road corners like Joshimath and Mana village.\nKedarnath Badrinath Temple Timings: Kedarnath doors welcome visitors from 4:00 AM until 3:00 PM, and again from 5:00 PM until 9:00 PM. Badrinath gives viewing times from 4:30 AM until 1:00 PM, and 4:00 PM until 9:00 PM.\nThings to pack for do Dham Yatra: Heading, How heavy winter garments including woollen coats, gentle woollens and thermals. Take warm hand gloves, caps, and muffler. Pack solid boots, plastic ID cards, travel papers, and basic cold medicine.\nHotels around Kedarnath Badrinath: Nice rooms in Guptkashi and Sitapur. Stay in very basic tent camps or lodges near Kedarnath.At Badrinath, easily pick a cheap charity room or costly hotel.\nDo Dham Yatra Registration: This step is super necessary. Please fill out details on the official state website: registrationandtouristcare.uk.gov.in. nofollow\nHaridwar to Kedarnath Badrinath trip cost: We offer a fair Haridwar to Kedarnath Badrinath trip cost. The starting price is normally around INR 15,400 per person.\nRoute Map for Badrinath Kedarnath Yatra: Following this road order is the smartest way:Haridwar \u2192 Rishikesh \u2192 Devprayag \u2192 Srinagar \u2192 Rudraprayag \u2192 Guptkashi \u2192 Sonprayag \u2192 KedarnathKedarnath \u2192 Sonprayag \u2192 Guptkashi \u2192 Joshimath \u2192 Badrinath.\n\nHow to Book Badrinath Kedarnath Yatra Package from Haridwar?\nStart planning your Do Dham Yatra from Haridwar for the upcoming season early to avoid rushing. To confirm this tour, simply dial our phone number or fill the website form. Our booking team replies fast. Ask us today to grab a huge discount on your package. Go on a peaceful ride and create sweet memories with loved ones. Contact our office right now and secure family seats!",
    "highlights": [
      "Your holy trip begins directly from the quiet parts of Haridwar.",
      "Finish visiting both temples in a simple five-day travel plan.",
      "We promise a completely guided Haridwar to Kedarnath Badrinath tour package.",
      "Look at shining rivers, green valleys, and white snow mountains.",
      "This tour includes quick entry passes.",
      "Sleep in carefully checked, safe, and super clean rooms every night.",
      "Our chosen drivers have years of driving experience on mountain roads.",
