  "baidyanath-dham-tour-2-days": {
    "overview": "Baidyanath Dham is one of the most sacred Jyotirlingas in the country. See More\n\nLocated in Deoghar, it is not only a revered pilgrimage of Lord Shiva, but is also an important Shaktipeeth, making it a powerful pilgrimage site. Every year, the Dham draws millions of devotees, especially in the peak season of the Shravan months, when hordes of Kanwar pilgrims arrive.In order to enjoy a hassle-free journey to the holy site, book our Baidyanath Dham Tour Package. This tour plan lasts for 2 Days / 1 Night, providing you ample time to seek Darshan of the temple. In addition, you also get to visit other places of high spiritual importance. During your stay, you get to stay in quality hotels, eat delicious meals, and enjoy hassle-free transport services. With our 24/7 assistance, you can enjoy your trip with ease of mind, without having to worry about the travel logistics. Contact us now to go on a smooth and convenient pilgrimage!See Less\n\nLocated in Deoghar, it is not only a revered pilgrimage of Lord Shiva, but is also an important Shaktipeeth, making it a powerful pilgrimage site. Every year, the Dham draws millions of devotees, especially in the peak season of the Shravan months, when hordes of Kanwar pilgrims arrive.\n\nIn order to enjoy a hassle-free journey to the holy site, book our Baidyanath Dham Tour Package. This tour plan lasts for 2 Days / 1 Night, providing you ample time to seek Darshan of the temple. In addition, you also get to visit other places of high spiritual importance. During your stay, you get to stay in quality hotels, eat delicious meals, and enjoy hassle-free transport services. With our 24/7 assistance, you can enjoy your trip with ease of mind, without having to worry about the travel logistics. Contact us now to go on a smooth and convenient pilgrimage!",
    "highlights": [
      "Seek blessings at Baba Baidyanath Jyotirlinga, one of the 12 sacred Jyotirlingas of Lord Shiva.",
      "Visit the holy Parvati Temple inside the Baidyanath Dham complex.",
      "Feel the powerful spiritual aura of the Shakti Peeth, revered by thousands of devotees.",
      "Offer prayers at the sacred Basukinath Temple, known as the divine \u201cShiva\u2013Parvati Darbar.\u201d",
      "Enjoy a peaceful trek to Trikut Pahar, famous for its mythological significance and beautiful views.",
      "Explore the serene surroundings of Tapovan, home to ancient caves and temples associated with Sage Valmiki.",
      "See More"
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1: Arrival at Deoghar",
        "description": "On arrival at Baidyanath Dham, you will be greeted by our representative at the Airport/Railway station.\nThereafter, you\u2019ll be transferred to your pre-booked hotel at Deogarh.\nEnjoy leisure time. If time permits, you\u2019ll be driven to sightseeing places.\nEnjoy the overnight stay at the hotel."
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 2: Baba Baidyanath Temple and Sightseeing",
        "description": "Wake up early in the morning. You\u2019ll be taken for Darshan and Poojan at Baba Baidyanath Temple.\nAlso, seek Darshan of Mata Parvati Temple, which is also a Shaktipeeth.\nThen you\u2019ll be taken to Basukinath Dham, Trikuti Hill, Naulakha Temple, Tapovan Pahar, and Satsang Ashram.\nThereafter, you\u2019ll be transferred back to the hotel. Pick your belongings.\nNow, you\u2019ll be transferred to the Airport /Railway Station from where you can continue your further journey.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      }
    ],
    "faqs": []
  },
  "bali-combo-tour": {
    "overview": "Bali is the perfect combo of relaxation, adventure, and culture. And if you are planning a holiday on this beautiful island, then our 5-day Bali Combo Tour Package is the best option to make your holiday absolutely memorable.\n\nFrom beautiful beaches, peaceful temples, to having absolute fun at the key attractions, this tour itinerary has everything for you! So, are you ready to experience the beauty of this gorgeous island? Let's explore!\n\nFrom beautiful beaches, peaceful temples, to having absolute fun at the key attractions, this tour itinerary has everything for you! So, are you ready to experience the beauty of this gorgeous island? Let's explore!\n\nTour Itinerary\n\n\nDay 1 : Arrival in Bali\n\n\nWelcome to the land of gods, Bali!\nAfter arriving at Bali International Airport, you'll meet our representative, who will take you to your hotel in Ubud in a private air-conditioned car. Check into your hotel and relax for a while.\nDay 1 of this Bali tour combo package is absolutely free for you to explore the city. Ubud is famous for its art, culture, and natural beauty.\nHere's What you Can Do in Ubud:\n\nExplore the Ubud Market (famous for art paintings, handicrafts, Warungs, etc)\nVisit the nearby Sacred Temples\nWalk past the Rice Fields (there are a lot of rice fields around)\nExperience the Elephant Cave, also known as Goa Gajah\nVisit Bali's Iconic Monkey Forest\nTry Authentic Balinese Street Food\nRelax near the Poolside of your hotel\n\nKey Tourist Attractions in Ubud\n\nBali Swing\nATV & Rafting Adventure\nElephant Park\nKanto Lampo Waterfall\n\nAfter exploring Ubud and enjoying the first day in Bali, you can head back to your hotel and relax at the poolside. Or, if you want, you can go to the nearby beach to watch the sunset.\nHave your dinner (at the hotel) or at a local restaurant, before you come back to your hotel for the overnight stay.\nImportant:\nSome of these attractions have entry fees, so make sure to carry some cash with you.\n\nEntry Fee at Monkey Forest: IDR 130,000 (Adults) & IDR 100,000 (Children)\nEntry Fee at Goa Gajah: IDR 50,000 per person\nAt some Temples, you have to pay a small donation for entry.\nStarting Price for ATV Ride: Single ATV Quad Bike - IDR 400,000 to IDR 600,000 for one person & Double ATV Quad Bike - IDR 600,000 to IDR 900,000 for two persons\n\n\n\n\n\nDay 2 : Bali City Sightseeing and Evening Cruise\n\n\nToday is going to be a full day of sightseeing in Ubud. Get up early (probably 2 am) and meet your driver, who will take you for sightseeing.\nThe first key attraction is the Kintamani Volcano area.\nAfter a short drive through the scenic roads, beautiful waterfalls, and mountains, you'll be dropped at the base of the mountain, from where you have to do a trek to reach the top.\nFrom there, you have to reach Mount Batur (famously known as Kintamani Volcano). Witness the breathtaking views of the iconic volcano and the beautiful Lake Batur. You can spend some time capturing photos and having a walk around.\n\nTrek Time: 1 hour (if dropped in halfway) and 2 to 2.5 hours (from the base). It is up to you, from where you have to start.\nEntry Fee: Kintamani Area - Adults: IDR 50,000 & Children: IDR 30,000\nEntry Fee: Mount Batur - Starting from IDR 350,000 per person\n\nSlowly, the sun starts rising, and you'll get to experience one of the best sunrises of all time. This is the perfect moment to click some Instagram-worthy pictures.\nAround 7 to 8 am, you'll be free to explore more tourist places. Other tourist places that you can explore nearby:\n\nPura Ulun Danu Batur Temple\nToya Devasya Hot Springs\nBatur Natural Hot Springs\n\n(Additional entry fee charges applicable)\nNext, you'll head to the Tegallalang Rice Terrace. After a 1-hour drive, you'll get to experience the iconic lush green landscape, the beautifully cultivated terraced fields, and the most stunning views.\nYou can:\n\nWalk through the pathways of the rice fields\nClick some amazing photographs\nWatch local people working in the fields\nTry some Balinese food from the local cafes and shops\n\nCrucial Advice: The best time to visit the Tegallalang Rice Terrace is early morning. It is better to go early in the morning to avoid the crowds. Plus, there are small entry fees of IDR 10,000 per person, and locals may ask for small donations. So, make sure to carry some cash with you.\nCome back to the hotel for dinner. Overnight stay in Ubud\n\n\n\n\nDay 3 : Tegenungan Waterfall, Uluwatu Temple & Kecak Fire Dance\n\n\nToday, you'll travel from Ubud to Kuta. After having breakfast, meet your driver who will take you to your hotel in Kuta.\nNext, you'll leave to visit another key tourist attraction: Tegenungan Waterfall. Here, you can spend quality time for a quick refreshing bath in the natural pool surrounded by scenic views.\n\nTip: Carry an extra pair of clothes and comfortable footwear\nEntry Ticket: IDR 20,000 (adults) and IDR 10,000 (children)\n\nNearby Attractions and Tourist Spots\n\nBali Glass Bridge - Famous for its panoramic views\nSukawati Art Market - for traditional Balinese art and craft\nBali Zoo - watch 600+ animals, go on safari, special animal shows\nBali Bird Park - more than 1300 different birds, click photographs, feed them.\n\nNote: You can visit these attractions for a fun and adventurous experience. Remember, each place has a different and separate entrance fee.\nAround 3 pm, you can continue your drive to the most iconic sea temple in Bali, Uluwatu Temple. Situated 70 meters above on a mountain cliff, this is a sacred temple that is famous for its stunning views, along with the breathtaking SUNSETS.\nEnjoy the perfect sunset while settling yourself near the Kecak Dance Performance area. This is the major attraction of this Bali tour.\nHighlights of the attraction:\n\nExperience the heritage, culture, and spirituality of the temple\nWatch the stunning sunset\nEnjoy the special dance performance\n50+ Balinese men chanting \"Chak Chak Chak\" in sync to create a vocal music\nNarrating the story of the great Hindu epic \"Ramayana\"\nThe performance ends with a mesmerizing Fire Dance, which is the key highlight of the whole performance.\n\nTimings & Tickets\nUluwatu Temple\n\nOpening Timing: 7 AM to 7 PM\nEntry fee: IDR 50,000 (Adult) & IDR 30,000 (Children)\n\nKecak Dance Performance\n\nShowtime: 6:00 PM - 7:00 PM (Every Day)\nTicket Price: Adults: IDR 150,000 per person & Children (2 - 9 years old): IDR 75,000 per child\n\nAfter the show ends, you'll be driven back to the hotel for dinner.\nOvernight stay in Kuta\n\n\n\n\nDay 4 : Water Sports at Tanjung Benoa Beach & Sunset at Tanah Lot\n\n\nLet's get ready to experience some thrill and adventure at the beaches. After having your breakfast, you'll head towards Tanjung Benoa Beach, which is famous for its thrilling water sports activities.\nTop Water Activities are:\n\nBanana Boat Ride\nFlyboard\nFly Fish\nParasailing\nScuba Diving\nSnorkeling\nTurtle Island\n\nThe prices are different for each activity. Plus, there are multiple packages (combo of activities) for which the starting price is IDR 325,000 per person.\nSo now that you've enjoyed at the beach and had a fulfilling experience with the watersports, we'll proceed towards the final attraction of this Bali tour package.\nThe next location will be the Tanah Lot Temple. Yet another iconic temple surrounded by the ocean and the crashing waves.\nKey Highlights of the Temple\n\nAncient Hindu Temple\nTurns into an Island during high tide\nPeople can walk through and seek blessings during low tide\nPerfect for Breathtaking Sunset Views\n\nOther nearby Attractions\n\nBatu Bolong Temple\nTanah Lot Cultural Park\nKedungu Beach and Beraban Beach\n\nOpening Hours:\nTicket Price: IDR 40,000 (children) & IDR 75,000 (adult)\n\n\n\n\nDay 5 : Departure from Bali\n\n\nAnd the final day of this amazing trip to Bali...\nBreakfast at Hotel & Drop Off at the Airport\nStart your day with a delicious breakfast at the hotel itself before you leave for the airport.\nPack your luggage, check out from the hotel, and meet your driver at the reception.\nYour driver will drop you off at the airport.\nSo this was your experience on this beautiful island. Say a final Goodbye to Bali while remembering all those moments that you spent during these last 5 days, that made this tour an unforgettable one.",
    "highlights": [
      "Arrive at Bali International Airport",
      "Explore Ubud's Local Art Market, Monkey Forest & Street Food",
      "Visit Tegallalang Rice Terrace, Experience Panoramic View of Mount Batur",
      "Refreshing Tegenungan Waterfall, Visit Sea Temple, Fire Dance Performance",
      "Thrilling Water Sports Activities at the Beach & Stunning Sunset",
      "Fly Back Home"
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1 : Arrival in Bali",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 2 : Bali City Sightseeing and Evening Cruise",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 3 : Tegenungan Waterfall, Uluwatu Temple & Kecak Fire Dance",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 4 : Water Sports at Tanjung Benoa Beach & Sunset at Tanah Lot",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 5 : Departure from Bali",
        "description": ""
      }
    ],
    "faqs": []
  },
