  "bali-singapore-package": {
    "overview": "For 7 days and 6 nights forget the fast paced life through Singapore with Bali tour package which will not only be rejuvenating but will also be an entirely new experience. You will be taken through the rich wilderness and exotic locations of Bali and some of the most breathtaking views in Singapore. Experience life through a new perspective and welcome yourself to the places where the water is as blue as the sky and your dreams run free.\n\nSingapore Bali Tour Itinerary Package\n\n\nDay 1 :Arrival in Bali\n\n\nOnce you arrive at Bali you will immediately be transferred to your hotel where you are free to relax. During late in the evening you will be free to do all your leisure activities and explore the nearby places. This is the best opportunity for you to try out some local cuisines like, Lawar, Bebek Betutu, satay and much more which will be a treat for your taste buds.\nYou can also shop for souvenirs in the nearby local markets like, traditional handicrafts and paintings, jewellery pieces, home d\u00e9cor items, ecofriendly bags and a whole range of other items.\n\n\n\n\nDay 2 :Bali Sightseeing\n\n\nThe first half of your day will be free for your leisure activities and the sightseeing of this beautiful lush city will commence in the evening you will be made to proceed towards Tanjung Benoa Beach, which is best if visited during the evening, when the entire peninsula comes to life.\nHere you can choose from various fun activities like, snorkeling, sea walking, parasailing, rolling donuts and so much more. Cruise will be your next option where you will be served dinner. You will also witness the grand sun setting in the horizon before heading back to your hotel.\n\n\n\n\nDay 3 :Bali Sightseeing\n\n\nJust like the previous day, the first half of your day will be free for you to do some leisurely activities while the main activities will commence in the afternoon starting with a wonderful sunset experience, and then you will be driven to Uluwatu, which is located on the South western tip of Bali and is one of the top tourist destinations among vacationers.\nA prime surfing destination, this place is also home to numerous holy temples including Pura Uluwatu, which is located on a cliff top which gives its visitors a panoramic view of the shimmering, unending blue ocean.\nYou will also be made to enjoy the local Kecak dance form of the Balinese performance along with a delicious dinner.\n\n\n\n\nDay 4 :Bali \u2013 Singapore\n\n\nEarly in the morning, you will be driven to the airport from where your journey towards Singapore will commence. Once you arrive at Singapore you will be taken to your allotted hotel where the evening will be free for you to leisure around and explore the nearby places of interest.\n\n\n\n\nDay 5 :Singapore Sightseeing\n\n\nYour city sightseeing tour of Singapore will start off after breakfast and will begin with a visit to the Universal studio which is home to 24 different rides, various shows and numerous exciting attractions. These seven different themed zones make it an exciting holiday destination for families.\nNext you will be escorted to one of the prime locations in Singapore which is Jurong Bird Park, located on the highest point in Jurong region and is home to 5,000 animals belonging to 380 different species.\nYour evening will end at a rejuvenating note, by witnessing the glorious sunset at Sentosa. Here you will be taken on a mono cable car ride; you will also watch the dolphin lagoon where the dolphins will showcase their skills.\nAfter a fun and thrilling day you will be taken back to your hotel concluding your trip there.\n\n\n\n\nDay 6 :Singapore City Sightseeing\n\n\nThe entire day today is free for you to explore the magnificent city of Singapore. You can start by visiting one of the most popular tourist attractions, Gardens by the bay, which is a manmade towering garden which is engulfed in colorful and green vines climbing up till the top of the tower. This is a wonderful effort made by the Singapore government to improve the quality of air and let the citizen breath air free of pollutants. Your next stop can be Merlion Park, the Singaporean landmark of half fish and half lion spouting water.\nLater on you can head towards a giant observation wheel known as Singapore flyer, which is in the form of a ferris wheel. One can view the entire city of Singapore from top of the wheel and have a panoramic view of the city. The 541 feet high wheel is a great way of getting the bird\u2019s eye view.\nFinally you will head on to do some shopping of souvenirs in the colorful and vibrant marketplaces before reaching your hotel.\n\n\n\n\nDay 7 :Singapore Departure\n\n\nYour day will commence with a hearty breakfast meal before being escorted to the airport from where you will catch your flight onwards.",
    "highlights": [
      "Trying out the local cuisines like the Lawar, Bebek Betutu and Satay at Bali",
      "Bali shopping adventure would be at your fingertips to get some souvenirs and local items like, traditional handicrafts and paintings, jewellery pieces, home d\u00e9cor items, ecofriendly bags etc.",
      "Some exciting beach activities at the Tanjung Benoa Beach with fun activities like, snorkeling, sea walking, parasailing, rolling donuts and finally the cruise.",
      "Have a divine visit to the Pura Uluwatu shrine",
      "Singapore sightseeing starting with the famous Jurong Bird Park",
      "Witness the spectacular sunset on Sentosa Island",
      "Enjoy the grandeur of the Merlion Park, the Singaporean landmark of half fish and half lion spouting water",
      "Ride the giant observation wheel the Singapore flyer"
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1 :Arrival in Bali",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 2 :Bali Sightseeing",
