  "best-of-gujarat-tour-package": {
    "overview": "Gujarat, the westernmost state of India is worldwide for its white sandy deserts, holy destinations, historical and cultural places, and glimmering beaches. Browsing our Best of Gujarat Tour Package offers you an opportunity to explore various other tourist destinations dotted in the state. As you are on a family tour and the taste of each family member is different so we have compiled all such destinations that could match with the taste of each member of your group.\n\nBest of Gujarat Tour Itinerary Package\n\n\nDay 1 :Arrival in Ahmedabad\n\n\nOnce you get down at the Ahmedabad airport or the railway station, you will find our representative waiting for you and then take you to one of your pre-decided hotels through a private transfer. Once you are ok with all the formalities required to do the check-in at the hotel get yourself ready to explore the destinations scheduled for today. The day visit commences with the exploration of Gandhi Ashram, Sidi Saiyyed Mosque, a perfect example of architecture grandeurs, enjoy visiting boat ride in Kankaria Lake, Akshardham Temple, and Adalaj Temple. After completing the day visitation, retire to the hotel for gorging upon the night cuisine and staying overnight.\n\n\n\n\nDay 2 :Drive to Dwarka via Jamnagar\n\n\nPost goring upon your morning meal, get yourself done with the formalities needed to check-out from the hotel and get ready to explore the leftover destinations that are covered under the Gujarat tour package. From Ahmedabad, you will be taken to Jamnagar en-route which you can visit Lakhota Museum and Lakhota Lake. After visiting these spots you will drive straight towards Dwarka by the road where you can seek the blessings of Bala Hanuman Temple. After covering a long distance from Ahmedabad to Dwarka and on reaching Dwarka, drive towards the hotel where you can accommodate yourself with your family and can relax for the next day trip. If time allows you then visit the Dwarkadhish Temple in the evening where you can participate in the evening Aarti ceremony.\n\n\n\n\nDay 3 :Sightseeing in Dwarka\n\n\nGive a perfect start to your third day of the trip with a relishing breakfast at the hotel and after treating your taste buds with the morning meal, take a holy dip into the River Gomati and then start your temple-hopping tour in Dwarka. Nageshwar Jyotirlinga Temple, Gopi Talav, and Bet Talav are some of the best destinations and after completing these destinations when you drive back to Dwarka via the boat ride visit the popular Rukmini Devi Temple. Spend your afternoon in exploring the coastal attractions including the lighthouse standing tall at the beach. If you are left with some energy after the daily schedule then attend the evening Aarti at the Dwarkadhish Temple. Conclude your third day of the tour with a scrumptious Gujarati meal served at the night.\n\n\n\n\nDay 4 :Transfer to Somnath via Porbandar\n\n\nThis is your last day in Dwarka from where you will drive straight to Somnath via Porbandar. On the way to Somnath, make your visit to the destinations falling en-route especially Kirti Mandir which is considered to be the place where Mahatma Gandhi was born and also visit the Sudama Temple. This is the time to start exploring the destinations established in Somnath. On reaching the destination town, complete the check-in formalities at the hotel where you are going to stay in Somnath. Bhalka Tirth, Geeta Mandir, and Triveni Sangam are some of the destinations you are exploring today. Later in the evening, visit the Somnath Temple again for attending the evening Aarti ceremony and to participate in the light and sound show at the temple. This is all for the day so conclude your day with a relaxing overnight stay.\n\n\n\n\nDay 5 :Drive to Diu and Sightseeing\n\n\nAccording to the schedule of the Gujarat tour package, check-out from your stay in Somnath drive towards Diu with your family members. On reaching the destination city, enter your room after completing the check-in formalities and then unwind yourself. Here you will be visiting Nagaon Beach, Diu Fort, and Diu Museum, Gangeshwar Temple, Naida Caves, and Chakratirth Beach. By the time it gets dark, drive back to the hotel for a night of sound sleep.\n\n\n\n\nDay 6 :Jungle Adventure in Gir\n\n\nEarly morning after completing the check-out formalities at the hotel and continue your drive towards Gir where on arrival you will be dropped at the hotel to get freshen up and unwind yourself followed by a trip to Gir National Park. Board the bus to spot Asiatic lions where you can enjoy the incredible wildlife of Gujarat. On the 6th day of the tour you will be treating your taste buds with the traditional Gujarati cuisines in dinner which is then followed by a relaxing night stay.\n\n\n\n\nDay 7 :Goodbye Gujarat\n\n\nOn the very last day of your Gujarat Trip, kick start your day with a relishing morning meal. Finally, the day has come where you will be returning to Ahmedabad and on the way to Junagarh including Navlakha Palace, Gondal, and Uparkot Fort. After covering such destinations, you will be escorted back to the Ahmedabad Airport or the railway station from where you board the flight or train for your onward journey towards home. I hope you had a great time in Gujarat with us and wish you a happy and safe journey.",
    "highlights": [
      "Visiting the Kankaria Lake and the Gandhi Ashram in Ahmedabad.",
      "Covering Gopi Talav and Bet Dwarka beach where you can enjoy the boat ride and other water sport activities.",
      "Go for a sightseeing tour at Diu Fort and Naida Caves.",
      "Visiting Dwarkadhish Temple in Dwarka for participating in the grand evening Aarti ceremony.",
      "Enjoy visiting sightseeing destinations at Porbandar and go on a temple visit."
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1 :Arrival in Ahmedabad",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 2 :Drive to Dwarka via Jamnagar",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 3 :Sightseeing in Dwarka",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 4 :Transfer to Somnath via Porbandar",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 5 :Drive to Diu and Sightseeing",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 6 :Jungle Adventure in Gir",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 7 :Goodbye Gujarat",
        "description": ""
      }
    ],
    "faqs": []
  },
  "best-of-kerala-tour": {
    "overview": "This well-curated Kerala tour package mainly covers Munnar, Guruvayur, Alleppey and Thekkady in 7days and 6 nights. See More\n\nYou will start your journey in Cochin and visit the famous destinations of Kerala. You will have a lot of options in seven days from Thekkady wildlife tour to houseboat rides in Alleppey. Our packages come with all the amenities ensuring you do not have to worry about anything during the tour. You can choose the kind of accommodation you want, places you want to visit and duration of the tour. Whatever be your preference we try our best to cater to your unique needs.\n\nYou will start your journey in Cochin and visit the famous destinations of Kerala. You will have a lot of options in seven days from Thekkady wildlife tour to houseboat rides in Alleppey. Our packages come with all the amenities ensuring you do not have to worry about anything during the tour. You can choose the kind of accommodation you want, places you want to visit and duration of the tour. Whatever be your preference we try our best to cater to your unique needs.\n\nTour Gallery\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nTour Name\nBest of Kerala Tour Package\n\n\nTour Duration\n7 Days / 6 Nights\n\n\nMeals\nBreakfast & Dinner\n\n\nVehicle Type\nSedan / SUV\n\n\nStarting & Ending Point\nCochin\n\n\nDestination Covered\nCochin - Munnar - Thekkady - Alleppey \n\n\nPickup Time\nDepend on your Flight Timing \n\n\n Tour Benefits\nBest price & enjoyable travel guarantee",
    "highlights": [
      "Experience the breathtaking beauty of Alleppey on a houseboat.",
      "Sightseeing tour of Munnar.",
      "Witness rare flora and fauna at the Periyar Wildlife Sanctuary.",
      "Spice plantation tour.",
      "Seek the blessings of Lord Krishna at Guruvayur Temple.",
      "Picturesque drive to Guruvayur."
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1:  Cochin Arrival - Transfer to Guruvayur (3 Hrs/100 Kms)",
        "description": "Arrival at Kochi airport or railway station and then transfer to Guruvayur.\nOn the way you will see some natural scenic spots and waterfalls.\nOn arrival at Guruvayur you will check into your pre-booked hotel and relax and unwind for the rest of the day.\nVisit the Elephant Camp that houses different varieties of elephants.\nSeek the blessings of Lord Krishna at Guruvayur Temple where the entry is permitted only for the Hindus.\nAfter the sightseeing tour, get back to your hotel and have an overnight stay.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "DAY 2: Guruvayur - Munnar (6 Hrs/180 Kms)",
        "description": "From Guruvayur you\u2019ll head out on a scenic drive to Munnar, a scenic hill station.\nOn the way, you will appreciate the breathtaking sceneries ranging from towering mountains to spice plantations and beautiful tea gardens.\nUpon arrival in Munnar, you will check-in to your pre-booked hotel.\nYou can spend the rest of the day as you like relaxing in your room or exploring the local attractions."
      },
      {
        "title": "DAY 3: Munnar Sightseeing",
        "description": "After a delicious breakfast you will head out for sightseeing tour of Munnar.\nYou will visit the famous attractions including\nMattupetty Lake & Dam\n,\nEcho Point\n,\nKundale Lake\n,\nTea Gardens\nand\nRajamalai (Eravikulam National Park)\n.\nMattupetty Lake & Dam:\nMattupetty Lake & Dam is one of the most beautiful attractions of Munnar with lush greenery and towering hills.\nEcho Point:\nEcho Point is famous for its natural beauty. Here you can listen to your voice echoing from the hills.\nRajamalai (Eravikulam National Park):\nThis national park is home to diverse flora and fauna.\nTea Gardens:\nFor nature lovers and tea enthusiasts, tea gardens are an absolute dream. You can sample freshly brewed teas over here.\nKundala Lake:\nThis is a man-made marvel surrounded by flowers and lush green trees. This lake is ideal for pedal boating.\nReturn to your hotel after the sightseeing tour and have an overnight stay.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "DAY 4: Munnar- Thekkady (03 hrs/110 Kms)",
        "description": "Post breakfast, you\u2019ll head to Thekkady. On the way you'll appreciate the beautiful sceneries and splendid views.\nUpon arrival at Thekkady, check-in at your hotel. Explore the\nspice plantations\n, which will revive your mind with the aroma of different spices.\nExplore\nPeriyar Forest\nof Thekkady, the finest wildlife reserve in India. You can also enjoy boating at\nPeriyar Lake\n.\nHead out for\nspice plantation tour\nand fall in love with the aromatic smell of the spices.\nOvernight stay at your hotel in Thekkady.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "DAY 5: Thekkady- Alleppey. (Houseboat) (4 Hrs/140 Kms)",
        "description": "After breakfast you will head out on a scenic drive to Alleppey, which is also known as the Venice of the East.\nAlleppey, also referred to as Alappuzha, is hailed as one of the oldest planned towns in the region. It is renowned for houseboat cruises, clear beaches, and boat races.\nOption 1: Stay at Hotel\nUpon arrival, you will check into the pre-reserved hotel and spend the rest of the day as you want. You can indulge in some interesting activities including:\nShopping:\nStock up on your favourite items from the local bazaars and floating markets of Alleppey. You can buy spices, paintings, artworks, and banana chips.\nSunset Cruise on Vembanadu Lake (Optional):\nWitness the sunset as you enjoy a cruise on Vembanadu Lake at your own price.\nAlleppey Beach:\nStroll by the shoreline of Alleppey Beach or spend a peaceful moment by the sea admiring the breathtaking views.\nOption 2: Houseboat Stay\nAfter arriving at Alleppey you can stay in a houseboat and sail along the backwater.\nHouseboat Cruise:\nThe fanciful and strikingly beautiful houseboats transport you to a world of luxury and royalty, making it a once-in-a-lifetime experience.\nYou can either stay the whole night in these majestic boathouses, or you can book your stay for a few hours as per your preference.\nYou can also have a mesmerizing view of the seawater and the greenery as the boathouse floats in the water.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "DAY 6: Alleppey \u2013 Kovalam \u2013 Trivandrum (4 Hrs/164 Kms)",
        "description": "Post breakfast, you will leave for Kovalam. On arrival at Kovalam, begin the city excursion and visit the popular tourist attractions including:\nSree Padmanabhaswamy Temple:\nThis is a well-known Hindu temple dedicated to Lord Anantha, Lord Vishnu\u2019s avatar. The temple\u2019s architecture is an amalgamation of Dravidian and Kerala style, and it features a hundred-foot tall gopuram.\nOptional Sightseeing:\nIf you have time on hand, you can plan to visit the main tourist attractions such as the City Museum, Napier Museum, and other nearby sites.\nAfter visiting Trivandrum you\u2019ll proceed to Kovalam, a serene coastal retreat of Kerala. You can stroll by the Kovalam beach and appreciate the scintillating sceneries.\nYou will then have an overnight stay at your hotel in Kovalam.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "DAY 7: Kovalam \u2013 Trivandrum / Cochin Departure (6 Hrs/220 Kms)",
        "description": "Watch the stunning sunset on Kovalam beach and then enjoy breakfast.\nPost breakfast, you\u2019ll be transferred to Cochin or Trivandrum depending on your convenience.\nOur driver will drop you off at the railway station or airport.\nWith this, the Kerala tour package will come to an end."
      }
    ],
    "faqs": []
  },
