  "chardham-package-from-hyderabad": {
    "overview": "The Chardhams are some of the holiest sites in Hinduism. Set out on a memorable pilgrimage with our well-crafted Chardham Yatra package from Hyderabad. You'll visit Kedarnath, Badrinath, Gangotri, and Yamunotri. In this tour plan, you get meals, hotels, and transport. Enjoy a relaxing scenic road trip with experienced hill drivers and guided tours.\n\nThis spiritual tour will undoubtedly bring you closer to the divine. Wait no more and book now!\n\nOverview of the Char Dham from Hyderabad Package\n\n\n\nDetail\nInformation\n\n\n\n\nDestinations Covered\nYamunotri, Gangotri, Kedarnath, and Badrinath\n\n\nBest Time to Visit\nMay to June & September to October\n\n\nYatra Duration\n14 Days / 13 Nights\n\n\nStarting Point\nHyderabad \u2192 Delhi \u2192 Haridwar \u2192 Char Dhams\n\n\nModes of Travel\nRoad Travel\n\n\nCost\nINR 43,900\n\n\n\nOpening & Closing Dates 2026\n\nYamunotri & Gangotri open: 19 April 2026 (Akshaya Tritiya)\nKedarnath opens: 22 April 2026\nBadrinath opens: 23 April 2026\nAll four close: October-November 2026 (dates announced closer to Diwali)\nBest time from Hyderabad: May-June (peak) or September-October (less crowded)\n\nChardham Registration 2026\n\nRegistration is mandatory for all 4 Dhams - without e-pass you'll be stopped at checkpoints\nRegister free at: registrationandtouristcare.uk.gov.in\nAlso via WhatsApp: Send 'Yatra' to +91 8394833833\nApp: 'Tourist Care Uttarakhand' on Google Play / App Store\nOffline counters: Haridwar, Rishikesh, Barkot, Uttarkashi, Sonprayag, Joshimath\nDocuments needed: Aadhaar card + mobile number for OTP\n\nSpecial Services for South Indian Pilgrims from Hyderabad\n\nTelugu/Hindi speaking tour guide available on request\nSouth Indian vegetarian meals (rice, dal, sambar) at select hotels in Haridwar, Rishikesh, Guptkashi, Badrinath\nSpecial group departures for Hyderabad devotees in May and September\nPickup available from Hyderabad, Secunderabad, Madhapur\n\nDo Dham and Ek Dham Options from Hyderabad\n\nBadrinath Kedarnath Do Dham Yatra from Hyderabad - 7-10 days\nGangotri Yamunotri Do Dham Yatra from Hyderabad - 7-10 days\nKedarnath Ek Dham Yatra from Hyderabad - 6-8 days\nBadrinath Ek Dham Yatra from Hyderabad - 6-8 days\n\nAltitude Sickness Section\n\nSymptoms: headache, nausea, dizziness, breathlessness\nDrink 3-4 litres water/day. Walk slowly. Rest on first day at each base town.\nMedical camps at Sonprayag, Gaurikund, Kedarnath, Joshimath\nSenior citizens must carry a doctor's fitness certificate - mandatory at health checkpoints\n\nCancellation & Refund Policy\n\n30+ days before: 10-20% charge\n15-30 days before: 30-50% charge\nWithin 15 days: 75-100% charge\nTravel insurance strongly recommended for weather/temple closure situations\n\nWhy Choose Chardham Yatra Package from Hyderabad?\nThere are various benefits of booking a package, such as:\nSeamless Hyderabad Connectivity\nHyderabad is very well connected to cities like Haridwar, Dehradun, and Rishikesh \u2014 which are the gateway to the Chardhams. From Hyderabad, you can easily get flights or trains to these gateway hubs. Road connectivity is also quite good.\nBesides Hyderabad, My Quick Trippers offers you Chardham Yatra from Secunderabad and Packages from Madhapur as well!\nEnd-to-End Logistics\nWith a package, you get travel plan designed by experts. You don't have to worry about hotel bookings at multiple places either. You also get hassle-free VIP passes, helicopter arrangements, and transfer assistance. You won't have to lift a finger and all these arrangements will be made for you! It's perfect for those who want a stress-free travel.\nCost-Effective\nGetting a package proves to be cost-effective as compared to self-planned travel. Travel agencies often book hotels and transport vehicles on a group basis, which at the end of the day reduces the total cost.\nLocal Support and Guidance\nMany tour operators also offer you tour guides or group leaders, who make for a very enriching tour. They will also keep you updated about routes as well as supply you with information about local culture. You'll also be escorted by an experienced hill driver throughout the journey.\nAll this is highly useful at the high altitudes of Uttarakhand.\nIdeal for Families and Senior Citizens\nPackaged tours provide a very comfortable tour, reducing stress and fatigue. Some plans also offer senior-friendly itineraries and a gentle pace, which is also invaluable to families travelling with kids. A to Z helicopter arrangements and medical assistance are also provided.\nEfficient Itinerary\nPackage itineraries are designed by experts who ensure proper acclimatisation and sufficient rest days in between travels. The routes are also optimised to ensure minimum backtracking and fast travel. Buffer days are also there for weather delays.\nBetter for First-Time Pilgrims\nFirst-timers are unaware of so many travel logistics. They can benefit greatly from guided support and expertly crafted tour packages which take care of everything \u2014 from their meals to transfers to accommodation. This makes their journey quite smooth and comfortable.\nPeace of Mind\nWith all your Darshan arrangements made and logistics handled, you can focus on the spirituality of the trip. With a tour package, your Yatra is actually about living the sacred experience rather than being bogged down with planning details and dealing with trip challenges.\nTypes of Chardham Package from Hyderabad\nMy Quick Trippers offers you a variety of packages catering to different kinds of pilgrims. Here are our wide range of plans:\nLuxury Package\nOur luxury tours are ideal for those who want to explore the sacred sites in a smooth and fuss-free way. These packages mainly include top-rated accommodations, private AC vehicle (Innova Crysta), scrumptious meals, private transfer, and VIP Darshan. You also get a personalised tour manager and dedicated support.\nIt's best for NRIs and international travellers and senior citizens. The price ranges from \u20b970,000 \u2014 \u20b91,50,000+ per person.\nBudget Package\nIf you do not want to mess with your budget while planning your pilgrimage, then our affordable tour plans can be your go-to choice. These Chardham tour packages include budget hotels, simple meals, and basic logistics support. It's ideal for budget travellers and solo travellers. The cost is between \u20b930,000 \u2014 \u20b945,000 per person.\nPrivate Package\nIn this tour, you get fully customised itinerary and a dedicated vehicle for your group. Both departure dates and routes are flexible. You get to decide the hotels and room types. You can also make stops along the way as per your comfort and liking. It's best for families and small groups. The price varies between \u20b945,000 \u2014 \u20b990,000+ per person.\nHelicopter Package\nChardham Helicopter Package from Hyderabad is ideal for those looking for a luxurious pilgrimage experience. You enjoy helicopter transfers to all the four Dhams. You also get accommodation with meals. You are also provided with VIP Darshan passes and boarding assistance.\nIt's best for pilgrims who are senior citizens, time-constrained, and first-timers. The price ranges from \u20b91,30,000 \u2014 \u20b93,00,000+ per person.\nStandard Packages\nYou get comfortable 3 to 4 star hotels. Daily meals of breakfast and dinner are included. You'll get SUV for transport. Your package also includes sightseeing and Darshan assistance. It's perfect for first-time pilgrims and working professionals. The cost is around \u20b945,000 \u2014 \u20b965,000 per person.\nGroup Tour Packages\nYour departure date and itinerary are fixed in this plan. You get an AC tempo traveller. You also get coordination with temple Darshan and sightseeing. You are provided with a tour leader for entire Yatra. Your breakfast and dinner are also included in this package. The price ranges from \u20b945,000 to \u20b965,000 per person. It's best for multiple families travelling together, devotional groups, and corporate sets.\nSenior citizen Special packages\nIn this plan, you enjoy easy-paced itinerary and extra rest days. You'll be provided with hotels with easy access rooms. Helicopter will be arranged for Kedarnath and Yamunotri. It is ideal for people who are 60+ or those who have mobility constraints. The cost goes from \u20b955,000 \u2014 \u20b990,000 per person.\nFamily-friendly packages\nIn this special plan, you get hotels which are suitable for families. Kid-friendly meals and snacks are also made available. Itinerary pace is comfortable, keeping in mind children and elders in the family. The cost is around \u20b945,000 \u2014 \u20b975,000 per person. It's best for families travelling with kids or multi-generational groups.\nNRI packages\nYou get flight coordination for your entry in India. You also enjoy airport pick-up and drop services. You get Visa assistance (if needed). You also receive full logistics support. This travel plan is best for NRIs and international devotees. The price ranges from \u20b980,000 \u2014 \u20b91,80,000 per person.\nWhy Choose Us for Chardham Yatra?\nThere are many tour operators for the Chardham Yatra, such as travel agencies in Ameerpet, Kukatpally, LB Nagar, and more! My Quick Trippers offers you organised pilgrimages with zero hidden charges. Our transparent pricing model has earned us recurring customers, too.\nAnd at the very core of it, we understand the need of pilgrims at high altitudes. We strive to take care of their unique requirements and provide them with a highly satisfying experience.\nTo book with us, simply give us a call (+91-9711616316), and we'll plan your next spiritual adventure!\nHow to Reach Char Dham from Hyderabad?\nThere are a variety of ways via which you can reach the Char Dham. Here's the travel guide:\nBy Air\nHyderabad to Char Dham Yatra by flight and road is one of the best options for this journey. This combo trip really eases your comfort. From Rajiv Gandhi International Airport (Hyderabad), you can board a direct flight to Jolly Grant Airport (Dehradun).\nSeveral flights are available, and the duration is around 2.5 hours. Now, from Dehradun, you can take a bus or hire a taxi to Haridwar or Rishikesh. You can book the same via GMVN.\nBy Train\nYou can also opt for Hyderabad to Char Dham Yatra by train. Board a train from Hyderabad to Haridwar. Trains are available from Secunderabad Junction to Haridwar, but direct services are limited in frequency. Many pilgrims travel to Delhi first and then board a Haridwar-bound train or taxi. Check IRCTC website for latest schedules.\nBy Road\nIf you want to travel by road, you can drive to Delhi from Hyderabad. It will take around 25-30 hours to complete the journey. From Delhi, you can take a bus or hire a cab to Haridwar (200 km). From there, you can continue your Chardham journey.\nCost of Char Dham Package from Hyderabad 2026\nThe cost of Chardham Yatra Packages from Hyderabad is INR 43,900. In this tour plan, we offer you accommodation, food, and dedicated transport services with a professional driver.\nOn top of that, you get customisable itinerary with which you can increase/reduce your trip duration, include more sightseeing attractions, and even choose your private vehicle through our transport services!\nTrekking Guide\nThe trekking is required only at Yamunotri and Kedarnath. Gangotri and Badrinath are well-accessible by motorable roads.\nThis is the trekking guide to Yamunotri and Kedarnath:\n\n\n\nCategory\nYamunotri Trek\nKedarnath Trek\n\n\n\n\nTrek Route\nJanki Chatti \u2192 Yamunotri\nGaurikund \u2192 Kedarnath\n\n\nDistance (One Way)\n6 km\n16 km\n\n\nDifficulty Level\nEasy\u2013Moderate\nModerate\u2013Challenging\n\n\nAverage Time\n2\u20133 hrs\n6\u20138 hrs\n\n\nStarting Point\nJanki Chatti\nGaurikund\n\n\nFacilities Available along the Route\n\n\nFood stalls\nToilets\nmedical aid\n\n\n\n\nMedical camps\nShelters\nFood stalls\n\n\n\n\nSuitable For\n\n\nFirst-time trekkers\nSeniors with basic fitness\nFamilies\n\n\n\n\nPhysically fit pilgrims\nExperienced trekkers\n\n\n\n\nTrail Condition\n\n\nWell-paved path\nGentle ascent\n\n\n\n\nRocky terrain\nSteep climbs\n\n\n\n\nWeather Impact\nRain may make paths slippery\nFog, rain, and cold winds are common\n\n\nBest Time to Trek\nMay\u2013June, September\u2013October\nMay\u2013June, September\u2013October\n\n\nAlternative Options\nHelicopter, Pony, and Palki\nHelicopter, pony, and Palki\n\n\n\nTips for Trekking\nHere is important advice for trekking:\n\nStart your trek early in the morning.\nDo not rush. Walk at a pace that is comfortable to you.\nTake breaks regularly \u2014 20-30 minutes.\nKeep yourself hydrated.\nDo not trek after dark.\nFollow instructions given by police/SDRF.\nIf you develop altitude sickness symptoms (breathlessness, dizziness, chest discomfort, or severe fatigue), then descend immediately and seek medical help.\n\nComplete Route Map from Hyderabad\nHere's the route map from Hyderabad to the four Dhams:\nHyderabad \u2192 Nagpur \u2192 Bhopal \u2192 Gwalior \u2192 Agra \u2192 Delhi \u2192 Haridwar \u2192 Barkot \u2192 Yamunotri \u2192 Barkot \u2192 Uttarkashi \u2192 Gangotri \u2192 Uttarkashi \u2192 Guptkashi \u2192 Gaurikund \u2192 Kedarnath \u2192 Gaurikund \u2192 Guptkashi \u2192 Joshimath \u2192 Badrinath \u2192 Joshimath \u2192 Rudraprayag \u2192 Devprayag \u2192 Rishikesh \u2192 Haridwar \u2192 Hyderabad\nDistance from Hyderabad to Chardham\nHere is the distance chart from Hyderabad to Chardhams. The travel duration to cover the individual segments is also included.\n\n\n\nRoute Segment\nDistance (Approx.)\nTravel Time (Approx.)\n\n\n\n\nHyderabad \u2192 Haridwar\n1,650 km\n28\u201332 hrs (train/road) or 5\u20136 hrs (flight + road transfer)\n\n\nHaridwar \u2192 Barkot\n210 km\n7\u20138 hrs\n\n\nBarkot \u2192 Janki Chatti (Yamunotri base)\n45 km\n1.5\u20132 hrs\n\n\nJanki Chatti \u2192 Yamunotri (trek)\n6 km\n2\u20133 hrs\n\n\nBarkot \u2192 Uttarkashi\n82 km\n3\u20134 hrs\n\n\nUttarkashi \u2192 Gangotri\n100 km\n3.5\u20134.5 hrs\n\n\nUttarkashi \u2192 Guptkashi\n220 km\n8\u20139 hrs\n\n\nGuptkashi \u2192 Gaurikund (Kedarnath base)\n30 km\n1\u20131.5 hrs\n\n\nGaurikund \u2192 Kedarnath (trek)\n16 km\n6\u20138 hrs\n\n\nGuptkashi \u2192 Badrinath\n190 km\n7\u20138 hrs\n\n\nBadrinath \u2192 Rudraprayag\n160 km\n6\u20137 hrs\n\n\nRudraprayag \u2192 Haridwar\n140 km\n5\u20136 hrs\n\n\n\nAccommodation Options at Chardhams\nHere are some viable accommodation options in the Chardham:\nYamunotri\nThere are no hotels or lodges right at the Yamunotri Temple premises What most pilgrims do is stay at Janki Chatti or Barkot, as these are the best bets for hotels in Yamunotri.\nTypes of Accommodation Available\n\nBudget lodges and guest houses \u2014 You get basic rooms with shared bathrooms\nGMVN Tourist Rest House \u2014 you can trust them to be reliable and clean\nDharamshalas \u2014 They are very economical but have limited facilities\nHomestays \u2014 Expect warm hospitality and simple meals\n\nFacilities Available\n\nHot water is provided in buckets upon request. Geysers are generally not available.\nLimited heating facilities \u2014 carry warm clothes with you.\nPower cuts are possible.\n\nGangotri\nThere are a limited number of hotels in Gangotri. However, you can still find budget-friendly options as well as some 3-star hotels here. You can get lodges with better amenities at Harsil (22 km).\nTypes of Accommodation\n\nGMVN Gangotri & Harsil \u2014 This is the most trusted option here\nBudget Hotels \u2014 They are available near the temple; however, they are quite basic\nMid-range Hotels in Harsil \u2014 You enjoy better comfort and heating facilities here\nAshrams and Dharamshalas \u2014 These are cost-effective and offer basic comfort\n\nFacilities Available\n\nBed, pillow, blanket, and basic furniture\nBetter hot water\nSome rooms have views\nWestern-style washrooms\n\nKedarnath\nYou'll find very basic hotels in Kedarnath. You can get better quality accommodations in nearby towns such as Guptkashi and Sonprayag.\nTypes of Accommodation\nAt Kedarnath\n\nGMVN tents and dormitories\nAshrams and Dharamshalas\ncottages (They're seasonal though)\n\nAt Gaurikund/Sonprayag\n\nBudget hotels and lodges\nDharamshalas\n\nAt Guptkashi\n\nMid-range hotels\nPremium riverside resorts\nHelicopter package hotels\n\nFacilities Available\n\nBed and blankets\nHeater in the room\nElectricity\nAttached bathroom\n\nBadrinath\nHotels in Badrinath are the best among all four Dhams. You get better facilities and lodges catering to budgets of all kinds.\nTypes of Accommodation\n\nGMVN Tourist Rest House\nBudget hotels and lodges\nMid-range hotels\nPremium hotels and resorts\n\nWhat to Expect\n\nBetter heating facilities\nMore dining options\nParking facility\nEasy hotel availability (even in peak season)\n\nBest Time for Chardham Yatra\nThe best time for Chardham Yatra is during May-June and September-October.\nIn these months, the weather is pleasant, and there are very low chances of rainfall. You can enjoy various activities during these months, such as sightseeing and camping, in addition to temple tours.\nYou should avoid planning your visit in the monsoon (July-August) when landslides and heavy rains are common. During this time, the roads may be blocked, making travelling very difficult.\nDuring winter, the Chardham shrines remain closed due to heavy snowfall and extreme weather conditions. The Chardham Yatra is halted during this period, and the idols are shifted to their winter seats.\nSeason-Wise Temperature at Char Dhams\n\n\n\nSeason\nYamunotri\nGangotri\nKedarnath\nBadrinath\n\n\n\n\nSpring (Apr\u2013Jun)\n6\u00b0C \u2013 15\u00b0C\n5\u00b0C \u2013 14\u00b0C\n3\u00b0C \u2013 12\u00b0C\n7\u00b0C \u2013 16\u00b0C\n\n\nMonsoon (Jul\u2013Sep)\n10\u00b0C \u2013 18\u00b0C\n9\u00b0C \u2013 17\u00b0C\n7\u00b0C \u2013 15\u00b0C\n11\u00b0C \u2013 19\u00b0C\n\n\nAutumn (Oct\u2013Nov)\n0\u00b0C \u2013 10\u00b0C\n-2\u00b0C \u2013 8\u00b0C\n-5\u00b0C \u2013 6\u00b0C\n2\u00b0C \u2013 12\u00b0C\n\n\nWinter (Dec\u2013Mar)\n-10\u00b0C \u2013 2\u00b0C\n-12\u00b0C \u2013 0\u00b0C\n-15\u00b0C \u2013 -2\u00b0C\n-8\u00b0C \u2013 4\u00b0C\n\n\n\nHow to Plan Chardham Yatra from Hyderabad?\nHere's a quick guide to planning your pilgrimage:\n\nDecide on when to travel. Summers and post-monsoon seasons are the best.\nComplete registration for the Chardham Yatra, which is mandatory. You can do so by visiting Uttarakhand Tourism Portal.\nPick your mode of travel from Hyderabad \u2014 flight, train, or road trip all the way!\nPack essentials like warm clothes, trekking shoes, and rain gear etc.\nIf you're hiring a travel agency, then decide which package type to book, such as a budget tour, family package, senior-citizen-friendly Yatra, luxury plan, etc.\nPre-book your accommodation and transport at least two months in advance. Hotels at base towns like Barkot, Uttarkashi, and Guptkashi have the best facilities.\nPrepare yourself physically for this high-altitude trip by walking for 30-40 minutes daily. Also, do light workout and breathing exercises.\nBook your helicopter in advance if you do not want to trek at Yamunotri and Kedarnath. You can also make arrangements for pony/Palki.\n\nPlan your travel carefully and make sure you book the necessary arrangements in advance.\nWhat to Pack?\nHere are some important items that you should carry with you for a smooth trip:\nClothing Essentials\n\n2-3 long-sleeved moisture-wicking shirts\n2-3 woollen pants or leggings\n1-2 fleece jacket\n1 insulated jacket\n1 waterproof/windproof jacket\n4-5 pairs of woollen socks\nWarm hat and gloves\nFleece scarf\n\nFootwear\n\nComfortable trekking shoes with good grip\nLightweight slippers/sandals (for hotel use)\n\nFood and Snack Items\n\nInstant noodles and canned food\nEnergy bars, biscuits, and crackers\nDry fruits, Nuts and seeds\nChikki (jaggery bars), roasted chana\nRehydration gels\n\nTravel Gear\n\nBackpack\nWaist pouch for valuables\nReusable water bottle\nTorch\nPower bank\nSunglasses (UV protection)\nSunscreen (SPF 30+)\nLip balm and moisturiser (skin protection against cold weather)\n\nMedical and Health Kit\n\nPersonal prescription medicines\nBasic first-aid kit\nPain reliever and fever medicine\nAnti-nausea and motion sickness tablets\nORS packets\nBand-aids and antiseptic cream\nInhaler (if required)\nAltitude sickness tablets (if doctor advised)\n\nDocuments to Carry\n\nGovernment ID (Aadhaar card)\nChar Dham registration slip\nMedical certificate (if applicable)\nTravel insurance copy (optional)\nHotel and transport booking details\nEmergency contact list\n\nToiletries\n\nToothbrush and toothpaste\nSoap and body wash\nHand sanitizer\nWet wipes and tissues\nTowel (quick-dry travel towel works best)\n\nPuja and Spiritual Items (Optional)\n\nRudraksha/mala\nSmall puja kit\nIncense sticks\nCamphors\n\nSenior Citizens Specials\n\nWalking stick\nKnee cap or support belt\nFoldable stool (optional)\nExtra medicines and prescriptions\n\nTravel Tips for Pilgrims\nHere are some travel tips that might come in handy:\n\nAcclimatise well before undertaking the trek. Rest adequately and drink enough amount of water.\nCheck the weather forecast before you head out for the day, as the weather can be very unpredictable at these sites.\nCarry a walking stick, good trekking shoes, a raincoat, and warm clothes (even in summer), as the weather can change abruptly.\nAlways book your tour package in advance, at least a month or two.\nGet travel insurance that offers good coverage against any medical emergencies.\nDo not travel in the monsoon season as there are chances of landslides and road blockage.\nGet all the required permits and register yourself before embarking on the holy pilgrimage.\nGet yourself examined by a healthcare professional and ensure you do not have any physical ailments.\n\nHow to Book the Best Chardham Yatra Package from Hyderabad 2026?\nThere are so many travel operators out there. My Quick Trippers offers you value-for-money tour plans. They include comfortable accommodation, nutritious meals, smooth transfer, and exciting sightseeing. With our 24x7 customer support and dedicated travel team, you don't have to worry about any travel-related logistics.\nTo book the package, simply fill up the query form and our travel rep will get in touch with you within minutes!",
