  "chardham-yatra-package-from-ahmedabad": {
    "overview": "Embark on a soulful journey to the Chardham sites with our Chardham Yatra Package from Ahmedabad. The Chardham Yatra comprises a tour of four of the religious destinations in Uttarakhand, including Gangotri, Yamunotri, Kedarnath, and Badrinath. Gangotri is the sacred abode of Goddess Ganga, and Yamunotri is a sacred site where you can seek the Goddess Yamunotri. Kedarnath houses Lord Kedar's Temple, and Badrinath is Lord Badri's sacred abode.\n\nEach package has been designed with complete understanding and care, allowing you to have a divine vacation with your loved ones, friends, and family. From sightseeing to adventurous activities and spiritual excursions, you can enjoy various top-notch services and amenities with this package. Book our Chardham pilgrimage package from Ahmedabad to immerse yourself in the wonders of Uttarakhand and purify your soul. \nTypes of Chardham Package from Ahmedabad\nLuxury Chardham Tour Packages\nWith the luxury Ahmedabad to Chardham Yatra packages, pilgrims can feel like royalty at every point of the journey. You can enjoy VIP darshan, world-class amenities, and private transportation with this package.\nBudget Package\nBudget Chardham tour from Ahmedabad caters to the needs of those who're looking to have a hassle-free pilgrimage without overspending. Though the amenities and services are basic, you will enjoy the yatra to the fullest with this package.\nPremium Package\nPremium Chardham Yatra Package from Ahmedabad is ideal for those who have a lavish budget and want to have the best pilgrimage experience. It is ideal for those who seek luxury and comfort throughout their trip and want to have the best experiences.\nHelicopter Package\nOur Helicopter Chardham yatra 2026 from Ahmedabad allows you to relish Uttarakhand's breathtaking vistas from hundreds of meters above the sky. It is the fastest and most convenient way for the pilgrims to complete the Chardham Yatra. Business professionals, those with mobility issues, and senior citizens can opt for this package.\nWhy Choose the Char Dham Pilgrimage From Ahmedabad?\nYou can plan your trip from Ahmedabad to the Chardham sites as it offers great access to Uttarakhand's main cities. From Ahmedabad, you can fly to Dehradun and then continue your journey to the Chardham sites via bus or taxi. Some tour operators in Ahmedabad offer personalized travel package trips that have been specifically curated for Gujarati pilgrims. The road journey from Ahmedabad to the Chardham's starting point is very picturesque.\nCost of Char Dham Yatra from Ahmedabad\nThe starting price of the Chardham Yatra Package from Ahmedabad is INR 35,000 per person. This will include meals, accommodation, transportation, and driver expenses. If you embark on the Chardham journey in summer, you may have to pay a higher price.\nChardham Route Map from Ahmedabad\nAhmedabad \u2192 Delhi / Haridwar \u2192 Barkot \u2192 Yamunotri \u2192 Uttarkashi \u2192 Gangotri \u2192 Guptkashi \u2192 Kedarnath \u2192 Pipalkoti (optional) \u2192 Badrinath \u2192 Joshimath (optional) \u2192 Srinagar / Rudraprayag \u2192 Rishikesh \u2192 Haridwar / Delhi \u2192 Ahmedabad\nBest Time to Visit\nSummer\nSummer is considered to be the peak season for the Char Dham yatra, as during this time the weather is comfortable and pleasant. The summer season typically begins in May and ends in June. During this time of the year, thousands of devotees embark on the Char Dham Yatra. The prices of accommodation and transportation are very high during this time of the year.\nMonsoon\nMonsoon season lasts from July to August. This is not a good time for the Chardham yatra due to the chances of heavy rainfall and landslides. During this time of the year, the roads may be blocked, and the conditions of the roads are poor. Most of the accommodations are closed during this time of the year.\nWinter\nDuring winter, the Chardham sites remain closed due to heavy snowfall. During this time, for 6 months, the deity's idol is shifted to their winter home. You can visit the idols at their winter homes, including Kharsali (Yamunotri Temple), Ukhimath Kedarnath Temple, Mukhba (Gangotri Temple), and Joshimath (Badrinath Temple).\nHow to Reach?\nBy Air\nYou can book a direct flight from Ahmedabad (Sardar Vallabhbhai Patel International Airport) to Dehradun (Jolly Grant Airport). The nearest airport to the Chardham sites is Jolly Grant Airport in Dehradun. Outside the airport, you will easily find taxis to reach the starting point of the Chardham sites. \nBy Train\nTraveling by train from Ahmedabad to Haridwar/Rishikesh takes around 24-28 hours. Trains that run on a regular basis on this route include Ahmedabad-Haridwar Express (19019), Sabarmati Express (19167), and Yoga Express (19031). \nBy Road\nTo travel one way via road, you will have to cover around 1,500 kilometers. You can drive from Ahmedabad to Delhi. From Delhi, you will have to reach Haridwar or Rishikesh via cab or bus. You can then head to the starting point of the Chardham sites. \nAccommodation Options\nGangotri\nGangotri has good-quality guest houses and Dharamshalas, which are equipped with all the basic amenities. The surrounding towns of Uttarkashi and Harsil offer tourists a wide selection of mid-range accommodation options that come with better facilities. \nYamunotri\nAt Yamunotri, you'll find good-quality accommodations situated amidst surreal landscapes. For a more pleasant stay experience, you can book resorts and hotels at Barkot and Hanuman Chatti. They come with all the modern amenities and offer a pleasant pilgrimage experience.\nKedarnath\nIn Kedarnath, you will find GMVN guest houses and hotels with all the modern facilities. Some of the best accommodation options in Kedarnath include RK Tourist Lodge, Jamloki Tourist Lodge, Hotel Aligarh Bhawan, Hotel Jaipur House, Shivlok, Hotel Anshuman, Hotel Green View Inn, and Hotel Behl Ashram.\nBadrinath\nThere are many tents, camps, ashrams, and Dharamshalas in Badrinath ensuring good food, warm hospitality, and decent rooms. The best stay options include Badriville Resort, Hotel New Snow Crest, Hotel Sarovar Portico, Hotel New Yoga, and Hotel Badrinath Inn.\nTravel Tips for Pilgrims\n\nMake your reservation in advance, especially if you're travelling in peak season, as there are limited stay options.\nDispose of waste materials only in the designated bins.\nDo not rest in areas that have been marked as dangerous.\nKeep all your important belongings in a waterproof bag.\nConsult your healthcare professional before embarking on the yatra and ensure you're physically fit for the yatra.\nRegister yourself for the Chardham yatra and obtain a medical fitness certificate.\nDo not drink alcohol, smoke, or eat non-vegetarian food during the journey.\nDo not click pictures in areas where photography has been prohibited.\n\nWhat to Pack\nClothing\nUpper Wear\n\n1-2 sweaters/fleece jackets\n2-3 thermals or cotton T-shirts\nRaincoat or waterproof windcheater\nMonkey cap or woolen cap\n\nLower Wear\n\nThermal leggings\n2 pairs of trek pants\nUndergarments\n\nFootwear\n\nSlippers/sandals for hotel or campsite use\nSturdy trekking shoes with good grip\n3-4 pairs of cotton and woolen socks\n\nFirst Aid & Medicines\n\nMedicines prescribed by your doctor\nBasic medications for cough, cold, fever, and ache\nAntiseptic and bandage\nTablets for motion sickness",
    "highlights": [],
    "itinerary": [
