  "chardham-yatra-package-from-mumbai": {
    "overview": "Feel like being one with the divine with our Chardham Yatra Package from Mumbai, crafted by our experts to meet your unique needs. This sacred Yatra takes you on an exploration of Uttarakhand's four ancient temples, including Kedarnath, Badrinath, Gangotri, and Yamunotri. You can have the Darshan of Lord Kedar at Kedarnath, pay homage to Lord Badri at Badrinath, experience solitude at Gangotri, and seek the blessings of Mata Yamuna at Yamunotri Temple. We offer a wide range of packages, ranging from budget to premium and deluxe to helicopter packages.\n\nOur packages include everything required to enjoy your time to the fullest at the Chardham sites, such as delicious food, comfortable accommodations, transportation, and exciting activities. We can also customize the packages based on your needs and aspirations. Contact us now to book the Badrinath Kedarnath Gangotri Yamunotri tour package now!\nTypes of Chardham Package from Mumbai\nLuxury Chardham Tour Packages\n\nIf you want a package that offers the perfect blend of comfort and spirituality, then you can opt for luxury tour packages. \nThese packages come with all the modern conveniences, ensuring you can have a unique travel experience.\n\nBudget Package\n\nThe budget package is perfect for those who want to have the Chardham tour within their limited budget. \nThis tour package includes basic accommodation, comfy transport, and tasty meals throughout.\n\nPremium Package\n\nThe premium package is ideal for those looking to have one-of-a-kind travel experiences. \nOur premium Chardham Yatra Tour Package from Mumbai 2026 comes with everything ranging from premium accommodation to VIP Darshan, gourmet meals, and interesting activities.\n\nHelicopter Package\n\nThe traditional route for visiting the Chardham shrines can be a bit long, depending on the road and weather conditions.\nIf you do not want to deal with lengthy travel, then a helicopter package can be your best option. Helicopter service is ideal for working professionals, senior citizens, and those with physical mobility or time-constrained schedules.\n\nWhy Choose the Char Dham Pilgrimage From Mumbai?\nYou should opt for the Chardham Yatra Package from Mumbai because Mumbai is well-connected with all the major Indian cities via road, flight, and train. Flights are readily available from Mumbai to Dehradun. If you opt for a road journey, you'll be awe-struck by the surreal views on the way to the Chardham sites.\nOur 13-Day Itinerary Ensures:\n\nGradual altitude acclimatization\nSafe and comfortable transfers\nExperienced drivers trained for Himalayan routes\nPre-arranged accommodations\nProper darshan assistance\nBalanced travel and rest days\n\nAbout the Chardham Circuit\nThe Chardham Yatra is a route that encompasses four holy temples located in the Garhwal Himalayas of Uttarakhand. The shrines are of immense religious importance and linked to the gods and goddesses of the origin of rivers.\n1. Yamunotri Temple (3,293 meters)\nYamunotri is a spiritual rejuvenating place encircled with snow-capped mountains and thermal springs, which provides an ideal start to the Yatra.\n2. Gangotri Temple (3,100 meters)\nGangotri, unlike Yamunotri, can be easily reached through roads, thus accessible to pilgrims of all ages. The temple rituals and peaceful banks of the river make an environment of divinity.\n3. Kedarnath Temple (3,583 meters)\nKedarnath is one of the twelve sacred Jyotirlingas of Lord Shiva, which is the most difficult and yet the most beneficial Dham.\n4. Badrinath Temple (3,133 meters)\nBadrinath is a pilgrimage devoted to Lord Vishnu and is approachable by road and provides a relaxing and well-organized pilgrimage climate.\nOur Expertise in Chardham Yatra Operations\nWe have the experience of years in the functioning of pilgrimage circuits in Uttarakhand and thus we have seamless directing contacts between Mumbai and the Himalayas.\n\nHotel Confirmed Hotels in All Destinations\nLocal Ground Support Teams\nReal-Time Weather Tracking\nOpen Pricing System\nTemple Timing Coordination\nSenior and Group Friendly planning\n\nWe are familiar with the landscape, changing seasons, and religious significance of every Dham. We handle logistics and pilgrims concentrate on devotion by means of our operational knowledge.\nCost of Char Dham Yatra from Mumbai\nThe cost of Chardham Travel Packages from Mumbai 2026 starts at \u20b942,000 per person (excluding flight). The package includes private transport, driver fees, hotel stays, and meals. The cost of the package can increase based on the season of travel and the inclusions in the package.\nChardham Route Map from Mumbai\n\nMumbai to Delhi: 1152 kilometers\nDelhi to Haridwar: 253 km\nHaridwar to Barkot: 180 km \u25025 hours\nBarkot to Yamunotri: 36 km (drive) + 7 km (trek) \u2502 1.5 hours + 4 to 5 hours (trek)\nBarkot to Uttarkashi: 82 km \u25023 hours\nUttarkashi to Gangotri: 100 km \u25024 hours\nUttarkashi to Rudraprayag: 177 km \u25025 to 6 hours\nRudraprayag to Kedarnath: 76 km by road \u250216 km trek \u2502(takes nearly a day)\nRudraprayag to Badrinath: 155 km \u25025 hours\nBadrinath to Rishikesh: 297 km \u250210 to 11 hours\nRishikesh to Haridwar: 23 km\nHaridwar to Delhi: 230 kms\nDelhi to Mumbai: 1152 kms\n\nBest Time to Visit\nApril - June (summer)\n\nApril to June is the best time for the Char Dham Yatra due to the moderate weather. During these months, you can have Darshan and undertake trekking without worrying about challenging weather scenarios. \nOn the downside, you will have to deal with large crowds, and you will have to pay premium rates everywhere. For Darshan at the shrines, there will be long lines.\n\nJuly-August and up to mid-September (Monsoon Season)\n\nDuring the monsoon, you should avoid undertaking the Char Dham Yatra. During the monsoon, you will have to encounter heavy rains. \nThere are also chances of landslides during this time of the year, resulting in delays and road blockages. Heavy rain can lead to more severe issues.\n\nMid-September to October and November (Winter Season)\n\nWinter is not a good time to visit the Chardham sites due to the harsh weather conditions.\nThe initial rush of pilgrims may be less, but heavy snowfall may make it difficult to access the shrines.\nAll the Chardham shrines get closed on or just after Diwali.\n\nHow to Reach?\nBy Air\nJolly Grant Airport in Dehradun is the nearest Airport to the Chardham sites. You can take a flight from Mumbai to Dehradun. Once you have reached Dehradun, you can board a bus or hire a taxi to reach the Chardham site's starting point.\nBy Train\nA direct train is not available to Chardham. Rishikesh and Haridwar are the nearest railway stations to the Chardham sites. Once you reach any of these destinations, you can board a bus or taxi to reach the Chardham site's starting point.\nBy Road\n\nBy road, you will have to first drive from Mumbai to Haridwar, covering a distance of around 1,400 km.\nAdditionally, via the NH48 route, the Yatra will take around 24 hours and can be done by bus or private car.\nFrom Dehradun or Haridwar, you can join a tour group or book a taxi to continue your Yatra to the Char Dham sites.\n\nAccommodation Options\nKedarnath\n\nAt Kedarnath, you will find comfortable accommodation options, including GMVN guest houses, Dharamshalas, and ashrams.\nSome of the good-quality accommodation options include The Kedar Camp, Kedarnath Ashram, and Sanskritik Ashram.\nYou can plan your stay in nearby towns like Sonprayag and Guptkashi for better amenities.\n\nBadrinath\n\nBadrinath has basic accommodations, including GMVN rest houses, budget-friendly hotels, and Dharamshalas with wonderful amenities.\nYou can plan your stay at Hotel Narayan Palace and Badrinath Ashram.\nNearby towns like Joshimath and Govindghat also offer good accommodation options.\n\nGangotri\n\nYou will find both budget-friendly and luxury hotels in Gangotri with all the modern facilities and scenic views.\nFor better amenities, you can plan your stay at Harshil and Dharali. Gangotri Glacier Retreat, Shristi Guest House, and Tapovan Cottage are some of the best stay options in Gangotri, where you can plan to stay by booking our Chardham Yatra Package from Mumbai.\n\nYamunotri\n\nYamunotri has several Dharamshalas, ashrams, and budget-friendly stay options where you can enjoy basic facilities.\nSome of the stay options that you can consider include The Yamunotri Resort, Hotel Vivek Palace and Restaurant, and Aditya Palace.\n\nTravel Tips for Pilgrims\n\nChardham Yatra requires the pilgrims to be in excellent physical condition. At least one to two months before the Chardham tour from Mumbai, you should begin doing cardio workouts such as swimming, cycling, or running. You should aim for a cardio workout of at least 30 minutes five days a week.\nCarry with you all the important numbers, including your medical places and operator for any emergency. You should keep the addresses of the nearest clinics or hospitals handy, as this will be very helpful in case of an emergency.\nShow respect to the traditions and customs of the local people. Follow all the customs during the time of rituals and prayers.\nBuy travel insurance that covers any kind of medical emergency and trekking events.\nYou should identify the symptoms and signs of altitude sickness. The common indicators include dizziness, headaches, nausea, and fatigue.\nCarry all the important documents, including your ID card, permit, medical certificate, and photographs.\nKeep yourself hydrated and avoid undertaking the unknown routes while trekking.\n\nWhat to Pack\nClothing Essentials\n\n3-4 T-shirts\n2 pairs of woollen track pants\nFleece jacket\nInner thermals\nWarm gloves\nSun caps\nUndergarments\nRaincoat/Poncho\n\nEssential Medicines and First Aid Kit\n\nAntibacterial powder\nBand Aid\nVolini Spray\nAntacid\nORS/Electrolyte\nParacetamol\nBandage\nAntibiotic\n\nFootwear\n\nSturdy trekking shoes with good grip.\nA pair of flip-flops or floaters.\n\nBasic Gear\n\nRain cover and backpack\nDay pack\nTrekking poles\nLED torch\nWater Bottle\nSwiss Knife\nCamera and camera accessories",
