  "chardham-yatra-package-from-pune": {
    "overview": "The Chardham Yatra package from Pune offers a well-structured way for pilgrims to undertake the spiritual journey. During this holy journey, you will get a chance to visit four sacred attractions, including Kedarnath, Badrinath, Gangotri, and Yamunotri. The Char Dham sites are considered to be immensely sacred for the Hindus, offering them a chance to get away from the sins they committed in their past lives.\n\nWe guide you throughout the trip and ensure you can enjoy the best amenities. Whether you're traveling alone or with your family, your safety and comfort are always our top priority. With our well-crafted Char Dham tour package from Pune, you can have a spiritually uplifting journey that will remain etched in your heart forever.\nTypes of Chardham Package from Pune\nLuxury Chardham Tour Packages\nIf you're someone who doesn't want to make any compromise with their comfort during the Chardham tour, you should opt for luxury packages. These packages include superior amenities such as top-rated accommodations, VIP darshan, and transportation via a private vehicle.\nBudget Package\nBudget packages ensure that you can have the best Chardham yatra experience without worrying about your finances. With this package, you can enjoy good-quality services and amenities within your budget. You may not get world-class services with this package, but the basic amenities are also well-curated.\nPremium Package\nWith a premium Chardham yatra package from Pune, you can have an unforgettable yatra experience. This package is ideal for those looking to enjoy utmost luxury and sophistication. However, this package may be a bit costly considering the world-class amenities you get to enjoy with it.\nHelicopter Package\nWith our helicopter package, you can bypass lengthy treks and travel to the holy sites directly. This package includes VIP darshan, premium accommodation, smooth transfer, and vegetarian meals.\nWhy Choose the Char Dham Pilgrimage From Pune?\nYou should choose the Char Dham Pilgrimage from Pune because Pune has good connectivity with Uttarakhand. You can opt for a flight from Pune to Dehradun and then travel to the Chardham sites via road. When you travel from Pune via road, you can witness the most picturesque views.\nCost of Char Dham Yatra from Pune\nThe Chardham yatra package from Pune will cost you around 35000 to 60000, depending on the inclusions of the package and the duration of the tour. If you're travelling in peak season or want additional amenities, you may have to pay more for the Chardham package.\nChardham Route Map from Pune\nPune- Haridwar \u2192 Rishikesh \u2192 Chamba \u2192 Tehri \u2192 Dharasu \u2192 Barkot \u2192 Syanachatti \u2192 Hanuman Chatti \u2192 Jankichatti \u2192 Yamunotri \u2192 Uttarkashi \u2192 Harsil \u2192 Gangotri (Gaumukh) \u2192 Srinagar \u2192 Rudraprayag \u2192 Augustmuni \u2192 Phata \u2192 Sitapur \u2192 Guptkashi \u2192 Gaurikund \u2192 Kedarnath \u2192 Ukhimath \u2192 Chopta \u2192 Gopeshwar \u2192 Chamoli \u2192 Pipalkoti \u2192 Joshimath (Auli) \u2192 Govindghat \u2192 Hanuman Chatti \u2192 Badrinath\nBest Time to Visit\nSummer (April to June)\nSummer is considered to be the best time to visit the Chardham sites, as people living in Pune can get away from the scorching heat of Maharashtra. During these months, the average temperature ranges around 10\u00b0C to 25\u00b0C.\nMonsoon (July to September)\nDuring the monsoon, the Chardham sites get dotted with lush greenery, making it ideal for photography. However, travelling during this time can be risky due to the chances of a landslide and blocked roads.\nWinter (December to March)\nThe doorways of all Char Dham temples remain closed from December to March due to heavy snowfall and freezing temperatures. However, during these months, the idols are shifted to Joshimath for Badrinath and Ukhimath for Kedarnath.\nHow to Reach?\nBy Air\nFrom Pune, you can take a flight to Dehradun. Jolly Grant Airport in Dehradun is the nearest airport to the Chardham sites. From Dehradun, you can board a bus or taxi to reach the starting point of the Chardham sites.\nBy Train\nA direct train is not available from Pune to Uttarakhand's main stations, so you will have to reach Haridwar or Delhi first. From Haridwar, you can take a taxi or bus to Rishikesh, which serves as the base for the remaining part of the journey.\nBy Road\nFrom Pune, you will have to travel via NH 58 to Haridwar. You can either drive on your own, take a cab, or bus. From Rishikesh, the routes are well-connected to Badrinath and Gangotri, but trekking will be required to reach Yamunotri(from Janki Chatti) and Kedarnath (from Gaurikund).\nAccommodation Options\nGangotri\nPilgrims can find GMVN guest houses, Dharamshalas, and tent accommodations with basic amenities and services. Harsil and Uttarkashi are nearby towns where you can find decent accommodations with clean and hygienic rooms and all the modern amenities.\nYamunotri\nYamunotri offers comfortable accommodation options, including GMVN rest houses and Dharamshalas. At Janki Chatti and Barkot, you will find better quality accommodation options. Pushpanjali Yatri Niwas (Janki Chatti), Hotel Aswal (Barkot), Hotel Samrat (Barkot Yamunotri), Bahuguna Yatri Niwas, Hotel Yamuna Divya Darshan, and Hotel Himdarshan are some of the comfy stay options.\nKedarnath\nFrom government guest houses to hotels, you will find a wide range of accommodation options at Kedarnath. You can also plan your stay at nearby towns such as Sonprayag and Sitapur. Popular stay options include Hotel Ganga, Sidharth Camp, Gayatri Nivas, and Behl Ashram.\nBadrinath\nWith the Char Dham pilgrimage from Pune, you can plan your stay at various accommodation options, including guesthouses, camps, budget-friendly hotels, and Dharamshalas. Famous stay options include Panchvati Inn, Mountain Trex Retreat, and Janki Guest House.\nTravel Tips for Pilgrims\n\nObtain all the necessary permits required for the pilgrimage.\nMonths before the Char Dham pilgrimage tour from Pune, you should begin physical preparation and focus on strength training and cardio.\nTo avoid altitude sickness, you should acclimatize to high altitudes. Spend a few days at elevations between 2,000 and 2500 meters. It will allow your body to adjust to the altitude.\nBuild physical fitness to improve your cardiovascular endurance. You can indulge in jogging, brisk walking, and cycling.\nStay hydrated during the yatra to prevent dehydration.\nDuring the Pune to Uttarakhand pilgrimage tour, you should avoid caffeine, smoking, and alcohol.\nCarry all the important medicines to deal with any kind of health-related concern.\n\nWhat to Pack\nClothing Essentials\n\nHeavy woolens\nGloves\nRaincoat\nWaterproof clothing\nJacket\nSunhat\nLong sleeve shirt\nWoollen pants\n\nFootwear\n\nSturdy, comfortable trekking shoes.\nLight slippers\n\nFirst-Aid Kit\n\nPain relief spray\nBand aid\nBasic medicines for fever, headache, nausea, or acidity.\nEnergy bars or glucose powder for instant energy.\nAntiseptic cream\n\nMiscellaneous Items\n\nA walking stick\nWaist pouch or backpack\nEnergy bars and dry fruits\nORS sachets and a water bottle\nTorch or flashlight\nMobile essentials and powerbank",
