  "chardham-yatra-package-from-rishikesh": {
    "overview": "Rishikesh Chardham Yatra Package is among the most enriching pilgrimage trips in India which have spiritual significance. This holy yatra begins at the sacred town of Rishikesh, the Yoga Capital of the World and the devotees pay visits to the four Himalayan shrines of divinity - Yamunotri, Gangotri, Kedarnath and Badrinath. The pilgrimage is a combination of religious worship, exploration, and nature and hence a once in a lifetime experience to Indians and other pilgrims the world over.\n\nRishikesh is one of the best places to start the Char Dham Yatra, since it is well connected by road, is a religious site, and it is located close to the Garhwal Himalayas. The package is aimed at providing comfort, safety and a well-balanced itinerary of more than 10 days so that pilgrims can do the yatra without physical depletion. \nWhy Start Chardham Yatra from Rishikesh?\nThere are several benefits of beginning your Chardham Yatra at Rishikesh, both spiritually and logistically.\nSpiritual Importance of Rishikesh\n\nRishikesh is located on the shores of the sacred River Ganga.\nIt is estimated that the Char Dham Yatra is complete when it starts at Rishikesh.\nThere is also the location of ancient temples and ashrams and the famous Ganga Aarti at Triveni Ghat.\n\nLogistical Advantages\n\nGood accessibility and connectivity to key cities in India.\nServes as a natural acclimatization area before going to high altitude areas.\nGood hotels, transport, and health care institutions.\n\nChardham Yatra Package Highlights\nThis 10 Days / 9 Nights Chardham Yatra tour starting at Rishikesh is a well thought-through initiative to provide a comfortable, well-paced tour and spiritual enriching experience to the Himalayan sacred places. The package will also cover pick up and drop services at Rishikesh where you will have a hassle-free beginning and end of your pilgrimage. The route has clean and comfortable hotels and guesthouses that accommodate the travellers, which provides the much-needed comfort after extensive mountain trips. Breakfast and dinner are also covered on a daily basis and the pilgrims are able to concentrate on prayers without the concern of having to eat. The trip is accompanied by an adept local driver and properly serviced car, which guarantees the security on difficult hill routes. Moreover, special services are offered in case of darshan of temples and obligatory registrations, and the pilgrims are guided by the process as easily as possible, and time is saved.\nDestinations Covered in the Chardham Yatra\nThis pilgrimage is a visit to all the four sacred shrines found in the circuit of Chardham.\n\nThe yatra starts at Yamunotri Dham, the origin of the holy Yamuna River, then Gangotri Dham, the source of the sacred Ganga.\nPilgrims next go to Kedarnath Dham, which is one of the twelve Jyotirlingas of Lord Shiva located in the midst of the snow-clad grandiose of mountains.\nThe pilgrimage ends at the Badrinath Dham which is devoted to Lord Vishnu and stands on the banks of the Alaknanda River.\nThe package also covers sightseeing in Rishikesh and Haridwar as well as the Chardham temples enabling pilgrims to have the spiritual feel of the holy cities.\n\nBest Time to visit Rishikesh to Chardham Yatra\nThe best season to go to the holy Chardham Yatra at Rishikesh is either in the summer or and after the monsoon period that when the weather and the roads are most favourable.\n\nMay through June be able to be regarded as one of the most favourable seasons, as the weather is not hot, the snow is no longer on the roads to the high altitudes, and all temples are open in full.\nThe other fine month is September to October, which is the end of the monsoon season, skies are not cloudy, and there are relatively few pilgrims, and therefore the trip becomes smoother and more comfortable.\nIt is recommended that the travellers not visit the Himalayan region during July and August because during this period it is the monsoon season; and it is likely to experience heavy rains, landslides, and road blockages.\nThe yatra cannot also be done during the winter season as the temples are still closed as a result of heavy snowfall and extremely cold weather conditions.\n\nChardham Yatra Registration and Travelling Tips\nMandatory Registration\nOnline registration has been mandatory among all the Chardham pilgrims by the Uttarakhand Government. This is registered with the biometric check and this check is compulsory at various points throughout the route. The pilgrims need to be armed with proper government-issued identification and registration certifications during the journey to prevent any inconvenience.\nHealth & Safety Tips\nSince the place they will visit is quite high and the weather may alter, pilgrims must be particularly mindful of their health.\n\nThey recommend that one carry personal medicines and a basic first-aid kit, in case one has pre-existing medical conditions.\nIt is important to maintain proper acclimatization to avoid altitude sickness, so there should not be any rus; it is better to be hydrated.\nIt is highly recommended that pilgrims should abstain from alcohol and smoking as this may aggravate the problem of breathing at elevated altitudes.",
    "highlights": [
      "The yatra starts at Yamunotri Dham, the origin of the holy Yamuna River, then Gangotri Dham, the source of the sacred Ganga.",
      "Pilgrims next go to Kedarnath Dham, which is one of the twelve Jyotirlingas of Lord Shiva located in the midst of the snow-clad grandiose of mountains.",
      "The pilgrimage ends at the Badrinath Dham which is devoted to Lord Vishnu and stands on the banks of the Alaknanda River.",
      "The package also covers sightseeing in Rishikesh and Haridwar as well as the Chardham temples enabling pilgrims to have the spiritual feel of the holy cities."
    ],
