  "chennai-mahabalipuram-thanjavur-trichy-madurai-tour": {
    "overview": "Explore beautiful heritage of South India with our Chennai Mahabalipuram Thanjavur Trichy Madurai Tour. Journey starts from Chennai, a city full of history, temples and beautiful beaches. See More\n\nNext explore Mahabalipuram, especially known for the Krishna Mandapam, which was created from a single rock. Imagine how skilled the artists were, and it\u2019s also a great photo spot. Now, the tour moves to Thanjavur where the famous Brihadeeswarar Temple is the main attraction.\nAnother popular site is Trichy, and don\u2019t miss trying the tasty local drink, Jigarthanda. The last stop is Madurai, where tourists always visit the Meenakshi Temple. It was once attacked by Muslim invaders from Delhi Sultanate, but later rebuilt with great devotion. Its beautiful and unique architecture attracts visitors from all over the world. Every places has its own charm and story so plan your Chennai Mahabalipuram Thanjavur Trichy and Madurai trip to make new memories.\nSee Less\n\nNext explore Mahabalipuram, especially known for the Krishna Mandapam, which was created from a single rock. Imagine how skilled the artists were, and it\u2019s also a great photo spot. Now, the tour moves to Thanjavur where the famous Brihadeeswarar Temple is the main attraction.\n\nAnother popular site is Trichy, and don\u2019t miss trying the tasty local drink, Jigarthanda. The last stop is Madurai, where tourists always visit the Meenakshi Temple. It was once attacked by Muslim invaders from Delhi Sultanate, but later rebuilt with great devotion. Its beautiful and unique architecture attracts visitors from all over the world. Every places has its own charm and story so plan your Chennai Mahabalipuram Thanjavur Trichy and Madurai trip to make new memories.",
    "highlights": [
      "Start your journey in Chennai and enjoy South India\u2019s culture, history and relaxing beaches.",
      "See unique rock monuments in Mahabalipuram, visit the Brihadeeswarar Temple in Thanjavur and enjoy historical places in Trichy.",
      "Experience Madurai\u2019s Meenakshi Temple, local culture and unique architecture.",
      "Enjoy shopping for silk Sarees in Kanchipuram and create lasting memories in tour.",
      "See More"
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1: Arrive at Chennai - Mahabalipuram - Pondicherry (Approx. 208 km/ 4-5 Hours)",
        "description": "Start your trip to with a warm welcome at Chennai Airport or Railway Station. Our\nMy Quick Trippers\nrepresentative will meet you and help you travel to Mahabalipuram. If you include a guide, he will come with the driver to assist you throughout the day.\nAfter pick-up, you will start your tour and visit-\nArjuna\u2019s Penance\n(Monument)\nKrishna Mandapam\n(Rock cut cave temple)\nCave Temples\nPancha Rathas\n(UNESCO World Heritage Site)\nAfter completing the main sightseeing in\nMahabalipuram\n, drive to\nPondicherry.\nOn arrival, check into your hotel and enjoy your overnight stay in Pondicherry.\nNote-\nArjuna\u2019s Penance timings are from\n6:00 AM\nto\n6:00 PM.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "DAY 2: Pondicherry- Chidambaram - Kumbakonam (Approx. 133 km / 3 hrs Drive)",
        "description": "Morning after breakfast, check out from the hotel and visit\nAuroville Matrimandir\n, a place for meditation. It is believed that it took 37 years to build Matrimandir (It is a beautiful spot to click photos).\nAfter checking into your hotel, visit Sri\nAurobindo Ashram\n, a famous and wealthy ashram in India, where people from all over the world come to relax and feel calm.\nNext, explore\nArulmigu Manakula Vinayagar Temple\n, dedicated to Lord Ganesh.\nGo to the\nPuducherry Museum\n, where the huge Chola-era statues look so real, it feels like they could move any moment.\nLater, drive to\nChidambaram\n, a temple town famous for the\nThillai Nataraja Temple\n, spread over 40 acres and part of the Pancha Bhoota, which represents Sky (Akasha).\nProceed to\nGangaikonda Cholapuram\n, popular for the\nBrihadeeswarar Temple\n, dedicated to Lord Shiva. The temple has one of the largest Shivling in India, around 13.5 ft tall.\nDrive to\nKumbakonam.\nOn arrival, check into the hotel. Overnight stay at the hotel.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "DAY 3: Kumbakonam - Thanjavur (Tanjore) - Rameshwaram (300 - 310 km / 5.5-6 Hrs Drive)",
        "description": "After breakfast, check out of the hotel and visit\nKumbakonam\n, popular for\nAdi Kumbeswarar Temple\n, and go to the nearby\nMahamaham Tank,\nwhere pilgrims take a holy dip. Later,\nThen explore\nAiravatesvara Temple\nat\nDarasuram\n, a UNESCO World Heritage Site. The temple walls show dances, musicians, and stories of gods that will amaze art lovers!\nDrive to Thanjavur (Tanjore). On arrival, travel to the Brihadeeswara Temple. The interesting fact is that no cement was used in this temple.\nNow, go to\nThanjavur Palace\n, where the Maratha kings lived from 1674 to 1855 and explore\nThanjavur Art Gallery.\nDrive to\nRameshwaram\n, located on\nPamban Island.\nAccording to legend, this is the place where Lord Rama built a bridge across the sea to Lanka to rescue Sita from Ravana.\nOn arrival, check into the hotel. Overnight stay at\nRameshwaram.\nNote-\nWear comfortable shoes as there will be a lot of walking at the temples.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "DAY 4: In Rameswaram - Full Sightseeing Tour",
        "description": "Early in the morning, around\n5:00 AM\n, proceed to the\nSpatika Linga Darshan\n, also called\nMani Darshan\n, where the natural crystal Shivling (not man-made) is very important in Hinduism and looks very beautiful.\nLater you will head out for\nAgni Teertham\nto have a holy bath in the sea.\nFurther proceed to the main temple through North gate and\nTake sacred bath with holy water of the 22 wells, inside the\nRamanathaswamy Temple\nduring\nTheerth Snanam.\nThen proceed for darshan and pooja at the main temple.\nAfter breakfast, proceed for a full sightseeing tour of\nRameswaram\n, which includes\nFive-faced Hanuman Temple, Ramar Patham, Kothandaramaswamy Temple, Gandamadana Parvatham\n(where Lord Rama\u2019s Footprint is located),\nRama Setu / Adam\u2019s Bridge,\nFormer President\nA. P. J. Abdul Kalam House\n, and\nDhanushkodi.\nAfter finishing the sightseeing, return to the hotel and stay overnight in\nRameswaram.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "DAY 5: Rameswaram - Kanyakumari - (312 km/ 7 hrs)",
        "description": "In the Morning, visit the\nRamanathaswamy Temple\nonce again or take a\nSamudra Snanam\n(holy dip in the sea).\nAfter this, check out of the hotel and drive to\nKanyakumari\nwhere the\nBay of Bengal\n, the\nArabian Sea\nand the\nIndian Ocean meet.\nKanyakumari\nis special because it\u2019s the only place where you can see both the sunrise and sunset over the ocean (perfect spot for amazing photos ).\nOn arrival check into your hotel and relax for the rest of the day.\nOvernight stay at the hotel.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "DAY 6: Kanyakumari - Madurai (243 Kms/4hrs)",
        "description": "Wake up early to enjoy the sunrise view in\nKanyakumari\n. Return to the hotel for breakfast.\nAfter breakfast, you can visit\nSwami Vivekananda Rock Memorial\n, located on a small rock surrounded by water, the landscape views of the sea is outstanding! Walk over the Sea by Glass bridge to reach Thiruvalluvar Statue.\nThen, travel to\nKanyakumari Mandir\n, this temple is built in\nKerala-style architecture\n, so just get ready to click photos.\nNext, see\nTri Samudra Milan\nand\nGandhi Mandapam\n, and later\ndrive to Madurai\nNote-\nYou can\u2019t take pictures inside the inner temple.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "DAY 7: Madurai -Tiruchirappalli (Trichy) (132 km/ 2-3 hrs)",
        "description": "Morning after breakfast, check out of the hotel and begin a sightseeing tour of\nMadurai.\nVisit\nMeenakshi Sundareswarar Temple\n, Here, the temple\u2019s famous elephant, Parvathi, used to bless people by softly placing her trunk on their heads. She was loved by many tourists.\nAfter temple Darshan, visit\nThiruparankundram Murugan Temple.\nNext, travel to\nTiruchirappalli (Trichy)\n, known for its rich heritage and monuments. Once you reach, check into the hotel and stay overnight.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "DAY 8: Tiruchirappalli (Trichy) - Tiruvannamalai (223 Kms / 4-5 Hrs)",
        "description": "Morning after breakfast, check out from the hotel and start your sightseeing tour of\nTiruchirappalli.\nYour tour starts at the\nSri Ranganatha Swamy Temple\nin Srirangam, one of the 108 holy Vishnu temple, famous for its 21 towers and impressive architecture (great photo spot).\nNext, visit the nearby\nJambukeswarar Akilandeswari Temple\n, the fact is that it represents the element of Water and the temple's underground water never dries up, even when removed.\nThen, explore the\nUcchi Pillayar Temple\n, built on top of Rockfort. From here, enjoy a stunning view of the city and the Cauvery River (don\u2019t forget to click pictures).\nAfter that visit\nGovernment Museum\nat\nRani Mangammal Mahal\n- where unique artwork and the region's history will amaze you..\nNext, visit the\nButterfly Park\n, a calm place full of colorful butterflies. Then travel to\nNakshatra Vanam\n, a beautiful garden nearby.\nAfter sightseeing, proceed to\nTiruvannamalai\n. On arrival, check in to your hotel and relax.\nOvernight stay at\nTiruvannamalai.\nNote-\nTry the local snacks near Rockfort - it\u2019s tasty and part of Trichy\u2019s culture.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "DAY 9: Tiruvannamalai - Kanchipuram (130 Kms / 3 Hrs)",
        "description": "Morning after breakfast, check out from the hotel and visit the\nAnnamalaiyar Temple\n, one of the biggest temples in India. It\u2019s a peaceful place where you can feel strong spiritual vibes.\nAfter your temple visit, drive towards\nKanchipuram\n. Long ago, Kanchipuram was a great learning hub where people studied Hinduism, Jainism, and Buddhism.\nOn arrival, check in to the hotel. Overnight stay at Kanchipuram.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "DAY 10: Kanchipuram - Chennai (Departure) (74 Kms/1-2 Hrs )",
        "description": "After breakfast, check out of the hotel and visit\nKamakshi Amman Temple\ndedicated to Goddess Kamakshi where devotees believe their wishes are fulfilled if they go with a pure heart.\nNext visit\nVaradharaja Perumal Temple\n, dedicated to Lord Vishnu and one of the 108 Divya Desams.\nContinue to\nKailasanathar Temple\n, it\u2019s 1,350 years old temple dedicated to Lord Shiva.\nThen explore\nEkambareswarar Temple\ndedicated to Lord Murugan. It is part of the Pancha Bhoota (five elements) and is connected with the earth element (Prithvi).\nAlso visit\nKumarakottam Temple\n, dedicated to Lord Murugan.\nIf time allows, go shopping in\nKanchipuram\n, famous for its hand-made silk Sarees.\nLater, drive to Chennai. Your\nChennai Mahabalipuram Thanjavur Trichy Madurai travel package\nends with happy memories as you are transferred to Chennai Airport or the railway station for your journey to your next destination.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      }
    ],
    "faqs": []
  },
