  "cochin-munnar-thekkady-alleppey-tour": {
    "overview": "Cochin Munnar Thekkady Alleppey Tour Package is perfect for travelers who want to see Kerala's nature, wildlife, and culture - all in one tour. See More\n\nImagine walking through green hills, enjoying calm backwaters, and breathing in fresh air!\nEach place has its own attractions and surprises. Start with Cochin, known for its beautiful colonial buildings that give a true European vibe. In Munnar don't miss Kundale Lake -- its early morning fog makes the place truly magical.\nIn Thekkady, visit Periyar Tiger Reserve where tourists can see elephants, deer, and many other creatures on a boat ride. Animal lovers will really enjoy this. Alleppey is also one of the best spot, known for its peaceful backwaters, beaches, and floating villages. Our itinerary covers many more amazing places - just plan your 6 Days trip to Cochin Munnar Thekkady Alleppey, and enjoy the best of Kerala!\nSee Less\n\nImagine walking through green hills, enjoying calm backwaters, and breathing in fresh air!\n\nEach place has its own attractions and surprises. Start with Cochin, known for its beautiful colonial buildings that give a true European vibe. In Munnar don't miss Kundale Lake -- its early morning fog makes the place truly magical.\n\nIn Thekkady, visit Periyar Tiger Reserve where tourists can see elephants, deer, and many other creatures on a boat ride. Animal lovers will really enjoy this. Alleppey is also one of the best spot, known for its peaceful backwaters, beaches, and floating villages. Our itinerary covers many more amazing places - just plan your 6 Days trip to Cochin Munnar Thekkady Alleppey, and enjoy the best of Kerala!",
    "highlights": [
      "Explore Kerala's beauty with a mix of nature, wildlife and culture on this 6-day trip.",
      "Visit Cochin's colonial sites, Munnar's tea gardens and lakes, Thekkady's wildlife and Alleppey's backwaters.",
      "Enjoy peaceful boat rides, spot different birds, relax on beaches and capture amazing photos and videos.",
      "Shop for spices, tea, handicrafts and experience local village life along the journey.",
      "See More"
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 01- Cochin Arrival and Sightseeing",
        "description": "When you arrive at Cochin Airport, our My Quick Trippers representative will welcome you and take you to the hotel for check-in. If you have hired a guide, they will come with the driver and help you in the whole trip.\nAfter check-in, enjoy your Cochin tour and visit-\nJewish Synagogue\nDutch Palace (Mattancherry Palace):\nFamous for its beautiful wall paintings that show stories from the Ramayana and Mahabharata.\nSt. Francis Church\nChinese Fishing Net-\nFamous spot in Cochin, introduced by Chinese traders. The sunset view here is stunning (Don't forget to click pictures).\nOnce your sightseeing is done, relax and stay overnight in\nCochin.\nNote-\nDutch Palace is closed on Fridays.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 02- Cochin - Munnar (131 Kms/3 Hrs.)",
        "description": "In the morning have breakfast and then drive to\nMunnar\n, one of Kerala's top destination.\nExperience the journey as you travel through beautiful landscapes full of green hills, rivers, and flowing waterfalls.\nOn the way, enjoy the beautiful\ntea gardens,\nspice plantations\nand thick forests. Their fragrance makes journey refreshing and shows Kerala's beauty.\nWhen you reach Munnar, check into your hotel and spend the day relaxing or exploring the surroundings freely.\nOvernight stay at\nMunnar\n.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 03- Munnar Sightseeing",
        "description": "After an early morning breakfast get ready to explore the scenic beauty and attractions of\nMunnar\n.\nWalk through Munnar's beautiful\ntea gardens\nfamous for their high quality tea. Smell the fresh leaves and learn how tea is made.\nVisit\nMattupetty Lake\nand\nDam\n, a peaceful spot surrounded by hills, where you can enjoy boating (optional).\nNext go to\nEcho Point\nand have fun in this unique spot as your voice bounces back from hills.\nNow proceed to\nKundala Lake,\na calm spot perfect for photography and enjoying the peaceful surroundings. If you get time try to meditate here.\nExplore\nRajamalai\nfamous for the rare\nNilgiri Tahr,\nand enjoy the amazing views. You can also see unique plants and wildlife here.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 04 - Munnar - Thekkady (122 Kms/3-4 Hrs )",
        "description": "After breakfast, go to\nThekkady\n, a perfect spot for nature lovers. Drive takes you through green valleys, tea gardens, and hills with great views all around.\nVisit\nPeriyar Tiger Reserve\nin Thekkady and explore its rich wildlife, full of animals, birds, and natural beauty.\nStay overnight at the hotel.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 05- Thekkady - Alleppey (155 Kms/3.5 Hrs)",
        "description": "After breakfast proceed to\nAlleppey\n(Alappuzha), famously known as the \"Venice of the East.\"\nOption 1- Stay at Hotel\nOn arrival check into your hotel.\nEvening Activities-\nGo on a peaceful cruise ride on\nVembanad Lake\n(optional) and enjoy the calm water and sunset. (Pay separately)\nWalk along\nAlleppey Beach\n, enjoy the peaceful surroundings, and take some time for a small picnic.\nEnjoy\nshopping\nin local markets where you can find unique gifts, handmade crafts, and regional products.\nReturn to your hotel for an overnight stay in Alleppey.\nOption 2- Houseboat Stay\nOn arrival check in to your traditional\nKettuvallam\n(Houseboat) for a unique backwater experience.\nAs the boat moves, you'll pass through local villages, see many coconut trees, and spot different bird species - it's a special time to take amazing videos.\nEnjoy fresh meals on the houseboat, including a delicious dinner.\nStay overnight on the houseboat.\nNote\n- Mosquitoes can be around while on the houseboat, so don't forget to bring some insect repellent.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 06- Alleppey - Cochin (53 km / 1 hour)",
        "description": "After a breakfast, leave the hotel or houseboat and go to Cochin, you will be dropped at the bus station, airport, or railway station for your next destination.\nThank you for choosing us for your journey. Your\ntrip\nends with happy memories you will always remember.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      }
    ],
    "faqs": []
  },
