  "colorful-rajasthan": {
    "overview": "The 12 Nights / 13 Days Colorful Rajasthan Tour package offers a captivating exploration of Rajasthan\u2019s enchanting destinations. In addition to this, you will have the opportunity to embark on a city tour in Delhi and Agra.\n\nImmerse yourself in the vibrant culture and delectable cuisine of Rajasthan during this remarkable tour. One of the highlights of this trip is witnessing the architectural brilliance and the harmonious blend of Hindu, Mughal, and Rajput influences. Nowhere else in the world will you find streets, markets, and bazaars as vibrant and lively as those in Rajasthan. For a more comprehensive understanding of this extraordinary journey, please refer to the detailed itinerary provided below.\n\nImmerse yourself in the vibrant culture and delectable cuisine of Rajasthan during this remarkable tour. One of the highlights of this trip is witnessing the architectural brilliance and the harmonious blend of Hindu, Mughal, and Rajput influences. Nowhere else in the world will you find streets, markets, and bazaars as vibrant and lively as those in Rajasthan. For a more comprehensive understanding of this extraordinary journey, please refer to the detailed itinerary provided below.\n\nColorful Rajasthan Tour Itinerary Package\n\n\nDay 1 :Delhi \u2013 Sariska (271 Kms / 4 Hrs)\n\n\nOn arrival at Delhi Airport/ Railway station, our Namaste India Representative will greet you and later drive to Sariska- A National Park. Upon arrival check in at hotel. We take Jungle Safari to Sariska Tiger Reserve which has characteristics Fauna of dry zone and antelopes, deer, caracal, jungle cat, hyena, jackal with plenty of birds in the natural valley. Overnight at the hotel.\n\n\n\n\nDay 2 :Sariska \u2013 Ranthambore\n\n\nThe morning after breakfast transfer to Ranthambore, check into a hotel, after lunch visit to Ranthambhore National Park. (Entrance fee to National Park are extra).\n\n\n\n\nDay 3 :Ranthambore \u2013 Sawai Madhopur \u2013 Jaipur\n\n\nThe morning after breakfast, transfer to Jaipur. Enroute Visit Sawai Madhopur and check into the hotel on arrival at Jaipur. Evening free for shopping and for the scroll on the city. Overnight stay at Jaipur.\n\n\n\n\nDay 4 :Jaipur Sightseeing\n\n\nThis morning, after breakfast, visits the ancient capital of the Kachwaha Rajputs, Amer. One can take an elephant ride or the jeep ride up to the fort. Thereafter, enjoy a photo-stop at Hawa Mahal \u2013 the Palace of Winds. Later, visit the City Palace and the apartment housing museums with an array of textiles, costumes, arms, weapons and paintings and finally visit Jantar Mantar, the observatory built by Maharaja Jai Singh-II. The founder of Jantar Mantar is Maharaja Jai Singh II, he had built Jantar Mantar in five different locations of India, out of which Jantar Mantar at Jaipur is the largest. The observatories, or \u2018Jantar Mantar\u2019 as they are commonly known, incorporate multiple buildings of unique form, each with a specialized function for astronomical measurement.\nLater you are free to enjoy shopping in the local market. The market of Jaipur will delight you with the exotic blue pottery, the batik painting, block printed textiles of Sanganer and Bagru, tie and dye fabrics, Mojari \u2013 (the local shoe), sandalwood carving items, beautiful stone carvings etc.\n\n\n\n\nDay 5 :Jaipur \u2013 Bikaner (335 Kms / 6 Hrs)\n\n\nToday After breakfast drive to Bikaner, Enroute visit Deshnok Temple and Camel-breeding Farm just before Bikaner. Overnight stay at Bikaner.\n\n\n\n\nDay 6 :Bikaner \u2013 Jaisalmer (329 Kms / 5.5 Hrs)\n\n\nMorning half Day visits fabulous Junagarh Fort & Lalgarh Palace and proceeds for Jaisalmer. Visit Kheechan on the way, and reach Jaisalmer Check-in at hotel in Jaisalmer. Overnight stay at Jaisalmer.\n\n\n\n\nDay 7 :Jaisalmer Sightseeing\n\n\nVisit Jaisalmer Fort & Museum after breakfast. Also, see the Jain Temple. Take a walk through the back streets to the Patwon Ki Haveli & Kothari Haveli. After lunch proceeds to Kuldhera \u2013 An abandoned habitation, and then to Sam Sand Dunes. Here camp stay will be provided with folk dance and songs with Rajasthani Dinner.\nSam Sand Dunes: Sam sand dunes are becoming the major attraction in Jaisalmer. This is the closest place from where you can lose yourself in \u2018The Great Thar Desert\u2019. Sam has a truly magnificent stretch of sweeping dunes, with sparse or no vegetation.\n\n\n\n\nDay 8 :Jaisalmer \u2013 Pokhran \u2013 Jodhpur (307 Kms / 6 Hrs)\n\n\nThe morning after breakfast transfer to Jodhpur, The Sun City. On the way to Jodhpur, you can have your lunch at Fort Pokaran which literally means the palace of five mirages. Enroute you can also visit Bishnoi Villages where people believe in conserving the natural environment and animal hunting is banned there. You can spot numerous deer in Bishnoi Village. Arrive Jodhpur and get assisted check into the hotel. After taking some rest in the hotel we begin the city tour of Jodhpur which comprises of visit to the impressive Mehrangarh Fort \u2013 This magnificent fort was built in the 15th century and has seven gates which still witness marks of the battle fought by armies of Jodhpur to protect their people, Jaswant Thada \u2013 Looks like a temple, this white marble was constructed in the memory of Maharaja Jaswant Singh II, last but not to miss is Umaid Bhawan Palace \u2013 This stunning palace which today also serves as the residence to the royal family and a part of it is transformed into a luxurious hotel. The evening is free to relax and overnight stay is in Jodhpur.\n\n\n\n\nDay 9 :Jodhpur \u2013 Udaipur (270 Kms / 05 Hrs)\n\n\nThe morning after breakfast transfer to Udaipur, A beautiful romantic city also known as the City of Lakes\u201d. Enroute visit Ranakpur Jain Temple \u2013 These temples were built in the 15 century during the rule of Rana Kumbha and today the temples are one of the most sacred places for Jainism. The main temple to visit is the Chaumukha Temple or four-faced temple. Upon arrival, a warm greeting awaits you at the hotel check into the hotel. Evening you can enjoy boat ride on the beautiful Lake Pichola. Overnight stay is at hotel in Udaipur.\n\n\n\n\nDay 10 :Udaipur Sightseeing\n\n\nToday we are fully packed with Udaipur Sightseeing. After breakfast proceeds to explore the attractions of the city including City Palace, Saheliyon Ki Bari, Lake Pichola, Jagdish Temple, Kumbhalgarh Fort, Dolls Museum and Fateh Sagar Lake. Overnight stay at Udaipur.\n\n\n\n\nDay 11 :Udaipur \u2013 Pushkar (283 Kms / 5:30 Hrs)\n\n\nThe morning after breakfast drive by surface to Pushkar. On arrival check into the hotel. Afternoon proceeds for sightseeing tour of Dargah (Indian\u2019s Macca) in Ajmer and Lord Brahma Temple at Pushkar. This little town is hugely known for the \u201cPushkar Fair\u201d (where the mass trading of camels takes place), \u201cthe Lord Brahma Temple\u201d, a \u201cpicturesque lake\u2019 and \u201ccamel fair\u201d. Rest of the day free for leisure activities. Overnight at the hotel.\n\n\n\n\nDay 12 :Pushkar \u2013 Ajmer \u2013 Jaipur (132 Kms / 3 Hrs)\n\n\nThe morning after breakfast transfer to Jaipur. Enroute stop for the worship of saint Khwaja Moinuddin Chishti who came with Muhammad Ghori from Persia in 1192 settled here. Thus the place where he was buried is today known as the Dargah Sharif. Later drive to Jaipur. Evening free for shopping. At night we are set for local cousins, music, and dance at Chokhi Dhani. Overnight stay at Jaipur.\n\n\n\n\nDay 13 :Jaipur \u2013 Delhi Departure (132 Kms / 3 Hrs)\n\n\nThe morning after breakfast, drive to Delhi for your onward journey. Tour ends here.",
    "highlights": [
      "Be a part of Chokhi Dhani includes bamboo acrobatics, a magic show, pottery making, Bhopa-Bhopi dance performances, snake dance, and other activities.",
      "Be a part of the Yellow city Jaisalmer",
      "Visit to Jaisalmer fort (UNESCO site)",
      "Enjoy the calmness of the Gadisar Lake",
      "Jodhpur city sightseeing",
      "Get and hand on the gems of Rajasthan with the Kundan Jewellery",
      "Pay homage at the Ajmer Dargah and Pushkar Lake",
      "Enjoy the grandeur of the Mughals at Fatehpur Sikri"
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
