  "corbett-nainital-tour-package-from-delhi": {
    "overview": "Curious to walk near beautiful lakes and experience nature\u2019s wildlife? See More\n\nThis 4-day Corbett Nainital Tour Package from Delhi is full of adventures and calm atmosphere you\u2019ll remember forever. The journey begins in Nainital, where you\u2019ll explore Naini Lake, shaped like a human eye and people enjoy its magical sunset views.Don\u2019t miss Snow View Point, known for its stunning views of the snow-covered Himalayas. You can also take a Ropeway Ride where clouds pass by and everything below looks small and beautiful, which creates a memorable experience.Now, the tour moves to Jim Corbett National Park, India\u2019s first national park. Animal lovers will have a fantastic time here, with the jungle safari as one of the most exciting part of this trip. If time permits, try to explore the hidden waterfalls, a perfect spot to relax and enjoy the peaceful forest. This Delhi to Corbett and Nainital Travel plan includes transport, hotel stays and guides. Let\u2019s dive into this adventure!See Less\n\nThis 4-day Corbett Nainital Tour Package from Delhi is full of adventures and calm atmosphere you\u2019ll remember forever. The journey begins in Nainital, where you\u2019ll explore Naini Lake, shaped like a human eye and people enjoy its magical sunset views.\n\nDon\u2019t miss Snow View Point, known for its stunning views of the snow-covered Himalayas. You can also take a Ropeway Ride where clouds pass by and everything below looks small and beautiful, which creates a memorable experience.\n\nNow, the tour moves to Jim Corbett National Park, India\u2019s first national park. Animal lovers will have a fantastic time here, with the jungle safari as one of the most exciting part of this trip. If time permits, try to explore the hidden waterfalls, a perfect spot to relax and enjoy the peaceful forest. This Delhi to Corbett and Nainital Travel plan includes transport, hotel stays and guides. Let\u2019s dive into this adventure!",
    "highlights": [
      "Explore Nainital with Naini Lake, Snow View Point, Tiffin Top, boating, and local shopping.",
      "Enjoy charm of nature with its hills, green forests and scenic lakes including Bhimtal, Sattal and Naukuchiatal.",
      "Go on jeep safari in Jim Corbett to spot tigers, elephants, leopards, deer and birds with optional elephant rides.",
      "We take care of transport, hotels and guides, you can also customize your trip with extra tours or longer stays.",
      "See More"
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1: Arrive Delhi- Nainital (315 kms / 7 hours)",
        "description": "Today\u2019s plan-\nWelcome to Delhi! You will be received by My Quick Trippers representatives at the airport or railway station and taken to Nainital, the famous hill station of Kumaon. After reaching, check into your hotel and relax for a while.\nIn the evening get ready to explore the beautiful sights of Nainital-\nNaini Lake-\nThis lake is famous for boating, where you can enjoy a ride on the water (also a popular spot for photos).\nMall Road-\nExplore the local shops known for unique candle designs, herbal jams, and bamboo cloth items.\nOvernight stay at your hotel in Nainital.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 2: In Nainital",
        "description": "Today\u2019s plan-\nStart your day with a delicious breakfast at the hotel.\nLater spend the whole day visiting Nainital\u2019s natural beauty and nearby places-\nTiffin Top\nSnow View Point (Best spot for photos)\nNaini Lake Boating\nMall Road Shopping\nBhimtal\nSattal\nNaukuchiatal\nAfter a day of visiting beautiful spots, return to your hotel in\nNainital\nfor dinner and an overnight stay.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 3: Nainital - Corbett (141 kms / 4 hours)",
        "description": "Today\u2019s plan \u2013\nIn the morning, go and explore the lakes around Nainital.\nSattal \u2013\nSeven beautiful lakes surrounded by nature.\nBhimtal-\nThe biggest lake in the area, surrounded by green pine and oak trees, is perfect for bird lovers. You can see some birds like the Emerald Dove and Tawny Fish Owl.\nNaukuchiatal-\nThe lake has nine corners and pretty views perfect for taking photos.\nAfter visiting the lakes, continue your journey to Corbett National Park and relax at your hotel.\nOptional Activity-\nIn the evening enjoy an optional elephant ride at Corbett (can be arranged directly).\nHave dinner and relax for the night at your hotel in Corbett.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 4: Corbett \u2013 Delhi (255 kms/5-6hrs)",
        "description": "Begin your day in Corbett, breathe the fresh air, and enjoy your final moments in this wonderful place.\nGet ready to explore the beauty of\nCorbett National Park\n-\nJeep Safari at Corbett National Park-\nGo on a jeep ride where you can see wild animals in the forest.\nArrival in Delhi-\nAfter breakfast, our representatives will drop you at the airport or railway station. Your Nainital Jim Corbett package from Delhi ends with happy memories.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      }
    ],
    "faqs": []
  },
  "corbett-nainital-weekend": {
    "overview": "Looking for a quick weekend getaway in North India? My Quick Trippers brings you the fun Corbett Nainital weekend tour package for 4 days and 3 nights. Get in touch with nature and have a rejuvenating experience among the natural beauty. Visit some of the most serene, peaceful and calming destinations in India which are set against the backdrop of the snow-peaked mighty Himalayas. Get yourself some nature therapy with us.\n\nNainital Corbett Weekend Tour Itinerary Package\n\n\nDay 1 :Delhi \u2013 Nainital\n\n\nYou will be made to board the Volvo bus to Nainital, which is going to be an overnight journey of 7 to 8 hours.\n\n\n\n\nDay 2 :Nainital Local Sightseeing\n\n\nEarly in the morning, you will be made to explore the natural beauty of Nainital after your arrival and check in to your allotted hotel here. You will be made to visit the holy temples of Naina Devi Mandir \u2013 the place where Sati\u2019s (Lord Shiva\u2019s consort) eyes had fallen after her death making it one of the vital shakti peeths in India; Hanumangarhi will be your next destination which is dedicated to Lord Hanuman and one of the most popular temples in India.\nThe remainder of your day will be free for you to spend some time exploring interesting places in Nainital on foot including; Naini Lake \u2013 which is a kidney-shaped natural freshwater body where people visit to spend some time doing activities like boating and picnic against the green rolling majestic mountains. You also have the option of traveling on a ropeway to get the best views of the surrounding snowcapped mountain peaks (this will be done on a direct payment basis); you can also take a pony ride up to Naina peak from where you can savor the views of the city of Nainital below. Enjoy a stroll at the mall road.\nYou can shop for local souvenirs like \u2013 exquisite candles, intricately carved wooden artifacts, fresh locally produced apples, cherries and so much more.\nGorge on some of the most delicious food preparations of Nainital like \u2013 aloo ke Gutke (spicy boiled potatoes, Gulgula (a sweet snack), Baadi, Ras (a dish prepared with several Dals) and many more.\n\n\n\n\nDay 3 :Nainital \u2013 Corbett\n\n\nEarly in the morning, you will be taken on an excursion of the nearby lake attractions of Sattal (a group of 7 lakes) and the popular jade green Garud Lake. You will also be taken to Bhimtal and Naukuchiatal all of which are located extremely close to Nainital with only at a distance of half an hour to 45 mines. After this exciting sightseeing, you will be escorted to Corbett, where upon arrival you will be checked in to your hotel. You have the option of enjoying an elephant ride here (which can be hired directly thereon direct payment basis), you will also be taken to Girija Devi Mandir. The evening time will be saved for a DJ night party along with a delicious dinner.\n\n\n\n\nDay 4 :Corbett \u2013 Delhi Departure\n\n\nYou will be made to depart for Delhi after breakfast, which will be a 6.5 hours long road journey. You will be dropped at Delhi airport from where you will be free to head on to your desired destination.",
    "highlights": [],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1 :Delhi \u2013 Nainital",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 2 :Nainital Local Sightseeing",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 3 :Nainital \u2013 Corbett",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 4 :Corbett \u2013 Delhi Departure",
        "description": ""
      }
    ],
    "faqs": []
  },
