    "itinerary": [],
    "faqs": []
  },
  "darjeeling-gangtok-tour": {
    "overview": "Darjeeling and Gangtok are both situated at a height but are dissimilar. While Darjeeling has overtones of colonial legacy mixed with Hindu and Buddhist cultures, Gangtok is quintessentially Buddhist. Visit Gangtok and it seems as if you time has stood still. Sample the best of both in a 4 Nights and 5 Days Darjeeling Gangtok Holiday. A typical itinerary would be as follows:\n\nDarjeeling Gangtok Tour Itinerary Package\n\n\nDay 1 :Bagdogra/New Jalpaiguri \u2013 Gangtok\n\n\nFly into Bagdogra airport or arrive at the New Jalpaiguri railway station and our My Quick Trippers representative welcomes you and takes you along with other members of the group to Gangtok. The Sun is low when you arrive and this gives you time to refresh yourself and then take a stroll through the local marketplace. Stay overnight in your hotel room, the air fragrant with incense from the many temples around.\n\n\n\n\nDay 2 :Gangtok Sightseeing\n\n\nEnjoy a typical Sikkim breakfast and then set out to see the sights. You start with Tsomgo Lake in East Sikkim, which may be covered with ice depending on the weather and the season. After that you visit the Baba Harbhajan Temple and then go on to the Nathu La Pass from where you have a glimpse of the Chinese border. The view from a height of 4310 metres is simply astounding. You might also cherish the fact that you are standing on the famous Silk Route. Visit to the Nathu Pass depends on the day you arrive and on the Indian Army granting a pass since it is closed in winter and on Mondays and Tuesdays. Anyway, NamasteIndiaTrip takes care of the necessary permissions. After the soul-lifting visit to the Pass, the group returns to the hotel for rest. You could explore the monasteries like the Enchey Monastery to get a taste of Tibetan culture if you have the time.\n\n\n\n\nDay 3 :Gangtok \u2013 Darjeeling\n\n\nA hearty breakfast refreshes you for the onward trip to Darjeeling over scenic countryside. Check into your room and then relax or stroll along the Mall. If you like you can go for a ride on the Toy train and then buy something from the local markets to remember your trip.\n\n\n\n\nDay 4 :Darjeeling Sightseeing\n\n\nRise at 3 AM and set off for Tiger Hill. You and hundreds of other tourists wait with bated breath for the Sunrise over Kanchenjunga. This is one of the most beautiful sights as the white peaks slowly turn pink and then gold as the Sun puts in an appearance, bathing the entire area in a golden glow. On your return, you stop at the Ghoom Monastery and have a dekko at Batasia Loop. After lunch it is time to visit the Himalayan Mountaineering Institute, the Zoological Gardens, take a ride on the Ropeway and visit the Happy Valley Tea Estate to sample and buy fine Darjeeling tea. Round off the day with a visit to the Japanese Temple, the Peace Pagoda and the Gombu Rock. Rest for the night in your room.\n\n\n\n\nDay 5 :Jalpaiguri/Bagdogra\n\n\nTour ends after breakfast and you are assisted for your New Jalpaiguri/Bagdogra travel for return home.",
    "highlights": [
      "Enjoy the Gangtok sightseeing",
      "Visit the Baba Harbhajan Temple",
      "Pass through the Nathula pass",
      "Darjeeling welcoming",
      "Ghoom Monastery, Batasia Loop, Himalayan Mountaineering Institute, Zoological Gardens, Ropeway ride, and Happy Valley Tea Estate to sample and purchase fine Darjeeling tea.",
      "Visit to the Japanese Temple, the Peace Pagoda, and the Gombu Rock."
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1 :Bagdogra/New Jalpaiguri \u2013 Gangtok",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 2 :Gangtok Sightseeing",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 3 :Gangtok \u2013 Darjeeling",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 4 :Darjeeling Sightseeing",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 5 :Jalpaiguri/Bagdogra",
        "description": ""
      }
    ],
    "faqs": []
  },
  "darjeeling-heritage-tour": {
    "overview": "Darjeeling is a popular scenic hill resort in India and also a popular tourist destination due to its natural beauty and pleasant climate, which is set against the majestic snow-capped Himalayan peaks. Kanchenjunga, the world's third highest peak, can be seen from the town on a clear day. Avoid the months of June, July, and August, as well as December and January. Darjeeling has a plethora of options for those seeking an adrenaline rush. Red pandas, rhododendron blooms, and high-altitude trekking can all be found in Singalila National Park. Due to the park's lack of dangerous animals and snakes, it is the most popular family camping destination in the eastern Himalayas.\n\nDarjeeling Heritage Tour Itinerary Package\n\n\nDay 1 :Darjeeling\n\n\nArrive at the Darjeeling railway station or fly into the Jolly Grant and be received graciously by our My Quick Trippers representative who then takes you to the designated hotel. You can refresh and relax for the day. You might like to go out in the late afternoon for a walk through the Mall or enjoy a ride on the Toy Train, an experience not to be missed. Spend the evening sampling wares in the bazaars and local cuisines. Retire a bit early because you will be woken up quite early the next day.\n\n\n\n\nDay 2 :Darjeeling Sightseeing\n\n\n3 AM and it is time to wake up and depart for the Tiger Hill. God willing the skies will be clear and you will be able to watch one of the most magnificent spectacles, which is the sunrise over the Kanchenjunga Peaks. The sight is truly awesome as the snow-covered peaks take on crimson-rosy hues and then the sun puts in an appearance. After this the other sights can be a bit of a letdown but cheer up, there are interesting things in store. You go on to the Himalayan Mountaineering Institute to admire memorabilia and learn how people scale peaks. Then it is time for a visit to the Zoological Gardens and its mix of amazing flora and fauna. With so little time available you have to move on to the Dhirdham temple and then it is a ropeway ride with the valley below offering a lovely spectacle. Towards evening you take a walk through the Happy Valley Tea Estate, sample fresh tea and buy some to take home. The day finishes with a trip to the Peace Pagoda, the Japanese temple and the Lebong Racecourse as well as Tenzing. Rest for the night.\n\n\n\n\nDay 3 :Departure\n\n\nEnjoy a leisurely breakfast and then, if you like, the tour representative helps you on to the railway station. You may, of course, want to stay back and explore Darjeeling on your own.",
    "highlights": [
      "The famous Toy train ride",
      "Visit to the Mall road",
      "Magnificent sunrise view of the Kanchenjunga peaks",
      "Visit to the Himalayan Mountaineering Institute for learning how to trek and some fun",
      "Be a part of the flora and fauna at the Zoological garden",
      "A tour of the Dhirdham Temple, followed by a ropeway ride with a beautiful view of the valley below.",
      "A walk through the Happy Tea Estate",
      "Finishing the tour at the Tenzing, the Peace Pagoda, the Japanese temple, and the Lebong Racecourse"
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1 :Darjeeling",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 2 :Darjeeling Sightseeing",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 3 :Departure",
        "description": ""
      }
    ],
    "faqs": []
  },
  "darjeeling-honeymoon-package": {
    "overview": "Popularly known as \u201cQueen of Hills\u201d, Darjeeling is one of the most eminent holiday destinations of almost every travel enthusiast. The breathtaking views of the mountains, picturesque surroundings, beautiful monasteries, and panoramic landscapes take Darjeeling tourism a notch higher.\n\nThis gorgeous hill station is blessed with steep mountain ridges bestowed with lush green tea plantations and offers you mesmerizing views of the sunrise from snow-peaked mountains.\nGangtok, the capital city of Sikkim, leaves every traveler awestruck and spellbound with its impeccable spiritual aura and tremendous scenic vista. The city boasts of various exciting tourist places where travelers from far around the country visit and feel immensely astonished with the views of Kanchenjunga, the third highest mountain peak in the world. It happens to be one of the best places to start your newly married life with positivity and love.\nOn this 5 nights and 6 days long Darjeeling honeymoon package you will be provided with enough time and opportunity to witness the glory and charm of these cities and can enjoy some really amazing and romantic moments with your family and friends. On this honeymoon trip, My Quick Trippers will provide you great services and facilities that include transportation, food, a cozy and comfy stay, and many more.\n\nThis gorgeous hill station is blessed with steep mountain ridges bestowed with lush green tea plantations and offers you mesmerizing views of the sunrise from snow-peaked mountains.",
    "highlights": [
      "Shopping and trying out local cuisines at the mall (Bagdogra/New Jalpaiguri).",
      "Sunrise at Tiger hill.",
      "Complete guided Darjeeling excursion including visit to Ghoom Monastery, Batasia Loop, and Japanese Temple etc.",
      "Driving through the scenic mountain roads from Darjeeling to Gangtok.",
      "Half day trip in Gangtok to Hanuman Tok, Rumtek Monastery, Tashi view point etc.",
      "Eating delicious traditional Tibetan meals.",
      "Visit to Tsomgo Lake in East Sikkim.",
      "Adventure activities like visit to Nathula Pass (ancient silk route)."
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1 :New Jalpaiguri / Bagdogra - Darjeeling",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 2 :Darjeeling Excursions",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 3 :Darjeeling Local Excursions",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
