  "dharamshala-weekend-tour": {
    "overview": "Sitting peacefully in the district of Kangra Dharamshala is one of the most sought after tourist destinations in Himachal for a quick weekend getaway from the hustle and bustle of the city life. Our Dharamshala Weekend Tour Package which lasts for 4 days and 3 nights will take you on a soulful journey across some of the most picturesque avenues and panoramic vistas. Explore this breathtaking destination and take away with you a lifetime worth of memories.\n\nDharamshala Weekend Tour Itinerary Package\n\n\nDay 1 :Delhi \u2013 Arrival in Dharamshala\n\n\nYour journey to Dharamshala will commence once you are made to board the bus heading towards this vibrant and peaceful hamlet. This is a journey of 12 hours which means that you will be spending the night on the bus.\n\n\n\n\nDay 2 :Arrival in Dharamshala (Local Sightseeing)\n\n\nEarly in the morning, you will be reaching the beautiful hill town of Mcleodganj after which you will be made to freshen up after which your sightseeing tour will commence. The sightseeing destinations here will include visits to \u2013 Bhagsunag temple and Dalai Lama temple which are set against a lush green backdrop of green covering and a cascading set of waterfall. Once your sightseeing comes to an end, by evening, you will be free to explore the wonderful hill station that is Dharamshala on your own. You will be taken to your allotted hotel for an overnight stay here.\n\n\n\n\nDay 3 :Dharamshala Sightseeing\n\n\nAfter having your breakfast in the morning your sightseeing of Dharamshala will continue, where you will be covering places of interests like \u2013 war memorial, Kangra art museum, Chinmaya Tapovan Ashram, Norbulingka Institute, doll museum, tea garden, Chamunda Devi Temple and the highest cricket ground in India \u2013 HPCA stadium. Finally, after a day of stunning sightseeing expeditions, you will be assisted back to your hotel for an overnight stay.\n\n\n\n\nDay 4 :Dharamshala Departure \u2013 New Delhi\n\n\nAfter having our breakfast in the morning, your half the day is free for you to shop for local and authentic souvenirs by strolling through the mall road. By evening as the time for your departure approaches, you will be assisted to the bus stop and made to board the bus heading onwards to New Delhi, a journey of 12 hours where you will be spending the night in the bus.",
    "highlights": [],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1 :Delhi \u2013 Arrival in Dharamshala",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 2 :Arrival in Dharamshala (Local Sightseeing)",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 3 :Dharamshala Sightseeing",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 4 :Dharamshala Departure \u2013 New Delhi",
