  "discover-majestic-rajasthan": {
    "overview": "Fairy tale castles and intimidating forts may be found across this area, along with endearing folk songs that celebrate life and love and bright costumes that stand out against the arid, bleak landscape and shifting sands.\n\nRajasthan stands out, though, as a place whose energy and excitement have remained constant over time. See how the dunes catch the last rays of the setting sun as you travel through a golden city and arrive at your destination for the night in the desert. Let the white, blue, and pink cities unveil their own legends, traditions, and civilizations that have been developed over many years as you take in the serene lake lapping them. With this 6 days / 5 nights tour you will experience the best of all the fairy tale experience of royal Rajasthan.\n\nRajasthan stands out, though, as a place whose energy and excitement have remained constant over time. See how the dunes catch the last rays of the setting sun as you travel through a golden city and arrive at your destination for the night in the desert. Let the white, blue, and pink cities unveil their own legends, traditions, and civilizations that have been developed over many years as you take in the serene lake lapping them. With this 6 days / 5 nights tour you will experience the best of all the fairy tale experience of royal Rajasthan.\n\nMajestic Rajasthan Tour Itinerary Package\n\n\nDay 1 :Jaipur Arrival\n\n\nWelcome to you in \u2018Pink City\u2019! Arrive at Airport / Railway Station in Jaipur and transfer to your hotel. On arrival check-in into your hotel. Overnight stay at Jaipur. Rajasthan\u2019s beautiful Pink City Jaipur was the stronghold of a clan of rulers whose three hill forts and series of palaces in the city are important attractions. Known as the Pink City because of the color of the stone used exclusively in the walled city, Jaipur\u2019s bazaars sell embroidered leather shoes, blue pottery, tie and dye scarves and other exotic wares. Western Rajasthan itself forms a convenient circuit, in the heart of the Thar Desert which has shaped its history, lifestyles and architecture.\n\n\n\n\nDay 2 :Jaipur City Tour\n\n\nThis morning, after breakfast, visits the ancient capital of the Kachwaha Rajputs, Amer. One can take an elephant ride or the jeep ride up to the fort. Thereafter, enjoy a photo-stop at Hawa Mahal \u2013 the Palace of Winds. Later, visit the City Palace and the apartment housing museums with an array of textiles, costumes, arms, weapons and paintings and finally visit Jantar Mantar, the observatory built by Maharaja Jai Singh-II. The founder of Jantar Mantar is Maharaja Jai Singh II, he had built Jantar Mantar in five different locations of India, out of which Jantar Mantar at Jaipur is the largest. The observatories, or \u2018Jantar Mantar\u2019 as they are commonly known, incorporate multiple buildings of unique form, each with a specialized function for astronomical measurement.\nLater you are free to enjoy shopping in the local market. The market of Jaipur will delight you with the exotic blue pottery, the batik painting, block printed textiles of Sanganer and Bagru, tie and dye fabrics, Mojari \u2013 (the local shoe), sandalwood carving items, beautiful stone carvings etc.\n\n\n\n\nDay 3 :Jaipur \u2013 Jodhpur (335 km/8 hrs)\n\n\nFrom Jaisalmer transfer to Jodhpur and check into the hotel on arrival. Rest of the day at leisure. Overnight stay at the hotel.\n\n\n\n\nDay 4 :Jodhpur \u2013 Udaipur (295 km/6.5 hrs)\n\n\nJodhpur sightseeing tour visiting Umaid Bhawan Palace, Mehrangarh Fort, Mandore Garden and Jaswant Thada. Afternoon proceeds to Udaipur and overnight stay at the hotel.\n\n\n\n\nDay 5 :Udaipur Sightseeing\n\n\nTake a full day sightseeing tour and visit the City Palace, Saheliyon ki Badi, Maharana Pratap Smarak and Pear Hill. Overnight stay at the hotel.\n\n\n\n\nDay 6 :Udaipur Departure\n\n\nToday after breakfast we will drop you railway station/ Airport for your onward journey.",
    "highlights": [
      "A full coverage of the best three cities of the Land of Kings",
      "Enjoying the forts and places of the cities of Jaipur, Jodhpur and Udaipur",
      "Trying out the local delicacies",
      "Best hotel accommodations and the best facilities available for the tour"
    ],
    "itinerary": [
