  "do-dham-yatra-by-helicopter": {
    "overview": "Badrinath and Kedarnath are highly sacred temples in Hinduism. If you're thinking of visiting these temples in a comfortable way, without the physical stresses, then book the Do Dham Yatra by Helicopter 2026. In this tour plan, our team will take care of your meals, ground transfers, VIP Darshan, helipad assistance, and more. Get in touch to know more about our custom plans! See More\n\nThe journey to Badrinath and Kedarnath by helicopter will begin from Sahastradhara Helipad in Dehradun. From here, you'll be taken to the Kedarnath Helipad first. After Darshan at Kedarnath, you fly to Badrinath Helipad. From there, it's a short walk to the Badrinath temple. Finally, you'll be taken back to the Sahastradhara Helipad in Dehradun, concluding your Do Dham journey.\nWhy Start the Do Dham Yatra by Helicopter?\nStarting the Do Dham package by helicopter is the best option for time-saving ways to visit the Kedarnath and Badrnath temples. This option is helpful for visitors who want to complete this journey without any challenges due to long treks and mountainous road travel. \nMainly a helicopter journey reduces time to complete the sacred pilgrimage within one day instead of several days by road. It is comfortable for elderly pilgrims, families as well as for those who have limited time and wish to take blessings of these holy shrines. With organized arrangements, priority darshan, and smooth transfers, the helicopter option ensures a safe, comfortable, and well-managed pilgrimage experience for devotees undertaking the Do Dham Yatra. \nHow to Reach Dehradun / Sahastradhara Helipad\nSahastradhara Helipad is the starting and ending point of the Do Dham helicopter Yatra. Here's how to reach Dehradun from major cities:\n\n\n\nFrom City\nBy Air\nBy Train\nBy Road\n\n\n\n\nDelhi\n1 hr flight to Jolly Grant Airport, Dehradun\nShatabdi/Jan Shatabdi: 5\u20136 hrs to Dehradun station\n~300 km | 6\u20137 hrs via NH-58\n\n\nMumbai\n2 hrs direct flight to Jolly Grant Airport\nNo direct train \u2014 connect via Delhi\nNot practical\n\n\nBangalore\n2.5\u20133 hrs direct or via Delhi\nNo direct train \u2014 connect via Delhi\nNot practical\n\n\nKolkata\n3 hrs via Delhi\nNo direct \u2014 connect via Delhi\nNot practical\n\n\n\nJolly Grant Airport (Dehradun) to Sahastradhara Helipad: approximately 20\u201325 km by road, takes 45\u201360 minutes. Cab services and prepaid taxis are available outside the airport.\nDo Dham Helicopter Package Cost\nThe Do Dham Helicopter tour cost is INR 1,35,000 per person. This same day Kedarnath Badrinath by helicopter plan covers your meals, accommodation, transfers, ground handling, and VIP Darshans. You also get full assistance at the helipads.\nNote: Price is per adult. Children above 2 years are charged at full adult fare as per terms.\nWe also offer customised plans, where you can tweak the trip duration and even add sightseeing destinations. Multi-day options are available \u2014 overnight stay at Kedarnath or Badrinath can be arranged on request. Contact our team for customised itineraries.\nTemple Darshan Timings\n\n\n\nTemple\nMorning Darshan Opens\nAfternoon Break\nEvening Darshan\nCloses\n\n\n\n\nKedarnath\n4:00 AM (Abhishek)\n1:00 PM \u2013 5:00 PM\n5:00 PM \u2013 7:00 PM\n7:00 PM\n\n\nBadrinath\n4:30 AM (Abhishek)\n1:00 PM \u2013 4:00 PM\n4:00 PM \u2013 9:00 PM\n9:00 PM\n\n\n\nFor helicopter visitors: Arriving between 8\u201311 AM gives the best Darshan window at both temples. The afternoon break at both temples (1 PM onwards) means planning your landing times carefully is important. VIP Darshan passes included in the package help skip regular queues but the temple still follows its schedule.\nDo Dham Opening and Closing Dates\nHere are the opening and closing dates of Badrinath and Kedarnath:\n\n\n\nDham\nOpening Date 2026\nClosing Date 2026\nClosing Festival\n\n\n\n\nBadrinath Temple\n23 April 2026\n13 November 2026 (Tentative)\n1-2 weeks after Diwali\n\n\nKedarnath Temple\n22 April 2026\n11 November 2026 (Tentative)\nBhai Dooj (2 days after Diwali)\n\n\n\nPassenger Guidelines\n\nFollow the instructions given by the pilot and ground staff.\nEach flight carries 6 passengers and 1 crew.\nDo not approach the helicopter from the rear.\nAdhere to the baggage limit (maximum 5 kg).\nReport your body weight correctly. The maximum weight limit for a person is 75\u201380 kg.\nKeep 1\u20132 buffer days in your itinerary as flight delays are common due to bad weather.\nDo not touch the helicopter parts. Always maintain a safe distance from helicopter rotors at all times.\nTotal payload capacity is 420 kg for 6 passengers (as per Terms & Conditions).\nChildren above 2 years of age are treated as full-fare adult passengers \u2014 no concession on ticket price or weight allowance.\n\nWeight Limits\n\n\n\nCategory\nWeight Limit\nImportant Notes\n\n\n\n\nPassenger Body Weight\n75\u201380 kg per person\nExact limit depends on helicopter type and operator. Passengers exceeding limit may be offloaded \u2014 declare weight honestly at booking.\n\n\nLuggage Allowance\n3\u20135 kg per person\nOnly soft bags (duffel/backpack) permitted. No hard suitcases.\n\n\nTotal Payload (6 pax)\n420 kg maximum\nPilot has final authority to offload passengers if combined weight exceeds limit. No refund for de-boarding due to incorrect weight.\n\n\nChildren (above 2 yrs)\nFull adult ticket\nNo concession. Child's weight is included in total payload calculation.\n\n\n\nAltitude & Health: What Helicopter Pilgrims Should Know\nKedarnath sits at 3,583 m and Badrinath at 3,100 m. Even by helicopter, you will be at these altitudes for 1\u20133 hours. Altitude sickness (AMS) is a real risk even for helicopter visitors.\nSymptoms to watch: persistent headache, nausea, dizziness, breathlessness at rest, confusion. If any of these appear at the temple \u2014 inform our ground staff immediately. Do not ignore symptoms hoping they'll pass.\n\n\n\nCondition\nRisk Level\nOur Recommendation\n\n\n\n\nHeart conditions (BP, angina, pacemaker)\nHigh\nMandatory doctor clearance before booking. Inform us at the time of booking.\n\n\nAsthma / COPD\nModerate\u2013High\nConsult pulmonologist. Carry prescribed inhaler. Supplemental oxygen may be needed.\n\n\nDiabetes\nModerate\nCarry medicines, glucose tablets. Altitude affects blood sugar levels.\n\n\nAge 70+ with no high-altitude history\nModerate\nMedical certificate recommended. Start with light acclimatisation if possible.\n\n\nPregnant women (2nd/3rd trimester)\nHigh\nNot recommended above 3,000 m. Consult OB/GYN before booking.\n\n\n\nBest Time to Visit\nThe best time to visit Badrinath and Kedarnath is in two windows: May\u2013June and September\u2013October. The weather in these windows is quite pleasant, and therefore, makes for a comfortable time to go on temple tours and even indulge in sightseeing in the nearby areas. \nAvoid going in the monsoon season (July\u2013August) as the heavy rainfall makes the road slippery and accident-prone. Plus, there's an additional risk of landslides. Even for helicopter pilgrims, monsoon means frequent flight cancellations due to cloud cover and low visibility. May\u2013June booking is recommended for first-time visitors. \nAnd in the winters (November\u2013April), the temples remain closed, and Darshan is not possible. \nDo Dham Yatra Significance\nThe Do Dham Yatra holds great spiritual significance in Hinduism. It is believed that whoever completes this pilgrimage has their sins cleansed and moves towards moksha.\nSpiritual Significance of Kedarnath\n\nThis is also one of the 12 Jyotirlingas of Lord Shiva. \nThis is the place where Pandavas sought the blessing of Lord Shiva for atonement of their sins accumulated during the Mahabharata war. \nBeing located at a very high height, the Kedarnath Yatra is seen as a test of faith and endurance. \nKedarnath also forms part of the Panch Kedar circuit \u2014 the five sacred abodes of Lord Shiva in Garhwal. The other four are Tungnath, Rudranath, Madhyamaheshwar, and Kalpeshwar. \n\nSpiritual Significance of Badrinath\n\nDedicated to Lord Vishnu, this temple is a part of both the Chhota and Bada Dham circuit. \nIt's also one of the 108 Divya Desams. \nIt's believed that thousands of years ago, Lord Vishnu meditated here. \nBadrinath is the most significant of the four Char Dhams and is traditionally the final stop of the Char Dham Yatra sequence. The Badrivishal idol here is a Shaligram (black stone) idol \u2014 one of the most ancient in all of India. \n\nAccommodation Guide\nKedarnath accommodation is only available if overnight stay is booked separately. Same-day helicopter package does not include Kedarnath stay \u2014 only Badrinath overnight option exists in standard package. \n\n\n\nLocation\nBest For\nAccommodation Options\nKey Note\n\n\n\n\nDehradun / Sahastradhara\nPre-Yatra stay, helipad boarding\nLuxury: JW Marriott, Lemon Tree, Four Points by Sheraton | Mid-range: Hotel Pacific, The Landmark | Budget: Hotel Ajanta, Madhuban\nStay near Sahastradhara Helipad for easy early-morning departure\n\n\nKedarnath\nTemple Darshan overnight stay\nGMVN & ITBP dorms, local guesthouses, tented camps\nStandard same-day package does NOT include Kedarnath stay. Overnight must be requested as add-on.\n\n\nBadrinath\nPost-Darshan rest / overnight\nGMVN Tourist Rest House, Hotel Vasundhara, budget hotels & Dharamshalas\nBadrinath has better facilities than Kedarnath \u2014 deluxe options available\n\n\n\nWhat to Pack\n\n\n\nCategory\nItems to Carry\n\n\n\n\nLuggage\nSoft duffle bag only | Small backpack\n\n\nClothing\nThermal innerwear, Full-sleeve T-shirts, Woollen sweater, Windproof jacket, Trek pants, Woollen cap, gloves, Socks\n\n\nFootwear\nComfortable walking shoes with good grip | Lightweight slippers\n\n\nMedicines\nPersonal medicines, First-aid kit, ORS, Diamox (after doctor consultation)\n\n\nPersonal Care\nSunscreen SPF 50+, Lip balm, Moisturiser, Hand sanitizer\n\n\nDocuments\nGovernment photo ID, Helicopter booking confirmation, Yatra registration slip\n\n\nPuja Items\nSmall puja thali, flowers, Chandan, Kumkum, Akshat (rice), coconut, prasad items. Temple priests are available for puja but carrying basic items is recommended for personal puja.\n\n\n\nPayment & Cancellation Policy\nPayment Policy:\n\nAdvance payment of 50% of total package cost to confirm booking.\nRemaining 50% to be paid at least 15 days before departure.\nPayment methods: NEFT, UPI, or Debit/Credit Card.\nDelay in payment may result in cancellation of booking.\nAfter successful payment, a booking confirmation will be sent via email and WhatsApp within 24 hours. This confirmation must be carried to the helipad.\n\nCancellation/Refund Policy:\n\n30+ days before departure: 75% refund\n15\u201329 days before departure: 50% refund\n7\u201314 days before departure: 25% refund\nLess than 7 days before departure: 0% refund\n\nWeather cancellation policy: If flight is cancelled by the operator due to bad weather, a complimentary rescheduling to the next available date is offered. If rescheduling is not acceptable, 90% refund is processed (10% retained as administrative charge). This policy applies only to operator-initiated cancellations.\n\n\nWhat to Do in Bad Weather\nThe content here is mostly practical and good. One addition needed \u2014 concrete rescue/refund protocol: \n\nIf your flight is delayed, stay calm and don't panic.\nFollow the instructions of the pilot. If they decide to delay or cancel the flight, comply. Safety is of utmost importance.\nStay in touch with your tour coordinator or helipad manager for updates.\nStay warm and keep yourself hydrated.\nCarry extra food for delays caused by bad weather.\nDo not insist on flying in bad weather.\nDo not look for new helicopter bookings during delays.\nBe patient. Mountain weather often clears in early mornings.\nIf stranded overnight due to weather: Our coordinator will arrange accommodation at the nearest available facility. Additional hotel cost incurred due to force majeure is borne by the passenger as per terms.\nEmergency contact: Always save the emergency helpline \u2014 Uttarakhand Disaster Helpline: 1077 | SDRF: 112\n\nHelipads for Do Dham Yatra by Helicopter\nHere is the information about Kedarnath Badrinath helicopter helipad locations, their features, and more. \nSahastradhara Helipad Dehradun\nIt is located in Dehradun and is the main operational base for helicopter flights headed towards Badrinath & Kedarnath. It is an important part of the Do Dham helicopter Yatra itinerary. \n\nThis is the gateway hub for the Do Dham as well as Char Dham Yatra.\nIt is located close to Dehradun's Jolly Grant Airport, which is very well-connected to cities like Delhi, Mumbai, Bangalore, and Kolkata. This makes Sahastradhara helipad an ideal point for starting the aerial journey.\nIt is located at lower altitude than Kedarnath and Badrinath, and therefore, offers much more reliable and safer takeoffs and landings.\nIt can handle large passenger traffic.\nIt is easily accessible from both the temple and the city centre.\n\nKedarnath Helipad\n\nThe helipad is located just 500\u2013700 metres away from the temple.\nYou can reach the temple from the helipad by a short walk.\nPassengers must go through security checks before boarding.\nPilgrims are required to follow DGCA guidelines.\nThere are 3 helipads serving Kedarnath \u2014 Phata (~12 km), Sirsi (~14 km), and Guptkashi (~30 km). The operator assigns the helipad based on slot availability. All three require a government shuttle to reach the Kedarnath helipad landing zone.\n\nBadrinath Helipad\nThis is the official helipad for the Badrinath Yatra. This is one of the most widely used helipad in Do Dham Yatra and offers the pilgrims a fast & comfortable way to reach the temple. \n\nIt's located just a short drive from the temple.\nSecurity screening is mandatory at this helipad.\nPassengers are required to strictly follow crew instructions for boarding and de-boarding.\nWheelchair assistance can also be arranged on request.\n\nSee Less",
    "highlights": [
      "Exciting helicopter ride",
      "VIP darshan experience",
      "Additional sightseeing in Badrinath",
      "Stay in luxury accommodation",
      "Smooth transfers in car",
      "See More"
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1: Dehradun (Sahastradhara Helipad) \u2013 Kedarnath \u2013 Badrinath",
        "description": "The helipad is located at a distance of one km from the temple. We have arranged for our car service, which is a part of your Do Dham Yatra by Helicopter, to take you to the temple once you deboard the helicopter. Know that our hospitable staff will always assist you with anything you require in enjoying a wonderful Darshan.\n[07:00 am Departure Sahastradhara Helipad \u2013 Dehradun]\nSame Day: Kedarnath\n[08:00 am Arrival Kedarnath via Phata/Sitapur shuttle]\nOn our way to Kedarnath from Dehradun Helipad, we will change our helicopter service once at Phata/Sitapur. This is in congruence with the government regulation insisting on the shift to shuttle service of about eight minutes to take one quite close to the temple premises. Our staff will help you in enjoying a blissful Darshan of Lord Kedarnath.\nWe will provide you with the VIP Darshan that will let you have Darshan without having to stand in long queues. Please know that this incurs no additional costs from you as our package is inclusive of the VIP passes.\nThe whimsical moods of Mother Nature at Kedarnath is quite famous. One is therefore advised to finish the darshan within 1.5 hours and return to the helipad.\n[09:45 am Departure Kedarnath Helipad]\nSame Day: Badrinath\n[10:30 am Arrival Badrinath]\n[01:00 pm Departure from Badrinath]\nWe have arranged for ground assistance and temple transfer to ensure a smooth Darshan experience. You will have time for Tapt Kund visit and nearby sightseeing before departure.\n[01:40 pm Arrival Dehradun (Sahastradhara Helipad)]\nWe have successfully finished the pilgrimage to two of the holiest shrines in India within a day. The pilgrimage is set to end around 1:40 pm with our helicopter landing you safely near the Dehradun helipad.\nPlaces You'll See"
      }
    ],
    "faqs": []
  },
  "do-dham-yatra-gangotri-yamunotri": {
    "overview": "Set out on the Gangotri Yamunotri Do Dham Yatra \u2014 one of the most peaceful and spiritually rewarding pilgrimages in Devbhoomi Uttarakhand. This journey takes you to two of the holiest shrines in the Garhwal Himalayas.\n\nThe Yamunotri Gangotri Yatra Package from Delhi involves a spiritual quest to two sacred destinations, Gangotri and Yamunotri. Whether you're a nature lover, spiritual enthusiast, solo traveler, or someone traveling with your family, we offer various packages that cater to your budget and needs. We offer budget, premium, and helicopter packages as we understand our clients' preferences. With years of experience in the industry, we have built a reputation for transparency and trustworthiness. You can also explore the nearby locations and enjoy various interesting activities with our Yamunotri Gangotri Do Dham Yatra Package from Delhi. Contact us now to have an unforgettable Do Dham Yatra experience and appreciate the enchanting beauty of the Himalaya. \nHow to Plan Your Do Dham Tour?\nPlanning your GangotriYamunotri Yatra is important to have a smooth yet fulfilling Yatra experience. You first need to decide on your budget, select a travel date, plan your itinerary, and check weather conditions before embarking on the Yatra. You also need to be physically fit for the pilgrimage.\nBest Time for Do Dham Yatra\nSeptember to mid-October and May-June are considered to be the best times to visit Yamunotri and Gangotri, as the roads are easy to travel and the weather is pleasant. In the summer months, the average temperature ranges between 10 and 20 degrees Celsius, which is ideal for visiting the temples and sightseeing.\nMonsoon (July-August) is not a good time to visit Do Dham due to the chances of heavy rainfalls that may result in slippery roads and landslides. This makes traveling a bit dangerous. The autumn season is a good time to visit Gangotri and Yamunotri due to clear, and a calm pilgrimage experience.\nDuring winters (November to April), both the shrines are closed due to heavy snowfall and adverse weather conditions.\nGangotri Yamunotri Opening Date for 2026\n\nYamunotri Opening Date 2026: 19 April 2026 (Akshaya Tritiya)\nGangotri Opening Date 2026: 19 April 2026 (Akshaya Tritiya)\nYamunotri Closing Date 2026: 11 November 2026 (Tentative)\nGangotri Closing Date 2026: 10 November 2026 (Tentative)\n\nNote: Yatra season is short - April to November only. Book in advance.\nCost of Do Dham Yatra 2026\nThe Do Dham Yatra package cost will vary depending on the package you select, the amenities you choose, the activities you undertake, and the season when you decide to travel to these sacred sites. On average, the Yatra will cost you around INR 20,000 to INR 60,000.\nGangotri Yamunotri Route and Yatra Distance\nThe distance between Gangotri and Yamunotri is around 228 km. It includes a 6 km trek to Yamunotri from Janki Chatti. The distance from Gangotri to Janki Chatti by road is around 222 kilometers. It will take around 6-8 hours to complete this journey.\nHaridwar \u2192 Barkot: ~210 km, 6-7 hrs\nBarkot \u2192 Janki Chatti (Yamunotri trek base): 45 km, 1.5-2 hrs\nJanki Chatti \u2192 Yamunotri (trek): 5-6 km, 2-3 hrs\nBarkot \u2192 Uttarkashi: 82 km, 3-4 hrs\nUttarkashi \u2192 Gangotri: 100 km, 3.5-4.5 hrs\nTrekking Guide\nYou do not need to trek to reach Gangotri as the temple is easily accessible by road. From Janki Chatti, you will have to undertake a 6 km trek to Yamunotri. The trek is of moderate difficulty and steep. If you do not want to trek, you can opt for Pitthu (human porter who carries you on a backpack chair), Palkis, and ponies.\nYou're advised to commence the trekking journey early in the morning so that you can return before dusk.\nWhat to Pack\nClothing Essentials\n\nShirts: 2/3, Pants: 2\nFull-sleeve Woollen sweater\nThe windproof jacket with a hood\nWoollen cap, socks (3-4 pairs), gloves\nThermal inner wear\nRaincoat\n\nFootwear\n\nWaterproof and comfortable shoes with a good grip\nLightweight slippers\n\nOther Essentials\n\nWater bottle - 1 Litres\nSunglasses, Trekking pole, Walking stick\nCap / Hat\nLip Balm, Sunscreen Lotion\nTorch / Flashlight (with extra batteries)\nHand Sanitizer\nPersonal toiletries\nSmall day bag / fanny pack for trek day (for ID, cash, snacks on Yamunotri trek)\nMobile phones with a charger\nPrinted Yatra registration e-pass (mandatory - carry throughout journey)\n\nMedical Kit\n\nAvil 25mg (allergies)\nDiamox (to prevent altitude sickness)\nDigene (acidity)\nCombiflam (Pain killer)\nNorflox TZ (diarrhea)\nAvomine (motion sickness)\nKnee Cap\nCrocin (fever)\nCotton, Crepe Bandage\nMoov spray\nBetadine\nBand-aid\nGauze\n\nBoth Yamunotri (3,293m) and Gangotri (3,100m) are at high altitude. Pilgrims coming from plains cities may experience altitude sickness - headache, nausea, dizziness, or breathlessness.\nPrevent it: drink 3-4 litres of water daily, walk slowly, rest on your first day at each base town. If symptoms don't improve within 30 minutes of rest, descend immediately.\nMedical aid posts are available at Janki Chatti, along the Yamunotri trek route, and at Gangotri. Senior pilgrims and those with heart/BP/diabetes must carry a doctor's fitness certificate.\nTypes of Packages\nBudget Packages\nBudget Do Dham Yatra packages allow you to save money while still enjoying the benefits of exploring the Do Dham sites. This package includes comfortable accommodation, vegetarian meals, and smooth transportation.\nLuxury Packages\nThe Luxury Do Dham tour package allows you to have the best travel experience. With this package, you can avail of various amenities, including tasty meals, luxurious accommodations, and transfer via a private vehicle.\nPremium Packages\nPremium packages sit between Budget and Luxury. You get 3-4 star hotels, a private AC vehicle, and VIP Darshan at both temples - without the full luxury price tag. A good choice for families who want comfort without overspending.\nHelicopter Packages\nWith the Do Dham Yatra package by helicopter, you can avoid the physical exhaustion that is often associated with long-distance driving by road. The helicopter journey is a faster, luxurious, and more comfortable way to explore Gangotri and Yamunotri.\nDo Dham Yatra 2026 for Senior Citizens\nDo Dham journey involves a moderate difficulty trek, so seniors should ensure they're physically fit for the pilgrimage. They should get their medical check-up done before the Yatra and stay hydrated. During the Yamunotri trek, seniors can opt for a Pony/Palki ride to reduce the physical strain associated with the traditional journey. Helicopter Yatra is also a good option for seniors.\nBest Tourist Places to See\nHarsil Valley\nHarsil is a hidden jewel of Uttarakhand situated in the lap of the Himalayas. This place is quite famous among nature lovers and travel enthusiasts, as there are many treks near this site.\nBarkot\nSituated at an altitude of around 1,220 meters, Barkot serves as a scenic gateway. This charming hamlet offers a tranquil haven for pilgrims embarking on the Do Dham Yatra.\nHanuman Chatti\nHanuman Chatti is situated near the confluence of the Hanuman Ganga and the Yamuna Rivers. Around Hanuman Chatti, there are many shrines, including the Hanuman Temple.\nSurya Kund\nSurya Kund is a naturally boiling hot spring (~90\u00b0C) located near the Yamunotri temple. It is named after Surya Dev (the Sun God), as Goddess Yamuna is believed to be the daughter of Surya. Pilgrims traditionally cook rice and potatoes wrapped in cloth in this spring as prasad - DO NOT bathe in Surya Kund. For a holy dip, use the nearby Jamunabai Kund.\nKharsali\nKharsali is a picturesque village in Uttarakhand's Uttarkashi district. It is known for being the Goddess Yamuna's winter home. During winter, the Yamunotri Temple's idol is brought here.\nHow to Reach\nBy Flight\nJolly Grant Airport (Dehradun) is the nearest airport to the Do Dham sites. It has good connectivity with major Indian cities including Mumbai, Delhi, Chennai, and Kolkata. From Jolly Grant Airport, take a taxi or bus to Haridwar or Rishikesh (about 1-1.5 hrs) and begin your Yatra from there.\nBy Train\nHaridwar and Rishikesh are the nearest railway stations to Gangotri and Yamunotri. From Rishikesh or Haridwar, you can book a taxi or bus to Gangotri or Janki Chatti, from where the trek to Yamunotri starts.\nBy Bus\nFor Yamunotri: buses from Rishikesh/Haridwar go to Barkot. From Barkot, local shared taxis run to Janki Chatti (45 km), which is the trek base for Yamunotri.\nBy Helicopter\nHelicopter service to Yamunotri and Gangotri starts from the Sahastradhara helipad at Dehradun.\nGangotri Yamunotri Yatra Registration 2026\nRegistration is mandatory for visiting both Yamunotri and Gangotri in 2026. Without a valid registration e-pass, you will be stopped at checkpoints and denied entry to the temples. Registration is completely free.\nHow to Register:\n\nOnline: registrationandtouristcare.uk.gov.in\nWhatsApp: Send 'Yatra' to +91 8394833833\nApp: Download 'Tourist Care Uttarakhand' from Google Play Store or App Store\nOffline counters: Haridwar, Rishikesh, Barkot, Uttarkashi, Hanuman Chatti\n\nDocuments needed: Aadhaar card + mobile number for OTP verification. Carry your printed or digital e-pass throughout the journey.",
    "highlights": [
      "Visit to the Har Ki Pauri for the evening Ganga Aarti",
      "Enjoy the Yatra to Yamunotri through trekking, ponies or Palki",
      "Full Darshan of the temple",
      "Visit the Deodar and the torrential Bhagirathi and Mukhba, the winter home of Goddess Gangotri",
      "Gangotri temple visit and Darshan",
      "Enjoy the local cuisine and Prasad"
    ],
