  "dwarka-somnath-tour": {
    "overview": "Are you planning a Dwarka Somnath tour from Ahmedabad? Let's visit two of these best places in Gujarat. Dwarka is known as the city where Lord Krishna lived, and it has the beautiful Dwarkadhish Temple, which is around 600 years old and also a part of the Char Dham pilgrimage.\n\nSomnath is famous for its ancient temple dedicated to Lord Shiva, which is believed to be the first Jyotirlinga in India. The Mughals broke this shrine six times, but it was rebuilt again.\nThese two places are surrounded by the beautiful Arabian Sea, which attracts many tourists. Apart from temples, this tour also includes many other interesting destinations to see and enjoy. Everything like sightseeing, verified hotels, and transport is already covered in our package. So get ready for this unforgettable trip to Dwarka and Somnath from Ahmedabad and create new memories!\nBest Time to Visit Dwarka and Somnath from Ahmedabad\n\nIf you want to enjoy pleasant weather, plan your trip between October and February.\nWinter is the best time to go because the temperatures stay between 10\u00b0C and 25\u00b0C, so you can explore the temples and beaches without dealing with heat or heavy rain.\n\nWhy this time is special (festivals and experiences)\n\nIt is not just about good weather. You also get to enjoy Diwali lights, Makar Sankranti kites, and see decorative temples.\nThe festival vibe in Dwarka and Somnath is something you must see.\n\nHow to Reach Dwarka and Somnath from Ahmedabad\nYou can easily go to Dwarka and Somnath by train, flight or road - all options are well-connected and simple.\nBy Flight\nNearest airport to Dwarka is Jamnagar Airport (around 130 km away). Flights and trains are available from Ahmedabad.\nNearest airport to Somnath is Diu Airport (about 85 km away). Flights are only available from Mumbai and Ahmedabad.\nBy Train\n\nBoth Dwarka and Somnath have their own railway stations, so trains go directly there.\nYou can get a regular train to these places from Ahmedabad.\n\nBy Road\n\nBuses and taxis are easily available from Ahmedabad.\nAhmedabad has good road connectivity to both Dwarka and Somnath.\n\nDistance between Dwarka and Somnath\nDwarka to Somnath distance is around 233 km and it takes 4.5 to 5 hours by road.\nTravel Tips for Dwarka and Somnath\n\nControlling Rush- Temples get crowded in winter so it's better to go early to avoid waiting.\nKeep Basic Medicines- It's a good idea to bring your regular medicines, as local shops may not have your brand.\nTry Local Dishes - Don't miss trying Gujarati food like Thepla, Dhokla and Khichdi - it's simple and delicious.\nWatch Out for Monkeys- Monkeys near the temples can grab food or loose stuff, so avoid carrying fruits or open bags.\n\nPlaces to Visit in Somnath and Dwarka\nThere are many places to explore in Somnath and Dwarka that visitors should never miss because they will give a wonderful experience.\nPanch Pandav Gufa\nIn 1949, the late Baba Narayandas discovered this cave, which was made for the five Pandava brothers. Panch Pandav Gufa is a great place to explore because not many people know about it. From the cave, you can see the whole city, and the view is amazing.\nGopi Talav\nGopi Talav is a famous lake in Dwarka, Gujarat. It is believed that Lord Krishna danced here with the Gopis (his female admirers) during his childhood. The Gopis from Vrindavan came to dance with him one last time. During this holy dance, they gave up their lives and returned to the ground.\nSomnath Beach\nNear the temple, Somnath Beach is a peaceful spot to rest and enjoy nature. Visitors can watch beautiful sunsets, walk on the beach and enjoy local culture with camel and pony rides.\nDwarka Lighthouse\nAbout 2 km from Dwarka city, the 43-meter Dwarka Lighthouse is a popular sunset spot. Many people visit here to relax and take pictures of the stunning sea and sky. While visitors are not allowed to go inside the lighthouse, the view from outside is still worth the visit.",
