  "enchanting-himachal": {
    "overview": "Himachal Pradesh is one of the romantic lands of India and houses many of the important hill stations of the country. Manali, located on the banks of Beas River, is one very popular hill station of this place which is visited every year by thousands of tourists from the world over.\n\nThe state capital, Shimla, has historic monuments and presence of \u2018old world charm\u2019 in its store. While Dharamsala and Chamba located in the upper regions of the land are ideal for the peace seekers. If you are looking for adventure in Himachal Pradesh, there are options for hiking and trekking trails in areas like Kufri, Khajjiar and Chail. You can even opt for golfing in Naldera which is known to own one of the \u2018highest golf courses\u2019 in India. Bless yourself with an unforgettable experience in Himachal Pradesh.\nHimachal holds the treasure of picturesque landscapes including the deep gorges, green valleys, lofty mountains that are snow-clad, enchanting lakes, flower-treading meadows, fast-flowing mountain rivers, serene monasteries and attractive temples. This package gives you access to the fresh mountain air of Himachal Pradesh at highly competitive rates. My Quick Trippers packages for Himachal Tour are a total getaway package with options in sightseeing, excursion, temples and gardens visits. You can also choose the customized package to plan a trip that will fit your budget and other requirements, making it a comfortable stay.\n\nThe state capital, Shimla, has historic monuments and presence of \u2018old world charm\u2019 in its store. While Dharamsala and Chamba located in the upper regions of the land are ideal for the peace seekers. If you are looking for adventure in Himachal Pradesh, there are options for hiking and trekking trails in areas like Kufri, Khajjiar and Chail. You can even opt for golfing in Naldera which is known to own one of the \u2018highest golf courses\u2019 in India. Bless yourself with an unforgettable experience in Himachal Pradesh.",
    "highlights": [
      "Fantastic local tour of the Queen of the hills Shimla",
      "Kufri excursion",
      "Manali sightseeing",
      "Enjoy the local tour in Kullu",
      "Travel through the Rohtang pass and mesmerize in the snowcapped mountains",
      "Enjoy the vibrant Chandigarh city with its rose gardens and parks",
      "Indulge in the delectable local cuisines"
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1 :Delhi to Shimla (330 kms / 9 hrs)",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 2 :Shimla to Kufri and Back to Shimla",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 3 :Shimla to Kullu to Finally Reach Manali",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 4 :Manali Sightseeing",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 5 :Manali to Rohtang Pass (Snow Point)",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 6 :Manali to Chandigarh",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 7 :Chandigarh to Delhi",
        "description": ""
