  "enchanting-kerala": {
    "overview": "Kerala is an enchanting destination dotted with breathtaking landscapes, backwaters, historical locations, religious sites, and waterfalls that invite tourists for amazing trips and experiences.See More\n\nWith our Kerala tour packages, you can have the dream vacation of your life that you have always envisioned. This 6-day 5-night Enchanting Kerala tour package will give you a chance to stay in the houseboat in Alleppey and allow you to undertake a jungle safari ride in Rajamalai, where you\u2019ll see the wildest of the creatures gazing at you. Come join us on this adventurous trip and be swayed away by the land of this mesmerizing beauty.\n\nWith our Kerala tour packages, you can have the dream vacation of your life that you have always envisioned. This 6-day 5-night Enchanting Kerala tour package will give you a chance to stay in the houseboat in Alleppey and allow you to undertake a jungle safari ride in Rajamalai, where you\u2019ll see the wildest of the creatures gazing at you. Come join us on this adventurous trip and be swayed away by the land of this mesmerizing beauty.\n\nTour Gallery\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nTour Name\nEnchanting Kerala Tour Package\n\n\nTour Duration\n6 Days / 5 Nights\n\n\nMeals\nBreakfast & Dinner\n\n\nVehicle Type\nSedan / SUV\n\n\nStarting & Ending Point\nCochin\n\n\nDestination Covered\nCochin - Munnar - Alleppey - Trivandrum \n\n\nPickup Time\nDepend on your Flight Timing \n\n\n Tour Benefits\nBest price & enjoyable travel guarantee",
    "highlights": [
      "Sail through the scenic backwaters in Alleppey.",
      "Stroll through the sprawling tea plantations of Munnar.",
      "Sightseeing tour of Cochin.",
      "Explore the architectural marvels of Trivandrum.",
      "Enjoy the scenic sunset at Kovalam Beach."
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1: Arrive at Cochin",
        "description": "As you arrive at the Kochi Airport or railway station, you\u2019ll be greeted by one of our representatives who will transfer you to your pre-booked hotel.\nRelax for some time and then prepare yourself to visit the famous attractions of Cochin, including:\nJewish Synagogue:\nThe Jewish Synagogue is one of the most religious sites in South India. In the Commonwealth of Nations, it is the oldest synagogue.\nDutch Palace (Mattancherry Palace):\nThe Dutch Palace is the finest example of the Kerala architectural style. It is known for its spacious and long halls with its central courtyard.\nSt. Francis Church:\nSt. Francis Church is considered to be the first European Church in India that reflects the colonial past of the city.\nChinese Fishing Nets:\nThese are a type of fishing net that you will find along the harbor's mouth at Fort Kochi.\nHave an overnight stay at your hotel in Kochi.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "DAY 2: Cochin- Munnar (04 hrs/140 Km)",
        "description": "Post breakfast, you will be driven to Munnar, one of the most beautiful hill stations in India.\nOn the way, you will witness the breathtaking landscapes and lush green spice plantations.\nOnce in Munnar, you can experience the natural beauty of the hill station, adorned with spice plantations, beautiful rivers, cascading waterfalls, and dense forests. You will check in at your hotel and have an overnight stay."
      },
      {
        "title": "DAY 3: Munnar Sightseeing",
        "description": "After breakfast, you will proceed on a sightseeing tour of Munnar and visit the famous attractions.\nMattupetty Lake & Dam:\nGet a chance to experience the best that nature has to offer at this destination.\nEcho Point:\nAt Echo Point, your voice echoes back to you because three mountain ranges are present in this area \u2013Mudrapuzha, Kundala, and Nallathanni.\nRajamalai (Eravikulam National Park):\nRajamalai National Park houses Anamudi Peak, the highest peak in the Western Ghats. It spans 97 square kilometres and has a wide variety of flora and fauna.\nTea Gardens:\nRelish the aroma and taste of freshly brewed tea as you explore the tea gardens of Munnar.\nHave an overnight stay at your hotel.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "DAY 4: Munnar- Alleppey (04 hrs/165 Kms)",
        "description": "In the morning, drive from Munnar to Alleppey. Alleppey is a coastal city interconnected with canals and lakes. The paddy field of Kuttanad, also known as \u2018 Kerala\u2019s rice bowl,\u2019 is found in the city.\nAfter arriving at Alleppey, you\u2019ll check in to your hotel and indulge in the following activities.\nStroll by Alleppey Beach:\nAlleppey Beach is known for its splendid beauty and long coastline. You can enjoy a sunset by the beach and chill under the palm trees.\nSunset Cruise on Vembanad Lake (Optional):\nOne of the best ways to enjoy the sunset is by undertaking a cruise on Vembanad Lake.\nShopping:\nIndulge in shopping at the local markets in Alleppey that offer amazing quality products.\nOvernight stay at your hotel in Alleppey.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "DAY 5: Alleppey \u2013 Kovalam \u2013 Trivandrum (4 Hrs/164 Kms)",
        "description": "Savour a tasty breakfast in the morning as your houseboat sails through the backwater and allows you to relish splendid views.\nAs your houseboat arrives at Alleppey fishing point jetty, you will check out and head to Kovalam.\nYou will also visit the famous\nattractions of Trivandrum.\nSree Padmanabhaswamy Temple\nThis temple is a sacred Hindu shrine built in honour of Lord Vishnu. It is considered to be one of the 108 sacred places of Vishnu.\nYou will continue your journey to Kovalam and stroll on the Kovalam beach.\nHave an overnight stay at your Kovalam hotel.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "DAY 6: Kovalam \u2013 Trivandrum / Cochin Departure (6 Hrs/220 Kms)",
        "description": "Post breakfast, check out from your hotel and meet our driver outside your hotel.\nOur driver will transfer you to Trivandrum or Cochin."
      }
    ],
    "faqs": []
  },
  "enchanting-orissa-tour": {
    "overview": "Odisha, the land of paddy fields and palm-fringed silver beaches, temples, rivers, waterfalls, and tribal people, has a plethora of major attractions, including the Bhubaneswar and Puri temples, miles of clean beaches, and the magnificent Sun Temple of Konark. Justifying the exceptional, peaceful, and serene eastern part of India as a travel destination for those wishing to see the elements that contribute to the country\u2019s uniqueness.\n\nOdisha, which is bordered by the Bay of Bengal on the east, is a lesser-known beach destination that should no longer be kept a secret. Odisha, home to a plethora of Hindu temples and, surprisingly, Buddhist shrines, is a tourism destination that transports you to Ashoka the Great\u2019s glorious time. This 6 days / 5 nights tour would be covering all the best spots planned.\n\nEnchanting Orissa Tour Itinerary Package\n\n\nDay 1 :Arrival at Bhubaneswar\n\n\nWelcome to Bhubaneswar, You are greeted on arrival at Bhubaneswar airport/railway station by My Quick Trippers representative and transfer to hotel. Later if time permit half day sightseeing of famous city temples including Raja Rani, Parsurameswar, Mukteshwar (Gem of Orissa architecture), & Lingaraj (it is the biggest temple in Bhubaneswar). Overnight at Bhubaneswar.\n\n\n\n\nDay 2 :Bhubaneswar \u2013 Dhauli \u2013 Hirapur \u2013 Pipli \u2013 Konark \u2013 Puri\n\n\nMorning visit to Khandagiri & Udayagiri Jain Caves (oldest rock cut Caves, the caves are reminiscent of the influence of Buddhism and Jainism in Orissa). Then drive to Puri en route visit Dhauli (Buddhist Stupa/ peace pagoda), Pipli (the appliqu\u00e9 work village). And visit the Sun temple (one of the world famous heritage site & famously known as Black Pagoda). Enroute visit to Ramachandi Temple & Chandrabhaga beach (one of the finest beaches with a long stretch of clean sands & the beach has its own lovely serenity). Return back to Puri. Relax on the golden beach of Puri. Overnight at Puri.\n\n\n\n\nDay 3 :Puri \u2013 Chilika\n\n\nMorning drive to Chilika lake at Barkul (the largest Ramsar site of Asia and famous for its migratory birds coming from distance places). Take the boat cruise to visit the temple island, birds island at Nalabana. Relax at the Lakeside cottage. Overnight at Chilika.\n\n\n\n\nDay 4 :Chilika \u2013 Taptapani\n\n\nThe morning after breakfast drive to Tapta Pani en route visit Taratarini temple (the legendary temple on the hillock). Also, visit Silk city Berhampur to find the SILK Saree on your own choice. Later proceed to Taptapani. Overnight at the Hill Resort.\n\n\n\n\nDay 5 :Taptapani \u2013 Chandragiri (Tibetan Camp) \u2013 Gopalpur\n\n\nMorning has a Sulphur bath at Taptapani then post breakfast you can visit Tibetan settlement at Chandragiri to explore the new world Amidst of natural forest.\nChandragiri with rare scenic beauty, which presents a picturesque landscape, is a paradise for all nature lovers. Surrounded by luxuriant tropical forest, gurgling rivers, exquisite mountain slopes and roaring hilltops this exotic place of Orissa is widely known for the Tibetan refugee colony, where immigrants from Tibet have been rehabilitated. Bestowed with bounties of nature, this place is famous for seasonal fruits, Tibetan woolen garments, carpets and dogs of various breeds. The large-scale horticulture plantations, as well as the cultural activities of the Tibetan refugees, make this place more colorful and attractive. This hillside settlement of Tibetans, which is also an ideal health resort, attracts both domestic and foreign tourists from far and wide for its pleasant ambience. Tibetan spiritual leader and by His Holiness Dalai Lama to inaugurate Buddhist monastery at Chandragiri in Orissa\u2019s on 12 Jan 2010.\nVisit the Padmasambhava and University. Have lunch over there and later drive back to Gopalpur on Sea.\n\n\n\n\nDay 6 :Departure from Bhubaneswar\n\n\nToday a Bid farewell of Exotic Odisha tour, after breakfast transfer to Airport/ Railway Station for the onward journey.",
    "highlights": [
      "Visit to the famous Lingaraj Temple Bhubaneswar",
      "The famous Konark Sun temple tour",
      "The Jagannath Temple Puri Darshan",
      "Morning drive to the Chilika Lake, the largest lake for migratory birds",
      "Enjoy the boat cruise to the birds and temple island, Nalabana",
      "Visit to Taptapani famous for the sulphur bath",
      "Visit to the Chandragiri Tibetan Camp",
      "Padmasambhava and Lunch",
      "Gopalpur on sea"
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1 :Arrival at Bhubaneswar",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 2 :Bhubaneswar \u2013 Dhauli \u2013 Hirapur \u2013 Pipli \u2013 Konark \u2013 Puri",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 3 :Puri \u2013 Chilika",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 4 :Chilika \u2013 Taptapani",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 5 :Taptapani \u2013 Chandragiri (Tibetan Camp) \u2013 Gopalpur",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 6 :Departure from Bhubaneswar",
        "description": ""
      }
    ],
