  "fascinating-kerala": {
    "overview": "Kerala is an amalgam of the very best of nature. The coconut palm trees, the houses made of red tiles, and the beautiful lakes and beaches will remain forever in every visitor\u2019s heart.See More\n\nFrom the majestic heights of the Western Ghats, the country presents a scene of silent valleys showcasing god\u2019s grandeur. With our Kerala tour package, you can stroll through the tea plantations of Munnar, sail through the backwaters in a houseboat in Alleppey, and explore the famous attractions of Cochin. Our packages can be customized as per your unique needs and come with all the essential amenities.\n\nFrom the majestic heights of the Western Ghats, the country presents a scene of silent valleys showcasing god\u2019s grandeur. With our Kerala tour package, you can stroll through the tea plantations of Munnar, sail through the backwaters in a houseboat in Alleppey, and explore the famous attractions of Cochin. Our packages can be customized as per your unique needs and come with all the essential amenities.\n\nTour Gallery\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nTour Name\nFascinating Kerala Tour Package\n\n\nTour Duration\n5 Days / 4 Nights\n\n\nMeals\nBreakfast & Dinner\n\n\nVehicle Type\nSedan / SUV\n\n\nStarting & Ending Point\nCochin\n\n\nDestination Covered\nCochin - Munnar - Alleppey \n\n\nPickup Time\nDepend on your Flight Timing \n\n\n Tour Benefits\nBest price & enjoyable travel guarantee",
    "highlights": [
      "Stroll through the tea plantations of Munnar.",
      "Explore the famous attractions of Cochin.",
      "Sail through the backwaters in a houseboat in Alleppey.",
      "Enjoy lip-smacking South Indian cuisines."
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1:  Arrival at Cochin and Sightseeing",
        "description": "You\u2019ll arrive in Cochin, where a team member will greet you - either at the airport or the railway station.\nAfter arrival, we\u2019ll take you straight to the hotel. Settle in, freshen up - then it\u2019s time to explore Cochin!\nExplore well-known spots - the Jewish Synagogue, Dutch Palace, and the St. Francis Church - during your trip.\nOnce you're done with sightseeing, head back to the hotel for an overnight stay.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "DAY 2: Cochin - Munnar (4 Hrs/140 Kms) Sightseeing",
        "description": "Savour a tasty breakfast in the morning, and then you will embark on a drive to Munnar, admiring the breathtaking scenery.\nWitness the sprawling tea plantations, exotic species of flora and fauna, and aromatic spices that make this destination breathtakingly beautiful.\nAfter that, you'll head back to your hotel and have a soothing sleep in your room"
      },
      {
        "title": "DAY 3: Munnar Sightseeing",
        "description": "Relish a tasty breakfast in the morning and then get ready to visit the famous attractions of this region, including:\nTea Gardens:\nTake a stroll through the tea gardens and sample different varieties of tea.\nMattupetty Lake and Dam:\nMattupetty Dam and Lake are situated at a distance of around 11 kilometres outside Munnar. They offer the perfect setting for exploring breathtaking surroundings, leisurely strolls, and embarking on scenic boat trips.\nEcho Point:\nSituated at a distance of 15 kilometres from Munnar and at an altitude of 600 ft., Echo Point is located in the lap of misty hills and a quaint lake. This spot is known for its illustration of the echoing phenomenon.\nKundala Lake:\nThis lake is renowned for its pedal boat rides and Kashmiri-Shikara boat rides. You can also see here cherry blossom trees.\nRajamalai (Eravikulam National Park):\nRajamalai Wildlife Sanctuary is a UNESCO World Heritage Site, and it is home to a diverse variety of flora and fauna.\nHave an overnight stay at your hotel in Munnar after the sightseeing tour.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "DAY 4: Munnar - Alleppey (Houseboat) (5 Hrs/160 Kms)",
        "description": "Today you will travel to Alleppey from Munnar. Alleppey is famous for its picturesque backwater cruise, lush greenery, and serene atmosphere. It also boasts floating markets and old-style bazaars where you can purchase everything at the lowest possible prices. Alleppey is also referred to as the \"Venice of the East.\"\nOption 1: Stay at the Hotel\nOnce you reach Alleppey, we\u2019ll get you settled into your hotel. Later, feel free to try these activities.\nTake an optional sunset boat trip on Vembanad Lake, known for its stunning views\nAlleppey Beach: It is a lovely spot to unwind, share a meal, and spend time with your loved ones.\nShopping: Alleppey boasts several markets where you can get what you want without overspending.\nReturn to your hotel after the exploration and have a relaxing sleep in your room.\nOption 2: Houseboat Stay\nSpend your night in a gorgeous houseboat in Alleppey to experience the local life. You can also admire the natural surroundings from the balcony of your houseboat.\nYou can also relish traditional South Indian cuisines during your stay at the houseboat.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "DAY 5: Alleppey - Cochin Airport Departure (90 Kms/2 hrs)",
        "description": "Post a lip-smacking breakfast, check out of your hotel, and then you will head to Cochin. Once you have arrived at Cochin, you\u2019ll be transferred to the railway station or airport from where you\u2019ll continue your forward journey.\nThis also marks the end of the tour, giving you tons of memories."
      }
    ],
    "faqs": []
  },
  "fascinating-sri-lanka": {
    "overview": "The island country of Sri Lanka is one of the most charming holiday destinations in the world. Adorned with numerous picturesque holiday spots and holy sites of pilgrimage, Sri Lanka has always attracted a throng of travelers from far and wide. A fascinating Sri Lanka tour package will provide you with a memorable journey across some of the most highly acclaimed tourist destinations in this treasure trove of island. For 4 days and 3 nights stay engulfed in and unparalleled unique vibrancy.\n\nFascinating Sri Lanka Tour Itinerary Package\n\n\nDay 1 :Arrival in Colombo \u2013 Kandy\n\n\nUpon arriving at the Colombo international airport our tour representative will escort you to the vehicle that will transfer you to Kandy after covering a distance of 3 hours.\nEn route you will be made to stop at Pinnawala elephant orphanage which will be your very first location for visit. It is home to orphaned, injured and abandoned elephants where the volunteers and caretakers take care of them. You will be given an opportunity to play around and bathe with these gentle giants.\nYour journey will then continue towards the wonderful destination of Kandy, which is at a distance of 1 hour 30 minutes from the elephant orphanage. Upon arriving at Kandy you will be taken on a citywide sightseeing tour which will cover the following sites: Sri Dalada Maligawa (temple of the tooth) \u2013 an iconic temple which houses Lord Buddha\u2019s tooth relic; royal botanical gardens Peradeniya \u2013 an exuberant presentation of numerous colorful flowers and plants; gem museum \u2013 home to the finest quality of precious and semi-precious gemstones in the world.\nIn the evening you will be made to witness a traditional Sri Lankan cultural dance show (entry fees will not be included). After a wholesome day you will be taken to your hotel in Kandy for an overnight stay.\n\n\n\n\nDay 2 :Kandy \u2013 Nuwara Eliya\n\n\nAfter having a delicious breakfast in the morning, you will be transferred to the \u2018city of lights\u2019, Nuwara Eliya. Also known as \u2018little England\u2019 a city wide sightseeing tour will commence upon your arrival. You will be covering the following tourist attractions of the city: golf course; trout stream; Victoria park \u2013 home to a number of rare birds and lush greenery; Lake Gregory \u2013 for fishing and boating; tea factory \u2013 which produces some of the world\u2019s finest quality of tea, orange pekoe tea.\nYou will also be made to visit the holy site of Seetha Amman temple \u2013 the site where Sita was held captive by Ravana and where she used to pray for Rama to rescue her, as mentioned in the Hindu epic, Ramayana. It also houses a footprint of Lord Hanuman on a rock; Hakgala garden \u2013 a temperate garden with numerous water lilies and peaceful serenity.\nFinally, you will be taken to your allotted hotel for an overnight stay.\n\n\n\n\nDay 3 :Nuwara Eliya \u2013 Colombo\n\n\nAfter having a delicious breakfast in the morning you will be transferred to Colombo (the largest city and the commercial capital of Sri Lanka) which is situated at a distance of 5 hours from Nuwara Eliya.\nThe sightseeing tour of this western coastal city of Sri Lanka will cover the following attractions: Galle face green \u2013 a 500 metres long ocean side urban park; Viharamahadevi Park \u2013 oldest and the largest public park; National Museum \u2013 the largest museum in Sri Lanka; Colombo world trade centre \u2013 500 feet tall, 39 storied twin building; old parliament building and independence square (the entry fees to these places will not be included by us).\nYou will then be taken to some of the prime shopping locations of Odel, house of fashion, Beverley Street, majestic city and Noritake.\nFinally, after a day filled with exciting fun activities, you will be made to head back to your hotel for an overnight stay.\n\n\n\n\nDay 4 :Colombo Departure\n\n\nPost breakfast, you will be made to proceed towards the international airport where you will be made to board the flight heading towards your desired destination.",
    "highlights": [
      "Visit the famous Pinnawala Elephant Orphanage",
      "Kandy city sightseeing",
      "Witness the Sri Lankan culture dance performance",
      "Be a part of the city of lights, Nuwara Eliya",
      "Pay your respect at the divine shrine of Sita Amman temple, here Devi Sita was captivated by Ravana.",
      "Colombo sightseeing",
      "Taste the local cuisine"
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1 :Arrival in Colombo \u2013 Kandy",
        "description": ""
