  "ganges-northern-india": {
    "overview": "A trip to northern India would not be considered complete without a stop in Varanasi, which is known as India\u2019s most sacred city. This travel itinerary provides a comprehensive experience of Indian society, starting in Delhi and then exploring the beautiful cities of Udaipur and Jaipur in Rajasthan.\n\nWitnessing the sunrise at the iconic Taj Mahal is a must before continuing the journey into rural Madhya Pradesh, passing by the abandoned palaces of Orchha and reaching the awe-inspiring temples of Khajuraho, renowned for their exquisite erotic sculptures. Finally, conclude your journey in Varanasi, where you can join the devoted pilgrims who gather along the banks of the holy River Ganges to partake in their timeless religious rituals.\n\nWitnessing the sunrise at the iconic Taj Mahal is a must before continuing the journey into rural Madhya Pradesh, passing by the abandoned palaces of Orchha and reaching the awe-inspiring temples of Khajuraho, renowned for their exquisite erotic sculptures. Finally, conclude your journey in Varanasi, where you can join the devoted pilgrims who gather along the banks of the holy River Ganges to partake in their timeless religious rituals.\n\nNorthern India Ganges Tour Itinerary Package\n\n\nDay 1 :Delhi Arrival\n\n\nWelcome to India! On Arrival at Delhi International Airport, My Quick Trippers Representative will greet and meet you and transfer you to Hotel. Check into Hotel. Evening time is free for you to explore Delhi Haat. Later back to hotel and Overnight stay at Delhi.\nDelhi: Delhi takes pride in being the capital of the country for many dynasties. It is, in fact, a city wrapped in legend, where time flows differently, and where every moment becomes a moment of history. A vibrant melting pot, it encapsulates two very different worlds, the \u2018old\u2019 and the \u2018new\u2019, each representing delectably different experiences. It is sprinkled with glittering gems like: captivating ancient monuments, magnificent museums, a vivacious performing-arts scene and some of the subcontinent\u2019s yummiest places to eat. Delhi blends within its folds the great cultural variety of India with many attraction including Red Fort, The Qutub Minar, The Humayun\u2019s Tomb, The India Gate, The Lotus Temple, The Akshardham Temple.\nChandni Chowk, Delhi Haat, Janpath market, Connaught Place, Khan market are top markets in Delhi which is a treasure trove of goods waiting to be discovered.\n\n\n\n\nDay 2 :Delhi City Tour/ Varanasi By Train\n\n\nToday after having a hearty breakfast, we are fully packed to explore the old and in New Delhi including Red Fort, the Jama Masjid and the Humayun Tomb. Along the streets of old Delhi you will see the Raj Ghat and Mahatma Gandhi Memorial. Return to your hotel in the evening. Later we will transfer you to railway station to catch your train towards Varanasi. Overnight Journey.\n\n\n\n\nDay 3 :Arrive Varanasi\n\n\nArrive in Varanasi. Met on arrival at Varanasi railway station and transfer to Hotel (standard check-in time at the hotel is 1200 hrs noon). Afternoon sightseeing tour of Varanasi visiting bathing ghats, The Kashi Vishwanath Temple, The Durgakund, The Sankat Mochan \u2014 Shrine of Monkey God Hanuman. Overnight in Varanasi.\n\n\n\n\nDay 4 :Varanasi \u2013 Prayagraj\n\n\nMorning, after breakfast transfer towards Varanasi by Train. Upon arrival, transfer to Hotel, later we will go to have a sacred bath in Triveni Sangam (Meeting point) of the three rivers \u2013 Ganga, Yamuna & Saraswati. Here the Maha Kumbh Mela is held every 12 years which is a major Hindu festival. Later visit Ananda Bhawan & lying Hanuman Temple. Evening free for leisure. Overnight Stay at Prayagraj.\nSangam: Around 7 km from Civil Lines, overlooked by the eastern ramparts of the fort, wide flood plains and muddy banks protrude towards the sacred Sangam. At the point at which the brown Ganges meets the Greenish Yamuna, pandas (priests) perch on small platforms to perform puja and assist the devout in their ritual ablutions in the shallow waters. Beaches and ghats are littered with the shorn hair of pilgrims who come to offer Pind for their deceased parents.\n\n\n\n\nDay 5 :Prayagraj \u2013 Khajuraho (300 kms/7 hrs)\n\n\nToday Morning after breakfast we will move towards Khajuraho by road. On arrival in Khajuraho, check-into Hotel. Evening free to enjoy light and sound show. Overnight in Khajuraho.\nKhajuraho: Khajuraho, the temple city of central India, is famous Khajuraho Temple, Khajuraho Tourism Throughout the world for its exquisitely carved temples in stones. Thousands of visitors and tourists from all over the world flock together to envisage this immortal saga of Hindu art and culture engraved in stone by shilpies (stone craftsmen) millennia ago. Today, apart from the temples, Khajuraho is a small village but a thousand years ago it was a large city of the Chandelas, medieval Rajput kings who ruled over Central India.\n\n\n\n\nDay 6 :Khajuraho \u2013 Orchha (180 kms/03 hrs)\n\n\nToday after Breakfast go for sightseeing tour of Khajuraho visiting Eastern and Western group of temples. Later departure for Orchha by road and check into the Hotel. Overnight in Orchha.\nOrchha: Once the capital of the Bundelas, Orchha is now just a village set amidst a complex of well-preserved temples and palaces. It was built by Bir Singh Deo in 1531.\n\n\n\n\nDay 7 :Orchha \u2013 Gwalior (120 kms /03 hrs)\n\n\nToday after breakfast go for the sightseeing of Orchha. The tour of Orchha takes you to the Jehangir Mahal \u2013 the largest of the palaces, the Raj Mahal with its murals and the Raj Praveen Mahal built near a garden, You would also visit Dinman Hardaul`s palace with its interesting story. The temples of Orchha are highly preserved. The two main temples are the Ram Raja Temple with its lofty spires and the Chaturbhuj temple. Later drive to Gwalior by road. On arrival in Gwalior check into the Hotel. Overnight in Gwalior.\n\n\n\n\nDay 8 :Gwalior \u2013 Agra (120 kms/03 hrs)\n\n\nToday after breakfast visit Gwalior including The Gwalior Fort, The Teli Temple, The Sas Bahu Temple and The Jain Sculptures. Also visit The Archaeological Museum, Jai Vilas palace and museum. Later, drive to Agra by road and check into the hotel. Overnight in Agra.\n\n\n\n\nDay 9 :Agra \u2013 Jaipur (250 kms /05 hrs)\n\n\nToday morning after breakfast visit The Taj Mahal and later drive to Jaipur. Enroute visit Citadel Mughal Emperor Akbar\u2019s Fatehpur Sikri. Check into your hotel on arrival at Jaipur. Evening free for leisure. Later we will move for dinner at \u201cChokhi Dhani\u201d which is famous for Rajasthani Cuisne. Overnight in Jaipur.\nJaipur: Apart from being the capital of Rajasthan, Jaipur is also the largest city of the state. The foundation of the city dates back to the eighteenth century, with credit to the great warrior and astronomer Maharaja Sawai Jai Singh II. The glorious past of Jaipur comes alive in the palaces and forts in the city where once lived the royal clans. The majestic forts and havelis, the beautiful temples, the serene landscapes, and the rich cultural heritage, have made Jaipur an ideal destination for tourists.\n\n\n\n\nDay 10 :In Jaipur\n\n\nMorning after breakfast; enjoy visiting Amber Fort with an elephant ride there. Later on enjoy sightseeing city tour of Jaipur. Visit City Palace Museum, Jantar Mantar and Hawa Mahal, Jal Mahal. Evening free for shopping local handicraft. Overnight stay at Jaipur.\n\n\n\n\nDay 11 :Jaipur \u2013 Delhi and Depart\n\n\nToday farewell to India with lots of Love and memorable pictures. We will drop you airport for you\u2019re onwards journey.",
    "highlights": [
      "The Varanasi tour start with exploring the Tulsi Birwa Manas Temple, Mother India Temple, Hanuman Temple, Sankat Mochan Temple, and Vishwanath Temple",
      "Be in sync with river Ganges with the grand evening Ganga Aarti ceremony at the popular Dashashwamedh Ghat",
      "Early morning boat ride on river Ganga and a holy dip will fulfill your soul for the next whole day",
      "At Prayagraj enjoy the holy dip into the Sangam and explore those places popular for religious and historical significance",
      "After visiting the shrines of Naimisharanya, hit the road towards Dudhwa National Park",
      "At Katarniaghat Wildlife Sanctuary enjoy the boat ride and spot the Gangetic Dolphin, Birds, Gharials, and crocodiles",
      "At Vrindavan be in sync with the divine, the birth place of Lord Krishna"
    ],
