  "golden-triangle-tour": {
    "overview": "The Golden Triangle trip takes you on an exciting journey to the three famous cities in India such as Delhi, Agra, and Jaipur. See More\n\nYour journey starts in Delhi, the capital city, where you will visit popular places like the Red Fort, India Gate, Qutub Minar and more, which are full of old history and modern life.Agra is known for the iconic Taj Mahal, a symbol of love, with the impressive Agra Fort and Fatehpur Sikri. Jaipur often called the Pink city of India, famous for Amber Fort and Hawa Mahal, which have beautiful architecture, and a great place for shopping traditional crafts in its vibrant markets. Our Golden Triangle Tour Packages cover everything, including the best accommodations, meals, comfortable transports, and amazing sightseeing. In addition, visitors can customize the trip for a more personal experience. Our customer support is also available 24/7. These places are filled with local culture, delicious food, and special history. Book this trip now and enjoy this amazing journey to make an unforgettable tour.See Less\n\nYour journey starts in Delhi, the capital city, where you will visit popular places like the Red Fort, India Gate, Qutub Minar and more, which are full of old history and modern life.\n\nAgra is known for the iconic Taj Mahal, a symbol of love, with the impressive Agra Fort and Fatehpur Sikri. Jaipur often called the Pink city of India, famous for Amber Fort and Hawa Mahal, which have beautiful architecture, and a great place for shopping traditional crafts in its vibrant markets.",
    "highlights": [
      "Explore India\u2019s most famous travel circuit covering Delhi, Agra, and Jaipur.",
      "Visit top UNESCO World Heritage Sites, including the magnificent Taj Mahal.",
      "Experience Delhi\u2019s rich history and vibrant markets in both Old and New Delhi.",
      "Make a spiritual stop at Mathura & Vrindavan, the birthplace of Lord Krishna.",
      "Enjoy colourful bazaars, local food, and traditional crafts throughout the journey.",
      "Learn from expert English-speaking guides at major monuments.",
      "Relax with smooth pick-up and drop-off services for a hassle-free trip.",
      "Travel comfortably in a private AC vehicle, at your own pace.",
      "Follow a thoughtfully planned itinerary for a memorable travel experience.",
      "See More"
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1: Arrival at Delhi",
        "description": "When you land at New Delhi\u2019s Indira Gandhi International Airport, a representative will greet you and assist you in making your way to the designated hotel. You\u2019ll spend the night at the hotel."
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 2: Sightseeing in Delhi",
        "description": "After breakfast, begin your full-day sightseeing tours of New Delhi and Old Delhi.\nOn a tour of Old Delhi, there will be stops at Raj Ghat, Jama Masjid, and Red Fort are all included. From Jama Masjid to Chandni Chowk, take a cycle rickshaw and take in the scenery.\nA New Delhi sightseeing tour includes stops at the spectacular India Gate, Parliament House, President House, Humayun\u2019s Tomb, Qutab Minar, and a drive down Rajpath. You\u2019ll eat and spend the night at the hotel. (The monuments in Delhi are closed on Monday)\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 3: Delhi to Agra (221 kms, Approx. 5 hrs drive)",
        "description": "After breakfast, travel to Agra, stopping en route to view Sikandra, the tomb of renowned Mughal emperor Akbar. Upon your arrival in Agra, the city home to the Taj Mahal, a representative from our business will assist you in travelling to the desired hotel. Visit the Taj Mahal and the majestic Agra Fort, two well-known love monuments.\nThe Taj Mahal was built by Mughal emperor Shah Jahan as a memorial to his devoted wife Mumtaz Mahal. The breathtaking memorial to love is crafted from white marble and has inlay work. In 1565, Mughal emperor Akbar built Agra Fort. Visit Itmad-ud-Daula Tomb, also known as the Baby Taj Mahal by Daulah. Stay the night and eat breakfast in your hotel."
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 4: Jaipur to Agra (238 kms, Approx. 5-6 hrs drive)",
        "description": "After breakfast, take a drive to Jaipur, also referred to as the Pink City and the capital of Rajasthan. The Mughal emperor Akbar erected Fatehpur Sikri in the late 16th century but abandoned it because of a lack of water. You will stop at this location along the way. You will also see Buland Darwaza, the largest entryway in the world. Continue your journey to Jaipur, the \u201cPink City,\u201d our representative will assist you in getting to the hotel once you arrive in Jaipur. You\u2019ll eat and spend the night at the hotel.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 5: Jaipur sightseeing",
        "description": "After breakfast at the hotel, go out for the hilltop Amber Fort. travel to the fort on an elephant. Later, take in the city of Jaipur\u2019s sights include City Palace, Hawa Mahal, and Jantar Mantar. Enjoy shopping at the thriving neighborhood bazaars throughout the city as well. You\u2019ll eat and spend the night at the hotel.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 6: Jaipur - Delhi (Departure) (261 Kms, 5-6 Hours Drive)",
        "description": "Drive back to Delhi after having breakfast. We will drop you off at the airport or station with happy memories."
      }
    ],
    "faqs": []
  },
  "grand-gujarat-tour": {
    "overview": "Gujarat is every tourist\u2019s dream destination. This colourful and vibrant destination tucked in the westernmost edge of the subcontinent is rich in history, heritage, culture, mythology and an immaculate biodiversity. From being the erstwhile kingdom of Lord Krishna to being the only home of Asiatic Lions in the world, Gujarat is definitely a one-of-a-kind holiday destination. Check out the Grand Gujarat Tour Package for a wholesome well-rounded trip. Explore Gujarat like never before with this special tour package.\n\nGrand Gujarat Tour Itinerary Package\n\n\n Day 1 :Arrival in Ahmedabad\n\n\nUpon your arrival in Ahmedabad, you will be greeted by our tour manager. After being greeted by the manager, everyone will be checked in to the hotel via a private car. After freshening up you will be taken for a full-day tour of Ahmedabad. The sightseeing places here will include visit to some of the top tourist attractions in Ahmedabad like \u2013 Akshardham Temple, ISKCON Temple, Vaishno Devi Mandir etc. the day will end when you are headed back to your hotel in Ahmedabad for dinner and an overnight stay.\n\n\n\n\n Day 2 :Ahmedabad \u2013 Jamnagar\n\n\nAfter breakfast, you will be checked out of your hotel in Ahmedabad and then be made to head on to your next destination in Jamnagar. On reaching Jamnagar you will be checked into your hotel here before heading out for an exciting and fun-filled sightseeing. This sightseeing of tourist places in Jamnagar will include a visit to Lakhota Lake and Museum, Bala Hanuman Mandir, etc. finally after a full day of sightseeing exploration the day will end by heading back to your hotel for dinner and an overnight stay.\n\n\n\n\n Day 3 :Jamnagar \u2013 Dwarka\n\n\nEarly in the morning, after checking out of your hotel in Jamnagar you will be taken to your next destination on the itinerary which is Dwarka. After reaching Dwarka and checking in to your allotted hotel here you will be taken for a sightseeing exploration in Dwarka. This will also include a visit to the famous Char Dham pilgrimage temple of Dwarkadhish. Dwarkadhish Mandir is built on top of the place of residence of Lord Krishna and occupies the heart of Gujarat region. This place is a must visit. Other tourist attractions in Dwarka includes \u2013 Rukmini Mandir, Nageshwar Jyotirlinga, Gomti Ghat, Gopi Talav etc. finally the day will end on reaching back to your hotel in Dwarka for dinner and an overnight stay.\n\n\n\n\n Day 4 :Dwarka \u2013 Somnath\n\n\nToday will be the day when you will be taken to the holy land of Somnath after checking out from your hotel in Dwarka. Prior to reaching Somnath, on the way a brief visit to Sudama Temple and Kirti Mandir will take place. Upon arriving at Somnath you will immediately be checked in to your hotel. This will be followed by a Darshan and a visit to the Somnath Mahadev Temple. Other places of tourist interest in Somnath include Triveni Sangam, Bhalka Tirth, Geeta Mandir etc. finally after a full day of Darshan and tourism you will be taken back to your hotel in Somnath for dinner and an overnight stay.\n\n\n\n\n Day 5 :Somnath \u2013 Gir National Park\n\n\nAfter having breakfast in the morning at your hotel in Somnath you will be transferred to your hotel in Gir national park which is known for being the final and only home of the rare Asiatic Lions. Finally, upon arrival at the national park you will be headed for an exciting, educational and thrilling jeep safari ride experience. After this you will be taken back to your jungle resort in Gir national park for dinner and an overnight stay.\n\n\n\n\n Day 6 :Gir National Park \u2013 Ahmedabad Departure\n\n\nYou will be driven to Ahmedabad from Gir early in the morning. On reaching Ahmedabad you will be dropped off at your point of departure that can be either a train station or the airport or anywhere else that you may prefer. The drop-off will mark the end of your exciting Dwarka Somnath Gir National Park Tour Package with us.",
    "highlights": [
      "Aarti and Darshan at Dwarkadhish Temple.",
      "Full day sightseeing in Jamnagar and Ahmedabad.",
      "Somnath Mahadev Jyotirling Darshan experience.",
      "Jeep safari and Asiatic Lion viewing in Gir National park.",
      "Full day sightseeing in Somnath region."
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1 :Arrival in Ahmedabad",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 2 :Ahmedabad \u2013 Jamnagar",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 3 :Jamnagar \u2013 Dwarka",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 4 :Dwarka \u2013 Somnath",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 5 :Somnath \u2013 Gir National Park",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 6 :Gir National Park \u2013 Ahmedabad Departure",
