  "guruvayur-thrissur-athirapally-package": {
    "overview": "The Guruvayur - Thrissur - Athirapally Tour Package takes the best out of a two-day plan of spiritual exploration and natural adventure.See More\n\nServing the interests of individuals who wish to explore the culture of a specific place and admire its stunning landscape, this package combines some of the most popular attractions in Kerala. Taking spiritual breaks to holy temples, such as Guruvayur in Thrissur, with their divine atmosphere, sophisticated design, and rich culture, provides an additional spiritual touch. In addition, the divine tour offers an opportunity to observe the rich religious life in Kerala. Apart from this, you also get to witness the cultural aspect of this state of spices.\nAlong with this spiritual aspect, there is also a journey to Athirappilly Falls, the most grandiose of natural marvels in India. The waterfalls form an awesome view surrounded by green trees and foggy views, and thus, it is a must-visit location among nature lovers and photographers. The package will include transfers, a comfortable stay including breakfast, and guide assistance during the trip to make it smooth. This package will have you with wonderful memories, whether you are a devotee seeking blessings, or you are a traveler in Kerala exploring its heritage, or you are a nature lover in search of scenic beauty.\nBook your Guruvayur-Thrissur-Athirapally Tour Package today! and enjoy a journey of divine blessings and breathtaking beauty.\n\nServing the interests of individuals who wish to explore the culture of a specific place and admire its stunning landscape, this package combines some of the most popular attractions in Kerala. Taking spiritual breaks to holy temples, such as Guruvayur in Thrissur, with their divine atmosphere, sophisticated design, and rich culture, provides an additional spiritual touch. In addition, the divine tour offers an opportunity to observe the rich religious life in Kerala. Apart from this, you also get to witness the cultural aspect of this state of spices.",
    "highlights": [
      "Excursion to Kalady, the birthplace of the Hindu philosopher Shri Adi Shankaracharya.",
      "Visit Sringeri Mutt, which was constructed on the place where Adi Shankaracharya was born.",
      "Witness the charm of the Guruvayur and Thrissur temples, which are characterized by the sense of divinity, murals, and rituals.",
      "Savor the religious atmosphere and the usual worship in the old Kerala temples.",
      "Go to Athirapally Waterfalls, which is popularly referred to as the Niagara of India.",
      "Spacious and well-furnished rooms and other amenities.",
      "Convenient drop-off service at the railway station or airport."
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1: : Arrival and Welcome in Thrissur",
        "description": "You will be warmly welcomed by our representative at Cochin Airport/ Thrissur Railway Station, and then you will be taken to Kalady, which is the birthplace of Sri Adi Shankaracharya. It is in the place of Kalady that Adi Shankaracharya practiced miracles through his presence. He got the Vedas perfect and devoted his life to the preaching of the Vedic Dharma by founding four mutts at Puri, Sringeri, Dwaraka, and Joshimath. It was rediscovered in the late 19th century by the then Shankaracharya of Sringeri, and the following consecration of a temple to Sri Adi Shankara in 1910.\nVisit Sringeri Mutt:- Sringeri Mutt was constructed at the same location where the house of Adi Sankara was located.\nAfter check-in, later drive to Guruvayur. Take a spiritual tour to Thrissur and Guruvayur temples. Experience the Divine atmosphere of these ancient shrines, covered with complicated carvings and colorful murals.\nExperience the magical rites and sacrifices, with worshipers coming together to receive blessings of the gods. The calm and the inner spiritual volatility of these temples is indeed a very rewarding experience.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 2: Exploring Athirapally Falls and Departure",
        "description": "After having breakfast, gear up to visit Athirappilly Falls, commonly known as the Niagara of India. The waterfall falls 80 feet into a tranquil pond. The green fields and foggy mist cover it, forming a magical sight that is enjoyed by a large number of people. The loudness of the water, the vividness of the forest colors, and the cool mist are to be remembered.\nTo take the bus or train, or the airport, exit the building after making a visit.\nWe are happy to be travelling with you. Thank you, we appreciate your time and wish to meet you soon.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      }
    ],
    "faqs": []
  },
