  "hanoi-danang-ho-chi-minh-city-tour": {
    "overview": "Book our Hanoi Danang Ho Chi Minh City Tour package and you're guaranteed to see the best of Vietnam. Your journey will begin from the cultural capital of Hanoi itself! Marvel at the ancient temples, colonial architecture, and beautiful lakesides that are its star attractions. Also, enjoy the luxe cruise across the Halong Bay which is beautifully surrounded by majestic emerald waters.See More\n\nThis 7 day tour will also take you to the coastal gem of Da Nang! Enjoy sandy beaches and swimming in its clear waters. You'll also take a trip to the charming Hoi An Ancient Town. Walk through the lantern-lit streets here which are surrounded by houses as old as they come! You'll also indulge in a thrilling cable car ride at the Ba Na Hills. Finally, end your adventure in the Ho Chi Minh City. You get to see everything here, ranging from tranquil Mekong Delta to the wartime museum of Cu Chi Tunnels. This tour really lets you uncover the soul of Vietnam. Book now or give us a call to know more about this trip! See Less\n\nThis 7 day tour will also take you to the coastal gem of Da Nang! Enjoy sandy beaches and swimming in its clear waters. You'll also take a trip to the charming Hoi An Ancient Town. Walk through the lantern-lit streets here which are surrounded by houses as old as they come! You'll also indulge in a thrilling cable car ride at the Ba Na Hills. Finally, end your adventure in the Ho Chi Minh City. You get to see everything here, ranging from tranquil Mekong Delta to the wartime museum of Cu Chi Tunnels. This tour really lets you uncover the soul of Vietnam. Book now or give us a call to know more about this trip!",
    "highlights": [
      "Trip to Hanoi, Da Nang, and Ho Chi Minh",
      "Explore Hanoi's Temple of Literature, Tran Quoc Pagoda, and Hoa Lo Prison Museum",
      "Enjoy a luxury cruise to Halong Bay",
      "Visit to Sung Sot Cave, Luon Cave, and TiTop Island",
      "Discover the Hoi An Ancient Town",
      "Enjoy the lantern-lit boat ride",
      "Take the thrilling cable car ride to Ba Na Hills",
      "Enjoy a walk across the stunning Golden Bridge",
      "Learn about Vietnam's history at Cu Chi Tunnels",
      "Marvel at the floating villages at Mekong Delta",
      "See More"
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1: HANOI ARRIVAL (NIL)",
        "description": "Once you arrive at the Hanoi airport, complete your immigration process and get your visa on arrival. Our driver will be waiting for you at the airport and will take you to your pre-booked hotel.\nOnce you reach the hotel, check in and freshen up. Then get ready for the capital city tour.\n13:30\n: You'll be picked up by our driver and then taken to the\nTemple of Literature\n. This is the first university of Vietnam and was established in the 11th century. Do click snaps of its courtyards and ancient gates.\n15:15\n: Now, visit the\nHoa Lo Prison Museum\n(aka \"Hanoi Hilton\") which showcases Vietnam's struggle for independence. You'll be surprised to know that this museum was actually once a prison used to keep political prisoners.\n16:15 - 16:30\n: Later, you'll be taken back to your hotel for an overnight stay.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 2: HANOI - HALONG BAY",
        "description": "Savour a delicious breakfast in the morning.\n08:00 - 08:30:\nNow a bus will take you to the scenic countryside to\nTuan Chau Island\nin Halong City. Our guide will also be there with you. We'll also take a refreshment break during the journey.\n12:00:\nOnce you arrive at the Tuan Chau Harbor, our crew will give you a warm welcome aboard the cruise ship. A safety briefing will also be given to you.\nGet ready for a 5-hour journey on this tour where you'll get to enjoy the breathtaking landscapes, full of islets and outcrops, named after their unique shapes!\nEnjoy the authentic, delicious\nVietnamese lunch\non the boat while admiring the beautiful scenery.\n13:45:\nYou'll arrive at the\nBo Hon archipelago\n. Deboard the ship and go for exploring the\nSurprising Cave\n(aka Sung Sot Cave). It houses impressive stalagmites and stalactites that resemble sea creatures!\nNow you can go kayaking or indulge in a\nbamboo boat ride\nin Luon Cave, and discover the beautiful lagoons.\nLater, visit\nTitop Island\n. You can enjoy the sandy beaches here that lie adjacent to the limestone Mountains. You can also take a trek to the top, from where you can get panoramic views of the whole area!\n16:30:\nReturn to your cruise ship, which will take you back to the Tuan Chau Harbour. During your journey back, indulge in sunbathing and music, and the natural scenery all around you.\n18:00:\nDisembark from the cruise ship and you'll be taken back to Hanoi via the new highway.\n20:00:\nYou'll reach your hotel. Enjoy an overnight stay.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 3: FLY TO DANANG - HOI AN",
        "description": "Relish a nice breakfast in the morning.\nAfter this you'll be transferred to the airport to take a flight to\nDanang\n. Once you reach there, check into your hotel and relax for a while. In the afternoon, get ready to explore the beautiful Hoi An Town.\n15:00:\nThis is a guided tour, and we'll arrange our guide to meet you at the hotel itself. Your\nHoi An City Tour\nbegins!\nThe very first place on the itinerary today is the\nHoi An Market\n. Get lost in its colourful sights, sounds, and smells! This bustling market is a must-visit if you want to do some real Vietnam shopping.\nOur guide will get you tickets to the\nHoi An Old Town\n(included in your package). Explore here the\nPhuc Kien Assembly Hall\n. The vibrant Chinese architecture here will treat you with bright gates, dragon statues, and grand rooftops!\nAlso, see the well-preserved old houses, like\nPhung Hung Ancient House\nand\nTan Ky House\n. These homes are here for over 200 years and have withstood centuries of weather and war! You can also learn about the lifestyle of merchants that used to live here.\nNow, visit the\nJapanese Bridge\n, which is over 400 years old. This was originally constructed to connect the Japanese and Chinese communities who live on either side of the waters.\nAlso, take a detour to the handicraft shops of Hoi An. You can explore the artwork galleries here.\nLastly, in the evening, take a stroll on the\nlantern-lit alleys\nand enjoy a boat ride on the\nThu Bon River\n. Tourists release the floating lanterns in the river to attract good luck. Do capture the reflections of the lantern-lit surroundings in the river.\nTake a restful night of sleep in your hotel at Da Nang.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 4: Full-Day Ba Na Hills Excursion (40 km / 1 hr each way)",
        "description": "Start your day with a delicious breakfast in the morning.\nNow, you'll be taken to the\nBa Na Hills\n, which is famous for everything from picturesque mountain scenery to entertainment complexes!\nOnce you get there, take a scenic\ncable car ride\nand enjoy the breathtaking landscapes that lie along the way.\nAlso, take a walk across the iconic\nGolden Bridge\n, which is held by the giant hands! Also, visit the following:\nFrench village with European-style buildings\nFlower Garden\nAmusement Park\nWax Museum\nLater, enjoy a delicious lunch at the mountaintop restaurants, which serve a variety of Vietnamese and international cuisine.\nLater in the evening, you'll be dropped off back at the hotel, where you can take rest for the night.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 5: Fly To Ho Chi Minh - Cu Chi Tunnel",
        "description": "Treat yourself to a nice breakfast in the morning.\nAfter this, check out of the hotel. Our driver will transport you to the Da Nang airport, from where you'll take the flight to the\nHo Chi Minh City\n.\nOnce you arrive there, relax for a while. You'll be taken to the\nCu Chi tunnel\nin the afternoon (60 km ride). Along the way, you'll get to see rice paddy fields and lush greenery. Also, enjoy the ducks and water buffaloes that swim in the rivers.\nBy 12:45 PM, you'll reach the tunnels. Admire this underground system of tunnels that span across 220 km! Discover the hidden chambers here, try the wartime food that the soldiers ate, and learn how the Vietnamese soldiers lived in these tunnels during wartime.\nYou'll also have the opportunity to shoot the AK-47, one of the main guns used during the war. (Completely optional).\nThe tour will finish by 7:00 PM, and after that, you'll be taken back to your hotel for an overnight stay.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 6: Mekong Delta",
        "description": "Relish a nice breakfast in the morning at the hotel.\nAround 8 - 8:30 am, your tour will begin. Get ready for a trip to\nMy Tho city\n, which serves as a gateway to the Mekong Delta. Take the one-and-a-half-hour bus ride, taking in the lush's greenery all around you.\nNow, take a\nboat ride on the Mekong River\n, enjoying the floating houses and fish farms along the way. Do not forget to capture these beautiful moments.\nOnce you're there, visit the\ncoconut candy workshops\nand see how the coconut candy is made. Take this time to also visit the bee farms where you can taste the real honey!\nYou can also enjoy the\nauthentic Vietnamese folk music\n(\u0110\u1eddn Ca T\u00e0i T\u1eed), which is also recognised by the UNESCO.\nAfter that, savour some delicious\nVietnamese traditional lunch\nunder a tree shade.\nNow, visit the\nVinh Trang Pagoda\nwhich is the largest pagoda in the delta.\nThe rest of the time is for leisure which you can utilise by discovering the region on your own.\nIn the evening, you'll be driven back to your hotel by our driver.\nEnjoy an overnight stay at the hotel.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 7: DEPARTURE",
        "description": "Savour a hearty meal in the morning and check out of your hotel.\nNow, our driver will drop you off at the airport from where you can take a flight back home.\nThis concludes your trip. Hope you have an amazing trip with us!"
      }
    ],
    "faqs": []
  },
  "hanoi-halong-da-nang-hoi-an-tour": {
    "overview": "The 5 day Hanoi - Halong - Da Nang - Hoi An tour will take you through Vietnam's most vibrant cities and have you witness the age-old heritage in one single trip! Your tour will begin from the bustling city of Hanoi itself! This is the cultural heartland of the country, and you'll see everything here from ancient temples to serene lakes to lively markets. This city is a living example where history meets modern charm. Take it all in before you start cruising for Halong Bay, which is all surrounded by emerald waters and limestone cliffs.See More\n\nAnd this is just the beginning of your trip. There's a lot of fun activities left for you to enjoy. You'll be taken to the coastal gem of the country, that is Da Nang! You'll get to enjoy the Thu Bon River boat ride, capture the lantern-lit streets, and explore the mystic Hoi An Ancient Town - all to your heart's content. Finally, conclude your trip with a cable car ride to the magical Ba Na Hills. My Quick Trippers's well-crafted itineraries are prefect for enjoying this trip full of adventure and fun. Book now or give us a call to know more about this unique Vietnam experience! See Less\n\nAnd this is just the beginning of your trip. There's a lot of fun activities left for you to enjoy. You'll be taken to the coastal gem of the country, that is Da Nang! You'll get to enjoy the Thu Bon River boat ride, capture the lantern-lit streets, and explore the mystic Hoi An Ancient Town - all to your heart's content. Finally, conclude your trip with a cable car ride to the magical Ba Na Hills. My Quick Trippers's well-crafted itineraries are prefect for enjoying this trip full of adventure and fun. Book now or give us a call to know more about this unique Vietnam experience!",
    "highlights": [
      "Thorough exploration of Hanoi - Temple of Literature, Tran Quoc Pagoda, and Hoan Kiem Lake",
      "Enjoy a luxury day cruise on Halong Bay",
      "Visit to the Sung Sot Cave and Luon Cave",
      "Discover the serene Cam Thanh Coconut Village",
      "Trip to the Hoi An Ancient Town",
      "Enjoy a cable car ride at Ba Na Hills",
      "Fun visit to the Fantasy Park",
      "See More"
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1: Hanoi arrival - Early check-in - Half day city tour (B) - Private",
        "description": "Once you arrive at\nHanoi's Noi Bai International Airport\n, you'll receive a warm welcome from our tour representative.\nNow, you'll be driven to your pre-booked hotel in your private luxury vehicle by our driver. The journey will take about one hour. You'll reach there after 14:00 hours.\nGet ready to enjoy your half-day city tour in the afternoon. Our very first stop will be at the\nTemple of Literature\n- the very first university of Vietnam dedicated to Confucius. Enjoy the\ntraditional architecture\nand the serene atmosphere here.\nAfter this, you'll be taken to the\nTran Quoc Pagoda\n. This is one of the oldest pagodas in Vietnam. It's located by the\nWest Lake\n, and the sunset view here makes for a perfect photo op. The surroundings here are really peaceful. Spare a moment to sit here and take in the whole serene vibe.\nOur last stop will be the\nHoan Kiem Lake\n. Considered as Hanoi's pretty centrepiece, this place has legends at every turn of the corner. Plus, you get to see the vibrant street life here.\nAfter this, you're free to stroll through the bustling Old Quarter on your own. Discover the charming narrow streets and enjoy the vibrancy of the place.\nReturn to the hotel for an overnight stay.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 2: Hanoi - Halong Bay Day cruise - Hanoi (B/L) - SIC",
        "description": "8.00-8.45:\nYou'll be picked up by our driver from your hotel in Hanoi Old Quarter/ Opera House, and will be taken to Halong Bay. On this three hour drive, we'll go through Hanoi, Haiphong, and Tuan Chau Highway. A 30-minute break will be taken on this trip for refreshments and relaxation.\n12:00\n: Once you arrive at the Tuan Chau Harbor, board the\nLuxury Cruise\n. You'll get our crew's full assistance for this. Relish the welcome drinks once you're on board.\n12:30\n: You'll be given the Vietnamese lunch on the boat. Enjoy your food while taking in the the beautiful scenery lined by limestone.\n14.00\n: Once you arrive at\nBo Hon Island\n, deboard the cruise and visit the\nSung Sot Cave\n. This cave has a lot of stalagmites and stalactites inside it and makes for a great exploration trip.\n14.45\n: Take a bamboo ride or kayaking through\nLuon Cave\n. You'll get to witness the beautiful lagoons here.\n15.15\n: Visit the picturesque\nTiTop Island\nand enjoy sandy beaches & swimming in the blue waters. You can also trek to the top of the island and have a panoramic view of the entire Halong Bay!\n16.30\n: Now get back to the boat for a trip back to the harbour. Enjoy a little sunset party with wine, tea, fruits, and biscuits on the boat.\n18.00-18.15\n: You'll reach the harbour. Now, get on the bus that will take you back to Hanoi.\n21.00\n: You'll be dropped off at the hotel. Enjoy the overnight stay.\nMeals\n: Breakfast, Lunch (local food)\nNotice\n: The cruise's itinerary depends on the specific cruise and The Cruise's program is object to be changed without notice by the cruise.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 3: Hanoi - Halong Bay Day cruise - Hanoi (B/L) - SIC",
        "description": "Relish a nice breakfast in the morning. After that, you'll be driven to the Hanoi airport by our driver from where you'll take a fight to the\nDa Nang\n.\nOnce you arrive at the Da Nang international airport. Our driver will warmly greet you and will drive you towards your hotel. (Check in after 14.00 PM)\nIn the afternoon, you'll be taken on an adventure trip where you'll visit the\nCam Thanh Coconut Forest\n. Enjoy a\nbamboo basket boat ride\nand float through serene waterways amidst lush greenery! You can also learn a local fishing technique or two!\nLater, you'll be taken to the\nHoi An Ancient Town\n, which is also a UNESCO World Heritage site. Stroll through its narrow streets and see the traditional houses that line them. Also, take a trip to the\nold assembly halls\nwhile enjoying the views of the\nlantern-lit shops\n. Do not forget to see the following as well:\nJapanese Covered Bridge\nTan Ky Old House\nFujian Assembly Hall\nIn the evening, take in Hoi An's magical aura. The streets get lit by the colourful lanterns - a sight to behold. Do take picture of its reflection in the\nThu Bon River.\nAlso, take a fun\nboat ride\nin the river. , Release paper lanterns into the water for good luck.\nAfter that, you'll be taken back to the hotel where you will enjoy your overnight stay.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 4: Da Nang - Bana Hills - Golden Bridge - Da Nang (B/L) - SIC",
        "description": "08h00:\nOur tour guide will pick you up right from your hotel. Now, you'll be taken to the Ba Na Hills.\n09h00:\nEnjoy the\nSuoi Mo cable car.\nThis is one of the world's longest cable ride and you'll get to enjoy stunning mountain views along the way.\n09h30:\nWalk across the iconic\nGolden Bridge\n. This 150-meter-long architectural wonder is held by giant stone hands. Also, visit the\nLinh Ung pagoda\n, where you can see the 27m high Buddha statue. Also, enjoy the following:\nLe Jardin\nDebay Wine Cellar of French\nLoc Uyen Garden\nQuan Am Cac\nNow, take the\nsecond cable car ride\nto Gare Debay, and reach the top of Ba Na. Enjoy a guided visit to the\nFantasy Park\nwhere you can indulge in Love Swing, Skiver Pilot, Fire Racing Track, Bumper Car, Ghost House, and more!\n12h30:\nEnjoy a lunch buffet at the hilltop restaurant there.\n13h30\n: Have some leisure time. Either rest or explore the surrounding areas. Now, hike to the\nPeak of Chua Mountain\n(1,487 m). Once you're there, visit the\nBa Chua Thuong Ngan Temple\n. You can see the panoramic views of the entire Da Nang City from here.\n15h30\n: Now, return to the cable car station and get back to Da Nang.\n16h30:\nYou'll be dropped off at your hotel. The rest of the day is free for you to enjoy as you please.\nHave a restful night of Danang.\nMeals\n: Breakfast, Lunch (local food)\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 5: Da Nang departure (B) - No guide",
        "description": "Have a delicious breakfast in the morning.\nNow, you can either take some time to rest in the hotel or do some last minute shopping on your own. (Check out time: before 12:00)\nLater, our drive will drop you at the Da Nang International Airport from where you can take a flight back home. Capture the beautiful coastal views along the route.\nThis concludes your journey. Hope to see you again soon!"
      }
    ],
    "faqs": []
  },
  "hanoi-halong-saigon-my-tho-tour": {
    "overview": "Explore the beauty and culture of Vietnam with this Hanoi Halong Saigon My Tho Tour Package. The journey starts from Hanoi, one of the favorite spot of every visitor. The main highlight here is Hoan Kiem Lake. The night view is completely amazing here, with colorful lights and a peaceful atmosphere.See More\n\nHalong is another great place where you can see small green islands that look like they\u2019re floating on the blue sea, which creates a truly magical experience. Next, the trip takes you to Saigon. The Sri Mariamman Hindu Temple is also a well-known attraction in this area.\nNot only Hindus but also many Vietnamese locals visit the temple to pray for luck, happiness and success in life. Another famous spot is My Tho, where tourists enjoy boat rides, visit tropical fruit farms, and shop in local markets. So to explore more plan your Hanoi Halong Saigon My Tho Trip!\nSee Less\n\nHalong is another great place where you can see small green islands that look like they\u2019re floating on the blue sea, which creates a truly magical experience. Next, the trip takes you to Saigon. The Sri Mariamman Hindu Temple is also a well-known attraction in this area.\n\nNot only Hindus but also many Vietnamese locals visit the temple to pray for luck, happiness and success in life. Another famous spot is My Tho, where tourists enjoy boat rides, visit tropical fruit farms, and shop in local markets. So to explore more plan your Hanoi Halong Saigon My Tho Trip!\n\nTour Gallery\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nTour Name\nHanoi Halong Saigon My Tho Tour Package\n\n\nTour Duration\n5 Days / 4 Nights\n\n\nMeals\nBreakfast\n\n\nVehicle Type\nPrivate AC Car\n\n\nStarting & Ending Point\nHanoi / Saigon\n\n\nDestination Covered\nHanoi - Halong Bay - Saigon - My Tho\n\n\nPickup Time\nDepend on your Flight Timing\n\n\n Tour Benefits\nBest price & enjoyable travel guarantee",
    "highlights": [
      "See Hanoi\u2019s charm with Hoan Kiem Lake, Old Quarter and ancient temples.",
      "Enjoy a Halong Bay cruise with caves, kayaking and island visits.",
      "Visit Saigon\u2019s top spots like Notre Dame Cathedral, Ben Thanh Market and Reunification Palace.",
      "Experience My Tho\u2019s boat rides, tropical fruits and peaceful Mekong countryside."
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "DAY 01- Arrive Hanoi - Half Day City Tour",
        "description": "Start your\nVietnam tour\nwith a warm welcome at Hanoi\u2019s Noi Bai International Airport. Our driver from My Quick Trippers will meet you and take you to the hotel, which takes around 50 - 60 minutes. If you book a guide, he will join the driver and help you the whole day.\nIn the afternoon, start your half-day city tour and visit-\nTemple of Literature\nTran Quoc Pagoda-\nOne of the oldest Buddhist temple in\nVietnam\n, located beside the beautiful West Lake.\nHoan Kiem Lake\nAfter sightseeing, spend some free time exploring the Old Quarter, filled with streets and local shops. Overnight stay in Hanoi.\nNote-\nBreakfast is included. Hotel check-in time is\n14:00\n, but early check-in is already part of the package.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 02- Hanoi - Halong Bay - Return to Hanoi (350 km/ 4-5 hours)",
        "description": "Between\n8:00\nand\n8:45 AM\n, meet the driver at your hotel in\nHanoi Old Quarter\nor at the\nOpera House\n(pickup point) to start your journey to\nHalong Bay\n.\nWe\u2019ll travel to\nHalong Bay\nthrough the\nHanoi-Haiphong-Tuan Chau\nHighway.\nOn the way, we stop for a short break of\n30 minutes\nto relax.\nAt\n12:00 PM\n, reach\nTuan Chau Harbor\nand get on the luxury cruise. The crew will welcome you warmly.\nHave a welcome drink before you start your journey.\nAround\n12:30\n, enjoy a tasty\nVietnamese\nlunch on the boat as you pass through beautiful small islands on both sides. Don\u2019t forget to click pictures!\nAt\n14:00\n, reach\nBo Hon Island\nand visit\nSung Sot Cave\n, one of the most beautiful caves. As you step inside, you\u2019ll see amazing, colorful lights - the view is so beautiful that you\u2019ll truly enjoy it!\n(14:45)\n, try\nkayaking\nor take a\nbamboo boat\nthrough\nLuon Cave\nand enjoy the peaceful surroundings.\n15:15\n, reach\nTi Top\nIsland and relax on the beach. Go for a swim, or you can enjoy some time at the small cafes nearby.\n16:30\n, enjoy a\nsunset party\non the boat with wine, tea, fruits, and biscuits while going back to the\nharbor\n(harbor means parking area for boats).\n18:00-18:15\n, arrive back at the\nharbor\n. Get on the bus and return to\nHanoi\n.\n21:00, you\u2019ll be dropped off at your hotel after the tour.\nStay overnight in\nHanoi\n.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 03- Hanoi - Fly to Saigon - Half Day City Tour (Approx. 1,160 km)",
        "description": "Have breakfast at the hotel before the driver takes you to the airport for your flight to\nSaigon\n. Once you land at\nTan Son Nhat Airport\nour driver will meet you and take you to the hotel for check in after 2:00 PM.\nIn the afternoon go to the\nReunification Palace\n, where visitors can see old helicopters, war rooms and underground tunnels - a perfect spot for history lovers.\nNext, stop at the\nNotre Dame Cathedral\n, a famous old church built in the French style. Its beautiful design and calm atmosphere attract many visitors.\nRight in front, you can see the\nSaigon Central Post Office\n. Its architecture is excellent.\nContinue to the\nSri Mariamman Hindu Temple\ndedicated to the goddess Mariamman.\nEnd the tour at\nBen Thanh Market\nwhere you can enjoy shopping and try tasty local snacks.\nHave a peaceful overnight stay in\nSaigon\n.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 04- Saigon - My Tho - Saigon",
        "description": "After breakfast, leave the busy city of\nHo Chi Minh\nand proceed to\nMy Tho\n, a peaceful town near the Mekong River.\nUpon arrival, visit\nVinh Trang Pagoda\n- one of the oldest temple. Its large Buddha statues and beautiful surroundings will surely impress you.\nThen, enjoy a\nsampan boat ride\non the river and see the four lovely islands \u2013\nDragon, Unicorn, Phoenix\n, and Tortoise. Keep your camera ready for this beautiful spot!\nAt Unicorn Island, take a walk through small village paths, see how fruits grow, taste them fresh, and see local people singing folk songs.\nEnjoy a slow boat ride through the small river paths of\nThoi Son Island\n. Visit a local\nhoney-bee farm, taste fresh honey tea\n, and see how coconut candies are made.\nHave lunch at a local restaurant and take a short break.\nIn the afternoon, you can go cycling around\nTan Thach Village\n, meet the locals, and see how people live in this beautiful riverside area. If you don\u2019t want to cycle, just relax on a hammock and enjoy the cool wind.\nReturn to\nHo Chi Minh City\n.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 05- Saigon Departure",
        "description": "Enjoy breakfast at the hotel. Your wonderful\ntrip to Vietnam\nends today.\nYou may have a short time to shop before our driver drops you off at the airport for your return flight.\nNote-\nCheck out time before 12:00"
      }
    ],
    "faqs": []
  },
  "hanoi-ninh-binh-halong-da-nang-hoi-an-tour": {
    "overview": "Travelling to Vietnam feels like turning the pages of an enchanting fairytale storybook. Our Hanoi-Ninh Binh-Halong-Da Nang-Hoi An Tour is an escape to some of the most serene corners of Vietnam. Your journey will start from the heart of Hanoi, where you tread the ancient halls of the Temple of literature and feel the delightful rush of trains passing just a foot away at the Train Street. Isn't it enchanting? The trail does not stop here. After the train view, you will visit the peaceful countryside of Ninh Binh, often called \"Halong Bay on Land\". Here you will drift down a calm river on a boat which is surrounded by majestic limestone mountains. The views of endless green rice fields will feel like you have been transported to the world of Ghibli movies.See More\n\nBoard a luxury cruise and explore the scenic lagoons, caves and breathtaking seascapes. After roaming in the North, we will take you to see the amazing attractions of Central Vietnam. Here you will see the majestic giant Buddha Statue, magical water coconut forest on a Bamboo basket boat and later to the ancient town of Hoi An. At Hanoi you will see the best evenings. The atmosphere becomes romantic when you see the glowing wonderland of Silk Lanterns. In the final chapter of our 7 Day Hanoi-Ninh Binh-Halong-Da Nang-Hoi An Tour, we tread to Ba Nah Hills for unbelievable mountain views. It's a perfect tour to enjoy vibrant culture, natural views and creating sweet moments with your loved ones.\nWe at My Quick Trippers with more than 15 years of industry experience will deliver the best services to write your own chapter in Vietnam without any hassle. So, Book our Tour and let the fun begin. See Less",
    "highlights": [
      "Thrill at Hanoi's Train Street",
      "Serene boat trip in Ninh Binh",
      "Delightful cruise trip on the emerald waters of Halong Bay and Sunset Party",
      "Kayaking into hidden caves and lagoons.",
      "Tour of the Lantern-Lit streets of Hoi An- A visual spectacle",
      "Giant stone hands in the Ba Na Hills",
      "Leisure walks at the famous Golden Bridge",
      "Bamboo Basket Boat ride to see the beautiful water coconut forest",
      "Beauty of Bana Hills",
      "See More"
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "DAY 01- Hanoi Arrival - Early Check-In, Afternoon: Half Day City Tour (D)",
        "description": "Arriving at Noi Bai International Airport, our local driver (No Guide) will be at the airport to pick you up. You will be warmly welcomed and then transferred to check in to your pre-booked hotel room.\nThe Check in Time will be 14:00 pm\nNote-\nMeals- Dinner (Indian Food)\nYou will not get Early Check-ins and Breakfast options at the hotel in our Package.\nIn the afternoon, you will enjoy a sightseeing\ntour of Vietnam\n. First, you will get a fascinating glimpse of Vietnam's heritage and royal past at the Temple of Literature. Then you will head to Old Quarter to explore Train Street and shops, cafes, eateries and enjoy exciting Nightlife.\nSightseeing Outline\nTemple of Literature-\nIt was built in 1076 and served as Vietnam's first university for 700 years. It was used to educate Vietnam's royalty, mandarins and members of the elite.\nWitness the beautiful well-preserved gardens and grand architecture which will take your breath away.\nTrain Street-\nIt's a famous narrow railway street located in the Old Quarter of Hanoi.\nEnjoy the thrill of trains passing by and sip an authentic Vietnamese coffee\nOld Quarter-\nExplore the beauty of centuries-old architecture, and rich cultural heritage and enjoy exciting nightlife.\nThis place has 36 narrow streets which were traditionally named after guilds or trade that were famous there such as silk, silver, bamboo, cotton.\nAlso visit some of the traditional shops to buy souvenirs.\nEnd your day with a peaceful stroll and witness a beautiful contrast of Hanoi's historical roots and rise of modernity.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "DAY 02- Hanoi - Ninh Binh - Hoa Lu Ancient Capital - Tam Coc (B/L/D)",
        "description": "Early in the morning after breakfast, we will depart from Hanoi and visit Ninh Binh province. It is 2 hours from the South of the City.\nEnjoy the Ninh Binh sightseeing Tour. First you will visit the ancient temples at Hoa L\u01b0 and then head to Tam Coc and enjoy a two-hour boat ride along the Ngo Dong River. Your next visit will be to the Bich Dong Pagoda complex.\nNote-\nMeals- Breakfast, Lunch, Dinner (Indian food)\nOvernight Stay at Hanoi\nSightseeing Outline\nHoa L\u01b0\nHoa L\u01b0 is one of\nthe best places to explore in Vietnam\n. It's an ancient capital of Vietnam during the Dinh and Le dynasties (10th-11th century).\nWitness the mesmerizing ancient temples of King Dinh Tien Hoang and King Le Dai Hanh and get good insights of the city's rich history.\nTam Coc\nIt's is also fondly known as 'Halong Bay on Land'\nBoard a traditional Sampan boat ride and enjoy a scenic 2 hours boat ride along the Ngo Dong River.\nFrom the serene waters, you will come across many scenic places like limestone karst mountains, lush rice paddies, and three natural caves that give Tam Coc its name.\nBich Dong Pagoda\nWe will not miss this beautiful Bich Dong Pagoda Complex. It is built on a mountain side near Tam Coc.\nSee the three levels of Pagoda- Lower Pagoda, Middle Pagoda, and Upper Pagoda and the breathtaking views of nearby areas and countryside by climbing at the top.\nAfter the day tour of the natural and historical places of Ninh Binh, we will return to Hanoi in the late afternoon or early evening. Overnight stay at Hanoi to rejuvenate your senses.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "DAY 03- Hanoi - Halong Day Cruise - Hanoi (B/L/D)",
        "description": "Sightseeing Outline for Day 3\n8:30 am-\nYou will be picked from your hotel room to explore the beauty of Halong Bay.\nToday we will cover\nHanoi- Haiphong- Tuan Chau Highway.\nIt will be a 3 hrs drive.\n12:00pm-\nWe will reach\nTuan Chau Harbor\nand get on a luxury cruise. You will get a warm welcome by our crew member. Enjoy a wholesome drink and start a delightful excursion tour to explore the breathtaking beauty of this heritage site.\n12:30 pm-\nSavor delicious Vietnamese lunch on board while enjoying beautiful views on both sides. See beautiful limestones.\n14:00 pm-\nWe will discover Bon Ho Island and See\nSung Sot Cave\n. It is one of the most beautiful caves with enchanting Stalactites and Stalagmites.\n14:45pm-\nThrough\nLuon Cave\n, enjoy the beauty of the Lagoon by Kayaking or Bamboo Boating.\n15:15 pm-\nAlso visit Titop Island with its scenic sandy beach. Try swimming or trek to the top to capture the beauty of the entire Halong Bay.\n16:30pm-\nReturn to the boat for a fun-filled sunset party which includes fresh fruits, wine, tea biscuits. While you enjoy the party, the boat will be cruising back to the harbor.\n18:00-18:15pm-\nAfter arrival at the harbor, go to the beach to return to Hanoi. Enjoy Dinner.\n21:30pm-\nwe will return to the hotel room. Tour ends.\nNote-\nOvernight Stay at Hanoi\nMeals- Breakfast, lunch (local food on cruise), Dinner (Indian food)\nThe itinerary of the cruise will depend on the specific cruise. The schedule of the cruise may be subject to change without any prior notice.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "DAY 04- Hanoi - Fly to Da Nang (Breakfast, Lunch, Dinner)",
        "description": "After enjoying breakfast at the hotel, our driver will pick you up and transfer you to\nNoi Bai Airport\nto take a flight to Da Nang.\nAfter arriving at\nDa Nang Airport\n, our driver will take you to a restaurant to enjoy a delicious dinner.\nLater, take a rest to fine-tune your spirit at the hotel.\nNote-\nMeals: We offer Brunch (local food), Dinner (Indian food)\nOvernight Stay at the hotel in Da Nang\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "DAY 05- Da Nang - Son Tra Peninsula - Linh Ung Pagoda - Cam Thanh Coconut Forest - Hoi An Ancient Town (B/L/D)",
        "description": "After breakfast, it's time for sightseeing.\nSightseeing Outline\nGet ready to explore\nSon Tra Peninsula\n. Capture mesmerizing sea views.\nVisit\nLinh Ung Pagoda\n. It's famous for its display of a giant Buddha Statue, overlooking the city and the ocean. It's a place for solace seekers. Immerse in the natural beauty of Da Nang's and get useful insights on its cultural heritage.\nHead to\nCam Thanh Coconut Forest\nfor a day thrill. Enjoy Bamboo basket boat rides and glide through scenic waterways. Learn local fishing techniques and enjoy lush green views.\nVisit\nHoi An\n. It's a beautiful ancient town and a UNESCO World Heritage Site. Explore narrow streets, traditional houses, assembly halls and lantern- lit shops. Some of the major sites to explore here are-\nJapanese Covered Bridge, Tan Ky Old House, and the Fujian Assembly Hall.\nExplore the magical charm of Hoi An's riverside. As the sunsets, you will see the streets are illuminated with awe-inspiring lanterns. Enjoy a boat ride along the\nThu Bon River\nand release paper lanterns into the water for good luck.\nNote-\nAfter sightseeing, go back to Da Nang hotel room\nMeals: Breakfast, Lunch, Dinner (Indian food)\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "DAY 06- Danang - Bana Hills (Golden Bridge) - Danang (B/L/D)",
        "description": "Sightseeing outline for Day 6\nExplore mountainous theme parks at an elevation of 1,500m high. It's a scenic hill resort developed by French people in the 1920's to enjoy cool mountain breeze and escape summer heat.\nExplore the cable car station at the foot of\nBa Na Mountain\n. It's a first leg cable car which got two\nGuinness World Records\nin 2009 for being the longest non-stop cable car (5,042m) and highest non-stop cable car (1,292m).\nFrom above in the cabin, see the scenic treeline of forests, waterfalls, lush greenery along with pristine ecological systems of the Ba Na Mountains.\nVisit\nLe Jardin\nwhich is popular for old vineries and remnants of French villas.\nExplore Linh Ung Pagoda's 27 m high Buddha Statue and then leave for the second cable car station to visit the top of the mountain and see the remains of old villas.\nWitness the scenic peak of\nChua Mountain at\nthe height of 1,487m. From here, you can capture the whole view of Da Nang city. After that, visit the\ntrail of Dreaming Stream, Rainbow Waterfall, Suspension Bridge, Golden Valley, and ruined Opera House.\nPlay with old monkeys and take beautiful pictures with your family and friends.\nTake a leisure walk at the golden bridge amidst the foggy hills. Capture the scenic\nDa Nang city.\nAfter that, return to the cable car and get back to Da Nang for overnight stay.\nNote-\nMeals- Breakfast, Lunch (local food), Dinner (Indian food)\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "DAY 07- Danang - Departure (B)",
        "description": "Take your own leisure time until the tour guide takes you to Danang Airport for your flight to your home.\nNote-\nMeals- Breakfast"
      }
    ],
    "faqs": []
  },
