  "haridwar-rishikesh-mussoorie-dhanaulti-tour": {
    "overview": "Experiencing the Haridwar Rishikesh Mussoorie Dhanaulti tour and see what makes this journey unique.See More\n\nStart your trip in Mussoorie, the queen of the hills. It is not just famous for natural beauty but also for adventure activities like paragliding, ropeway rides, and trekking. If you have time try these fun things. Kempty Falls is the main attraction here, and also a popular picnic spot.\nAfter Mussoorie, continue to Dhanaulti, a small hill station, located 2,286 meters above sea level. It\u2019s perfect for people who don\u2019t like big crowds and want a calm experience. Visitors will also see the Devi Temple near Dhanaulti, explore its beautiful architecture and enjoy peaceful surroundings.\nNext travel to Rishikesh, see the holy Ganga River views and take part in world-famous Ganga Aarti ceremonies. Visit Parmarth Niketan, a great place for yoga and meditation, so don\u2019t miss it. Travelers can also go to Haridwar to reach Mansa Devi Temple. People believe that those who visit with pure heart Goddess fulfills wishes of devotees. The hilltop here has amazing views of the surroundings. Get ready to start your blissful journey with our Haridwar Rishikesh Mussoorie Dhanaulti package.\nSee Less\n\nStart your trip in Mussoorie, the queen of the hills. It is not just famous for natural beauty but also for adventure activities like paragliding, ropeway rides, and trekking. If you have time try these fun things. Kempty Falls is the main attraction here, and also a popular picnic spot.\n\nAfter Mussoorie, continue to Dhanaulti, a small hill station, located 2,286 meters above sea level. It\u2019s perfect for people who don\u2019t like big crowds and want a calm experience. Visitors will also see the Devi Temple near Dhanaulti, explore its beautiful architecture and enjoy peaceful surroundings.",
    "highlights": [
      "Visit Laxman Jhula & Ram Jhula and enjoy riverside views.",
      "Try river rafting at Shivpuri for adventure.",
      "Visit Kempty Falls, famous spot in Mussoorie where you can relax, swim and enjoy its picnic vibes.",
      "Practice yoga and meditation at local ashrams.",
      "Mansa Devi Temple by Ropeway",
      "See More"
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1: Delhi - Dehradun (249 kms / 5-6 hours)",
        "description": "Start your\ntrip\nwith our\nMy Quick Trippers\nTeam. You will be welcomed at Delhi Airport / Railway Station then we will take you to Dehradun.\nNight stay-\nOvernight stay at a hotel in Dehradun."
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 2: Dehradun - Mussoorie (33 kms / 49 minutes)",
        "description": "Travel from Dehradun to\nMussoorie\nin morning. On the way, you\u2019ll see beautiful villages and small waterfalls, great places to pause and take photos.\nOn arriving in Mussoorie, check into your hotel and freshen up. Later, visit\nMussoorie Lake\nto enjoy boating.\nNow, walk on\nMall Road to shop\n, try local treats, and watch street performances. Explore ,b>Kempty Falls\n, the best place to swim and relax in\nAlso, in the evening, visit the Municipal Garden for a peaceful walk and\nsee Lal Bahadur Shastri Academy\nwith its impressive architecture.\nStay overnight in a hotel.\nNote-\nMussoorie Kempty Falls entry timing is from 6:00 am to 6:00 pm.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 3: Mussoorie - Dhanaulti - Rishikesh - Haridwar (150 km Approx. / 5-6hours)",
        "description": "After breakfast, travel to\nDhanaulti\nand visit\nMata Surkanda Devi\nTemple (It is believed that this temple is sacred where Goddess Sati\u2019s head fell when Lord Shiva carried her body).\nAt Dhanaulti, enjoy a quiet nature walk and fresh mountain air. The hills are full of deodar, oak, and pine, and on clear days the snow-covered Bandarpunch peaks are also visible.\nNext, head to\nRishikesh\nyoga capital of India. Visit famous places like\nRam Jhula\nand\nLaxman Jhula\n- big iron suspension bridges over Ganges River. Visitors should come here in the early morning to enjoy the views.\nExplore peaceful ashrams such as\nSivananda Ashram\nand\nGita Bhavan\nwhere you can feel spiritual vibe.\nDon\u2019t miss Parmarth Niketan, well known spot for yoga and meditation perfect to experience peace and learn about Indian spirituality.\nAfter that proceed to Haridwar, one of the holiest place in India where pilgrims take a dip in the sacred Ganges River.\nLater drive to\nHaridwar\nand stay overnight in a hotel.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 4: Haridwar - Delhi (214 kms/ 4 Hours)",
        "description": "Enjoy breakfast! Today, you\u2019ll be taken for a cultural tour of Indore!\nVisit landmark places like Rajwada and Lal Bagh Palace. Also, taste the local sweets.\nNow, you\u2019ll be driven back to the Indore Airport /Railway Station from where you can continue your further journey.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      }
    ],
    "faqs": []
  },
  "haridwar-rishikesh-sightseeing-tour": {
    "overview": "Low on time but want to experience a fulfilling spiritual trip? See More\n\nThen book our one day Haridwar Rishikesh Sightseeing Tour Package. This same-day trip packs all the must-visit locations in these two holy cities. Whether it\u2019s watching the ever-so-pleasant Ganga Aarti at Har ki Pauri, enjoying the famous Jhulas of Rishikesh, or a refreshing stroll along the riversides, this trip checks all the boxes for a nice little pilgrimage tour.Why choose us? Pick us because we provide you with the best professional services. In addition, we\u2019ll handle all your travel logistics, ranging from your meals to the transfers in and out of the cities. Get out of the humdrum of your daily life and set out on a tour where you enjoy an omnipresent divine atmosphere, murmuring of flowing rivers, and sacred chants that increasingly purify the atmosphere. Wait no more, call us now to go on a soul-uplifting trip. Perfect weekend exists!See Less\n\nThen book our one day Haridwar Rishikesh Sightseeing Tour Package. This same-day trip packs all the must-visit locations in these two holy cities. Whether it\u2019s watching the ever-so-pleasant Ganga Aarti at Har ki Pauri, enjoying the famous Jhulas of Rishikesh, or a refreshing stroll along the riversides, this trip checks all the boxes for a nice little pilgrimage tour.\n\nWhy choose us? Pick us because we provide you with the best professional services. In addition, we\u2019ll handle all your travel logistics, ranging from your meals to the transfers in and out of the cities. Get out of the humdrum of your daily life and set out on a tour where you enjoy an omnipresent divine atmosphere, murmuring of flowing rivers, and sacred chants that increasingly purify the atmosphere. Wait no more, call us now to go on a soul-uplifting trip. Perfect weekend exists!",
    "highlights": [
      "Same day trip that covers the major attractions of both Haridwar and Rishikesh",
      "Visit to the iconic sites in Rishikesh, like Ram Jhula, Laxman Jhula, and famous Ashrams",
      "A peaceful walk along the Ganges",
      "Enjoy the mesmerizing Ganga Aarti at Har Ki Pauri, Haridwar",
      "Full assistance from our tour representative",
      "See More"
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1: Arrival in Delhi - Rishikesh \u2013 Delhi (Approx. 466 km/12-13 hours)",
        "description": "Welcome to Delhi! You\u2019ll be greeted by our team representative at the railway station/airport.\nNow, you\u2019ll be driven to Rishikesh first. Enjoy sightseeing at:\nRam Jhula\nLaxman Jhula\nParmarth Niketan\nGita Bhawan\nSivananda Ashram\nRiverside cafes\nAfterwards, you\u2019ll be taken to Haridwar (about 1 hour drive), where you can witness the glorious\nevening Aarti at Har Ki Pauri\n. Watch hundreds of Diyas as they float by.\nNow, you\u2019ll be transferred back to Delhi. Our driver will drop you at the location of your choice!\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
