  "haridwar-rishikesh-with-mussoorie-tour": {
    "overview": "Get ready for a spiritually uplifting journey to nurture your mind with the healing touch of divine in Haridwar and Rishikesh with scenic views of majestic Himalayan peaks and Shivalik ranges. See More\n\nOur 4 Day Haridwar, Rishikesh, Mussoorie Tour is a perfect combination of sacred experience with Himalayan holidays and adventures. Behold some of the most sacred temples, ashrams along with stunning waterfalls, majestic peaks and scenic valleys. Book your 4 Day Haridwar, Rishikesh, Mussoorie Tour Package now and create everlasting memories. Don\u2019t worry about the hassle of hotel, meals, guide and transportation booking, We, My Quick Trippers have dedicated team to handle everything for you. So, don\u2019t wait, pack your bags and embark on a soul seducing journey to Haridwar, Mussoorie and Rishikesh.\nSee Less\n\nOur 4 Day Haridwar, Rishikesh, Mussoorie Tour is a perfect combination of sacred experience with Himalayan holidays and adventures. Behold some of the most sacred temples, ashrams along with stunning waterfalls, majestic peaks and scenic valleys. Book your 4 Day Haridwar, Rishikesh, Mussoorie Tour Package now and create everlasting memories. Don\u2019t worry about the hassle of hotel, meals, guide and transportation booking, We, My Quick Trippers have dedicated team to handle everything for you. So, don\u2019t wait, pack your bags and embark on a soul seducing journey to Haridwar, Mussoorie and Rishikesh.\n\nTour Gallery\n\n\n\n\n\n\nTour Name\nHaridwar Rishikesh with Mussoorie Tour\n\n\nTour Duration\n04 Days / 03 Nights\n\n\nMeals\nBreakfast\n\n\nVehicle Type\nSedan / SUV\n\n\nStarting & Ending Point\nDelhi\n\n\nDestination Covered\nDelhi - Haridwar - Rishikesh - Mussoorie\n\n\nPickup Time\nDepend on your Flight Timing \n\n\nTour Benefits\nBest price & enjoyable travel guarantee",
    "highlights": [
      "Seek divine blessings at the mesmerizing hilltop temples of Chandi Devi and Mansa Devi for an awe-inspiring sacred beginning at Haridwar.",
      "Immerse in the soulful rhythm of the delightful Ganga Aarti in the evening at Har-Ki-Paudi.",
      "Evoke powerful feelings of devotion by taking a ritualistic holy dip into the sacred Ganges.",
      "Explore Queen of the hills, Mussoorie\u2019s scenic views. Visit Kempty falls, Camel\u2019s back road, Municipal Garden, Mall Road and Mussoorie Lake.",
      "Explore some of the most iconic sights of the yoga capital, Rishikesh. Witness the beauty of Ram Jhula, Laxman Jhula and embrace the spiritual wisdom at ashrams like Parmarth Niketan.",
      "Witness the sacred Ganga Aarti in the evening at Rishikesh. Embrace eternal peace.",
      "See More"
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1: Arrival at Haridwar from Delhi (214km/5hr)",
        "description": "Welcome to Delhi. Our representative will pick you up from the airport/railway station and drive to Haridwar. After arrival, you will be transferred to your pre-booked hotel. Check in at the hotel and take some rest to rejuvenate your mind and body.\nLater, visit to some of the most famous places of Haridwar with your loved ones-\nChandi Devi Temple-\nSituated at Neel Parvat, dedicated to goddess Chandi Devi. It is a siddha Peetha.\nMansa Devi Temple-\nSituated at Bilwa Parvat, Mansa Devi Temple is dedicated to goddess Mansa. It is also known as Bilwa Tirth.\nHarihar Ashram-\nFeel inner peace at Harihar ashram. You can also stay here. Get the divine blessings of the sacred Parad Shivling.\nDaksha Mahadev Temple-\nSituated in Kankhal, the temple is dedicated to Lord Shiva.\nBhuma Niketan-\nLocated at Sapt Sarovar Marg, Bhuma Niketan is dedicated to Lord Shiva.\nPawan Dham Temple-\nIt is famous for attractive idols of gods and goddesses adorned with jewellery. You will also witness beautiful glass work on the temple walls.\nVaishno Devi Temple-\nIt is built as a replica of goddess Vaishno Devi of Jammu and Kashmir. Devotees from all over India come here to seek Vaishno Devi\u2019s blessings.\nDoodhadhari Temple-\nThe temple is a part of Doodhadhari Barfani Ashram. It is dedicated to Lord Rama, Devi Sita and Lord Hanuman.\nBharat Mata Mandir-\nIt\u2019s a unique temple dedicated to India. India is represented here as mother.\nEvening- Take a ritualistic evening bath in the sacred Ganga River and dive deep into the spiritual vibes at Ganga Aarti.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 2: Haridwar \u2013 Dehradun - Mussoorie (90km/3-4hrs)",
        "description": "In the morning after breakfast, you will be driven to Mussoorie via Dehradun.\nMussoorie is a beautiful hill station in the foothills of the Himalayas. It is also known as the queen of the hills. After arrival at Mussoorie, you will be transferred to your pre-booked hotel and take some rest.\nLater we will enjoy sightseeing at Mussoorie. We will explore-\nMussoorie Lake-\nEnjoy boating and adventurous rides like giant swings, sky cycling etc.\nMunicipal Garden-\nIt is also known as Company Bagh. It has a beautiful mini lake with a waterfall. You can also buy amazing souvenirs from the small market located here.\nKempty Falls-\nIt\u2019s a delightful picnic spot. The scenic 40 ft high Kempty waterfall will take your breath away.\nGun Hill-\nIt\u2019s the second highest peak of Mussoorie. You can see the entire Doon Valley and majestic Himalayan ranges from this peak.\nCamel\u2019s Back Road-\nBehold beautiful sunrise and sunset and embrace the beauty of nature. It is one of the most scenic nature sports for nature lovers.\nMall Road-\nIt\u2019s a lifeline of Mussoorie. Mall Road is one of the best shopping spots to buy amazing souvenirs, eat delicious street food and sit for a laid-back evening.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 3: Mussoorie - Dehradun - Rishikesh (85-90km/Approx. 3.5hrs)",
        "description": "Morning after breakfast, we will reach Rishikesh, the Yoga capital of India. You will be transferred to your pre-booked hotel and take some rest.\nLater we will enjoy the Rishikesh sightseeing tour. We will witness-\nRam Jhula and Laxman Jhula-\nScenic suspension bridge over the sacred river Ganges.\nSivananda Ashram-\nIt was constructed by Swami Shivananda in 1936. It is one of the best yoga and meditation centres in Rishikesh to nourish your mind.\nGita Bhawan-\nLocated in Swargashram, it is the best place to sit and listen to religious discourses and meditate for peace of mind.\nParmarth Niketan-\nIt is one of the most famous Yoga centres in Rishikesh located on the holy banks of ganga river. Find your soul\u2019s joy by doing a relaxing meditation.\nAdd Ons-\nIf energy permits, enjoy adventure activities like river rafting, bungee jumping or cliff jumping in Rishikesh (at your cost).\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 4: Rishikesh \u2013 Haridwar - Delhi (250-260 km/Approx. 6-7hrs)",
        "description": "After breakfast, the tour ends with happy memories. You will be driven back to the airport/railway station for further journeys."
      }
    ],
    "faqs": []
  },
  "haridwar-sightseeing-tour": {
    "overview": "Known worldwide as the gateway to god this place is the center for Hinduism and mysticism since a very long time. Sitting on the banks of River Ganga on the northern Indian plains, Haridwar is the hub for Hindu pilgrims from across the nation. The vibrancy and colors of Haridwar is unmatched and still remain unparalleled. This place serves as the focal point of religious activities and devotees seeking peace.\n\nHaridwar Sightseeing Tour Itinerary Package\n\n\nDay 1 :Arrival in Hardwar and Sightseeing\n\n\nAfter your arrival in Haridwar, you will be taken to your hotel where you will be checked in and offered breakfast. You will then head on towards your first destination.\nSituated on top of Neel Parvat on the Shivalik Hills, Chandi Devi Mandir can be reached via a ropeway. Built in 8th century by Adi Shankaracharya this temple is one of the ancient structure in Haridwar. This is also one of the most sacred and pious Sidhpeeth where it is believed that people\u2019s desires are fulfilled.\nAfter performing your puja rituals and offering your prayers you will be taken to your next destination of Baba Ramdev ashram. Patanjali Yogpeeth is the non-profit flagship project of Baba Ramdev which aims to carry welfare activities in the fields of health care, education and socio-economic.\nNext stop will be the Mansa Devi Mandir, which is located on top of Bilwa Parvat and dedicated to goddess Mansa Devi. This holy temple is known as the holy abode of goddess Mansa Devi (a form of Shakti), which is said to have emerged from Lord Shiva\u2019s mind. A visit here is said to fulfill all your wishes.\nAfter this, you will be served a wholesome lunch meal and then you will head on to your next stop.\nHar ki Pauri is one of the most famous and popular ghats in Haridwar and a major landmark in the holy town of Haridwar. This place is considered to be sacred since it is believed that Lord Shiva had visited the Brahma Kund in Har Ki Pauri during the Vedic period. Here you will be attending the highly revered Ganga Aarti before heading off back to your hotel.\nOnce at the hotel you will be served a delicious dinner meal and an overnight stay.\n\n\n\n\nDay 2 :Haridwar \u2013 Delhi\n\n\nAfter having your breakfast in the morning you will be taken to a temple visit starting with Saptarishi mandir.\nDedicated to Lord Dattatreya and other ancient Hindu gods and goddesses this temple holds immense significance to Hindu devotees and pilgrims. With its focus on the seven sages or Saptarishis who are the patriarchs of Vedic religion, this temple fills your soul with calmness and tranquility.\nAfter a religious and peaceful visit you will be taken back to Delhi from where you can head on towards your next destination.",
    "highlights": [
      "Hardwar the Gateway to the Chardham, have a divine exepreince in the tour.",
      "First visit would be Neel Parvat and Chandi Devi Mandir on the Shivalik Hills and is reached by a ropeway.",
      "Also visit the Baba Ramdev ashram, Patanjali Yogpeeth.",
      "Fulfill your wishes by visiting the Mansa Devi Mandir, which is located on top of Bilwa Parvat and dedicated to goddess Mansa Devi.",
      "Visit to the Saptarishi Mandir dedicated to Lord Dattatreya and other ancient Hindu gods and goddesses.",
      "Finally visit the famous Har ki Pauri Ghat where the evening aarti is just mesmerizing.",
      "Also get to taste the wholesome delicious meals and prasads from the temples in the trip."
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1 :Arrival in Hardwar and Sightseeing",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 2 :Haridwar \u2013 Delhi",
        "description": ""
      }
    ],
    "faqs": []
  },
