  "hills-of-kumaon-tour": {
    "overview": "Kumaon is known to be the most loved as this hill town is surrounded by Tibet in the North and Nepal in the East. It is known to be the revenue division of Uttarakhand. The scenic beauty is unparalleled and makes it more alluring for travelers around India and the world. The snow-peaked mountains and the lush green oak trees of different types just spread all over the hills and valleys of the region. It is a must-visit to such a heaven on earth and experience the natural beauty with the 7 days / 6 nights Kumaon Hills Tour package.\n\nHills of Kumaon Tour Itinerary Package\n\n\nDay 1 :Delhi \u2013 Nainital (330 kms / 7 hours)\n\n\nWelcome to Delhi, You are greeted on arrival at Delhi Airport / Railway station by My Quick Trippers representative and Drive to Nainital, the most beautiful hill station of Kumaon. Check in to your hotel and rest of the day at leisure. Evening you will walk to Naini Lake and Mall road. Night stay in Nainital.\n\n\n\n\nDay 2 :In Nainital\n\n\nThis morning, enjoy an excursion to the lakes which includes Sat Tal, a group of seven lakes including the famous jade green Garud Lake, the larger Bhimtal and Naukuchiatal. Rest of the evening, enjoy a stroll on the Mall road and shop for the famous wax candles or you can enjoy a boat ride on Naini Lake (on direct payment basis), Night stay at Hotel.\n\n\n\n\nDay 3 :In Nainital\n\n\nToday, you will proceed on a local tour of Nainital visiting the Naina Devi Temple and Hanuman Garhi. Rest of the day is free to enjoy a boat ride on the Naini Lake (boats can be hired directly) or take the ropeway to enjoy the best view of snowcapped peaks (on direct payment basis), Night stay at Hotel.\n\n\n\n\nDay 4 :Nainital \u2013 Ranikhet (80 kms / 3 hour)\n\n\nToday, you will drive to the popular hill station of Ranikhet. On arrival, check into your hotel. This afternoon, explore the temples and the wonderful sights in Ranikhet such as 9-hole golf course at Upat, a Government Fruit Garden and Research Station at Chaubatia and the fascinating temples in Dwarahat. Night stay in Ranikhet.\n\n\n\n\nDay 5 :Ranikhet \u2013 Almora\n\n\nAfter breakfast, drive to Almora, it\u2019s a very beautiful hill station. Later to proceed to explore the unspoiled flora & fauna of this beautiful hill station. Night stay in Almora.\n\n\n\n\nDay 6 :Almora \u2013 Binsar Wildlife \u2013 Mukteshwar\n\n\nAfter breakfast, full day excursion to Binsar Wildlife sanctuary a 30-minute drive from Almora. Day at the sanctuary. Night stay in Almora.\n\n\n\n\nDay 7 :Delhi (322 kms/7)\n\n\nReturn Home with Happy Memories",
    "highlights": [
      "Excursions for the famous lakes including Bhimtal, Naukuchiatal, and the Green Garud Lake",
      "Visit all the best hill towns in the region",
      "Enjoying the boat rides in the famous lakes",
      "Visit the Binsar Wildlife Sanctuary",
      "Best accommodation to luxury hotels and prompt travel cars",
      "Enjoying the local Kumaon cuisine."
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1 :Delhi \u2013 Nainital (330 kms / 7 hours)",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 2 :In Nainital",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 3 :In Nainital",
        "description": ""
