  "himachal-lovers-paradise": {
    "overview": "One of the most famous multi-day Honeymoon Tour in the Himachal. Mesmerizing Shimla & Adventure in Manali: explore Himachali cultures. Create Lifelong memories. We all go on many trips in a lifetime, but honeymoon is something special, always. Honeymoon is the most important trip of one\u2019s life. It is the first journey of you two being together giving your lives a new start. It is meant to be more than perfect, as these memorable days of your lives ain\u2019t going to return ever. In short, you plan it, we execute it. With our 10 days / 9 nights tour you have the most enticing and valuable offers for all the newlyweds. Bloom your love amidst the most fascinating & exquisite locations of Himachal the wonderland.\n\nHimachal Honeymoon Tour Itinerary Package\n\n\nDay 1 :Delhi \u2013 Shimla (330 kms / Approx.9 Hrs)\n\n\nYou are greeted by My Quick Trippers representative and transfer you to Shimla, where on arrival, you will check into your hotel. The rest of the evening is at leisure, Overnight stay at Shimla.\n\n\n\n\nDay 2 :In Shimla \u2013 Day Excursion to Kufri (20 kms / Approx. 1 hrs)\n\n\nMorning proceed for the sightseeing of Shimla covering Kalbadevi Temple, Jakhu Temple, Hanuman Temple or stop for a while at the beautiful stained-glass-windows of Christ Church, which was built in the 1850 \u2018s.\nAfternoon excursion to Kufri a 30 Minutes\u2019 drive from Shimla, an exotica of nature as a place surrounded by dense forest and snow caped mountains amidst virgin peaks and natures flora and fauna where one can completely relax and tune oneself for natural beauty, Evening free to enjoy the scenic beauty of Kufri. Fagu, Indira Gandhi Holiday Home and enjoy horse riding in the apple orchids. Return to the Hotel Rest of the day is free to explore various scenic sights or visit mall road and shopping, Night stay at Hotel.\n\n\n\n\nDay 3 :Shimla \u2013 Kullu \u2013 Manali (149 Km)\n\n\nMorning drive to Manali. Enroute visit Kullu valley, Beas River, Dashehra maidan etc. Evening free, Night stay in Manali.\nThe Kullu- is spread in the entire Kullu Valley which is lavishly gifted with superb scenic wealth. Kullu also known as \u2018Valley of Gods\u2019 has numerous temples. Kullu valley offers a scenic charm of peaceful wooded glades and rivers through the rocks. The Dussehra of Kullu is world famous. The ancient Hindus regarded Kullu as the farthest limit of human habitation \u2018Kulantapitha\u2019 and its original name finds mention in the epics, The Ramayana and Mahabharat as well as the Vishnu Purana. Kullu, which is located on the bank of river Beas is the Central point of this tourist complex. Running North to South, the main river valley is only 80 km. long and 2 km. at its broadest, yet a fairly wide area is open to the visitors to enjoy the spectacle of variegated mountain scenery. The deodar-fringed grassy Maidan, Dhalpur, is a stage for many colorful fairs.\n\n\n\n\nDay 4 :Manali \u2013 Rohtang Pass\n\n\nToday morning, proceed on a day excursion to the Rohtang pass. If roads to Rohtang pass are closed, then visit snow point where ponies/horses can be hired directly, later visit Solang Valley where Himachal\u2019s best ski slopes can be found( here you can enjoy paragliding, horse-riding, scooter riding etc. on direct payment basis). The rest of the day is free to explore this scenic town, Overnight stay at Hotel.\n\n\n\n\nDay 5 :Manali \u2013 Dharamsala (240 Km)\n\n\nToday we will progress to Dharamsala. The plan for the day is to shop in the bazaar for Tibetan handicrafts. Here you can full your bags with exquisite Tibetan handicrafts, Tibetan carpets, garments and other trinkets. Stay overnight at hotel in Dharamsala.\n\n\n\n\nDay 6 :Dharamsala local \u2013 Dalhousie (127 Km)\n\n\nMorning, after breakfast visit a quaint little town, Mcleodganj. Also known as \u201cLittle Tibet\u201d Mcleodganj is the place of residence of Dalai Lama. Later transfer to Dalhousie. Overnight stay at Dalhousie.\n\n\n\n\nDay 7 :In Dalhousie \u2013 Excursion to Khajjiar (23 kms/approx.1hrs)\n\n\nIn morning, drive to Khajjiar (commonly called as mini-Swiss of Himachal), a picturesque spot set amidst a backdrop of dense pines, deodars and lush green meadows. Khajjiar is exquisitely nestled down in the foothills of the imposing Dhauladhar ranges of the western Himalayas providing a panoramic and breathtaking view to the visitors. Khajjiar is part of the notified Kalatop \u2013 Khajjiar sanctuary. And later proceed to Chamba. Stands on the right bank of the river Ravi, It is well known for its splendid architecture and as the base for numerous excursions. Night stay at hotel.\n\n\n\n\nDay 8 :Dalhousie \u2013 Amritsar (190 Km)\n\n\nAfter breakfast visit Dalhousie local, later drive to Amritsar. Evening you can become a part of Wagah Border. Overnight stay at Amritsar.\n\n\n\n\nDay 9 :Amritsar Local \u2013 Chandigarh (220 Km)\n\n\nAfter Breakfast, Start your city tour with the blessings of Golden Temple-the most important Sikh shrine also known as Harmandir Sahib and Durbar Sahib. Then visit Jallianwala Bagh- the place that reminds every Indian of the brutal and heartless massacre by British general Dyer. Later Transfer to Chandigarh. Overnight at Chandigarh-Hotel.\n\n\n\n\nDay 10 :Chandigarh Local \u2013 Delhi Departure\n\n\nMorning Visit Chandigarh Local like Sukhna Lake, Rock garden, later transfers to Delhi to catch your train for boarding onward journey. Thanks you for your patronage and looks forward to serving you again in the near future.",
    "highlights": [
      "Visit to the best temples in the region",
      "Together with your partner enjoy the Rohtang pass",
      "A little blessing from the divinity in Dharamshala",
      "Special excursion to Khajjiar (mini Swiss of Himachal)",
      "Amritsar and Chandigarh city tours with the ethnic touch of Punjab"
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1 :Delhi \u2013 Shimla (330 kms / Approx.9 Hrs)",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 2 :In Shimla \u2013 Day Excursion to Kufri (20 kms / Approx. 1 hrs)",
        "description": ""
      },
