  "himachal-pradesh-with-delhi-darshan": {
    "overview": "Himachal Pradesh is famous for its Himalayan scenery and popular hill stations. Many outdoor activities, such as rock climbing, mountain biking, paragliding, ice skating, trekking, rafting, and heli-skiing, are popular tourist attractions in this region. Although once it was known as the summer destination, yet with time and enhancing tourism facilities now one can visit all year round. This 9 days / 8 nights would be a truly worthwhile vacation for you.\n\nHimachal with Delhi Darshan Tour Itinerary\n\n\nDay 1 :Delhi \u2013 Manali\n\n\nWelcome to Delhi, catch your Volvo from Delhi at 5.30 PM. Overnight-journey.\n\n\n\n\nDay 2 :Manali Arrive Local\n\n\nYou are greeted on arrival at Manali Volvo stand by My Quick Trippers representative and drive to the hotel, check-into hotel (12.00 Noon early check-in depend on availability). After fresh- up go for half day local sightseeing Morning proceed for a half day tour of Manali visiting Hadimba Devi Temple \u2013 built in the tranquil and serene woods, Vashisht Bath, Tibetan Monastery, and Roerich art Gallery. Later visit Manikaran has the World\u2019s hottest Sulfur Spring Waters and is a holy place for Hindus & Sikhs alike. Back to the hotel, have dinner. Overnight stay at Manali.\n\n\n\n\nDay 3 :Manali Sightseeing \u2013 Rohtang Pass\n\n\nToday morning, proceed on a day excursion to the Rohtang pass. If roads to Rohtang pass are closed, then visit snow point where ponies/horses can be hired directly, later visit Solang Valley where Himachal\u2019s best ski slopes can be found( here you can enjoy paragliding, horse-riding, scooter riding etc. on direct payment basis). The rest of the day is free to explore this scenic town, Overnight stay at Hotel.\n\n\n\n\nDay 4 :Manali Local & Manikaran \u2013 Kasol Valley \u2013 Kullu\n\n\nMorning After breakfast visit Famous Kullu- Manikaran- Kasol Valley, evening free. Night stay in Manali.\nThe Kullu- is spread in the entire Kullu valley which is lavishly gifted with superb scenic wealth. Kullu also was known as \u2018Valley of Gods\u2019 has numerous temples. Kullu valley offers a scenic charm of peaceful wooded glades and rivers through the rocks. The Dussehra of Kullu is world famous. The ancient Hindus regarded Kullu as the farthest limit of human habitation \u2018Kulanta Pitha\u2019 and its original name finds mention in the epics, The Ramayana and Mahabharat as well as the Vishnu Purana. Kullu, which is located on the bank of river Beas is the Central point of this tourist complex. Running North to South, the main river valley is only 80 km. long and 2 km. at its broadest, yet a fairly wide area is open to the visitors to enjoy the spectacle of variegated mountain scenery. The deodar-fringed grassy Maidan, Dhalpur, is a stage for many colorful fairs.\n\n\n\n\nDay 5 :Manali \u2013 Shimla\n\n\nMorning After breakfast transfer you to catch your deluxe bus from Manali to Shimla, capital of Britishers also set amidst, the snow copper, Shivalik, mountains which offer some of the most beautiful views of Himalaya where on arrival, you will check into your hotel. The rest of the evening is at leisure. Night stay in Shimla.\n\n\n\n\nDay 6 :In Shimla\n\n\nMorning proceeds for the sightseeing Shimla covering Kalbadevi Temple, Jakhu Temple, Hanuman Temple or stop for a while at the beautiful stained-glass-windows of Christ Church, which was built in the 1850s. Afternoon excursion to Kufri a 30 Minutes\u2019 drive from Shimla, an exotica of nature as a place surrounded by dense forest and snow capped mountains amidst virgin peaks and natures flora and fauna where one can completely relax and tune oneself for natural beauty, Evening free to enjoy the scenic beauty of Kufri. Fagu, Indira Gandhi Holiday Home and enjoy horse riding in the apple orchids. Return to the Hotel Rest of the day is free to explore various scenic sights or visit mall road and shopping. Night stay at Hotel.\n\n\n\n\nDay 7 :Shimla \u2013 Delhi\n\n\nMorning Proceed to Shimla Volvo stand at morning at 8.15 AM. Drive to Delhi, evening on arrival at Delhi, we will pick you and transfer to the hotel. Overnight stay at Delhi.\n\n\n\n\nDay 8 :Delhi City Tour\n\n\nToday we are fully packed for Delhi Local city tour including lotus temple, Akshardham temple, Chandni Chowk market, Qutub Minar etc. overnight stay at Delhi.\n\n\n\n\nDay 9 :Delhi Departure\n\n\nAfter breakfast, we will drop you at airport/ railway station for your onward journey.",
    "highlights": [
      "A visit to the Rohtang Pass",
      "Manali town tour",
      "Covering the Kasol Valley and Kulu",
      "Shimla sightseeing",
      "Delhi city tour",
      "Enjoying the local delicacies",
      "Best accommodation and Volvo booking"
    ],
