  "honeymoon-in-goa": {
    "overview": "Goa is known for being a wholesome blend of Portuguese culture and Indian heritage. This tiny colorful town is lined by numerous relaxing beaches and offers the travelers with a wide option of food and fun activities. If you are a newlywed couple looking for places to spend a memorable honeymoon then this Goa honeymoon tour package of 4 days and 3 nights will definitely do the trick.\n\nGoa Honeymoon Tour Itinerary Package\n\n\nDay 1 :Arrival in Goa\n\n\nUpon arriving at Goa, you will be escorted to your hotel where you will freshen up and get ready to explore the nearby place on your own. The evening will be free for you to spend some quality and rejuvenating time by the beach before heading back to your hotel.\nYou will be free to try out some local Goan cuisines here like, the famous Goan prawn curry, Balchao, Chicken Cafreal, kul kul (sweet) among others.\n\n\n\n\nDay 2 :North Goa Sightseeing Tour\n\n\nYour North Goa sightseeing tour will commence in the morning where you will be taken across some of the fascinating destinations in the northern part of Goa. Starting with a visit to the delightful city of Mapusa, which is a Portuguese influenced colorful town which is famous for its vibrant market places from where you can buy all sorts of products. Here you will be made to visit St. Jerome church, Bodgeshwar Mandir and Maruti Mandir.\nLater in the afternoon you will be made to visit the famous beaches in Goa which are Anjuna, Vagator, Calangute and more where you and your loved one can relax by the beach and spend some quality time together. Before returning to the room you have the option of having a delicious traditional Goan dinner.\n\n\n\n\nDay 3 :South Goa Sightseeing Tour\n\n\nAfter having your breakfast you will depart for a tour of South Goa. You will be made to experience some of the fabulous beaches here starting with Miramar and Dona Paula. After spending some quality time relaxing with your loved one you will be taken to one of the most prime attractions here, Bom Jesus Basilica. Later you will be driven to Mangueshi temple which is the largest and one of the most frequented temples here.\nYou will then be taken to Colva beach where you will enjoy the beautiful sun setting in the horizon before going for a cruise on Mandovi. The cruise will include dinner, drinks, live music and a dance floor. You will then return to your hotel after spending some memorable time with your better half.\n\n\n\n\nDay 4 :Goa Departure\n\n\nEarly in the morning, after breakfast, you will be escorted to your departure destination of either the railway station or the airport from where you will head towards your onward destination.",
    "highlights": [],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1 :Arrival in Goa",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 2 :North Goa Sightseeing Tour",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 3 :South Goa Sightseeing Tour",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 4 :Goa Departure",
        "description": ""
      }
    ],
    "faqs": []
  },
  "honeymoon-in-kashmir": {
    "overview": "Newly married? Looking for a place to spend your honeymoon calmly? Then Kashmir which is the mini Switzerland of India will be your preferred destination of choice. My Quick Trippers offers you a honeymoon in Kashmir tour package of 6 days and 5 days where you and your loved one can ignite your love and spend some quality time together away from the crowd.\n\nKashmir Honeymoon Tour Itinerary Package\n\n\nDay 1 :Arrival in Srinagar\n\n\nYou will be arriving in Srinagar where our tour representative will transfer you to a houseboat or a hotel, where you can rest and relax in the afternoon. During the evening you will be taken for a Shikara ride on the calm lake which will be extremely soothing. You will also witness the mesmerizing floating island and lotus gardens which are present inside the lake. As the sun sets, you will be taken back to your hotel for an overnight stay.\n\n\n\n\nDay 2 :Srinagar \u2013 Gulmarg \u2013 Khilanmarg \u2013 Srinagar\n\n\nYour journey towards the breathtaking town of Gulmarg will commence in the morning after breakfast. After covering a distance of 1 hour and 40 mines you will be reaching Gulmarg, where you will be made to leave for Khilanmarg which is accessible through a cable car ride, from where you will be able to view the unparalleled beauty of Kashmir Valley. You are free to indulge in a pony ride in the open meadows where there is a lake \u2013 which remains frozen till the month of June.\nFinally, you will be driven back to Srinagar for night stay.\n\n\n\n\nDay 3 :Gulmarg \u2013 Pahalgam\n\n\nYour full day trip to Pahalgam will commence early in the morning. Upon covering a 3 hours journey to this enthralling destination on the hills you will be duly checked in to your hotel, where you will be spending the night. Your evening time will be free for you to stroll around on foot and buy yourself some souvenir like, shawls, carpets, willow baskets, handicrafts and so much more.\n\n\n\n\nDay 4 :Pahalgam Sightseeing\n\n\nYou will be taken to Chandanwari \u2013 which is located at a distance of 16 km from Pahalgam, after breakfast. This place is accessible only by a jeep or a pony which can be hired directly. It is one of the most idyllic and picturesque places which provides breathtaking views throughout the year making it the perfect place for spending your honeymoon and creating lifetime memories. Adventure seekers can opt for trekking around this region. After a day filled with fun and frolic, you will be taken back to your hotel for an overnight stay.\n\n\n\n\nDay 5 :Pahalgam \u2013 Srinagar\n\n\nAfter a leisurely morning, you will be driven to the Kashmiri capital of Srinagar \u2013 which is located at a distance of 3 hours from Pahalgam. En route you will be made to visit the 1100-year-old temple of Lord Vishnu, Awantipura. Upon arriving at Srinagar you will be checked in to your hotel or houseboat, for an overnight stay. During the afternoon you will be made to visit the temple of Shankaracharya \u2013 which is located at a whopping height of 1,000 feet above sea level and is dedicated to Lord Shiva along with paying a visit to the vibrant Mughal gardens \u2013 whose beauty cannot be compared.\n\n\n\n\nDay 6 :Srinagar Departure\n\n\nYour honeymoon tour package of Kashmir will commence today after you are transferred to the airport, from where you will head on towards your preferred destination.",
    "highlights": [],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1 :Arrival in Srinagar",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 2 :Srinagar \u2013 Gulmarg \u2013 Khilanmarg \u2013 Srinagar",
