  "hyderabad-sightseeing-tour": {
    "overview": "The city of pearls, Hyderabad, is well known for being culturally rich and historically magnificent which makes it one of the prime centers of tourist attraction in the subcontinent. We bring to you the opportunity to explore this heritage land through our Hyderabad with Ramoji film city tour package which lasts for 4 days and 3 nights. Have a divine experience at this southern wonderland which is the perfect representation of the bygone era and the present age.\n\nHyderabad Sightseeing Tour Itinerary Package\n\n\nDay 1 :Arrival Hyderabad\n\n\nOnce you arrive in Hyderabad, you will be assisted by our tour representative for your brief sightseeing tour of Hyderabad city starting with a visit to the beautiful monument of Char Minar \u2013 a global landmark for Hyderabad which was constructed in 1591. This iconic UNESCO world heritage site structure is also a place where numerous local festivities are held since it also houses a mosque. You will further be assisted to your next location of Qutub Shahi tombs \u2013 located close to the glorious Golconda fort, which were built by the various kings and rulers of the Qutub Shahi dynasty in the south.\nYou will then be taken to your hotel for an where you will be staying the night.\n\n\n\n\nDay 2 :Hyderabad City Sightseeing Tour\n\n\nYou will be taken on your city-wide sightseeing tour of Hyderabad post breakfast where you will be covering places like \u2013 the famous and majestic Birla Mandir which is dedicated to Lord Vishnu and is perched at an elevation of 280 feet above sea level allowing you to have a panoramic view of the city below. You will then be taken to the famous Salarjung museum \u2013 which is home to numerous historical artifacts like daggers and other weapons of cultural importance.\nYou will then be taken for a boat ride at the panoramic and pristine Hussain Sagar Lake \u2013 which is home to a massive 57 feet tall Buddhist structure. After a fun and memorable boat Ride you will be assisted to the colorfully enchanting Lumbini gardens. Then finally after a fun packed day you will be escorted back to your allotted hotel for an overnight stay.\n\n\n\n\nDay 3 :Hyderabad \u2013 Ramoji Film City\n\n\nAfter the completion of your breakfast, you will be taken on a fun packed visit to Ramoji film city \u2013 where a number of movies were shot including Hindi, Telugu, Kannada, Bengali and Malayalam. It is also known for being one of the largest integrated film studios as certified by Guinness book of world records. The entire film city is dotted with a number of natural as well as artificial entertainment options like panoramic landscapes, hotels, miniature fun centres, amusement parks and so much more. This place pans over a large area which takes up your entire day to explore.\nFinally, after a day of fun and adventure, you will be taken back to your hotel for staying the night.\n\n\n\n\nDay 4 :Hyderabad Departure\n\n\nEarly in the morning after having your breakfast, you will be taken to your departure destination where you will be boarding the plane/train which will be headed to your desired destination hence ending your trip with us.",
    "highlights": [
      "Visit to the Charminar, the UNESCO World Heritage gate",
      "Explore more history with Qutub Shahi tombs located close to the glorious Golconda fort",
      "Be a part of the entertainment industry hub of the country, Ramoji Film city",
      "Enjoy the royal Hyderabadi local dishes, relishing the yester years"
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1 :Arrival Hyderabad",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 2 :Hyderabad City Sightseeing Tour",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 3 :Hyderabad \u2013 Ramoji Film City",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 4 :Hyderabad Departure",
        "description": ""
      }
    ],
    "faqs": []
  },
