  "increasable-kerala": {
    "overview": "If you think you\u2019ve explored everything, then visit Kerala\u2019s beautiful lagoons, traditional dances, calm backwaters, and welcoming people.See More\n\nThis Incredible Kerala Tour Package shows you the best of the state. The trip takes you to Munnar, Kerala\u2019s most loved hill station. All around, the endless tea gardens will make you feel like you\u2019ve entered an untouched place.\nKundala Lake is nearby and one of the best spot to relax and enjoy views. Alleppey is famous for its backwaters and beaches, where many visitors love spending time on a houseboat, surrounded by coconut trees. You will also visit Eravikulam National Park where you can see rare Nilgiri Tahr, a mountain goat that is very hard to spot elsewhere.\nThe park is full of Nilgiri Langurs, deer, and wild boars. Sometimes, you may see leopards, jungle cats, or even elephants, which can be adventurous for animal lovers. Over 4,000 travellers have explored Kerala with us and returned with happy memories. Our 4 Days Incredible Kerala trip plan helps you enjoy the perfect mix of nature, culture and relaxation. This journey creates memorable experiences for anyone who wants to explore real charm of Kerala.\n\nThis Incredible Kerala Tour Package shows you the best of the state. The trip takes you to Munnar, Kerala\u2019s most loved hill station. All around, the endless tea gardens will make you feel like you\u2019ve entered an untouched place.\n\nKundala Lake is nearby and one of the best spot to relax and enjoy views. Alleppey is famous for its backwaters and beaches, where many visitors love spending time on a houseboat, surrounded by coconut trees. You will also visit Eravikulam National Park where you can see rare Nilgiri Tahr, a mountain goat that is very hard to spot elsewhere.",
    "highlights": [
      "Explore Munnar\u2019s scenic tea gardens, Mattupetty and Kundala Lake and Eravikulam National Park to see rare Nilgiri Tahr and enjoy peaceful nature.",
      "Relax in Alleppey on calm backwaters, take a sunset cruise, visit the beach, explore local markets or spend a night on a traditional houseboat with fresh meals.",
      "Enjoy the best of Cochin by seeing St. Francis Church, Dutch Palace, Jewish Synagogue, colorful markets and traditional Chinese fishing nets.",
      "Experience perfect mix of nature, culture and relaxation to make your 4 days Kerala trip truly memorable and enjoyable."
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1: Cochin- Munnar (131 Km/03 hrs)",
        "description": "Start your\nKerala tour\nas our\nMy Quick Trippers team\nmeets you at Cochin Airport or railway station and takes you to\nMunnar\n, one of\nKerala\u2019s most popular hill station\n. If a guide is included, they will travel with the driver and help you whenever needed.\nOn the way, enjoy-\nStunning scenery\nwith\nrivers\nand\nwaterfalls\nthat make the place truly magical.\nGreen hills\nand\nforests\nBeautifully arranged tea and spice\ngardens\nwith a fresh, delightful fragrance all around.\nWhen you reach Munnar check into your hotel and rest. Feel free to explore the surroundings whenever you like. Stay overnight in Munnar.\nNote -\nKeep some cash; not all places accept cards or digital payments during journey."
      },
      {
        "title": "DAY 2: Munnar Sightseeing",
        "description": "After breakfast explore\nMunnar\n, a peaceful hill station with beautiful scenery.\nSee the well-known\ntea gardens\nand walk through the green tea fields. Learn how tea leaves are grown, picked, and prepared, while also enjoying the calm surroundings (a great photography spot).\nNext, go to\nMattupetty Lake\nand\nDam\n, a popular place for boating (optional) and surrounded by scenic hills.\nVisit\nEcho Point\nand hear your voice bounce back- a fun spot for everyone.\nVisit\nKundala Lake\n, perfect for relaxing and enjoying a picnic.\nLater, go to\nRajamalai (Eravikulam National Park)\nand see the rare goat\nNilgiri Tahr\nand known for its unique plants and animals.\nAfter a day of sightseeing return to your hotel and relax. Spend the night in\nMunnar\n.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "DAY 3: Munnar - Alleppey (Houseboat) (176 Kms/4-5 Hrs)",
        "description": "After breakfast, check out of your hotel in\nMunnar\nand travel to\nAlleppey\n. The town is well-known for its beautiful backwaters, small rivers, and green paddy fields.\nWhen you reach, go to your hotel and check in.\nOption 1- Stay at Hotel\nIn the evening, enjoy a sunset cruise on\nVembanad Lake\n(optional, at your own cost) and watch the beautiful sunset (Don't miss to click photos).\nSpend some time on\nAlleppey Beach\n, take a relaxing walk, and get a massage treatment there if you wish.\nGo to the\nlocal markets\nfor shopping, purchase handmade items, and try delicious local food.\nReturn to your hotel for an overnight stay in\nAlleppey\n.\nOption 2- Houseboat Stay\nWhen you arrive, check into your traditional\nKettuvallam (houseboat).\nEnjoy a peaceful houseboat ride through Kerala\u2019s backwaters, see the daily life of villagers, and the green paddy fields that make this journey truly special (try to make videos).\nHave freshly prepared meals served on the\nhouseboat\nincluding dinner.\nOvernight stay on the houseboat for a new experience.\nNote-\nMosquitoes may be present during houseboat trips. Carry a mild insect repellent, like lotion or spray, to stay comfortable and enjoy the ride.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "DAY 4: Alleppey - Cochin Airport (53 Kms/1 hrs)",
        "description": "Check out of your hotel after breakfast and travel to Cochin to continue your trip.\nOptional -\nEnjoy a sightseeing tour of Cochin-\nExplore\nJewish Synagogue\nin\nCochin\nand learn about the Jewish community.\nVisit the Dutch Palace (\nMattancherry Palace\n) and see its beautiful paintings showing stories from the Ramayana and Mahabharata.\nExplore\nSt. Francis Church\n, full of history and one of India\u2019s oldest European church.\nGo to the beach near\nFort Kochi\nand see people use\nChinese fishing nets\nto catch fish.\nExplore the markets in\nCochin\nand shop for handmade items and local products.\nLater transfer to the airport, bus station, or railway station for your departure.\nWe hope you enjoyed your\n4 days Kerala trip\nand made great memories!\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      }
    ],
    "faqs": []
  },
  "incredible-himachal-tour": {
    "overview": "Himachal is popular for its majestic, unparalleled beauty and one of the most preferred weekend getaway destinations for nearby cities. Admire the beauty of the hills in its full vigor with My Quick Trippers\u2019s Glorious Himachal tour package. For 10 days and 9 nights indulge in some peaceful solitude and gaze at the untouched wonders that the hills have to offer.\n\nIncredible Himachal Tour Itinerary Package\n\n\nDay 1 :Arrival in Delhi \u2013 Shimla\n\n\nUpon your arrival in Delhi, you will be transferred to one of the most popular tourist destinations in India \u2013 Shimla. After covering a journey of 9 hours you will be immediately checked in to your hotel for an overnight stay. The remaining of the evening is free for doing your leisure activities.\n\n\n\n\nDay 2 :Shimla \u2013 Kufri (Excursion)\n\n\nYou will be taken on a city-wide excursion of Shimla which will cover sites like, Kalbadevi mandir \u2013 which is dedicated to goddess Kalbadevi; Jakhu temple \u2013 dedicated to Lord Hanuman and Christ church \u2013 the second oldest church in northern India.\nYou will then be taken for an excursion at the neighboring town of Kufri \u2013 which is 30 mines. Drive from the main town of Shimla. You will then be taken to Fagu Indira Gandhi holiday home where you can enjoy a fun horse riding experience among the vast expanse of apple orchids. You are also free to explore the nearby colorful market places.\nAfter a day of fun and admiring the natural beauty you will then be taken back to your allotted hotel in Shimla for the night.\n\n\n\n\nDay 3 :Shimla \u2013 Kullu \u2013 Manali\n\n\nEarly in the morning your journey for Manali will commence, which will be a 7 hours and 20 mines journey. En route, after 5 hours and 30 mines you will be made to stop and admire the charm of Kullu. Kullu is known as the \u2018valley of gods\u2019 because of the presence of numerous temples that stud the region. After enjoying and taking pictures of some of the most scenic places in Kullu like Dussehra Maidan and Beas River, you will be headed on towards Manali, where you will be duly Cheeked in to your allotted hotel and spend the night there.\n\n\n\n\nDay 4 :Manali \u2013 Rohtang Pass\n\n\nEarly in the morning you will made to proceed for a day time excursion of Rohtang pass (Pir Panjal Himalayas) \u2013 a snow clad mountain pass which remains covered by snow throughout the year. In case due to certain reasons the pass is closed off, you will be taken to snow point, which is equally fun and quirky. Here you will be able to enjoy activities like, paragliding, horse riding etc. (all this will be done on the basis of direct payment).\nYou will then be taken back to Manali from where you will be free to explore this town on your own in the evening. Be sure to buy some whimsical and unique souvenirs from here like, woolen apparels, hand-woven carpets, rugs, traditional jewellery and so much more. You will be spending the night in Manali.\n\n\n\n\nDay 5 :Manali \u2013 Dharamshala\n\n\nToday early in the morning you will be made to proceed towards the scenic hill town of Dharamshala which will be a journey of 7 hours and 30 mines. Upon your arrival and after getting checked in to your hotel you will you will be free to do your leisurely activities.\nShop for local souvenir items like, woolen apparels, locally produced wooden artifacts, special local paintings called Thangkas, Dorjes (puja ritual object), Kullu shawls, Tibetan rugs and so much more.\nAlong with mesmerizing landscapes, food here is also delectable. You can try out some locally made cuisines like, Tibetan momos, thukpa, Lang Phing (turmeric flavored pancake), Bulgogi, Belgian waffles and Mani more.\n\n\n\n\nDay 6 :Dharamshala Local Sightseeing \u2013 Dalhousie\n\n\nYou will be made to proceed for an excursion of Mcleodganj \u2013 a suburb of Dharamshala which is also known as \u2018little Tibet\u2019 and home to Dalai Lama. It is located at a distance of just half an hour from the main town of Dharamshala. Here you will be made to visit the following local attractions in Dharamshala. Bhagsu temple and waterfall \u2013 An important place of worship for people belonging to Hindu as well as Gorkha communities; One can also take a dip in the water to cool off and freshen up; your next stop will be Kareri Lake \u2013 a freshwater high altitude, crystal clear lake; Naddi viewpoint \u2013 from where you can admire the surrounding snowcapped peaks, a thrill for every photographer and nature lover.\nLater after this, you will be taken to Dalhousie, which is at a distance of 3 hours and 30 mines. You will be immediately checked in to your hotel where you will be spending the night.\n\n\n\n\nDay 7 :Dalhousie \u2013 Khajjiar (Excursion)\n\n\nYou will be taken to Khajjiar, early in the morning, which is located at a distance of 1 hour and is also known as the mini Switzerland of Himachal which is nestled at the foothills of Dhauladhar ranges and amongst the thick covering of pine and deodar forests. Here you will be made to visit Kalatop Khajjiar sanctuary \u2013 this picturesque animal sanctuary is located on the path of River Ravi, and is surrounded by coniferous and oak tree forest. After a refreshing visit here, you will be made to proceed towards Chamba, a quaint hilly hamlet known for its medieval temples and breathtaking views.\nYou will finally be made to proceed back to Dalhousie where you will be spending the night.\n\n\n\n\nDay 8 :Dalhousie \u2013 Amritsar\n\n\nYou will be taken on a local sightseeing tour of Dalhousie including places like; St. John\u2019s church, St. Patrick\u2019s church and Chamera Dam, which are some of the prime places of tourist attraction in Dalhousie.\nYou will then be made to proceed towards Amritsar, which will be a journey of 4 hours and 30 mines. you will be made to be a part of the procedures that take place in Wagah border, after which you will be duly checked in to your hotel for staying the night.\n\n\n\n\nDay 9 :Amritsar Local Sightseeing \u2013 Chandigarh\n\n\nEarly in the morning after completing your breakfast, you will be taken on a local sightseeing tour of the city starting with a visit to the sacred Golden Temple \u2013 one of the most vital Sikh Shrines in India. You will also be taken to Harmandir Sahib and Darbar Sahib which are two of the other most important shrines in Amritsar. You will then be made to visit Jallianwala Bagh \u2013 one of the most heart-wrenching places any Indian can ever experience in their lifetime. You will later be transferred to Chandigarh, which is located at a distance of 4 hours and 15 mines.\nYou will be checked in to your hotel here for staying the night.\n\n\n\n\nDay 10 :Chandigarh (Local Sightseeing) \u2013 Delhi (Departure)\n\n\nEarly in the morning, you will be made to visit some of the local attractions in Chandigarh, like Sukhna Lake \u2013 where you can go for boating and enjoy the calming views; Rock garden will be your next destination \u2013 where the entire area is dotted with unique rock sculpture.\nAfter a brief sightseeing of the city you will be transferred to Delhi, which is located at a distance of 4 hours and 10 mines. You will then be made to board the train heading towards your onward destination.",
    "highlights": [
      "Shimla city tour and visit to Kufri",
      "Get the blessings at the Kalbadevi and Jakhu Temple",
      "Kullu and Manali Trip",
      "Tour to Rohtang pass",
      "Have the touch of divinity at Dharamshala, the house of his lord. Dalai Lama",
      "Excursion to Mcleodganj",
      "Dalhousie tour",
      "Khajjiar excursion",
      "Amritsar and Chandigarh sightseeing",
      "Enjoying local cuisines of the region"
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1 :Arrival in Delhi \u2013 Shimla",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 2 :Shimla \u2013 Kufri (Excursion)",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 3 :Shimla \u2013 Kullu \u2013 Manali",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 4 :Manali \u2013 Rohtang Pass",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 5 :Manali \u2013 Dharamshala",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 6 :Dharamshala Local Sightseeing \u2013 Dalhousie",
