  "indore-sightseeing-tour": {
    "overview": "Indore is the largest of cities in the state of Madhya Pradesh and stands along the banks of two rivers; River Khan and River Saraswati. Indore enjoys the reputation of being the state\u2019s most planned cities. The city is steeped in various architectural marvels & rich history. The city also enjoys the reputation of the state\u2019s \u2018commercial capital\u2019. Whether you are a history buff or a Nature lover, Indore has everything in it to satiate your wander lust. In other words, the city can indeed let you enjoy, unwind, admire and learn all at the same time. If you wish to explore this incredible city, make sure to embark on our 2 Nights / 3 Days Indore tour.\n\nIndore Sightseeing Tour Itinerary Package\n\n\nDay 1 :Arrive Indore & Go On A City Tour\n\n\nOn reaching Indore railway station, you will be taken to your pre-booked hotel. After checking in and freshening up we proceed for a short city tour of Indore visiting places like Khajrana Ganesh Mandir, Lal Bagh Palace, Kanch Mandir, Rajwada, Central Museum and Chokhi Dhani. The first of our sightseeing destinations for the day; Khajrana Ganesh Mandir is one of the most opulent Ganesh temples of the country and was constructed under the initiative of Rani Ahilyabai Holkar of the Holkar Dynasty. The deity of Lord Ganesha enshrined here has eyes encrusted with diamonds. After paying our tribute to Lord Ganesha at the temple, we proceed to visit our next sightseeing destination; the Lal Bagh Palace, the once upon a time royal residence of the kings of the Holkar dynasty. \nThe palace covers an area of about 28 acres and stands out as a real edifice of unmatched grandeur. After palace visit, we move on to our next destination for the day; the Kanch Mandir; a famed Jain Temple of Indore built by Seth Hukumchand Jain which is made out of glass. It exhibits marvelous detailing on the glasses and beautifully adorned glass panels portraying the various aspects pertaining to Jainism. Next, we visit the Rajwada palace; a 7 storied monument of unrivalled grandeur. \nThe architecture of this opulent palace dating back to nearly 200 years is a fine fusion of Maratha, Mughal and French architectures. After Rajwada we move on to our next stop; Central Museum also called as Indore Museum. This is a dual galleried museum showcasing artifacts dating back to 5000 BC. After Central Museum, we visit our next and last destination for the day; Chokhi Dhani; an ethnic resort village allowing us to get a sneak peek into the authentic culture and traditions of the region. The activities you can enjoy at the village are camel rides, puppet shows, elephant rides, magic shows, Folk dances. After having visited Chokhi Dhani we\u2019ll return to hotel for dinner and night stay.\n\n\n\n\nDay 2 :Rest of Sightseeing & Go Shopping\n\n\nNext day post breakfast we proceed for the rest of the sightseeing of Indore, visiting places such as Chhatris, Mahatma Gandhi Hall, Nehru Park and Patalpani. Today we start our city tour by visiting the Chhatris which were the cremation grounds of the kings and queens of the Holkar dynasty. The Chhatris come with intricate adornments and several temples constructed around them. Next, we visit the Mahatma Gandhi Hall; a magnificent town hall constructed by famed architect Mr. Charles Frederick Stevens in an Indo-Gothic architectural style. Previously, referred to as \u2018King Edward Hall\u2019, it was renamed as Mahatma Gandhi Hall in the year 1948. After Gandhi Hall, we proceed to visit the Nehru Park; a centrally located Children\u2019s park dating back to the pre-independence era.\nThe park comes with verdant greenery, variety of trees and flowering plants, a swimming pool and many wonderful rides such as mini train, battery run cars etc. After Nehru Park, we move towards Patalpani; the last of our Indore sightseeing destinations. Patalpani Waterfalls is a scenic destination with a roaring waterfall toppling down from about 300 meters height. The waterfall is located amid dense verdure and is an ideal photo stopover in Indore. Post sightseeing we return to hotel for lunch and rest. In the evening we go for some shopping in one of the most happening shopping hubs of Indore; the Sarafa Bazaar. It is an iconic jewelry market of Indore consisting in several stalls selling vibrantly colored imitation jewelries and brassware. Also, a plethora of street foods sold here make Sarafa bazaar a foodie\u2019s paradise.\n\n\n\n\nDay 3 :Indore Departure\n\n\nPost breakfast we will move towards Indore Railway Station from where your trip with us ends. We hope that you must had an enjoyable journey with myriads of sweet memories.",
    "highlights": [
      "The best tourists spots of Indore",
      "A visit to Khajrana Ganesh Mandir, Lal Bagh Palace, Kanch Mandir, Rajwada, Central Museum and Chokhi Dhani",
      "Pay your homage to the Khajrana Ganesh Mandir",
      "Visit the Lal Bagh Palace, Kanch Mandir, Rajwada, Central Museum and Chokhi Dhani",
      "Visit Mahatma Gandhi Hall, Nehru Park, Patalpani",
      "Go for shopping at the Sarafa Bazaar an iconic jewelry market and street food market of Indore"
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1 :Arrive Indore & Go On A City Tour",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 2 :Rest of Sightseeing & Go Shopping",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 3 :Indore Departure",
        "description": ""
      }
    ],
    "faqs": []
  },
  "indore-to-ujjain-omkareshwar-tour": {
    "overview": "If you\u2019re looking for a spiritual visit that is abundantly laced with temple visits, trip to serene Ghats, and spending time close to the holy rivers, then this trip is for you! See More\n\nFrom visiting the very Jyotirlingas to taking part in the holy Narmada Parikrama, this tour of faith is sure to add immensely to your spiritual merits. Another attraction of this tour is that we\u2019ll take you to not one, but two Jyotirlingas of the Mahakaleshwar Temple and Omkareshwar! Book this Indore Ujjain Omkareshwar Tour now, or simply give us a call!Are you wondering what all is included in this tour package? Well, for starters, we\u2019ll take special care of your accommodation. We only assign quality, comfy hotels to our customers. In addition, all your dining\u2013related bills are also on us. To ensure smooth and comfortable transfers within the city, we\u2019ll provide you with an experienced driver who will take care of all your transport needs. So think no more, this trip really has a lot for you. Book now!See Less\n\nFrom visiting the very Jyotirlingas to taking part in the holy Narmada Parikrama, this tour of faith is sure to add immensely to your spiritual merits. Another attraction of this tour is that we\u2019ll take you to not one, but two Jyotirlingas of the Mahakaleshwar Temple and Omkareshwar! Book this Indore Ujjain Omkareshwar Tour now, or simply give us a call!\n\nAre you wondering what all is included in this tour package? Well, for starters, we\u2019ll take special care of your accommodation. We only assign quality, comfy hotels to our customers. In addition, all your dining\u2013related bills are also on us. To ensure smooth and comfortable transfers within the city, we\u2019ll provide you with an experienced driver who will take care of all your transport needs. So think no more, this trip really has a lot for you. Book now!",
    "highlights": [
      "Visit to two Jyotirlingas of Lord Shiva \u2013 Mahakaleshwar in Ujjain and Omkareshwar",
      "Attend evening Aarti at Mahakaleshwar Temple",
      "Explore Ujjain\u2019s popular temples like Harsiddhi Temple, Bade Ganesh Ka Mandir, Shakti Peeth, and ISKCON Temple.",
      "Walk through the magnificent Mahakal Lok Corridor in Ujjain",
      "Trip to the serene Ram Ghat",
      "Enjoy holy dips in the Narmada River",
      "Explore the ancient Mamleshwar Temple",
      "Experience the 7 km long Narmada Parikrama",
      "Enjoy boat ride on the Narmada River",
      "Visit to the grand monument of Adi Shankaracharya \u2013 The Statue of Oneness",
      "Explore the historic Ahilya Bai Fort in Maheshwar",
      "Visit the serene Akhileshwar Temple",
      "Discover the heritage town of Maheshwar, known for its ghats, temples & handloom saris",
      "See More"
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1: Arrival in Indore - Maheshwar - Omkareshwar - Ujjain (Approx. 300 km - 10 hrs)",
        "description": "Our tour representative will give you a warm welcome once you arrive at the Indore airport/railway station.\nNow, you\u2019ll be taken to Maheshwar, where you\u2019ll visit:\nMahakaleshwar temple\nAhilya Bai Fort and Palace\nAkhileshwar Temple (inside fort complex)\nNarmada Ghat (for boating)\nNow, proceed towards Omkareshwar, another Jyotirlinga of Lord Shiva). Once you get there, be in awe of the town, which is in the shape of an 'Om' symbol.\nTake holy dips in the Narmada River first, before proceeding towards the Omkareshwar temple. Have Darshan to your heart\u2019s content and seek the Lord\u2019s blessings in return.\nLater, you\u2019ll be taken to the ancient Mamleshwar temple. This temple has its walls engraved with sacred inscriptions, dating back to 1063 AD! It was once given patronage by Maharani Ahilyabai Holkar, and today, it\u2019s a protected monument of ASI.\nNow, get ready for Parikrama around the Narmada River. This 7 km circular journey on the stairs lets you enjoy views of several temples and ashrams along the way. Also, enjoy the beauty of the Hanging Bridge over the Narmada River.\nIn the evening, take one last stop again at the Jyotirlinga Mahakaleshwar temple to attend its mesmerizing Aarti (if time permits)!\nNow, you\u2019ll be driven towards Ujjain for the overnight stay.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 2: Ujjain - Indore - (54 km 1- 1.5 hrs)",
        "description": "Enjoy a hearty meal at breakfast.\nAfterwards, you\u2019ll be taken for a sightseeing tour in the holy city of Ujjain, where you\u2019ll visit:\nMahakaleshwar temple\nISKCON temple\nShakti Peeth\nHarsiddhi Temple\nSandipani Ashram\nBade Ganesh Ka Mandir\nRam Ghat\nFinally, our representative will transfer you to Indore airport/railway station (as per your preference), from where you can continue your further journey. Hope you made great memories!\nNote :\nTo book Ujjain Mahakal Darshan online, visit:\nhttps://shrimahakaleshwar.com/sheeghra-darshan\n.\nNote :\nTo book Mahakal Bhasma aarti online, visit:\nhttps://shrimahakaleshwar.com/bhasmarti.\n. The Aarti lasts from 4 AM to 6 AM.\nNote :\nDuring the Sawan month, the tour may be impacted by the Kanwar Yatra, which can cause heavy\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      }
    ],
    "faqs": []
  },
