  "jagannath-puri-tour": {
    "overview": "Lord Jagannath seat in Puri is a place that offers total relaxation and spiritual calling. This site is well-known for its treasure of religious sanctuaries, historically-significant artifacts, architectural excellence, the amazing weather and the seaside beauty.\n\nAs Odisha prime coastal district, Puri beckons tourists from all the corners of the earth on a yearly basis. The Jagannath Temple is one of the biggest reasons for tourist attraction, especially during the time of 'Rath Yatra' which takes place annually. The temple architecture includes four gates for entrance namely Ashwadwara, Singhadwara, Vyaghradwara and Hatidwara signify four animals- horse, lion, tiger and elephant. The Lord 'Jagannath' is offered 'bhog' a total of six times daily and then dispensed off to the Ratnadevi worshippers. A visit to Jagannath, Puri will not only transcend you mentally but also spiritually, something you look for in a vacation. \nAbout The Package\n The 'Jagannath Puri Yatra' package offered by My Quick Trippers is an exclusive pilgrimage tour that will provide both mental and spiritual relaxation with no discomfort issues. You get to visit the Jagannath Temple and the nearby places including the sea beaches and a trip to Bhubaneswar \u2013 all included in the package. The professional experience of the My Quick Trippers is evident through the provisions made for the trip. This online travel agency also makes provision for the customization of packages if you are on a strict budget. All the necessities are taken care of during the course of your stay including your safety. My Quick Trippers strives to make sure that you get to enjoy your trip to the fullest and get what you aim for while planning a pilgrimage tour. \nAt a Glance \u2014 Jagannath Puri Tour Package\n\n\n\nDuration\n5 Days / 4 Nights\n\n\nDestinations\nBhubaneswar \u2013 Puri \u2013 Chilika \u2013 Konark \u2013 Bhubaneswar\n\n\nPrice From\nRs 12,999 per person (twin sharing)\n\n\nRath Yatra 2026\nJuly 16, 2026 | Bahuda Yatra: July 24, 2026\n\n\nBest Time\nOctober to March\n\n\nNearest Airport\nBhubaneswar (BBI) \u2014 60 km from Puri\n\n\nRailway Station\nPuri Junction \u2014 2.8 km from Jagannath Temple\n\n\n\nRath Yatra 2026 \u2014 Jagannath Puri\n\n\n\nMain Rath Yatra\nThursday, July 16, 2026\n\n\nBahuda Yatra\nFriday, July 24, 2026 (return procession)\n\n\nSuna Besha\nJuly 25, 2026 (deities adorned in gold)\n\n\nRoute\nJagannath Temple to Gundicha Temple (3 km, Bada Danda)\n\n\nChariots\n Nandighosa (Lord Jagannath) \u2014 45 ft, 16 wheels Taladhwaja (Lord Balabhadra) \u2014 45.6 ft, 14 wheels Darpadalana (Goddess Subhadra) \u2014 44.6 ft, 12 wheels \n\n\nImportant Note\nOn Rath Yatra day, temple entry is suspended \u2014 deities are on the chariot.\n\n\nBooking Advice\nBook hotels 3\u20134 months in advance for the Rath Yatra period.\n\n\n\nThings to Do in Puri & Around\nThe Jagannath Puri circuit offers far more than temple darshan. Here is what to do across all four destinations covered in this package:\n\nJagannath Temple Darshan \u2014 early morning: Arrive at the Singha Dwara before 7:00 AM on weekdays. The morning crowd is smaller, the temple priests are mid-ritual, and the atmosphere is at its most devotional.\nWatch the sunrise from Puri Beach: Puri's beach faces east \u2014 perfect for sea sunrises. The fishermen drag their boats in at dawn, the sky turns orange over the water, and the beach is almost empty. One of the better free experiences on this trip.\nEat Mahaprasad at Ananda Bazaar: Inside the Jagannath Temple complex, Ananda Bazaar is where the Lord's prasad \u2014 cooked in 752 earthen pots over wood fire \u2014 is sold to devotees from 2:00 PM. The 56 varieties of bhog served here are unlike any temple food in India.\nTake a dolphin-spotting boat ride at Chilika: Book a private boat from Satapada (approximately Rs 800-1,500 for a shared boat, Rs 2,000-3,500 for private). Go in the morning \u2014 dolphins surface more actively before 10:00 AM.\nVisit Kalijai Temple by boat: Combine with the dolphin cruise. The island temple on Chilika Lake is small but the boat crossing and the lake views make it worthwhile.\nBird watch at Nalaban (October to February): If visiting between October and February, the Nalaban Bird Sanctuary inside Chilika is unmissable. Flamingoes, painted storks, bar-headed geese, and osprey in extraordinary numbers.\nWalk through the Konark Sun Temple complex: Spend at least 90 minutes at Konark \u2014 most people rush through in 45 minutes and miss the detail. Walk around the full chariot base, study the 24 wheels (each marks the time of day), and look closely at the erotic sculpture panels, each with its own symbolic reading.\nExplore the Bhubaneswar temple circuit: Lingaraj, Mukteshwar, and Parasurameswara together form one of the finest concentrations of medieval Kalinga architecture in India. Best done in a 3-4 hour unhurried walk between temples.\nSunset at Khandagiri-Udayagiri Caves: The view from the top of Khandagiri Hill at dusk \u2014 city lights below, caves around you \u2014 is one of the quieter pleasures of Bhubaneswar. The caves themselves date to the 2nd century BCE.\nShop for Odisha handicrafts: Puri's market near Swargadwara is good for Pattachitra paintings (traditional cloth paintings with mythological scenes), Chandua patchwork, stone carvings, and conch-shell items. Prices are negotiable. Bhubaneswar's Utkalika showroom has a good fixed-price selection.\nVisit Raghurajpur Heritage Village (14 km from Puri): Raghurajpur is a traditional Odishan crafts village where every family practices a form of traditional art \u2014 Pattachitra, Gotipua dance training, Tussar silk painting. Worth a 2-hour visit if you have time on Day 2.\nTry Odishan cuisine: Dalma (lentils and vegetables cooked with coconut \u2014 Jagannath Temple's own recipe), machha jhola (mustard fish curry), pakhala bhata (fermented rice with accompaniments), and chhena poda (burnt cottage cheese dessert, invented in Odisha). Available at local restaurants near the beach.\n\nPlaces to Visit \u2014 Jagannath Puri Tour\nHere are the key places covered in this 5-day package, organised by destination:\nPuri\n\nJagannath Temple: One of the four Char Dham pilgrimages and the most sacred Vaishnava shrine in eastern India. Open to Hindu devotees only. The 65-metre Deul (main tower) is visible from across the city and from the sea.\nPuri Beach & Marine Drive: A 10-km stretch of sandy beach on the Bay of Bengal. Faces east \u2014 ideal for sunrise. The beach road (Marine Drive) connects Puri to Konark and is a pleasant drive.\nAnanda Bazaar: Inside the Jagannath Temple complex. Where the Lord's sacred Mahaprasad is sold daily from 2:00 PM. One of the largest temple kitchens in the world \u2014 752 clay pots cooked over wood fire.\nGundicha Temple: 3 km from the Jagannath Temple on Bada Danda (Grand Road). This is the 'Garden House' of Lord Jagannath \u2014 the destination of the Rath Yatra procession. Also called the 'Aunt's House'. Open to all.\nLokanatha Temple: An ancient Shiva temple near Puri beach, one of the oldest shrines in the city. Less crowded than Jagannath Temple \u2014 a peaceful visit.\nRaghurajpur Heritage Village (14 km): A protected heritage village where the entire community practices traditional Odishan arts \u2014 Pattachitra painting, Gotipua dance, Tussar silk work. One of India's best-preserved craft villages.\n\nChilika Lake (50 km from Puri)\n\nSatapada: The main gateway to Chilika Lake. Boat rides for dolphin sightings, Kalijai Temple, and Nalaban Bird Sanctuary all depart from here.\nKalijai Temple: Island shrine in the middle of Chilika Lake, dedicated to Goddess Kalijai. Reached by boat. Significant to the fishing communities of coastal Odisha.\nNalaban Bird Sanctuary: A protected island within Chilika, open October to February. Over 160 migratory species arrive from Central Asia, Siberia, and the Himalayas \u2014 including flamingoes, pelicans, and bar-headed geese.\nChandrabhaga Beach (near Konark): A quiet beach 3 km from the Konark Sun Temple, considered sacred as the point where the Chandrabhaga River meets the sea. Far less crowded than Puri Beach.\n\nKonark (35 km from Puri)\n\nKonark Sun Temple \u2014 'Black Pagoda': UNESCO World Heritage Site. A 13th-century temple designed as the chariot of the Sun God, with 24 stone wheels (each a functional sundial) and thousands of sculptures. One of the architectural masterpieces of medieval India.\n\nBhubaneswar (60 km from Puri)\n\nLingaraj Temple: The largest and most important temple in Bhubaneswar, dedicated to Lord Shiva. Built in the 11th century. The 55-metre shikhara is the tallest structure in Bhubaneswar. Open to Hindus only.\nMukteshwar Temple: 10th-century Shiva temple considered the gem of Odishan architecture. The arched torana (gateway) in front is exquisitely carved and unlike anything else in Indian temple architecture.\nParasurameswara Temple: 7th-century temple, one of the oldest surviving temples in Bhubaneswar. Famous for its ornate lattice windows and detailed stone carvings of mythological scenes.\nKhandagiri & Udayagiri Jain Caves: Twin hills with 33 rock-cut caves dating to the 2nd century BCE, commissioned by King Kharavela of the Mahameghavahana dynasty. The Ranigumpha (Queen's Cave) has some of the finest ancient relief sculpture in Odisha. Good sunset viewpoint from Khandagiri summit.\n\nPrice Details\n\n\n\nTour Name\nDuration\nDestinations\nTour Price\n\n\n\n\nJagannath Puri Tour Package\n5 Days / 4 Nights\nBhubaneswar - Konark - Puri - Chilika\nFrom Rs 12,999 per person*\n\n\n\n*Per person on twin sharing. Price varies by hotel category, group size, and season. Contact us for custom quote and group rates.\nBest Time to Visit Jagannath Puri\n\n\n\nSeason\nMonths\nSuitability\n\n\n\n\nWinter \u2014 Best\nOctober to March\nCool and pleasant (15-28\u00b0C). Ideal for Jagannath Temple darshan, Puri beach walks, Chilika bird watching, and Konark sightseeing.\n\n\nRath Yatra \u2014 Most Sacred\nJuly 16, 2026\nGrandest spiritual event. Millions of devotees. Book hotels 3-4 months in advance.\n\n\nSummer & Monsoon \u2014 Avoid\nApril to September\nHot and humid in summer. Rath Yatra falls in monsoon; otherwise travel disruptions likely.\n\n\n\nHow to Reach Puri\n\nBy Air: Biju Patnaik International Airport, Bhubaneswar (BBI) \u2014 60 km from Puri, approx. 1.5 hours by cab. Connected to Delhi, Mumbai, Kolkata, Hyderabad, and Bengaluru. Airport pickup from Bhubaneswar included in the package.\nBy Train: Puri Railway Station (PURI) is 2.8 km from the Jagannath Temple \u2014 the most convenient arrival point for pilgrims. Direct trains from Delhi (Puri Express, Utkal Express), Kolkata (Jagannath Express), and Bhubaneswar (frequent Konark Express service).\nBy Road: Puri is 60 km from Bhubaneswar on NH-316, about 1.5 hours. Konark is 35 km from Puri on the Marine Drive coastal road. OSRTC state buses and private AC coaches operate regularly on the Bhubaneswar-Puri route.\n\nJagannath Temple Puri \u2014 Important Visitor Information\n\nEntry: Shree Jagannath Temple is open to Hindu devotees only. Non-Hindu visitors may view the deities from the rooftop of the Raghunandan Library, located directly opposite the Singha Dwara (Lion Gate \u2014 main entrance).\nDarshan Timings (SJTA): Temple opens at 5:30 AM. Morning darshan: 5:30-7:30 AM (Jagamohana), 9:15-11:00 AM (Natamandir), 11:00 AM-1:00 PM. Afternoon: 2:00-5:30 PM. Evening: 8:00-10:00 PM. Timings change on festival days \u2014 verify at shreejagannatha.in before visiting.\nNo phones or cameras: Mobile phones, cameras, and leather items (belts, wallets) are not permitted inside. Free storage stands available at the Lion Gate.\nDress code: Men: dhoti or formal trousers (no shorts). Women: saree or salwar kameez. No sleeveless or revealing clothing.\nMahaprasad: Available at Ananda Bazaar inside the temple from approximately 2:00 PM. Non-Hindus may purchase it from outside the temple premises.\nSenior citizens: Free battery-operated vehicles run from Jagannath Ballav Parking to the temple main gate for senior citizens and physically challenged devotees.\n\nBook Your Jagannath Puri Yatra Tour Package\nPlan your pilgrimage to Puri with My Quick Trippers \u2014 Ministry of Tourism, Government of India approved operator. Our 5-day package covers Jagannath Temple darshan, Chilika Lake, Konark Sun Temple, and Bhubaneswar \u2014 fully customizable for families, senior citizens, and groups.\nCall or WhatsApp +91-9711616316 with your travel dates, group size, and budget. We will have your Puri yatra itinerary ready within hours.",
    "highlights": [
      "Visit to the famous Jagannath Mandir \u2014 one of the four Char Dham pilgrimage sites of India",
      "Local market tour",
      "Drive to the beautiful Chilika Lake",
      "Visit the Isles of Hillocks, Kalijai Temple and the Dolphin sighting at Satapada",
      "Visit the Konark Sun Temple, the Black Pagoda of India \u2014 a UNESCO World Heritage Site",
      "Mahaprasad experience at Ananda Bazaar inside the Jagannath Temple complex"
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1 :Arrival in Bhubaneswar - Transfer to Puri (56 km)",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 2 :Puri - Jagannath Temple Darshan & Local Sightseeing",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 3 :Puri - Chilika Lake - Puri (50 km each way)",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 4 :Puri - Konark - Bhubaneswar (75 km approximately)",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 5 :Bhubaneswar - Departure",
        "description": ""
