  },
  "jaipur-sightseeing-tour": {
    "overview": "Also known as \u2018pink city\u2019, Jaipur is popular for its traditional Rajasthani lifestyles and age-old iconic structures and opulent palaces. This colorfully vibrant city is replete with some of the most majestic and legendary landmarks which is visited by numerous international, national and domestic tourists on a daily basis. We bring you a carefully curated package of Jaipur sightseeing tour of 3 days and 2 nights which will make you experience authentic Jaipur.\n\nJaipur Sightseeing Tour Itinerary Package\n\n\nDay 1 :Arrival in Jaipur\n\n\nOnce you arrive in Jaipur our tour representative will greet you and guide you to your allotted hotel. You will be relaxing and freshening up in the hotel for a while before heading out. You will then be taken for a brief sightseeing tour of Jaipur which will cover the following place; Nahargarh Fort which was built in 1734 and stands majestically on the edge of Aravalli Hills which overlooks the entire city of Jaipur and Birla Mandir which is a part of all the other group of Birla temples which is spread across the country.\nIn the evening, you have the option of either exploring the nearby marketplaces or visit Chokhi Dhani \u2013 a luxury heritage property which showcases the Rajasthani culture, which will be done at your own expense. After a soulful exploration day you will be taken back to your hotel for an overnight stay.\n\n\n\n\nDay 2 :Jaipur City Tour\n\n\nAfter having your breakfast in the morning your full day sightseeing tour of Jaipur will commence where you will be taken to the following places: Amer fort \u2013 considered to be one of the prime tourist attraction in Jaipur this fort is perched on a hill which represents the classical Hindu architecture. You will also be made to indulge in a fun elephant safari of the fort. After an exploration of the fort, you will be taken to Kanak Vrindavan garden which is built in a valley and is surrounded by the Aravalli hills. You will then be taken to Hawa Mahal which is also known as the palace of winds due to the presence of 953 small windows. Post lunch you will be taken to city palace \u2013 which was built in 1732 and is a magnificent palace complex; Jantar Mantar \u2013 which is home to the world\u2019s largest sundial and is also a UNESCO world heritage site and Jal Mahal which is located in the middle of Man Sagar Lake and is one of the prime tourist attractions in Jaipur.\nYou will finally be escorted to your allotted hotel where you will be staying the night.\n\n\n\n\nDay 3 :Jaipur Departure\n\n\nDepending on your departure timings you will be made to check out of the hotel and transferred to your departure destination from where you will be heading onwards to your desired destination.",
    "highlights": [
      "Be a poart of history through the Nahargarh Fort tour, this was built in 1734",
      "Visit the famous Birla Mandir in Jaipur",
      "Enjoy local goods and foods at Chokhi Dhani",
      "Amer fort and Kanak Vrindavan garden which is built in a valley and is surrounded by the Aravalli hills both are magnificent to have a tour for",
      "Also visit the Hawa Mahal the pride of the city and Jantar mantar",
      "Relish the Rajasthani cuisines and handicrafts"
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1 :Arrival in Jaipur",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 2 :Jaipur City Tour",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 3 :Jaipur Departure",
        "description": ""
      }
    ],
    "faqs": []
  },
