  "kashi-gaya-prayagraj-ayodhya-naimisharanya-package": {
    "overview": "Kashi Gaya Prayagraj Ayodhya Naimisharanya tour takes you to places where India\u2019s spiritual heritage and traditions are still alive. See More\n\nKashi also called Varanasi, is the first stop. This city has many temples, but the Kashi Vishwanath temple is the main attraction here. It is around 3000 years old and one of the 12 Jyotirlingas.\nHere, you\u2019ll visit many more amazing places listed in the itinerary. After that, you will go to Gaya and explore Sita Kund, the place where Goddess Sita used to bathe during her exile (Vanvas). The journey then moves to Prayagraj, a city famous for the Triveni Sangam, the meeting point of three holy rivers - Ganga, Yamuna and Saraswati.\nThese rivers are very important in Hinduism. Now the journey continues to Ayodhya, which welcomes you with the glow of thousands of Diyas and colourful lights. It is the birthplace of Lord Rama and you\u2019ll love its rich culture. Next the final trip is Naimisharanya, a peaceful and beautiful place surrounded by nature.  Here, you can also visit the historic Pandav Kila, where they mediated. So plan your Kashi Gaya Prayagraj Ayodhya Naimisharanya package to explore more!\nSee Less\n\nKashi also called Varanasi, is the first stop. This city has many temples, but the Kashi Vishwanath temple is the main attraction here. It is around 3000 years old and one of the 12 Jyotirlingas.\n\nHere, you\u2019ll visit many more amazing places listed in the itinerary. After that, you will go to Gaya and explore Sita Kund, the place where Goddess Sita used to bathe during her exile (Vanvas). The journey then moves to Prayagraj, a city famous for the Triveni Sangam, the meeting point of three holy rivers - Ganga, Yamuna and Saraswati.",
    "highlights": [
      "Explore Kashi (Varanasi) including Kashi Vishwanath Temple, Annapurna Temple and the Ganga Aarti at Dashashwamedh Ghat.",
      "Visit Gaya to see Vishnupad Temple, Sita Kund and perform Pind Daan rituals for ancestors.",
      "Travel to Prayagraj with Triveni Sangam, Prayagraj Fort, Bade Hanuman Mandir and sacred rivers for holy dips.",
      "Spend time in Ayodhya and Naimisharanya, visiting Ram Janmabhoomi, Hanuman Garhi, Dashrath Mahal and enjoy at Pandav Kila surrounded by nature.",
      "See More"
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1: Arrival in Kashi",
        "description": "Welcome to Kashi! On arrival at Kashi Airport/ Railway Station, our\nMy Quick Trippers\nrepresentative will meet you and transfer you to your hotel for check-in and some rest. If you hire a guide, they will travel with the driver and help you during the journey.\nAfter checking in, you\u2019ll start exploring the sights of Kashi-\nShri Kashi Vishwanath Temple\n- A famous place where devotees come for salvation (moksha) and peace of mind.\nDarshan at Annapurna Temple\n- People pray here to the food Goddess for wealth and a life without hunger.\nVisit to Vishalakshi Temple\n- A peaceful Shakti Peeth temple, where the eyes of Goddess Sati fell.\nBaba Kal Bhairav Temple\n- Popular temple where devotees offer alcohol as Prasad to Kal Bhairav.\nEvening:\nTake a boat ride on the\nGanges\nand explore Kashi\u2019s old Ghats, and enjoy the city\u2019s spiritual vibe (optional, extra cost). Later, attend the beautiful\nGanga Aarti\nat\nDashashwamedh Ghat\n, either from the Ghat or on a private boat. Spend a comfortable night at your hotel in\nKashi.\nNote-\nThe Kashi Vishwanath Temple is open from\n3 AM to 11 PM\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "DAY 2: Kashi \u2013 Bodhgaya (284 kms/ 5-6 hrs)",
        "description": "After breakfast, travel to\nBodh Gaya\nand visit the\nMahabodhi Temple\n, a very peaceful spot and holy site for Buddhists.\nLater, go to the\nMahabodhi Tree\n, where Lord Buddha meditated.\nNext, visit\nMuchalinda Lake\n, a beautiful spot to take photos, then you will also see the 80-foot\nBuddha Statue.\nNext, visit\nWat Thai Temple, Japanese Temple, Bhutanese Temple, Metta Buddharam (White Buddha Statue),\nand\nKarma Temple,\neach place with unique architecture.\nAfter sightseeing, check into your hotel. Overnight stay at\nBodh Gaya.\nNote-\nThe Mahabodhi Temple is open from\n5 AM to 9 PM.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "DAY 3: Bodhgaya - Gaya - Kashi (255-260 km/ 5-5.5 hours)",
        "description": "Early in the morning, after breakfast go to\nGaya.\nOn arrival, explore\nVishnu Pad Mandir\nwhere you can perform Pind Daan, a holy ritual to respect your ancestors (family members who have passed away).\nNext, visit\nPhalgu Nadi\n, a holy river where pilgrims pray and perform rituals. After that, visit\nBrahmani Ghat\nand\nGayatri Ghat.\nThen travel to the sacred Sita Kund, and finally see\nMaa Sarva Mangla Gauri.\nPeople believe that visiting this temple brings the blessings of Goddess Gauri, who can remove difficulties and bring luck.\nReturn to Kashi in the evening and enjoy a relaxing overnight stay at your hotel.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "DAY 4: Kashi \u2013 Sarnath (10 km / 15-20 minutes)",
        "description": "Start your day with a boat ride on the Ganges and see the Ghats like\nAssi, Manikarnika,\nand\nHarishchandra.\nYou can also take a holy dip and optionally visit\nKashi Vishwanath Temple.\nLater, return to the hotel for breakfast.\nStart your day after breakfast by visiting Kashi\u2019s well-known temples-\nSankat Mochan Hanuman\n(located near Assi River, a great spot for sunset photos),\nDurga Mandir, Tulsi Manas\n(where Ramcharitmanas was written), and\nNew Vishwanath Temple.\nDon\u2019t miss a walk around the\nBHU campus nearby.\nIn the afternoon, drive to\nSarnath,\nthe sacred site where Lord Buddha shared his first teachings. Explore\nDhamek Stupa\n(best photo spot),\nChaukhandi Stupa,\nvarious\nBuddhist Temples\nand the\nSarnath Archeological Museum.\nReturn to\nKashi\nand check into your hotel for an overnight stay.\nNote-\nSarnath Archaeological Museum is closed on Fridays.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "DAY 5: Kashi - Vindhyachal - Prayagraj (150 km approx. / 4.5-5 hours)",
        "description": "After breakfast drive to\nPrayagraj.\nEnroute visit\nVindhyachal Devi\nfor a Darshan at Shaktipeeth. Later visit\nSitamarhi\n, the temple where Mother Sita went into the earth.\nWhen you reach\nPrayagraj,\ntravel to\nTriveni Sangam,\nwhere the Ganga, Yamuna, and Saraswati meet, and take a sacred dip there.\nEnjoy a peaceful boat ride and experience a holy bath at the Sangam.\nNext, visit\nBade Hanuman Mandir,\nthen go to\nAkshayavat Temple\ninside\nPatalpuri Temple\nat\nPrayagraj Fort.\nIt is believed that Lord Ram, Lakshman, and Sita once rested under this holy tree.\nVisit Prayagraj Fort, also called\nAllahabad Fort,\nbuilt by Emperor Akbar in 1583 near the Sangam, and then see the holy\nAlopi Devi Temple.\nIf time permits, visit\nLalita Devi Temple\nand\nShri Nagvasuki Temple.\nYou can also explore\nAnand Bhavan,\nhome of the Nehru family.\nOn arrival, check into the hotel. Overnight stay at\nPrayagraj.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "DAY 6: Prayagraj - Ayodhya (166 km/ 5-6 hours)",
        "description": "Enjoy breakfast then continue your journey to\nAyodhya.\nVisit\nRam Janmabhoomi Temple\na sacred place believed to be the birthplace of Lord Ram.\nGo to\nHanuman Garhi Temple\nlocated on a beautiful hill, which is perfect for photography.\nExplore Kanak Bhavan Temple,\na beautiful temple with gold plated domes dedicated to Lord Ram and Sita.\nIn evening watch the\nSaryu River Aarti\nat\nNaya Ghat,\na truly divine experience.\nNote\n- Ram Janmabhoomi Temple is open from\n6:00 AM to 10:00 PM.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "DAY 7: Explore Ayodhya\u2019s Culture and Spirituality",
        "description": "Early in the morning you can visit the\nSaryu River.\nTake a holy dip in the river or enjoy a peaceful boat ride if you wish (optional).\nAfter that, visit\nNageshwarnath Temple,\nwhich is one of the oldest temple in\nAyodhya,\ndedicated to Lord Shiva. Then see\nRam ki Paidi,\nand later return to\nRam Janmabhoomi Temple.\nNext, visit\nDashrath Mahal\nthe palace of Lord Ram\u2019s father, King Dashrath.\nIf time permits, you may explore\nValmiki Ramayana Bhawan\n(famous for Ramayana paintings),\nTreta Ke Thakur Temple\n(where King Vikramaditya placed idols of Lord Ram, Goddess Sita, and Lakshman), and also go to\nTulsi Udyan.\nLater, drive to Lucknow.\nIf time allows, enjoy an optional tour of\nBara Imambara, Rumi Darwaza, Residency Complex, Gomati Riverfront, Janeshwar Mishra Park,\nand\nAmbedkar Park.\nOn arrival, check into the hotel. Overnight stay in\nLucknow.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "DAY 8: Lucknow \u2013 Naimisharanya Sightseeing \u2013 Lucknow (180-190 km/ 6-7 hours)",
        "description": "After breakfast in the morning, drive to\nNaimisharanya.\nOnce you reach, visit\nChakrateertha\nfirst, (the spot where the Lord Brahma's chakra fell) then explore\nSuth Gaddi, Vyas Gaddi\n(best photo spot specially in sunrise), and\nManu Satrupa Tapsthali.\nLater, explore other important sites such as\nHanuman Garhi, Panch Pandav Kila, Gomati River\n(a beautiful riverside spot, perfect for evening walk),\nVishnu Temple, Dadhichi Kund,\nand the\nLalita Devi Temple\n(Shaktipeeth temple where Sati\u2019s heart fell).\nIn the evening, drive back to Lucknow.\nOn arrival you will be dropped at the airport/railway station to take your flight/train for your home.\nThis\nKashi Gaya Prayagraj Ayodhya Naimisharanya trip plan\nends with unforgettable memories.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      }
    ],
    "faqs": []
  },
