  "kerala-beaches-tour": {
    "overview": "Explore the pristine beaches of Kerala with our Kerala Beaches Tour Package. We offer bespoke packages that combine personalised service, expert knowledge, and unforgettable experiences. We take you to the exotic beaches, allow you to enjoy various water-based activities, and give you a chance to soak in the beauty of the breathtaking landscapes.\n\nAll the tours we design are tailored to the unique needs, interests, and preferences of our clients. We customize tours and try to accommodate all your unique needs. We offer group, family-friendly, and solo tours depending on your interest and budget.\nWhy Choose our Package?\nWe are one of the most reputed tour operators known for offering the best experiences within your budget. While curating itineraries, we keep in mind your budget, preferences, and unique aspirations. Whether you're traveling to South India for the first time or looking for unique experiences, you can rely on us to have the dream vacation of your life.\nOur Kerala Beaches Tour Package includes world-class accommodation, local cuisines, and smooth transportation. Every aspect is taken care of during the trip so that you can enjoy to the fullest and don't have to bother about your safety and convenience.\nTop Beaches to Visit in Kerala\nWe bring to you a list of the best beaches in Kerala.\nKovalam Beach\nWith our Kerala Beach Holiday Package, you will get a chance to visit Kovalam Beach, a tropical paradise with tranquil shores. It features three individual beaches: Hawa Beach, Lighthouse Beach, and Samudra Beach.\nVarkala Beach\nVarkala is known to be the most photographed beach in Kerala. It is renowned for its rocky cliffs and mineral springs. The Nature Care Centre and the two-thousand-year-old Sree Janardhana Swamy Temple are the main attractions here.\nBekal Beach\nBekal Beach is situated in Kasaragod and is known for its scenic beauty and backwaters. Overlooking the beach is Bekal Fort, the largest fort in Kerala. You can enjoy beach walks, kayaking, and scenic fort views from this beach.\nAlappuzha Beach\nAlso known as the Alleppey Beach, Alappuzha Beach is known for its one hundred and fifty-year-old pier and picturesque beauty. It hosts many festivals, such as the Alappuzha Beach Festival and the Sand Art Festival. Beside the beach, you can enjoy picnicking and enjoy the spectacular views of sunset.\nMarari Beach\nSituated around 11 km from Alleppey, Marari is a picturesque beach. National Geographic Survey has enlisted it as one of the world's top five hammock beaches. It is ideal for fishing activity. Snake boat races are also organized at this beach in August.\nElliot's Beach\nElliot's Beach forms the Marina Beach shore's endpoint and has been named after Edward Elliot. It has the Ashtalakshmi Kovil and Velankanni Church in the vicinity. It is considered to be one of the cleanest beaches in Chennai. You can stroll on this beach and enjoy water-based activities.\nHow to Reach Kerala\nYou can reach Kerala in the following ways.\nBy Air\nKerala has four international airports, namely Cochin International Airport, Trivandrum International Airport, Kannur International Airport, and Calicut International Airport. Kollam is a domestic airport that offers good connectivity among the major cities of the state.\nBy Train\nThere are more than two hundred railway stations in Kerala, connecting many major cities and small towns. Direct trains can be availed to various destinations in Kerala from major Indian cities such as Bangalore, Delhi, Mumbai, Chennai, and Kolkata. Express and superfast trains such as Duronto and Rajdhani connect the larger junctions, whereas passenger trains are also available.\nBy Road\nKerala has good connectivity via well-maintained roads to most nearby states. Buses and private taxis are easily available in all parts of the state. From nearby destinations, you can opt to drive your own vehicle to Kerala. Luxury overnight buses, some with built-in bathrooms, are available From Kottayam, Thrissur, Kozhikode, Alleppey, Kannur, Ernakulam, Palakkad, Thiruvananthapuram and Wayanad, luxury overnight buses are available for other cities across the state.\nTravel Tips\nKeep in mind these trips when embarking on a Kerala beach vacation.\n\nBook the Kerala Coastal Tour Package beforehand, especially if you're travelling in peak season.\nApply high SPF sunscreen for protection against heat rash and sunburn.\nEnjoy local food and drinks, look out for nice restaurants and beach shacks.\nPlan activities beforehand and decide your budget for the vacation.\nCarry a first aid kit that includes wound cleanser, antiseptic, and aloe gel.",
    "highlights": [
      "Enjoying the seafood of Cochin",
      "View Periyar and the Cardamom Hills",
      "Full coverage of Kumarakom and Mararikulam",
      "Enjoying all the local seafood on the beaches"
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1 :Cochin Arrival",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 2 :At Cochin",
