  "kerala-tamil-nadu-tour-package": {
    "overview": "Kerala is a magnificent masterpiece of nature, enriched with the cultures and traditions of the local folks.See More\n\nThe captivating hill stations, waterfalls, and backwaters with flourishing wildlife sanctuaries have made it one of the most enthralling destinations. Every traveler around the world dreams of a Kerala and Tamil Nadu holiday. With our Kerala tour with Tamil Nadu, you can explore the famous attractions of these southernmost states and indulge in many interesting activities. \nOur packages cater to the needs of families, couples, and solo travellers. You can customize the packages according to your unique needs and have tailored experiences. From accommodation to food and transportation to mind-blowing activities, we have included everything essential.\n\nThe captivating hill stations, waterfalls, and backwaters with flourishing wildlife sanctuaries have made it one of the most enthralling destinations. Every traveler around the world dreams of a Kerala and Tamil Nadu holiday. With our Kerala tour with Tamil Nadu, you can explore the famous attractions of these southernmost states and indulge in many interesting activities.\n\nOur packages cater to the needs of families, couples, and solo travellers. You can customize the packages according to your unique needs and have tailored experiences. From accommodation to food and transportation to mind-blowing activities, we have included everything essential.\n\nTour Gallery\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nTour Name\nKerala & Tamil Nadu Travel Package\n\n\nTour Duration\n11 Days / 10 Nights\n\n\nMeals\nBreakfast & Dinner\n\n\nVehicle Type\nSedan / SUV\n\n\nStarting & Ending Point\nCochin\n\n\nDestination Covered\nCochin - Munnar - Theddeky - Alleppey - Kanyakumari - Rameshwaram - Madurai \n\n\nPickup Time\nDepend on your Flight Timing \n\n\n Tour Benefits\nBest price & enjoyable travel guarantee",
    "highlights": [
      "Visit Tea Estates, Spice Plantation, Rose Garden, Blossom Park, and Honey Bee Plant of Munnar.",
      "Seek the blessings of Lord Shiva at Ramanathaswamy Temple.",
      "Houseboat cruise over the Backwater of Alleppey.",
      "Visit Meenakshi Amman Temple",
      "Witness the wildlife diversity and appreciate the breathtaking panoramas."
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1: Arrival at Cochin",
        "description": "Your tour will start as you reach Cochin Airport/Railway Station.\nAfter relaxing for some time, you will get ready to visit the famous destinations of Cochin, including St. Francis Church, Jewish Synagogue, and Fort Kochi.\nHave an overnight stay at your hotel after the sightseeing tour.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 2: Cochin- Munnar (04 hrs/140 Km)",
        "description": "After a delicious breakfast, you will be transferred to Munnar, one of the most famous hill stations of Kerala.\nExplore spice plantations, well-organized tea gardens, and lush green forests.\nAfter arriving at Munnar, you will check in to your pre-booked hotel and spend the rest of the day as you like, exploring the picturesque surroundings.\nHave an overnight stay at your hotel in Munnar."
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 3: Munnar Sightseeing",
        "description": "Today you will visit the famous sites of Munnar:\nEcho Point:\nEcho Point is the place where your voice echoes.\nKundala Lake:\nIt is a scenic tourist place. The area has Cherry Blossom trees, adding to this place\u2019s beauty. It is one of the most famous spots for photography.\nRajamalai (Eravikulam National Park):\nIt houses a large population of Nilgiri Tahr. People often visit this site to see the Neelakurinji flowers, which bloom once every twelve years. It is spread over 92 square kilometers and houses a wide range of flora and fauna.\nHave an overnight stay at your hotel in Munnar.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 04: Cochin - Thekkady (4 hrs/130 km)",
        "description": "After a delicious breakfast, you will head to Thekkady.\nOnce you have arrived at Thekkady, you will check into your pre-reserved hotel and relax for some time.\nIn the afternoon, you will embark on a sightseeing tour. You will visit the Periyar wildlife sanctuary. In 1978, this thick evergreen forest was declared a Tiger Reserve.\nYou can also enjoy various adventurous activities in Thekkady. You can visit pepper, cardamom, tea & coffee plantations and enjoy a boat cruise on the Periyar lake.\nYou will enjoy cultural programmes such as Kathakali & Kalarippayattu in the evening and visit the Spice market.\nYou will then return to your hotel and have an overnight stay.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 05: Thekkady - Alleppey",
        "description": "After a delicious breakfast, you will embark on a scenic drive to Alleppey, which is also known as Alappuzha.\nOnce you have arrived at Alleppey, you will check into the houseboat and enjoy the backwater life.\nAs you enjoy the cruise, you will witness the village area and canals. You will have dinner, breakfast, lunch, and evening tea at the houseboat.\nAfter the tasty dinner, you will have an overnight stay at your houseboat.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 06: Alleppey - Kovalam (4 hrs/154 km)",
        "description": "Have a tasty breakfast in the morning, and then you will head to Kovalam.\nIf you have time on hand, you will visit Sri Padmanabha Temple in Trivandrum (which is considered to be the capital of Kerala).\nLater on, you will embark on a drive to Kovalam, an internationally renowned beach that has three adjacent crescent beaches. It is considered to be the favourite of tourists for herbal massages, swimming, and relaxing on the beach.\nOnce you have arrived at Kovalam, you will check into your pre-booked hotel. You can spend the entire day relaxing at the beach.\nYou can enjoy various activities such as skiing, surfing, kayaking, and swimming.\nYou will have an overnight stay at your hotel in Kovalam.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 07: Kovalam - Kanyakumari (3 hrs/90 km)",
        "description": "Post breakfast, our driver will transfer you to Kanyakumari.\nOnce you have arrived at Kanyakumari, you will check in at your pre-booked hotel.\nYou will then visit Vivekananda Rock, where you will find a memorial that is dedicated to Swami Vivekananda.\nFrom the tip of India, you can enjoy the sunset of Kanyakumari. Return to your hotel and have an overnight stay.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 08: Kanyakumari - Rameshwaram",
        "description": "Embark on a drive to Rameshwaram.\nRameshwaram is known for its spiritual and historic relevance.\nAs per the legend, this is believed to be the site where Lord Rama built a bridge to rescue his consort Sita from Ravana.\nAfter arriving at Rameshwaram, you will check into your hotel, and later you will head to Agnitheertham, Ramjharoka Temple, and Ramanathaswamy Temple.\nYou will have an overnight stay in Rameshwaram.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 09: Rameshwaram - Full Day Sightseeing",
        "description": "Take a holy dip in Agni Theertham early in the morning, and then you will head out for Spatika Lingam Darshan, which is also known as Mani Darshan.\nAfter the Darshan and holy bath, you will return to your hotel and have breakfast. You will then head out for a sightseeing tour of Rameshwaram.\nYou will visit the famous attractions, including Five-faced Hanuman Temple, Kothandaramaswamy Temple, Ramar Patham, Gandamadana Parvatham, Rama Setu, and Dhanushkodi.\nHave an overnight stay at your hotel in Rameshwaram.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 10: Rameshwaram - Madurai (3 hrs/180 km)",
        "description": "Post breakfast, you will check out from your hotel and drive back to Madurai.\nOn the way, you will visit the Pamban Rail Scissors Bridge and the Pamban Bridge.\nOnce you have reached Madurai, you will check into your hotel.\nFresh up and then get ready to visit Thiruparankundram Murugan Temple and Madurai Meenakshi Amman Temple.\nAfter Darshan, you will return to your hotel and have an overnight stay.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 11: Madurai Departure",
        "description": "Relish a yummy breakfast, and then you will check out from your hotel and you will be transferred to Madurai railway station or Airport, from where you will continue your journey to your next destination."
      }
    ],
    "faqs": []
  },
