  "kerala-with-kanyakumari": {
    "overview": "Explore the gems of Southern India with our Kerala with Kanyakumari tour package. With this package, you get to experience the perfect combination of nature, serenity, and comfort. We prioritize personalized customer experiences and are dedicated to offering the perfect travel experience.\n\nOur packages come with everything essential, such as accommodation, meals, transportation, and sightseeing. Whether it's a luxury getaway, a quick escape, a family, a honeymoon, or a luxury vacation, we ensure a smooth travel experience.\nWhy Choose our Package?\nWe curate travel packages in a way that reduces stress and helps you save time by handling booking, planning, and other important trip details. The best thing is that our travel packages offer flexibility in terms of individual scheduling, duration, and amenities. Our local guides enhance your travel experience by answering questions, providing insights, and recommending hidden gems. When you book a Kerala Kanyakumari travel package from our site, you're paying for convenience and lavish experiences.\nTop Places to Visit in Kanyakumari and Tamil Nadu\nTake a look at the best places to visit in Kanyakumari and Tamil Nadu.\nBest Places in Kanyakumari\nVivekananda Rock Memorial\nSituated on a small island, Vivekananda Rock Memorial is one of the most popular attractions of Kanyakumari. This statue was built in 1970 on the site where Vivekananda got enlightenment. It comprises Shripad Mandapam, which has a museum and a study hall.\nKanyakumari Beach\nKanyakumari beach is the confluence of three water bodies: the Indian Ocean, the Bay of Bengal, and the Arabian Sea. The beach is not ideal for surfing or swimming as it is rocky. The beach is related to Devi Kanyakumari and has an association with Bhagavathi Amman.\nKanyakumari Bhagavathy Amman Temple\nLocated on the seashore of Kanyakumari, Kumari Amman Temple is a famous spiritual site. The temple is built in honor of the goddess Devi Kanya Kumari, who can be seen standing with a book in her hand. It is believed to be one of the 51 Shakti Peethas.\nPadmanabhapuram Palace\nThe Padmanabhapuram Palace was built in the sixteenth century, and it houses many unique artefacts and antiques. The unique thing about this palace is that it is made entirely from wood and adorned with wooden carvings. The palace houses many unique articles, such as brass lamps, stone sculpture and weapons.\nKanyakumari Wax Museum\nThe Kanyakumari Wax Museum offers visitors a chance to explore famous personalities' lifelike wax statues. You can see here a diverse collection of wax sculptures that depict political leaders, historical figures, cultural icons, and celebrities.\nBest Places in Kerala\nMunnar\nWith our Kerala with Kanyakumari tour package, you can visit Munnar, a scenic haven known for its lush greenery, tea estates, and viewpoints. This hill station is situated in the Idukki district and is known for the rare Neelakurinji flowers that only bloom once every twelve years, and the endangered Nilgiri Tahr.\nThekkady\nThekkady is a popular tourist attraction known for housing the largest Tiger Reserve in India- Periyar National Park. Here can enjoy bamboo rafting in Mullaperiyar Dam's catchment area. You can also enjoy night treks and go boating on the Periyar Lake.\nAlleppey\nAlleppey is renowned for its network of lagoons and canals with beautiful backwaters. It is situated in the southern part of Kerala, and its coastline offers some of the best beaches. It also has famous temples like Mullakkal Temple and Chettikulangara Devi Temple.\nKochi\nKochi is a port city lying in the southwest of India on the Malabar Coast. It has upmarket stores, heritage homes, art galleries, and the finest museums, such as the Kerala Folklore Museum and Hill Palace.\nVarkala\nVarkala is a coastal town renowned for the 15m high 'Northern Cliff' that lies adjacent to the Arabian Sea. It houses the Janardana Swami Temple and the samadhi of Sree Narayana Guru.\nHow to Reach Kanyakumari\nYou can reach Kanyakumari in the following ways.\nBy Rail\nKanyakumari Railway Station is the nearest railway station to Kanyakumari, situated around 4 Km from Kanyakumari City. It is a major junction and receives trains from many Indian cities.\nBy Air\nTrivandrum International Airport is the nearest airport to Kanyakumari, situated at a distance of around 90 Km in Kerala. You can fly to Trivandrum, and then you can travel to Kanyakumari by taking a road trip. The Trivandrum International Airport has good connectivity to the major Indian cities and direct international flights from Singapore, the Middle East, the Maldives, and Sri Lanka.\nBy Road\nKanyakumari has good connectivity by roads, so travelling by bus or car is very convenient. Kanyakumari is connected by major national highways to the other parts of South India. By driving from your city or taking the deluxe or State local bus, you can reach Kanyakumari. The preferred way to explore Kanyakumari is by private taxi or car.\nTravel Tips\nFollow these tips for a smooth Kerala Kanyakumari trip.\n\nPlan a visit to Kerala and Kanyakumari accordingly. The period from October to March is considered to be the best season to visit Kerala and Kanyakumari for sightseeing and outdoor activities.\nWhen visiting temples and sacred attractions, dress modestly.\nRespect the environment, support local craft, and avoid plastic. In villages, you should opt for community-based tourism initiatives.",
    "highlights": [
      "Exciting Munnar excursions",
      "Visit to the Eravikulam National Park",
      "Visit to Thekkady",
      "The lovely wildness of Periyar Wildlife Sanctuary will mesmerize you",
      "Welcome to Alleppey the Venice of the East, its waterways dotted with hundreds of houseboats",
      "Enjoy the breathtaking scenery of Kovalam and its beach",
      "A trip to Kanyakumari",
      "The excellent beach visit",
      "And have a journey to the Vivekananda Rocks",
      "Visualize the tip of India from the Rocks",
      "Trivandrum sightseeing"
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1 :Kochi \u2013 Munnar",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 2 :Munnar Excursions",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 3 :Munnar \u2013 Thekkady",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 4 :Thekkady \u2013 Alleppey",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 5 :Alleppey \u2013 Kovalam",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
