  "khatu-shyam-ji-salasar-balaji-yatra-by-helicopter": {
    "overview": "Book our Khatu Shyam Ji & Salasar helicopter Yatra package to explore two of Rajasthan\u2019s most sacred destinations in a hassle-free way. See More\n\nKhatu Shyam Ji is a Hindu temple dedicated to Khatu Shyam, a manifestation of Barbarika. You'll also visit Salasar Balaji, a prime religious site for devotees of Hanuman.\nThis Yatra will save you from physical exertion and allow you to savor the most breathtaking views from thousands of meters above the sky. Whether you're short on time or want to have a luxurious Yatra, our packages are ideal for you. Our packages also come with the scope of customization, ensuring you can have a personalized trip. Book our Khatu Shyam Ji Helicopter Tour now!\nSee Less\n\nKhatu Shyam Ji is a Hindu temple dedicated to Khatu Shyam, a manifestation of Barbarika. You'll also visit Salasar Balaji, a prime religious site for devotees of Hanuman.\n\nThis Yatra will save you from physical exertion and allow you to savor the most breathtaking views from thousands of meters above the sky. Whether you're short on time or want to have a luxurious Yatra, our packages are ideal for you. Our packages also come with the scope of customization, ensuring you can have a personalized trip. Book our Khatu Shyam Ji Helicopter Tour now!\n\nTour Highlights\n\n\nComfortable helicopter Yatra to two of Rajasthan's sacred shrines.\nSeek the blessings of Balaji at Balaji Temple.\nAttend the Aarti ceremony and absorb the sacred vibes of Khatu Shyam Ji.",
    "highlights": [
      "Comfortable helicopter Yatra to two of Rajasthan's sacred shrines.",
      "Seek the blessings of Balaji at Balaji Temple.",
      "Attend the Aarti ceremony and absorb the sacred vibes of Khatu Shyam Ji."
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1: Khatu Shyam Salasar Helicopter tour Itinerary or tour Plan",
        "description": "09:30 am: Departure time from Rohini Heliport\nAt Rohini Airport, you will meet one of our representatives who will welcome you with open arms and assist you with further travel-related requirements.\nYou will board the helicopter, and you will be taken to Khatu Shyam Ji.\n10:45 am: Arrive at Khatu Shyam Ji (Freshen-up Break)\nOnce you have arrived at Khatu Shyam Ji, you'll be taken to a nearby hotel where you will relax for some time, and then you will head out for the temple visit.\nAs per the Salasar Balaji Dham helicopter Yatra package, rooms will be allotted on a twin-sharing basis. You can also make a request for separate rooms, subject to availability and by paying extra.\n12:15 am: Estimated Departure Time to Salasar Balaji\nAt Khatu Shyam Ji Temple, you will have priority Darshan of the main deity, which is dedicated to Lord Krishna in his Shyam Baba form.\nAs reported by\nThe Print\nevery week, over two lakh pilgrims turn up at Khatu Shyam temple, making it one of the fastest-growing religious hubs in North India.\nThe main attraction of this temple is Khatu Shyam's idol, which is considered to be more than five hundred years old. Devotees visit this temple to offer prayers and have Darshan.\nThe complex of the temple has many other shrines that are dedicated to goddesses and gods.\nThe temple comprises Shyam Kund, a holy pond that heals those who enter it. Devotees take a dip in the pond to seek blessings from the deity and purify themselves.\n01:00 PM - Arrival and Darshan at Temple\nYou'll board a helicopter to Salasar Balaji.\nSalasar Balaji is the only Hanuman temple where Hanuman's idol has a moustache and beard.\nIt is also considered to be a Shakti Sthal (shrine) and Swayambhu (self-created).\nWhen you reach Salasar Balaji, you will be taken for priority Darshan.\nThe temple was built in 1754 and is considered a Shakti Sthal.\n02:00 PM - Packed Lunch Service and return journey\nSavor a packed lunch and then board your helicopter for the return journey to Delhi.\nAfter the Darshan, you'll board your helicopter.\nThis marks the end of your same-day Khatu Shyam Ji Helicopter Tour.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      }
    ],
    "faqs": []
  },
