  "madurai-rameshwaram-tour-package": {
    "overview": "The Madurai Rameshwaram tour is one of Tamil Nadu's most rewarding pilgrimage and sightseeing circuits. Four days. Two cities. And more sacred sites, living legends, and coastal beauty than most people expect.  See More\n\nThe journey starts in Madurai \u2014 home to the Meenakshi Amman Temple, one of India's grandest Dravidian temples with over 33,000 sculpted figures. From there you travel to Rameshwaram, the sacred island city where the Ramanathaswamy Temple \u2014 one of the 12 Jyotirlingas \u2014 stands at the edge of the sea. This is where Lord Rama himself is believed to have worshipped Lord Shiva before crossing to Lanka.\nApart from temple Darshan, you'll explore the iconic Pamban Bridge with its spectacular sea views, the haunting ruins of Dhanushkodi, and the birthplace of Dr. APJ Abdul Kalam. Thousands of pilgrims and families have trusted My Quick Trippers for a smooth, guided experience here \u2014 and we make sure you don't miss a single important stop.\n\n\n\n\nQuick Information\nDetails\n\n\n\n\nTour Name\nMadurai Rameshwaram Tour Package\n\n\nDuration\n4 Days / 3 Nights\n\n\nDestinations Covered\nMadurai \u2014 Rameshwaram \u2014 Madurai\n\n\nStarting & Ending Point\nMadurai Airport / Railway Station\n\n\nSuitable For\nFamilies, pilgrims, solo travelers, senior citizens, photography lovers\n\n\nMeals\nDaily Breakfast Included\n\n\nVehicle Type\nAC Sedan / SUV (based on group size)\n\n\nPick-up & Drop\nMadurai Airport / Railway Station (as per flight/train timing)\n\n\nPrice Starts From\n\u20b912,900 per person | Use Code NIT3GOLD \u2014 Save \u20b92,100\n\n\nBest Time to Visit\nOctober to March (pleasant weather, ideal for temple visits)\n\n\n\n\nAbout Madurai & Rameshwaram\nMadurai \u2014 The Temple City\nMadurai is one of India's oldest continuously inhabited cities, with a history stretching back over 2,500 years. It is the cultural capital of Tamil Nadu and the second largest city in the state. The city revolves around the Meenakshi Amman Temple at its literal centre \u2014 the city's streets were laid out in concentric squares around the temple.\nFor pilgrims, Madurai offers the Meenakshi Amman Temple, the Thiruparankundram Murugan Temple (one of Murugan's six sacred abodes), and the Koodal Azhagar Temple (one of the 108 Divya Desams). For those interested in history, the Thirumalai Nayakkar Palace and the Gandhi Museum add depth. And Madurai's food \u2014 particularly the Jigarthanda cold drink and the famous mutton biryani \u2014 is a destination in itself.\nRameshwaram \u2014 The Sacred Island\nRameshwaram is situated on Pamban Island in the Gulf of Mannar, connected to mainland Tamil Nadu by the Pamban Bridge. It is one of the holiest sites in Hinduism \u2014 a place where Lord Rama is believed to have worshipped Lord Shiva before crossing the sea to Lanka to rescue Goddess Sita.\nThe Ramanathaswamy Temple here is one of the 12 Jyotirlingas and part of the all-India Char Dham pilgrimage (the four dhams being Badrinath in the north, Dwarka in the west, Puri in the east, and Rameshwaram in the south). The temple's corridor is 1,212 metres long \u2014 the longest temple corridor in the world. The Theertham Snanam ritual, involving 22 sacred wells inside the temple, is unique to Rameshwaram and forms the spiritual centrepiece of the visit.\nPlaces Covered in This Package\nRameshwaram\n\n\n\n\nPlace\nSignificance\n\n\n\n\nRamanathaswamy Temple\nOne of 12 Jyotirlingas; 1,212-metre corridor \u2014 longest in world; temple of Lord Ramanathaswamy (Shiva)\n\n\nSphatik Linga (Mani Darshan)\nNatural crystal Shivlinga, believed installed by Goddess Sita; 5 AM darshan only\n\n\nAgni Theertham\nSacred sea beach at temple east entrance; ritual bath before temple entry\n\n\n22-Well Theertham Snanam\nRitual sacred bath in water from all 22 wells inside temple; 1.5\u20132 hrs; carry change of clothes\n\n\nGandamadana Parvatham\nHillock with Lord Rama's footprint shrine; panoramic island views\n\n\nKothandaramaswamy Temple\nOne of few temples where Vibhishana is also worshipped; on the south coast of the island\n\n\nFive-Faced Hanuman Temple\nPanchamukha Anjaneya \u2014 rare form of Hanuman facing five directions\n\n\nRam Setu (Adam's Bridge)\n48-km limestone shoal chain; believed to be bridge built by Lord Rama's army to Lanka\n\n\nAPJ Abdul Kalam's Residence\nBirthplace and childhood home of India's 11th President; maintained as a public memorial\n\n\nDhanushkodi\nGhost town at island tip, destroyed in 1964 cyclone; hauntingly beautiful ruins at Bay of Bengal + Indian Ocean confluence\n\n\n\n\nMadurai\n\n\n\n\nPlace\nSignificance\n\n\n\n\nMeenakshi Amman Temple\n14 towering gopurams, 33,000+ sculptures; dedicated to Goddess Meenakshi and Lord Sundareswarar; timings: 5 AM\u201312:30 PM, 4 PM\u20139:30 PM\n\n\nThiruparankundram Murugan Temple\nOne of the six Arupadaiveedu of Lord Murugan; 1,500+ years old; carved into rock face; 8 km from city\n\n\nPamban Bridge (en route)\nIndia's second-longest sea bridge, 2.3 km; spectacular views \u2014 best photography stop on the route\n\n\nPamban Rail Scissors Bridge\nCentury-old Scherzer Rolling Lift Bridge (built 1914); still operational; opens vertically for passing ships\n\n\n\n\nBest Time to Visit Madurai & Rameshwaram\nOctober to March is the ideal window \u2014 weather is pleasant (22\u00b0C\u201332\u00b0C), perfect for temple visits, outdoor sightseeing, and the sea bath at Agni Theertham. This is the peak pilgrimage season.\n\n\n\n\nSeason\nMonths\nWhat to Expect\n\n\n\n\nBest Season \u2713\nOct \u2013 Mar\nPleasant weather, 22\u00b0C\u201332\u00b0C. Clear skies. Ideal for all sightseeing and temple visits. Peak season.\n\n\nGood \u2713\nJul \u2013 Sep\nPost-monsoon freshness, fewer crowds. Occasional showers. Manageable for temple tours.\n\n\nHot, plan early\nApr \u2013 Jun\nTemperature 35\u00b0C\u201342\u00b0C. Early morning visits (before 9 AM) are essential. Avoid midday travel.\n\n\nPartial closures\nHeavy monsoon\nDhanushkodi beach access can be restricted. Pamban Bridge occasionally closed during high sea warnings.\n\n\n\n\nNote: For Sphatik Linga Darshan, arrive in Rameshwaram by Day 1 evening to be at the temple by 4:30 AM on Day 2. This is the most spiritually significant experience on the tour \u2014 plan your travel timing accordingly.\nHow to Reach Madurai\nBy Air\nMadurai Airport (IATA: IXM) operates regular flights from Chennai, Mumbai, Bengaluru, Hyderabad, Delhi, and Coimbatore. Most metro connections take 1.5\u20132 hours. The airport is 10 km from city centre \u2014 our driver will pick you up directly from the arrival gate.\nBy Train\nMadurai Junction (Station Code: MDU) is a major railhead on the Southern Railway network. Excellent connections from Chennai (Vaigai Express, Pandian Express \u2014 8\u20139 hrs), Bengaluru, Coimbatore, Trichy, and other major cities. This is the most convenient and budget-friendly option for most travellers.\nBy Road\nMadurai is on NH-44 (the North-South corridor). Regular bus services from Chennai (460 km, 7\u20138 hrs), Coimbatore (220 km, 3.5 hrs), Trichy (140 km, 2.5 hrs), and Kanyakumari (244 km, 4 hrs). State government SETC buses and multiple private operators run overnight routes from Chennai and Bengaluru.\nTravel Tips & Guidelines\n\nDress code: Strict at both Meenakshi Amman and Ramanathaswamy temples. Men: dhoti or full-length trousers (no shorts). Women: saree or salwar-kameez (no sleeveless, shoulders and knees covered). Dress codes are enforced at the entrance.\nTheertham Snanam: Carry a change of clothes in your day bag \u2014 you get completely wet from bucket-poured water. It is not a light sprinkling. Allow 1.5\u20132 hours for all 22 wells.\nSphatik Linga Darshan: Happens only at 5:00 AM. Arriving in Rameshwaram on Day 1 evening is the only way to experience this. Do not skip it.\nPhotography: Restricted inside Ramanathaswamy Temple and Meenakshi Amman Temple. Camera fees apply at select spots. Check at the entrance before shooting.\nDhanushkodi access: Private vehicles are not allowed beyond the Dhanushkodi checkpost. The last 18 km to the island tip is sand \u2014 only beach jeeps (local, approx. \u20b950\u2013\u20b9150 per person) cover this section.\nCash: Carry \u20b92,000\u2013\u20b93,000 in cash. Temple hundi, beach jeeps, and local prasad shops are cash-only. ATMs in Rameshwaram work but can run short during peak pilgrim season.\nEarly mornings: Ramanathaswamy Temple opens at 4:00 AM. Early darshan (4\u20137 AM) means shorter queues and a more peaceful experience. Afternoon queues can stretch to 2\u20133 hours during peak season.\nSenior citizens: Wheelchairs are available inside both Meenakshi Amman and Ramanathaswamy temples. Inform us at booking if special assistance is needed.\n\nPackage Price 2026\nPrices are per person based on double-sharing. Larger groups cost less per head. All prices include transport, hotel, and daily breakfast.\n\n\n\n\nHotel Category\n2 Persons\n4 Persons\n6 Persons\nIncludes\n\n\n\n\nStandard\n\u20b915,900\n\u20b913,900\n\u20b912,900\nHotel + breakfast + AC cab + sightseeing\n\n\nDeluxe\n\u20b918,900\n\u20b916,900\n\u20b915,500\nUpgraded hotels + all above\n\n\nLuxury\n\u20b924,900\n\u20b921,900\n\u20b919,900\nPremium hotels + all above\n\n\n\n\nSpecial Deal: Use coupon code NIT3GOLD at booking \u2014 save \u20b92,100 (original price \u20b915,000 \u2192 \u20b912,900). Best price guaranteed. Book online, pay later.\nWhy Book with My Quick Trippers\n\nApproved by Ministry of Tourism, Government of India \u2014 licensed and verified tour operator\nBest price guaranteed \u2014 show us a cheaper equivalent tour and we beat it\nBook Online, Pay Later \u2014 confirm your dates without full upfront payment\nFree cancellations and changes up to 7 days after booking\nExperienced drivers and guides who know temple timings, entry protocols, and local customs\nDedicated support via phone and WhatsApp throughout your journey \u2014 100% response rate, 2-hr response time\nThousands of verified travellers have completed this route with us\nCustomisable \u2014 extend to Kanyakumari, Kodaikanal, or Thanjavur on request\n\nReady to Plan Your Madurai Rameshwaram Tour?\nMadurai and Rameshwaram together cover some of the most spiritually significant and architecturally extraordinary sites in all of India \u2014 the 33,000 sculptures of Meenakshi Amman, the 1,212-metre corridor of Ramanathaswamy, the pre-dawn Sphatik Linga darshan, and the eerie beauty of Dhanushkodi at the edge of two seas.\nFour days is the right amount of time. October to March is the right season. And booking early is the right call \u2014 hotels in Rameshwaram fill up during peak pilgrim weekends and Tamil Nadu festival periods.\nWhatsApp us at +91-9711616316 or book online now. Use code NIT3GOLD and save \u20b92,100 on your booking. Confirmation within 2 hours.\nSee Less",
    "highlights": [
      "Ramanathaswamy Temple Darshan \u2014 one of the 12 Jyotirlingas of India and a site of the all-India Char Dham pilgrimage (Badrinath, Dwarka, Puri, Rameshwaram)",
      "Visit Pamban Bridge, Pamban Rail Scissors Bridge, Ram Setu (Adam's Bridge) and Dhanushkodi \u2014 iconic landmarks on the edge of India",
      "Ritual bath at Agni Theertham and Theertham Snanam in all 22 sacred wells inside Ramanathaswamy Temple corridor",
      "Sphatik Linga (Mani Darshan) at 5:00 AM \u2014 a rare natural crystal Shivlinga darshan, not man-made, available only in the early morning hours",
      "Meenakshi Amman Temple, Madurai \u2014 14 towering gopurams with over 33,000 sculptures, one of the finest examples of Dravidian architecture in the world",
      "Thiruparankundram Murugan Temple \u2014 one of the six Arupadaiveedu, over 1,500 years old, partially carved into a granite hill",
      "APJ Abdul Kalam's Residence, Rameshwaram \u2014 birthplace of India's Missile Man and 11th President, now a public memorial",
      "Stay at hand-picked hotels across both cities \u2014 standard, deluxe, and luxury options available to suit every budget",
      "See More"
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1: Madurai - Rameshwaram (173 km/ 3-4 hrs)",
        "description": "Start your trip with a pick-up from your selected spot in Madurai airport or railway station. Our\nMy Quick Trippers\nteam will receive you and transfer you comfortably to Rameshwaram. If you choose a guide, they will join the driver and help you during the tour.\nAfter pick-up and transfer, you will start your sightseeing tour and visit-\nRamanathaswamy Temple-\nA sacred place and one of the 12 Jyotirlingas.\nAgnitheertham-\nA holy beach where pilgrims take a ritual bath.\nRamjharoka Temple-\nIt is believed that Lord Rama once stayed here.\nAfter completing sightseeing, check into the hotel and enjoy an overnight stay in\nRameshwaram.\nNote-\nRamanathaswamy Temple timings are 4am\u20131pm and 3\u20138pm\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "DAY 2: In Rameswaram",
        "description": "Early in the morning, around\n5:00 AM,\nproceed to the\nSpatika Linga Darshan,\nalso called\nMani Darshan,\nwhere the natural crystal Shivling (not man-made) is very important in Hinduism and looks very beautiful.\nLater you will head out for\nAgni Teertham\nto have a holy bath in the sea.\nFurther proceed to the main temple through North gate and\nTake sacred bath with holy water of the 22 wells, inside the\nRamanathaswamy Temple\nduring\nTheerth Snanam.\nThen proceed for darshan and pooja at the main temple.\nAfter the holy bath and Darshan, return to the hotel for breakfast.\nNext, enjoy a sightseeing tour of\nRameshwaram\nand visit\nFive-faced Hanuman Temple, Ramar Patham, Kothandaramaswamy Temple, and Gandamadana Parvatham\n(where you can see Lord Rama\u2019s footprint). Also, explore\nRama Setu (Adam\u2019s Bridge),\nthe bridge Lord Rama built to reach Sri Lanka and rescue Goddess Sita.\nThen, go to Former President\nA.P.J. Abdul Kalam\u2019s House\nand\nDhanushkodi.\nOvernight stay in\nRameshwaram.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "DAY 3: Rameswaram - Madurai (200 km/ 4.5 hrs)",
        "description": "Morning visit to the temple again or take a\nSamudra Snanam\n(holy dip in the sea).\nAfter sightseeing, return to\nMadurai\nand stop to see\nPamban Bridge\nand the\nPamban Rail Scissors Bridge\non the way (Great photography spot).\nOn arrival in\nMadurai\n, check in to the hotel and freshen up.\nVisit\nMeenakshi Amman Temple\nand\nThiruparankundram Murugan\n(one of the oldest temple around\n1500\nyears) for Darshan.\nReturn to the hotel. Overnight stay at\nMadurai.\nNote-\nWear comfortable clothes and footwear as there will be temple visits and some walking.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "DAY 4: Madurai Departure",
        "description": "After breakfast, your\ntrip to Madurai Rameshwaram\nends with happy memories as you will be dropped off at Madurai Airport or the railway station for your next destination."
      }
    ],
