        "description": "When you land at New Delhi\u2019s Indira Gandhi International Airport, a representative will greet you and assist you in making your way to the designated hotel. You\u2019ll spend the night at the hotel."
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 2: Sightseeing in Delhi",
        "description": "After breakfast, begin your full-day sightseeing tours of New Delhi and Old Delhi.\nOn a tour of Old Delhi, there will be stops at Raj Ghat, Jama Masjid, and Red Fort are all included. From Jama Masjid to Chandni Chowk, take a cycle rickshaw and take in the scenery.\nA New Delhi sightseeing tour includes stops at the spectacular India Gate, Parliament House, President House, Humayun\u2019s Tomb, Qutab Minar, and a drive down Rajpath. You\u2019ll eat and spend the night at the hotel. (The monuments in Delhi are closed on Monday)\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 3: Delhi to Agra (221 kms, Approx. 5 hrs drive)",
        "description": "After breakfast, travel to Agra, stopping en route to view Sikandra, the tomb of renowned Mughal emperor Akbar. Upon your arrival in Agra, the city home to the Taj Mahal, a representative from our business will assist you in travelling to the desired hotel. Visit the Taj Mahal and the majestic Agra Fort, two well-known love monuments.\nThe Taj Mahal was built by Mughal emperor Shah Jahan as a memorial to his devoted wife Mumtaz Mahal. The breathtaking memorial to love is crafted from white marble and has inlay work. In 1565, Mughal emperor Akbar built Agra Fort. Visit Itmad-ud-Daula Tomb, also known as the Baby Taj Mahal by Daulah. Stay the night and eat breakfast in your hotel."
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 4: Jaipur to Agra (238 kms, Approx. 5-6 hrs drive)",
        "description": "After breakfast, take a drive to Jaipur, also referred to as the Pink City and the capital of Rajasthan. The Mughal emperor Akbar erected Fatehpur Sikri in the late 16th century but abandoned it because of a lack of water. You will stop at this location along the way. You will also see Buland Darwaza, the largest entryway in the world. Continue your journey to Jaipur, the \u201cPink City,\u201d our representative will assist you in getting to the hotel once you arrive in Jaipur. You\u2019ll eat and spend the night at the hotel.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 5: Jaipur sightseeing",
        "description": "After breakfast at the hotel, go out for the hilltop Amber Fort. travel to the fort on an elephant. Later, take in the city of Jaipur\u2019s sights include City Palace, Hawa Mahal, and Jantar Mantar. Enjoy shopping at the thriving neighborhood bazaars throughout the city as well. You\u2019ll eat and spend the night at the hotel.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 6: Jaipur - Delhi (Departure) (261 Kms, 5-6 Hours Drive)",
        "description": "Drive back to Delhi after having breakfast. We will drop you off at the airport or station with happy memories."
