  "maharashtra-5-jyotirlinga-package": {
    "overview": "Thinking how to visit all five holy temples in a single journey? This 5 Jyotirlinga tour package of Maharashtra makes it simple and convenient. See More\n\nYour journey begins with Bhimashankar Jyotirlinga, which is surrounded by a dense forest. It is believed that Lord Shiva defeated the demon Tripurasura here, and the Jyotirlinga is naturally formed, not man-made.Next, the tour takes you to Parli Vaijnath Jyotirlinga. People believe that praying here can remove negativity, fulfill wishes and bring good luck. You will then visit Aundha Nagnath, another sacred Jyotirlinga temple that was damaged by Aurangzeb. However it was rebuilt later and it still stands today as one of the 12 sacred Jyotirlingas.Your tour continues to the Grishneshwar Jyotirlinga, near the famous Ellora Caves, where many travelers love its excellent architecture. Finally, the journey takes you to Trimbakeshwar Jyotirlinga, from where the holy Godavari River flows naturally. People believe that water comes directly from the Shiva lingam itself. Besides visiting temples, the tour also includes stops at some other famous sites on the way. Just plan your Maharashtra Jyotirlinga tour package to make new memories!See Less\n\nYour journey begins with Bhimashankar Jyotirlinga, which is surrounded by a dense forest. It is believed that Lord Shiva defeated the demon Tripurasura here, and the Jyotirlinga is naturally formed, not man-made.\n\nNext, the tour takes you to Parli Vaijnath Jyotirlinga. People believe that praying here can remove negativity, fulfill wishes and bring good luck. You will then visit Aundha Nagnath, another sacred Jyotirlinga temple that was damaged by Aurangzeb. However it was rebuilt later and it still stands today as one of the 12 sacred Jyotirlingas.",
    "highlights": [
      "Visit all 5 Jyotirlingas in Maharashtra: Bhimashankar, Parli Vaijnath, Aundha Nagnath, Grishneshwar, and Trimbakeshwar, along with famous nearby sites.",
      "Experience temple history, and spiritual blessings at each sacred Jyotirlinga.",
      "Explore cultural and historical attractions on the way, including Ellora Caves, Bibi Ka Maqbara, Panchvati, and Ramkund.",
      "Convenient 4\u20135 day itinerary with comfortable travel, hotel stays, Darshan, Pooja, and memorable spiritual experiences.",
      "See More"
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1: Mumbai - Bhimashankar - Ahmednagar (361- 375 km/8 -10 hours)",
        "description": "Start your Maharashtra Jyotirlinga tour after our driver picks you up from your selected location in Mumbai, whether it\u2019s the airport or railway station. Our driver will take you, and then you will continue the tour. If you include a guide, they will come with the driver to help you all day.\nAfter pick-up, you will start your tour and visit-\nBhimashankar Jyotirlinga Temple-\nThis temple is not only important, but the surroundings are also very stunning, so keep your camera ready.\nAfter completing the temple visit, you will drive to\nAhmednagar\n. On arrival, check into the hotel. Stay overnight at Ahmednagar.\nNote-\nThe Bhimashankar Temple is open for morning Darshan from\n4:30 AM\nto\n3:15\nPM and for evening Darshan from\n4:00 PM\nto\n9:30 PM\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 2: Ahmednagar - Shani Shinganapur - Parli Vaijnath - Parbhani (324 km/6-7 hours)",
        "description": "After breakfast, drive to\nShani Shingnapur\n, a well-known temple of Lord Shani. In this village, houses have no doors, and crime is nearly zero because villagers believe Lord Shani keeps them safe. Take blessings here before going on to\nParli Vaijnath Temple\n.\nNext visit Parli\nVaijnath Temple\n. According to belief, Ravana of Lanka dropped the Shiva idol at this spot. Since then,\nParli Vaijnath\nhas been a very special place.\nEnjoy Pooja and Darshan, then continue your drive to\nParbhani\n. Check in at the hotel and stay overnight.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 3: Parbhani - Aundha Nagnath - Aurangabad (280 - 300 km/ 6-7 hours)",
        "description": "After breakfast, travel to\nAundha Nagnath\n, the Jyotirlinga Temple, for blessings. People believe Dharmraj, the eldest Pandava, built this temple during his\n14-year\nexile (Vanvaas).\nAfter the visit, drive to\nAurangabad\n. Once you arrive, check into the hotel. If time allows, explore\nBibi Ka Maqbara\nin the evening, known for its gardens and photo spots. Overnight stay at the hotel.\nNote-\nPhotography may be restricted inside Aundha Nagnath Temple, so check local rules before taking pictures.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 4: Aurangabad - Grishneshwar - Ellora - Shirdi (150-165 km/3.5-4.5 hours)",
        "description": "Morning after breakfast, proceed to visit the sacred\nGrishneshwar Temple\n(Jyotirlinga) for Darshan. Later, explore the famous\nEllora Caves\n(old rock caves with Hindu, Buddhist, and Jain designs) and then visit the Bhadra Maruti Temple (only temple where Lord Hanuman is seen in a sleeping posture).\nAfter sightseeing, drive to\nShirdi\n. On arrival, check into the hotel. In the evening, visit the\nShirdi Temple\nfor Darshan.\nOvernight stay at the hotel.\nNote-\nGrishneshwar Temple is open from 5:00-5:30 AM to 9:30 PM, Mangal Aarti is 4:00-5:30 AM, Evening Aarti at 7:30 PM; Ellora Caves are closed on Tuesdays.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 5: Shirdi - Nasik - Trimbakeshwar - Mumbai (290-350 km/7-8 hours)",
        "description": "Morning drive to\nNashik\nto visit\nPanchvati\nand\nRamkund\n(holy tank where Lord Rama is believed to have bathed). Later visit\nTrimbakeshwar Temple\n(Jyotirlinga). After darshan and Pooja, proceed to\nMumbai\n.\nThe\n5 Jyotirlinga in Maharashtra tour package\nends here, with wonderful memories of this spiritual journey.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      }
    ],
    "faqs": []
  },
  "maharashtra-jyotirlinga-yatra-package": {
    "overview": "This 3 Jyotirlinga Tour of Maharashtra is designed for pilgrims who want to visit three of Lord Shiva's most revered sacred shrines in a single, well-organised journey. You will be visiting Trimbakeshwar (Nashik), Grishneshwar (Aurangabad), and Bhimashankar (Sahyadri hills) \u2014 three of the twelve Jyotirlingas of India, all located within Maharashtra. Each shrine offers its own distinct spiritual significance, architecture, and setting. See More\n\nIn addition to the three Jyotirlingas, the tour includes a visit to Shirdi for Sai Baba Darshan and a cultural stop at the Ellora Caves \u2014 a UNESCO World Heritage Site with the iconic Kailash Temple. We handle all your travel logistics: AC transport, hotel stays, daily breakfast, and experienced drivers familiar with every route on this circuit. You focus on the Darshan; we take care of everything else.Departures from Mumbai. Customised pickups from Pune also available on request. Book now to confirm your dates.Temple & Travel GuidelinesDress code: Traditional attire recommended at all three Jyotirlinga temples. Men: dhoti or full-length trousers. Women: saree or salwar-kameez. Modest clothing ensures smooth entry \u2014 no shorts or sleeveless.Rudrabhishek at Trimbakeshwar: Requires advance booking. Cannot be done spontaneously on busy days. Timings: 7:00\u20138:30 AM. Charges are separate, payable at the temple \u2014 not included in the package.Mangal Aarti: Grishneshwar at 4:00 AM and Bhimashankar at 4:00 AM. Attending even one of these is highly recommended. The overnight stay at Ahmednagar (Day 2) makes the Grishneshwar 4 AM aarti possible.Ellora Caves closure: Ellora Caves are CLOSED every Tuesday. If Day 2 of your tour falls on a Tuesday, inform us at booking and we will plan accordingly.Bhimashankar ghat road: The approach to Bhimashankar involves a winding mountain ghat road. Motion sickness tablets recommended for those prone to ghat travel. Allow extra time on Day 3.Sawan / Shravan month: Trimbakeshwar and Bhimashankar see very heavy crowds during Shravan Mondays and the Kanwar Yatra period. Route diversions are possible. Book hotels 2\u20133 months in advance if travelling in this period.Photography: Restricted inside the main sanctum at all three Jyotirlinga temples. Outer courtyards and Ellora Caves allow photography. Confirm at entry.Cash: Carry \u20b92,000\u2013\u20b93,000 in cash. Prasad counters, puja shops, and Ellora Caves entry are cash-only at most counters. ATMs available in Nashik, Shirdi, and Aurangabad.About the 3 Jyotirlingas in Maharashtra1. Trimbakeshwar Jyotirlinga, NashikTrimbakeshwar is located 28 km from Nashik, at the foot of the Brahmagiri hills \u2014 the source of the sacred Godavari river. It is the only Jyotirlinga in India with the Trimbaka (three-faced) lingam, representing Brahma, Vishnu, and Mahesh. The temple is particularly known for Rudrabhishek, Tripindi Shraddha (ancestral peace rituals), and Kalsarpa Dosha Nivaran puja \u2014 pilgrims come specifically for these from across India.Jyotirlinga Number: 9th of 12Darshan Timings: 5:30 AM \u2013 9:00 PMRudrabhishek: 7:00 AM \u2013 8:30 AM (advance booking required)From Mumbai: 180 km | approx. 4 hrs2. Grishneshwar Jyotirlinga, AurangabadGrishneshwar is the 12th and last of the 12 Jyotirlingas, located near Ellora village \u2014 just 1 km from the Ellora Caves. The temple features beautifully sculpted red-stone architecture. The presiding deity here is Lord Grishneshwar (Ghushmeshwar) and the lingam is a Shivling situated in a sacred water tank. The temple is also notable for being one of the few where the deity's name means 'Lord of Compassion.'Jyotirlinga Number: 12th of 12 \u2014 the last in the sacred sequenceDarshan Timings: 5:30 AM \u2013 9:30 PMMangal Aarti: 4:00 AM | Evening Aarti: 7:30 PMFrom Mumbai: 340 km | approx. 6 hrsNote: Ellora Caves (1 km away) are CLOSED every Tuesday.3. Bhimashankar Jyotirlinga, Pune DistrictBhimashankar is set in the Sahyadri hills, roughly 110 km from Pune and 240 km from Mumbai. At an altitude of approximately 3,250 feet, the temple sits inside the Bhimashankar Wildlife Sanctuary \u2014 home to the Indian Giant Squirrel, Maharashtra's state animal. The Bhima river originates here. The approach involves a scenic ghat road through dense forest. Of the three temples on this tour, Bhimashankar offers the most distinctive natural setting.Jyotirlinga Number: 6th of 12Darshan Timings: Morning: 4:30 AM \u2013 3:15 PM | Evening: 4:00 PM \u2013 9:30 PMMangal Aarti: 4:00 AM | Evening Aarti: 7:30 PMFrom Mumbai: 240 km | approx. 5 hrsNote: Heavy traffic and route diversions possible during Sawan (Shravan) month due to Kanwar Yatra pilgrim rush.Places CoveredPlaceLocationSignificanceTrimbakeshwar TempleNashik (28 km)9th Jyotirlinga; Trimbaka 3-faced lingam; Rudrabhishek; source of GodavariPanchavatiNashik cityRamkund; Sita Gufa; Kalaram Temple; Godavari riverfront \u2014 Ramayana connectionShirdiAhmednagar districtSai Baba Samadhi Mandir \u2014 one of India's most visited pilgrimage destinationsGrishneshwar TempleAurangabad (30 km)12th (last) Jyotirlinga; Mangal Aarti at 4 AM; unique water-tank lingamEllora CavesAurangabad (1 km)UNESCO World Heritage Site; 34 rock-cut caves; Kailash Temple (Cave 16)Shani ShingnapurAhmednagar districtOpen-air Shani shrine; village with no doors \u2014 unique in IndiaBhimashankar TemplePune district6th Jyotirlinga; Sahyadri hills; Wildlife Sanctuary; origin of Bhima riverBest Time to VisitSeasonMonthsConditionsBestOct \u2014 MarPleasant weather (15\u00b0C\u201328\u00b0C). Clear roads. Ideal for all age groups. Peak pilgrimage season.GoodApr \u2014 MayWarm but manageable. Plan darshan before 9 AM to avoid the midday heat.Plan carefullyJun \u2014 SepMonsoon. Bhimashankar ghat roads can be wet and slippery. Sawan month = very heavy rush at Trimbakeshwar & Bhimashankar. Book hotels 2\u20133 months in advance.How to Reach MumbaiBy AirChhatrapati Shivaji Maharaj International Airport (BOM) connects to all major domestic and international cities. Pune Airport (PNQ) is also an option \u2014 pickup from Pune can be arranged on request.By TrainMumbai CSMT and Mumbai Central are major rail hubs. Direct trains from Delhi, Bengaluru, Chennai, Hyderabad, and Kolkata. Nashik Road Station and Kopargaon (near Shirdi) also have direct rail connections from many cities.By RoadMumbai is on NH-48 (Mumbai\u2013Bengaluru expressway) and NH-160 (Mumbai\u2013Nashik expressway). Nashik is 180 km from Mumbai (3.5\u20134 hrs); Pune is 150 km (3 hrs).Package Price 2026Per person, double-sharing. Larger groups cost less per head.Category2 Persons4 Persons6 PersonsHotel TypeStandard\u20b918,150\u20b916,800\u20b915,650Standard hotels (Shirdi + Ahmednagar)Deluxe\u20b922,000\u20b920,000\u20b918,500Deluxe hotelsLuxury\u20b927,000\u20b924,500\u20b922,000Luxury hotelsSpecial Deal: Use coupon code NIT3GOLD \u2014 save \u20b92,500 (original \u20b918,150 \u2192 \u20b915,650, double sharing). Best price guaranteed.Book Your 3 Jyotirlinga Yatra \u2014 Maharashtra 2026Trimbakeshwar, Grishneshwar, Bhimashankar \u2014 three sacred Shiva shrines, one well-planned three-day circuit from Mumbai. Add Shirdi, Ellora Caves, and Shani Shingnapur and this becomes one of the most complete pilgrimage itineraries in Maharashtra.October to March is the best window. Shirdi hotels and Sawan-season slots fill up fast \u2014 early booking is recommended.WhatsApp: +91-9711616316 | Use code NIT3GOLD \u2014 save \u20b92,500. Booking confirmation within 2 hours.See Less",
    "highlights": [
      "Visit three Jyotirlingas of Lord Shiva \u2014 Trimbakeshwar, Grishneshwar, and Bhimashankar",
      "Trip to the holy town of Shirdi for Sai Baba Darshan",
      "Panchavati, Nashik \u2014 Sita Gufa, Kalaram Temple & Godavari Ghat",
      "Ellora Caves \u2014 UNESCO World Heritage Site & iconic Kailash Temple (Cave 16)",
      "Visit to the village of Lord Shani \u2014 Shani Shingnapur",
      "Trimbakeshwar's rare Trimbaka (three-faced) lingam \u2014 the only Jyotirlinga representing Brahma, Vishnu & Mahesh together",
      "Early morning Mangal Aarti at Grishneshwar (4:00 AM) and Bhimashankar (4:00 AM) \u2014 the most spiritually powerful hours at both shrines",
      "Bhimashankar set inside the Bhimashankar Wildlife Sanctuary, Sahyadri hills \u2014 a unique blend of pilgrimage and nature",
      "See More"
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1: Arrival in Mumbai (180 km/4 hrs) Trimbakeshwar (30 km/30 min) Panchavati - Shirdi (100 km/2 hrs)",
        "description": "Welcome to Mumbai, the city of dreams! On your arrival at airport/railway station, our team representative will give you a warm welcome!\nFrom here onwards, you\u2019ll be taken to your very first\nJyotirlinga of Maharashtra\n, that is,\nTrimbakeshwar Temple\n. Perform Darshan and Poojan to your heart\u2019s content.\nNow, you\u2019ll be transferred to Nashik, where you can indulge in some sightseeing at:\nPanchvati\nRamkund\nIn the evening, you\u2019ll be taken to\nShirdi\nwhere you\u2019ll check into your hotel. Enjoy an overnight stay there.\nNote:\nThe Darshan timing of the Trimbakeshwar Temple are from 5:30 am - 09:00 pm, while the Rudrabhishek timing are from 07:00 am - 08:30 am.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 2: Shirdi (100 km/2 hrs) Grishneshwar - Ellora (110 km/3 hrs) Shani Shingnapur (50 km/1 hrs) Ahmednagar",
        "description": "Get up early in the morning and proceed for the\nDarshan of Sai Baba\n.\nThereafter, you\u2019ll be taken for a trip to yet another Jyotirlinga \u2013\nGrishneshwar Temple\n!\nAfter your Darshan, it\u2019s time for a cultural visit to\nEllora Caves\n.\nThe last spot on today\u2019s sightseeing is\nShani Shingnapur\n, a village dedicated to Lord Shani!\nFinally, you\u2019ll be driven to Ahmednagar for overnight stay.\nNote:\nEllora Caves are closed on Tuesdays.\nNote:\nThe Darshan timings for the Grishneshwar Temple are from 5:30 am - 09:30 pm. The Mangal Aarti begins at 04:00 am and timing of the Evening Aarti is from 07:30 pm.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 3: Ahmednagar (180 km/4 hrs) Bhimashankar (100 km/2 hrs) Mumbai",
        "description": "Start your day early and have breakfast.\nNow, proceed towards the final Jyotirlinga of this tour leg, that is\nBhimashankar Temple\n. Perform your Poojan and Darshan, and in turn, seek blessings from the Lord.\nAfterwards, you\u2019ll be taken back to Mumbai. Our representative will drop you off at the airport or railway station, as per your wish.\nYour tour here concludes with us. Hope you had nice trip filled with happy memories!\nNote:\nThe Darshan timings at the Bhimashankar Jyotirlinga are: Morning 04:30 am - 03:15 pm, Evening 04:00 pm - 09:30 pm.\nNote:\nThe temple hosts Mangal Aarti at 04:00 am, and the evening Aarti at 07:30 pm.\nNote:\nIf you visit here in the Sawan months, then be aware of the fact that there could be heavy traffic or route diversion, owing to the large pilgrim traffic from Kanwar Yatra.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      }
    ],
