  "majestic-kumaon-tour": {
    "overview": "The Kumaon hills are referred to as majestic because of the kingly, ostensible affluence of nature\u2019s beauty available in the region. Tourists generally flock in this land to take the pleasure of the floral opulence and the untouched beauty of fauna in the region.\n\nThey also come here for the snow-peaked mountains and the gurgling sound of rushing water bodies that flow down straight from the Himalayas. This region has definitely something worth boasting in terms of wildlife sanctuaries and national parks which include the world famous Corbett National Park. Right next to the Kumaon region fall Rishikesh and Haridwar, two of the most prominent religious sites for Hindus in India. So, while you are on a tour to Kumaon region you can take short detours to these sites to fulfill your spiritual aspiration. All in all, Kumaon is a must visit the land with lakes and deep forests and serene ambiance that will lure any nature-lover who desires to take pleasure in this beauty.\nThis tour package form Namaste India-Trip is a good way to explore the undiscovered and unknown hill region of Kumaon lying in the Himalayan region. Our tour packages are most competitive in price with facility for customizing them according to your requirements, especially if you are on a shoe-string budget. We take utmost care of all our customers so that they get back full services in lieu of the investment that they make through bookings. This tour gives you a full tour of the Kumaon region including the Corbett National Park and excursion of places like Ranikhet and Nainital for those in search of adventure. You will also come across the divine temples of ancient origins and sporting arenas like the golf course of this region while completing this tour. Enjoy the chilly air and fresh breath along with the scenic view of the Himalayas without any discomfort through this package of ours.",
    "highlights": [
      "Visit to the Jim Corbett National Park",
      "Be a part of nature at Ranikhet \u2018The Queen of Fields\u2019",
      "Get some divine blessings at the Baijnath Temple",
      "A sail through the Shimla lakes Sat Tal, Bhimtal, and Naukuchia"
    ],
