  "mathura-gokul-barsana-vrindavan-tour": {
    "overview": "Are you a Lord Krishna devotee? Then this 3 day trip in the state of Uttar Pradesh is for you! Book our Mathura Gokul Barsana and Vrindavan Tour Package and visit the lands of Lord Krishna in comfort and luxury.See More\n\nFilled with pilgrimage sites, ranging from where he took birth to the very place to where he was king in the adulthood of his life, you have a lot to explore and experience on this trip. Call us now to know more about this package!From Ghat visits to attending the holy Yamuna Aarti in the evening, your whole trip is blessed with special activities. We\u2019ll also be visiting Barsana, the birthplace of Radha, Lord Krishna\u2019s love consort. Plus, you\u2019ll be taking the highly spiritual Govardhan Parikrama. And we\u2019ll take care of all the tour logistics for you on this trip \u2013 from meals to accommodation. Book this package now and go on a smooth trip!\n\nFilled with pilgrimage sites, ranging from where he took birth to the very place to where he was king in the adulthood of his life, you have a lot to explore and experience on this trip. Call us now to know more about this package!\n\nFrom Ghat visits to attending the holy Yamuna Aarti in the evening, your whole trip is blessed with special activities. We\u2019ll also be visiting Barsana, the birthplace of Radha, Lord Krishna\u2019s love consort. Plus, you\u2019ll be taking the highly spiritual Govardhan Parikrama. And we\u2019ll take care of all the tour logistics for you on this trip \u2013 from meals to accommodation. Book this package now and go on a smooth trip!",
    "highlights": [
      "Visit Vrindavan, one of India\u2019s most popular spiritual destinations.",
      "Explore Old & New Delhi, with its monuments, history, and bustling markets.",
      "Divine visit to Mathura & Vrindavan, Lord Krishna\u2019s birthplace.",
      "Immerse in local culture, colourful bazaars, traditional crafts, and cuisine.",
      "Guided tours by professional English-speaking guides at key sites.",
      "Travel comfortably in a private AC vehicle with hassle-free pick-up and drop-off.",
      "Follow a curated itinerary for a memorable and enriching experience.",
      "See More"
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1: Arrival in Delhi - Travel to Mathura - Explore Gokul Temple (180-185 kms, Approx. 5-6 hrs drive)",
        "description": "Your tour will start from Delhi. Our representative will pick you up from the airport/railway station. Your Mathura-Gokul-Vrindavan tour begins!\nNow you\u2019ll be driven to\nMathura\n, a 4-hour drive approximately. Along the way, we\u2019ll stop for refreshment at a restaurant of your choice.\nOur very first stop on this tour will be at the\nShri Krishna Janmabhoomi Temple\n. This marks the birthplace of Lord Krishna. This is a temple complex and houses various other temples inside it, such as the\nKrishna Janmasthan Temple\nand the\nGarbha Griha\n. Feel free to explore them!\nThe next temple we\u2019ll be visiting is the Dwarkadhish Temple, where Lord Krishna is worshipped as the king of Dwarka. Do take photographs of the intricate architecture and the temple's fa\u00e7ade.\nAfter that, we\u2019ll take you to the\nVishram Ghat\n, which is famous for being the place where Lord Krishna rested after he defeated the cruel Kansa.\nNow, take a lunch break at any of the local restaurants in Mathura. Thereafter, you\u2019ll be taken on a drive to\nGokul\n(20 minutes).\nOnce you get there, get ready for a full-blown temple tour dedicated to Lord Krishna, such as:\nGokulnath Temple\nRaja Thakur Temple\nBrahmand Ghat\nRaman Reti\nChintaharan Mahadev and 84 Khamba\nAfter that, enjoy the\nYamuna Aarti\nat the Ghat. Take in the blessed vibes of the charged atmosphere!\nYour overnight stay will be in Mathura\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 2: Mathura to Vrindavan (18 kms, Approx. 30-35 minutes drive)",
        "description": "Treat yourself to a delicious breakfast in the morning. After that, you\u2019ll be taken to the divine lands of\nVrindavan!\nLord Krishna spent his youth here.\nHere, you'll be taken on a temple tour of:\nBanke Bihari Temple:\nYou\u2019ll find the atmosphere here filled with devotion.\nNidhivan\nStroll through the forest where once Lord Krishna and Gopis had Rasleela!\nISKCON Temple:\nThe serene environment here is next level! Do capture the pics of the temple domes and architecture.\nRadha Vallabh Ji Temple:\nThis temple symbolises the epitome of the divine love that Radha felt for Lord Krishna.\nVaishno Devi Temple:\nIt\u2019s a replica of Jammu\u2019s original shrine.\nPrem Mandir:\nThis temple has a load of sculptures of Lord Krishna, which depict his life. Do attend the Light and Sound Show here if time permits.\nNow, return to the hotel and get a restful night of sleep.\nNote:\nBanke Bihari Temple remains closed from 12 PM to 5:30 PM daily.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 3: Barsana \u2013 Nandgaon \u2013 Govardhan Parikrama \u2013 Transfer to Delhi (185 km/4 hrs)",
        "description": "Relish a delicious breakfast in the morning\nNow, you\u2019ll be driven to\nBarsana\n, which is the birthplace of Radha Rani.\nThe very first site that you\u2019ll visit here will be the\nRadha Rani Temple\n(aka the Shriji Temple or Ladli Ji). Enjoy the enthusiasm that devotees show here, and let some get brushed on you!\nAfter this, you'll be taken to the place where Lord Krishna spent his childhood, that is,\nNandgaon\n!\nAlso, take this time to visit the nearby prominent sites, like\nYashoda Kund\nand\nSunehri Kothi\n.\nNow, head towards\nGovardhan\n. This is the very place where Lord Krishna performed his divine Leela by lifting the whole Govardhan Mountain! Once you\u2019re there, take part in the\nGovardhan Parikrama\n, a distance of 7 km.\nYou can also explore the nearby temples, such as:\nMansi Ganga\nHaridev Temple\nDaan Ghati Temple\nThis concludes your trip. Now, you\u2019ll be driven to Delhi by our driver, where you\u2019ll be dropped off at the airport or railway station (by 10 PM). Hope you have made wonderful memories on this tour.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      }
    ],
    "faqs": []
  },
  "mathura-gokul-vrindavan-weekend-tour-from-delhi": {
    "overview": "Welcome to the Mathura-Gokul-Vrindavan tour! This divine trip will take you to the birthplace of Lord Krishna and so many more places that are deeply linked to him.See More\n\nWe\u2019ll be taking you to various temples on this trip where you can seek the blessing of the God. Visit the Dwarkadhish Temple and witness the lord in his most regal form, that is, a king! Enjoy the peaceful environment of the ISKCON Temple and see the beautiful Banke Bihari Temple.You can also learn more about the life of Lord Krishna through Prem Mandir. This temple showcases his life throughout sculptures. Stroll through the Nidhivan where Lord Krishna played Raas Leela with the Gopis! You\u2019ll also spend time at the Ghats, where you can enjoy evening Aarti. This devotional trip is perfect for you if you\u2019re a Lord Krishna devotee!\n\nWe\u2019ll be taking you to various temples on this trip where you can seek the blessing of the God. Visit the Dwarkadhish Temple and witness the lord in his most regal form, that is, a king! Enjoy the peaceful environment of the ISKCON Temple and see the beautiful Banke Bihari Temple.\n\nYou can also learn more about the life of Lord Krishna through Prem Mandir. This temple showcases his life throughout sculptures. Stroll through the Nidhivan where Lord Krishna played Raas Leela with the Gopis! You\u2019ll also spend time at the Ghats, where you can enjoy evening Aarti. This devotional trip is perfect for you if you\u2019re a Lord Krishna devotee!\n\nTour GalleryTour NameMathura Gokul Vrindavan Weekend Tour from DelhiTour Duration2 Days / 1 NightsMealsBreakfast & DinnerVehicle TypeSedan / SUVStarting & Ending PointDelhiDestination CoveredMathura - Gokul - Vrindavan Pickup TimeDepend on your Flight Timing Tour BenefitsBest price & enjoyable travel guarantee",
    "highlights": [
      "Visit Vrindavan, one of India\u2019s most popular spiritual destinations.",
      "Explore Old & New Delhi, with its historic monuments, bustling markets, and vibrant culture.",
      "Divine journey to Mathura & Vrindavan, the birthplace of Lord Krishna.",
      "Immerse in local life, from colourful bazaars and traditional crafts to delicious cuisine.",
      "Benefit from expert guidance with professional live tour guides at key sites.",
      "Enjoy hassle-free travel with pick-up and drop-off assistance.",
      "Travel comfortably in a private AC vehicle at your own pace.",
      "Follow a thoughtfully planned itinerary for a memorable and enriching experience.",
      "See More"
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1: Delhi \u2013 Mathura \u2013 Gokul (185 km/4 hrs)",
        "description": "Our representative will greet you with a warm welcome once you arrive at the Delhi airport/railway station.\nNow, you\u2019ll be driven to Mathura from here, which will take about 4 hours. Along the way, we\u2019ll stop at a restaurant for breakfast.\nOnce we arrive at the destination, you\u2019ll be taken to your very first temple of this tour, that is\nShri Krishna Janmabhoomi Temple\n- the birthplace of Lord Krishna! Explore the various shrines here, like the\nKrishna Janmasthan Temple\nand the\nGarbha Griha\n.\nAfter this, you\u2019ll be taken to the\nDwarkadhish Temple\n. This is one of the most revered temples of Mathura, where Lord Krishna is worshipped as the King of Dwarka! Do take pictures of the beautiful temple carvings at the temple!\nThe next place we'll be visiting is the\nVishram Ghat\n. Lord Krishna rested here after he defeated Kansa.\nNow, take some time out for lunch. Then, we\u2019ll drive you to\nGokul\n, which is just a short drive from here. Once you get there, visit the following:\nGokulnath Temple\nRaja Thakur Temple\nBrahmand Ghat\nRaman Reti\nChintaharan Mahadev and 84 Khamba\nSpend the evening at the\nYamuna Ghat\nand take in the divine atmosphere of the Aarti. The lit-up surroundings make for a perfect photo op!\nHave a rest at night at your hotel in Mathura\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "DAY 2: Vrindavan Temple Tour - Delhi Departure (159 km/4-5 hrs)",
        "description": "Relish a yummy breakfast in the morning.\nAfter that, you'll be taken on a temple tour with visits to:\nBanke Bihari Temple:\nThis is the heart of Vrindavan\u2019s devotion! Do take pictures of the colourful garlands at Banke Bihari!\nNidhivan:\nTake an afternoon visit to this mysterious grove where Krishna and Gopis are still believed to visit at night!\nISKCON Temple:\nThe serene and spiritual environment here will rejuvenate your soul\nRadha Vallabh Ji Temple:\nThis temple stands as a testament to the surreal love of Radha and Lord Krishna!\nVaishno Devi Temple:\nVisit the replica of the original Jammu temple!\nPrem Mandir:\nExplore the life of Lord Krishna, which is depicted beautifully here through the sculptural artwork. Do not forget to capture pics of the stunning illuminated facade of the temple.\nAfter this, you'll be taken back to Delhi, where you'll be dropped off at the airport or the railway station by 10 PM. Hope you have a blessed tour!\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      }
    ],
    "faqs": []
  },
