  "mumbai-sightseeing-tour": {
    "overview": "Popularly known as the city that never sleeps a tour package to Mumbai will take you across some of the most iconic sites and other impressive tourist attractions which makes this city what it is. Also known as the entertainment hub Mumbai has a vast and a fascinating history. Experience the eclectic blend of the bygone era and the modern age with our specially curated Tour to dream city Mumbai travel package which is available in the cheapest and pocket-friendly rates.\n\nMumbai Sightseeing Tour Itinerary Package\n\n\nDay 1 :Arrival in Mumbai\n\n\nUpon your arrival in Mumbai, our tour representative will guide you to your allotted hotel and get you checked in for an overnight stay. Evening time will be free for you to explore the city on foot and spend some leisurely time exploring this colorful city on your own. You have the option of visiting the famous Juhu beach and peacefully watch the setting sun. Do not miss out on savoring the staple and the most loved food item of Mumbai \u2013 Vada Pao.\n\n\n\n\nDay 2 :Mumbai Sightseeing\n\n\nEarly in the morning, your sightseeing tour of Mumbai will commence. Your first destination will be to the Elephanta cave \u2013 a 7th century UNESCO world heritage site containing ancient rock art linked to Lord Shiva. You will then be taken for a brief sightseeing of Gateway of India on your way back from the caves since the way to the cave is from here itself and is located at a distance of 10 kms from the shores of Mumbai. You will then be made to drive by some of the most iconic British era structures of Mumbai like \u2013 Mumbai University, Rajabai clock tower, high court and Chhatrapati Shivaji Terminus.\nIn case you are a shopaholic, you have the option of taking a stroll across the famous centre of fashion \u2013 Fashion Street which is a stretch of road adorned with shops containing export clothes and accessories. Later on in the evening, you will be made to drive past queen\u2019s necklace or also known as marine drive. After spending some quiet time at the drive you will be made to proceed on towards Malabar Hills which is home to the famous Jain temple, Kamla Nehru Park and Hanging garden.\nAfter wholesome tour of the city, you will be made to return back to the hotel for an overnight stay.\n\n\n\n\nDay 3 :Mumbai Departure\n\n\nEarly in the morning, you will be transferred to the closest railway station/airport from where you will be boarded the flight/train heading onward towards desired destination.",
    "highlights": [
      "Enjoy the relaxed beaches and savor the local Vada Pav",
