  "ooty-kodaikanal-tour": {
    "overview": "Experience the best of Ooty and Kodaikanal with My Quick Trippers\u2019s Ooty Kodaikanal Tour Package of 5 days and 4 nights. You will be immersed in the natural scenic beauty of the surrounding landscape which will definitely freshen up your mood. These two hill stations are a boon in the southern part of the sub-continent and holds reserve to some of the most charming destinations in India.\n\nOoty Kodaikanal Tour Itinerary Package\n\n\nDay 1 :Arrival in Ooty\n\n\nYou will be transferred to Ooty, the queen of hill stations in South India, from your pick up point of Coimbatore, which is located at a distance of 3 hours and 15 mines. Upon arriving in Ooty you will be straightaway escorted to your hotel leaving the evening free for you to do some leisure activities.\nStroll along with the vibrant market places of Ooty and get yourself some vital souvenirs like tea, chocolates, trinkets, handicrafts, and a whole plethora of quirky and whimsical items.\nYou can also gorge on some delicious locally made cuisines like egg dosa, ghee roast, Pongal, vada chutney and so much more.\n\n\n\n\nDay 2 :Ooty Sightseeing \u2013 Excursion to Coonoor \u2013 Ooty\n\n\nEarly in the morning, your tour of this wonderfully quaint hill station will commence, starting with a breathtaking visit to the highest mountain in Nilgiri Hills Doddabetta peak. The entire peak is surrounded with thick forests and it also houses a telescope house on the peak from where you will be able to view the magnificent rolling valley.\nYour excursion to Coonoor will commence after this, which takes 1 hour to reach. Here you will be made to take an exclusive tour of the city starting with Sim\u2019s park, which is home to a rich collection of birds, plants, and animals making it a pleasant picnic spot.\nYour next stop in Coonoor will be dolphin\u2019s nose from where you will feel like you are on top of the world since it is situated at a height of 5,075 feet above sea level. This enormous unique rock formation resembles a dolphin\u2019s nose (hence the name) and attracts numerous visitors who can view the Catherin falls from here.\nAs the afternoon approaches you will be transferred back to Ooty where you will be taken to the famous Ooty Lake, which is a manmade lake where people can enjoy several activities that take place on the shore as well as on the water. From different types of boating to spending some quality time with your loved ones in a picnic, this lake is a must-visit.\n\n\n\n\nDay 3 :Ooty \u2013 Kodaikanal\n\n\nYou will be transferred to Kodaikanal early in the morning for a half-day of sightseeing tour starting with a visit to Bryant Park, which dazzles the visitors with its glorious collection of colorful plants everywhere.\nTiming \u2013 9 am to 6 pm (7 days a week)\nEntry fees \u2013 rupees 30/- (adults); rupees 15/- (children)\nYour next stop will be the picturesque and magnificent site of Coaker\u2019s walk, which is like taking a walk in fairyland with mist flowing low. Walking by the hillside is definitely an experience to remember. You will be able to feast on the magnificent views of the rolling green hills from here.\nTimings \u2013 7 am to 7 pm\nEntry fees \u2013 rupees 10/-\nYou will then be transferred to Pillar Rock, which is another one of the most unique naturally occurring rock formations which are in the shape of three pillars. From here you will be able to view the never-ending mountains as far as your eyes can see.\nTiming \u2013 9 am to 4 pm\nEntry fees \u2013 rupees 5/-\nYour final sightseeing spot will be the manmade lake called Kodaikanal Lake and is Kodaikanal one of the most popular tourist attraction and landmarks attracting tourists from all over India and across the globe as well. Avail the boating services here, which will take you on a soothing ride on the calming blue water.\nTiming \u2013 6 am to 5 pm\nEntry fees \u2013 free of cost\nAfter a fun-packed day, you will be taken back to your hotel which is allotted for Kodaikanal.\n\n\n\n\nDay 4 :Kodaikanal Departure\n\n\nYou will be checked out of your hotel early in the morning and be preceded to your onward destination.",
    "highlights": [
      "Welcome to the Queen of the Hills Ooty and its sightseeing",
      "Visit the Dolphin Nose in Coonoor",
      "Go to visit the birds and plants at the Sim\u2019s Park",
      "Kodaikanal sightseeing with visit to Bryant Park",
      "Have a look at the Pillar Rock",
      "Enjoy the paddle boat rise at the famous Kodaikanal Lake"
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1 :Arrival in Ooty",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 2 :Ooty Sightseeing \u2013 Excursion to Coonoor \u2013 Ooty",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 3 :Ooty \u2013 Kodaikanal",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 4 :Kodaikanal Departure",
