  "pachmarhi-tour-package": {
    "overview": "The name Pachmarhi is said to have originated from the Hindi words Panch (\u201cfive\u201d) and Marhi (\u201ccaves\u201d). Tradition holds that during their thirteen years of exile, the five Pandava brothers of the Mahabharatha era built these caverns. The lofty position of the caverns makes them an excellent vantage point. One of the most famous tourist attractions in India is the isolated hill village of Pachmarhi, which is entirely covered in stunning flora. Pachmarhi does add a new flavour to this Central Indian curry, and the state is widely recognised for its rich heritage, historical sites, and lush forest. The Pachmarhi 3 days / 2 nights tour will take you on a short yet exciting journey.\n\nPachmarhi Sightseeing Tour Itinerary Package\n\n\nDay 1 :Pachmarhi Arrival\n\n\nThe My Quick Trippers representative will receive you at Pachmarhi and take you to the hotel for check-in and rest. You can come out later in the day to stroll around the town and shop from the local market. Overnight stay will take place in the Pachmarhi hotel.\n\n\n\n\nDay 2 :At Pachmarhi\n\n\nOn day 2 post breakfast you will drive to the various tourist spots in Pachmarhi all through the day. Your day will start with \u2018Jata Shankar\u2019 visit which is a \u2018sacred cave\u2019 situated under lose boulders displaying nature\u2019s unique architecture. Move on to \u2018Christ Church\u2019 which crucially reminds of the colonial rule here. The architecture of the church reminds you of the European style of architecture especially with the altar and walls brought from that region. You can take a break and get back to your hotel to take lunch. Post lunch you will be taken to other sites of tourist attraction in Pachmarhi. Go to the Bee Falls to get closer to nature and then move on to the \u2018Vaniki Sangrahalya\u2019 (Bison Lodge) followed by the \u2018Bal Udayan (Children\u2019s park). To get a scenic view of the sunset visit the \u2018Noka Vihar\u2019 and take a boat ride in the Pachmarhi Lake here. Proceed to Dhoopgarh which is the \u2018highest peak\u2019 in the Pachmarhi region. Return to your hotel for night stay.\n\n\n\n\nDay 3 :Pachmarhi\n\n\nDay 3 is the final day and after a filling breakfast, you will check out of the hotel. The My Quick Trippers representative will assist you safely to the point from where you will return home with unforgettable memories.",
    "highlights": [
      "Visit to the Jata Shankar the divine cave",
      "Tour to other spots in Pachmarhi",
      "A boat ride in the Pachmarhi Lake",
      "Enjoy the local flavor and hospitality"
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1 :Pachmarhi Arrival",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 2 :At Pachmarhi",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 3 :Pachmarhi",
        "description": ""
      }
    ],
    "faqs": []
  },
