  "panch-dwaraka-tour": {
    "overview": "The Panch Dwarka religious tour is one of the most sacred pilgrimages you can cover in India. This tour essentially consists of visiting the five sacred temples of Lord Krishna - Dwarkadhish Temple, Bet Dwarka, Ranchhodraiji Temple, Nathdwara Shrinathji Temple, and Kankroli Dwarkadhish Temple. Book our Pancha Dwaraka Tour Package and visit these shrines hassle-free. Give us a call now!\n\nDiscover the centuries of legends and learn about the divine miracles that have happened here. This spiritual tour is a must-visit for every Krishna devotee. To ease your tour, we offer you Pancha Dwaraka Yatra from Delhi, Mumbai, Bangalore, Ahmedabad, Pune, and other big cities. This temple tour in Gujarat and Rajasthan will fill you with devotion & peace, and you'll return home with abundance of blessings. Book the tour plan now or drop us an email if you have any queries about this trip.\nWhat is Pancha Dwaraka?\nThe Pancha Dwaraka pilgrimage tour refers to visiting the five sacred Krishna temples. Here are the shrines that you will visit on this tour:\n\nDwarkadhish Temple - This temple worships Lord Krishna as the king of the Dwarkadhish. It is over 2,000 years old. You'll find here the popular black stone idol of Dwarkadhish, which is revered with Aarti session on a daily basis. Come here for the Mangla Aarti and Bhog Darshan. The Dwarkadhish Temple Yatra is also a part of the Chardham pilgrimage.\nBet Dwarka - Welcome to Lord Krishna's royal residence! He used to live here with his family. The Dwaraka Bet island temple tour also offers you serene beaches and other peaceful temples in the nearby areas.\nRanchhodraiji Temple- An essential part of any Pancha Dwaraka Trip Package, this temple worships Lord Krishna as \"the one who left the battlefield\". Inside the temple, you'll find the 6-foot-tall black figure of Lord Krishna adorned with beautiful clothes and jewellery. Also, marvel at the Haveli-style architecture of the temple.\nShrinathji Temple - This temple worships Lord Krishna in his Govardhan-lifting form. You can come here for the Darshan, which is divided into 8 daily Jhankis.\nKankroli Dwarkadheesh Temple - Located near Rajsamand Lake, this shrine is a part of every Pancha Dwaraka pilgrimage circuit. It's also known as \"Haveli of Krishna\". Devotees just love the peaceful surroundings of this area.\n\nCost of Pancha Dwaraka Tour Package\nThe Pancha Dwaraka Tour Package price starts from INR 18,000 per person and goes up to INR 23,000. My Quick Trippers offers you customizable tour plans that let you go on a pilgrimage of your dreams.\nWe offer you a Panch Dwarka Darshan package with AC transport, which will help you travel to the holy shrines in utter comfort and ease. Also, on this holy trip, we'll take full care of your meals, Darshan assistance, and hotel bookings.\nBook our tour plans now and avail an early bird Pancha Dwaraka pilgrimage tour discounts! Give us a call now.\nWhy Book Your Pancha Dwaraka Pilgrimage With My Quick Trippers?\nWe are a trusted name in the travel industry and are one of the best Pancha Dwaraka travel agencies in India. Here are some reasons why you should book with us:\n\n10+ years of experience in pilgrimage tour\nKrishna temples Gujarat Darshan assistance\nPre-booked hotels near temples\nCustomizable Pancha Dwaraka tour itinerary\nExperienced and Verified drivers\nBudget Panch Dwaraka tour package with meals\n24\u00d77 Support throughout the trip\n\nBest Time to Visit Pancha Dwaraka Temples\nThe best time to visit Pancha Dwaraka is in the winter season - October to March. During this period, the heat subsides, giving way to the pleasant cold. In this window, you can comfortably cover your temple trips in addition to the sightseeing in nearby areas.\nTry to book Pancha Dwaraka Yatra package during the Janmashtami & Diwali festivals and see the grandeur of the temple in a new light! However, be wary of the fact that there would be large crowds during this time.\nWhere to Stay during Panch Dwaraka Trip?\nDuring your pilgrimage, you'll be visiting places like Dwarka, Nathdwara, and Udaipur. Here are some quality hotels that you can consider during your trip:\n\n\n\nDestination\nRecommended Hotels\n\n\n\n\nDwarka\n \u2022 Hawthorn Suites by Wyndham \u2022 Hotel Gomti Dwarka \u2022 VITS Devbhumi \n\n\nNathdwara\n \u2022 Justa Brij Bhoomi \u2022 Shree Vallabh Vilas Lords Plaza \u2022 The Marutinandan \n\n\nUdaipur\n \u2022 Hotel Lakend \u2022 The Fern Residency \u2022 Blu Feather Hotel \n\n\n\nYou can also book our Pancha Dwaraka temple tour with hotel and transport, and enjoy the trip without worrying about your accommodation or the transfers. We'll handle it all!\nHow to Reach Pancha Dwaraka Temples?\nYou can visit the temples in a variety of ways. The best route for Pancha Dwaraka Yatra is to reach Dwarka first and then continue the temple tour from there on. Here's how you can reach the holy city of Dwarka:\nBy Air\nFly to the Jamnagar Airport from your city. This is the nearest airport to Dwarka and takes about 3 hours to get there (137 km). The airport is served by regular flights from major cities like Delhi, Mumbai, Bangalore, Hyderabad, and more.\nBy Train\nReach the Dwarka Railway Station, which receives regular trains from hubs like Delhi, Mumbai, Ahmedabad, Vadodara, Jaipur, Kolkata, etc.\nPancha Dwaraka Tour Itinerary - Route to Temples\nOnce you reach Dwarka, the most convenient and fastest way to cover the Panch Dwarka temple circuit is by a road trip.\n\nStart your trip with the Dwarkadhish Temple. It's the westernmost temple and provides easy connectivity to the other temples.\nNow, proceed to Bet Dwarka. Reach the Okha Jetty (40 minutes) and from there on take a ferry to the island (15-20 minutes).\nThe third temple on the list is the Ranchhodraiji Temple. For this, go to Dakor - a journey of 430 km which will take about 8 hours. Here's the route map from Dwarka to Ranchhodraiji Temple:Dwarka \u2192 Jamnagar \u2192 Rajkot \u2192 Ahmedabad \u2192 Dakor\nNow, reach Nathdwara. This would be a 270 km journey and will take about 5-6 hours to cover the entire trip. Here's the route map from Dakor to Shrinathji Temple:Dakor \u2192 Modasa \u2192 Himmatnagar \u2192 Udaipur \u2192 Nathdwara\nThe last temple on the Panch Dwarka Temple Tour is the Kankroli Dwarkadhish Temple. It's located about 18 km from Nathdwara and can be reached by a 20-minute car drive.\n\nBook our all-inclusive Pancha Dwaraka tour and enjoy the whole trip in comfort and luxury. You'll be visiting the temples in your private, AC vehicle without worrying about any routes whatsoever. Our professional driver will take you to the shrines and all you have to do is sit back & relax! Book now!!\nTravel Tips for Pancha Dwaraka Yatra\nHere is some travel advice for your trip:\n\nStart your tour early in the morning to avoid traffic.\nDuring weekends, the ferry rush is especially large at the Bet Dwarka. So plan your trip accordingly.\nTo avoid rush and hassle, book your Aarti slots in advance for Shrinathji Temple.\nSmall shops near temples might not accept online payment methods like UPI. Therefore, we suggest carrying cash with you.\nWear modest clothes for your Panch Dwarka temple trip! Make sure your knees and shoulders are covered.\nDuring your travel, keep yourself hydrated and energised. Keep a water bottle with you and a few sachets of ORS.\nDo not engage in photography inside the temples.\n\nBook the Best Pancha Dwaraka Tour Package!\nHop on the temple tour of Pancha Dwaraka and experience the real devotion to Lord Krishna. You'll be covering the sacred Krishna temples tour in Gujarat and Rajasthan, all in luxury and comfort. Receive the divine blessings from the God himself and experience a deep spiritual awakening.\nWhether you're going solo or looking for a Pancha Dwaraka travel package for families, we provide it all. Our experienced travel team will see to it that you have hassle-free and memorable Darshan. Besides that, we'll have you travel in comfortable AC cars. Book now or give us a call to get a quote for this trip.",
    "highlights": [
      "Dwarkadhish Dham Darshan",
      "Homage at Rukmini Temple",
      "Nageshwar Temple visit",
      "Somnath temple visit",
      "Visit the Tara Mandir Planetarium before continuing on to Porbandar to see the Kirti Mandir, Mahatma Gandhi's home.",
      "V8isit to Junagadh and Godal",
      "Ahmedabad sightseeing",
      "Pay a visit to Matru Gaya Ambaji",
      "Mount Abu and Udaipur excursion"
    ],
