  "pancha-bhoota-sthalam-navagraha-package": {
    "overview": "Explore South India\u2019s famous temples with the Pancha Bootha Sthalam Navagraha Tour Package. See More\n\nIn 6 days, you will visit the five temples that represent Earth, Water, Fire, Air, and Space, and also explore nine special Navagraha shrines, dedicated to the nine planets.\nEach temple has its own story, importance, and unique rituals that tourists should never miss. In our itineraries, you\u2019ll get all the interesting details about the temples, what to see, and their special stories - all clearly explained for you.\nDistance is never a problem - we organize comfortable tours for people from all cities. We provide selected hotels, convenient transport, skilled guides, and more. So enjoy the Pancha Bootha Sthalam and Navagraha Temples Tour Plan with us for an unforgettable spiritual journey!\nSee Less\n\nIn 6 days, you will visit the five temples that represent Earth, Water, Fire, Air, and Space, and also explore nine special Navagraha shrines, dedicated to the nine planets.\n\nEach temple has its own story, importance, and unique rituals that tourists should never miss. In our itineraries, you\u2019ll get all the interesting details about the temples, what to see, and their special stories - all clearly explained for you.\n\nDistance is never a problem - we organize comfortable tours for people from all cities. We provide selected hotels, convenient transport, skilled guides, and more. So enjoy the Pancha Bootha Sthalam and Navagraha Temples Tour Plan with us for an unforgettable spiritual journey!",
    "highlights": [
      "Explore South India\u2019s famous Pancha Bootha Sthalam temples ( Earth, Water, Fire, Air, Space ) and 9 Navagraha shrines dedicated to the planets.",
      "Each temple has unique stories, rituals and attractions explained clearly in trip to make your visit meaningful and easy to follow.",
      "Comfortable travel with selected hotels, convenient transport and guides from all cities ensures a smooth 6-day spiritual journey.",
      "Top photo spots include Brihadeeswara Temple\u2019s towering vimana and Nandi statue, sunrise or late afternoon being the best time for pictures.",
      "See More"
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1: Tirupati - Srikalahasti - Kanchipuram (Approx. 175 kms/ 3-4 Hours)",
        "description": "Start your tour with a pick-up from your chosen spot in Tirupati, whether it\u2019s the airport, railway station, or any other location. Our\nMy Quick Trippers\nteam will pick you up and help you all day. If you book a guide, they will join the driver to assist during sightseeing.\nAfter pick-up, you will start your tour and visit-\nSrikalahasteeswara Temple:\nPart of the Pancha Bootha temples, which represents the Air element (Vaayu). A fascinating fact about this temple is that a lamp keeps moving on its own, even without any wind.\nOnce the darshan is complete, travel to\nKanchipuram.\nOn arrival, check into your hotel for the night.\nNote:\nSrikalahasteeswara Temple is open from 6 am to 9 pm.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "DAY 2: Kanchipuram - Tiruvannamalai (153 kms/ 3 Hours)",
        "description": "After breakfast check out of the hotel and visit\nKamakshi Amman Temple,\ndedicated to Goddess Kamakshi. This temple is also one of the Shakti Peethas, where Goddess Sati\u2019s navel ( nabhi ) fell.\nThen, see\nVaradharaja Perumal Temple\n, a famous Vishnu temple and one of the 108 Divya Desams.\nNow continue the journey to the\nKailasanathar Temple\n, which is around 1,300 years old, dedicated to Lord Shiva. Then proceed to\nEkambareswarar Temple,\nwhich represents the Earth element ( Prithvi ).\nTravel to\nKumarakottam Temple\n, dedicated to Lord Murugan. If time permits, you can also visit Kanchipuram\u2019s markets, famous for silk sarees.\nLater, drive to\nTiruvannamalai.\nThis town is known for the\nAnnamalaiyar Temple.\nThe temple is one of the largest in India and is part of the Pancha Bootha, connected to Fire (Agni). This place is beautiful, so don\u2019t forget to take some photos.\nWhen you arrive, check into your hotel and stay overnight in\nTiruvannamalai.\nNight stay at Tiruvannamalai\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "DAY 3: Tiruvannamalai \u2013 Pondicherry - Chidambaram - Kumbakonam (205 - 210 kms/ 5.5-6 Hours)",
        "description": "After breakfast check out from the hotel and drive to\nPondicherry.\nVisit\nAuroville Matrimandir\n, where people from different parts of the world come to meditate and experience peace. Try to meditate here - this place is known for its inner peace.\nThen check into your hotel and visit\nSri Aurobindo Ashram,\none of India\u2019s most famous and wealthiest ashrams, where people from across the world come for spiritual peace.\nNext, travel to\nArulmigu Manakula Vinayagar Temple,\ndedicated to Lord Ganesh.\nThen visit\nPuducherry Museum\n, famous for its impressive collection of 81 ancient metal statues from India\u2019s history. You will love the artwork !\nLater, drive to\nChidambaram,\na town famous for the\nThillai Nataraja Temple,\nspread over 40 acres. Nataraja Temple is one of the Pancha Bootha temples and represents the element of Sky (Akasha).\nAfter that, proceed to\nKumbakonam.\nIf time permits, explore two temples -\nGangaikonda Cholapuram\nand\nVaitheeswaran Koil.\nNote-\nPuducherry Museum remains closed on Mondays and public holidays.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "DAY 4: Kumbakonam ( Navagraha Tour )",
        "description": "Morning after breakfast, check out of the hotel and proceed for sightseeing in\nKumbakonam\na town famous for its many temples.\nExplore\nAdi Kumbeswarar Temple\nand also visit the nearby\nMahamaham Tank\nwhere pilgrims take a holy bath.\nThen go to\nAiravatesvara Temple\nat\nDarasuram,\na UNESCO World Heritage Site.\nNext continue your\nNavagraha temple tour\nand visit\nThingalur\n(Moon),\nAlangudi\n(Jupiter),\nThirunageswaram\n(Rahu),\nSuriyanar Kovil\n(Sun),\nKanjanur\n(Venus),\nVaitheeswaran Koil\n(Mars),\nThiruvenkadu\n(Mercury),\nKeezhaperumpallam\n(Ketu) and\nThirunallar temple\n(Saturn).\nAfter completing the temple visits return to your hotel in\nKumbakonam\nfor an overnight stay.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "DAY 5: Kumbakonam - Thanjavur- Trichy (140-150 / 3-3.5 Hours)",
        "description": "After breakfast, drive to Thanjavur (Tanjore).\nOn arrival, visit\nBrihadeeswara Temple\n, the main attraction of Thanjavur and is a UNESCO World Heritage Site. Its tall vimana tower is so high that you can see it from miles away - it feels like it touches the sky (a great photo spot).\nVisit\nThanjavur Palace\nnext, where the Maratha rulers lived from 1674 to 1855.\nThen, visit\nThanjavur Art Gallery\nto see a collection of old metal and stone statues and other historic items from Tamil history.\nLater, drive to\nTiruchirappalli\n(Trichy). On arrival, check into the hotel for an overnight stay.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "DAY 6: Trichy Local Sightseeing & Departure",
        "description": "After breakfast, check out from your hotel and begin your sightseeing tour of\nTiruchirapalli (Trichy).\nYour first stop will be the famous\nSri Ranganatha Swamy Temple\nin\nSrirangam\n- one of the 108 holy Vishnu temple known as Divya Desams.\nNext, proceed to\nJambukeswarar Akilandeswari Temple\n, this temple is part of Pancha Bhoota temples and represents Water. You can see water naturally flowing around the Shiva Lingam and even if you remove the water, it comes back - this is a unique fact here.\nThen, visit the\nUcchi Pillayar Temple\n, dedicated to Lord Ganesha, and located on the top of\nRockfort\n(a beautiful spot to click pictures).\nNext, stop at the\nGovernment Museum\nin\nRani Mangammal Mahal.\nFrom old paintings to fossils and old items, the museum is full of fascinating things that visitors will enjoy exploring!\nAfter that, go to the\nButterfly Park\nand see colorful butterflies all around. Then, visit\nNakshatra Vanam\n, a special garden with 27 trees linked to stars and 12 trees representing the zodiac signs.\nYour\nPancha Bootha Sthalam and Navagraha Tour\nfinishes with happy memories, and later we will drop you at Trichy Airport or railway station for your home.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      }
    ],
