  "puri-konark-tour-packages": {
    "overview": "Odisha is known as the soul of India for good reason. A well-planned Bhubaneswar Puri Konark Tour Package lets you experience the state's most iconic destinations within a compact 70 km triangle \u2014 Puri, Konark Sun Temple, and Bhubaneswar. Puri is one of the four sacred Char Dhams, home to the Jagannath Temple and the world-famous Rath Yatra. Konark's Sun Temple, built in the 13th century, is a UNESCO World Heritage Site and one of the finest examples of Kalinga architecture. Bhubaneswar, with over 600 ancient temples, is the historic capital that started it all. See More\n\nThis Bhubaneswar Puri Konark trip covers all three cities in 4 days and 3 nights. Hotel stays, daily breakfast, private AC vehicle, airport pickup, and an English-speaking guide are included. You visit the Jagannath Temple, Konark Sun Temple, Chilika Lake, Khandagiri-Udayagiri Caves, Dhauli Stupa, and Pipli village \u2014 in a well-paced circuit that works for first-time visitors, families, and pilgrims alike. \nRath Yatra 2026 falls on July 16. If you plan to visit around that date, book at least 8 weeks in advance \u2014 hotels across Puri fill up fast. The Jagannath Temple also closes for 14 days during Anavasara (after Snana Purnima, roughly June\u2013July) when Darshan is not available. Our team flags these dates at the time of booking. \nBest Time to Visit Puri, Konark & Bhubaneswar\n\n\n\n\nSeason\nMonths\nTemperature\nWhat to Expect\n\n\n\n\nWinter \u2014 Best\nOctober \u2013 February\n14\u00b0C \u2013 28\u00b0C\nPleasant weather, active dolphin season at Chilika, clear skies at Konark\n\n\nSpring\nMarch \u2013 April\n24\u00b0C \u2013 36\u00b0C\nWarm but manageable; good for temple visits in early morning\n\n\nSummer \u2014 Avoid\nMay \u2013 June\n36\u00b0C \u2013 42\u00b0C\nHigh heat and humidity; outdoor temple circuits are exhausting\n\n\nMonsoon\nJuly \u2013 September\n26\u00b0C \u2013 34\u00b0C\nHeavy rain; Rath Yatra in July; roads and beaches affected\n\n\n\n\n2026 Important Dates:\n\nRath Yatra \u2014 July 16, 2026: Lord Jagannath's chariot procession from the main temple to Gundicha Temple. The Jagannath Temple remains closed this day, but all visitors \u2014 including non-Hindus \u2014 can have darshan of the deities on the chariots. Puri hotels fill up 2\u20133 months ahead.\nBahuda Yatra (Return) \u2014 July 25, 2026: The chariots return and the Suna Besha ritual follows \u2014 deities adorned in gold.\nAnavasara Closure \u2014 approx. mid-June to early July 2026: Temple closed for 14 days after Snana Purnima. Exact dates confirmed by our team at time of booking.\nKonark Dance Festival \u2014 December 1\u20135, 2026: Classical dance performances at the open-air amphitheatre at Konark Sun Temple.\n\nKonark Sun Temple Light & Sound Show 2026\nThe Konark Sun Temple hosts a nightly Light & Sound Show after regular visiting hours. The 40-minute show narrates the history of King Narasimhadeva I and the Sun God Surya through projected lights and audio. Wireless headphones are provided in Hindi, English, or Odia.\nTimings:\n\nMarch to November: 7:30 PM and 8:20 PM (two shows nightly)\nDecember to February: 6:30 PM and 7:30 PM (two shows nightly)\n\nTicket Price: \u20b930 per person (separate from temple entry ticket of \u20b940)\nTickets are available at the Konark site entrance or online on the ASI e-ticketing portal. Online booking is recommended during peak season (October\u2013February). This show is an optional add-on \u2014 not included in the package price. If you want to attend, let us know at the time of booking and we will adjust the Day 2 schedule to allow for it.\nHow to Reach Bhubaneswar\nBy Air Biju Patnaik International Airport, Bhubaneswar (IATA: BBI) is connected to Delhi (approx. 2 hours), Mumbai (2.5 hours), and Kolkata (1 hour). Puri is 60 km from the airport, around 1.5 hours by road. Our representative meets you at the terminal exit.\nBy Train Bhubaneswar Railway Station is on the Howrah\u2013Chennai main line. Key trains from Delhi: Bhubaneswar Rajdhani (22\u201325 hours). From Kolkata: multiple express trains (5\u20136 hours). Puri Railway Station also receives direct trains from Kolkata and Delhi \u2014 pickup from both stations is available.\nBy Road Delhi to Bhubaneswar: approx. 1,750 km via NH44 (26\u201328 hours by overnight bus or self-drive). Kolkata to Bhubaneswar: 480 km via NH16, 7\u20138 hours. All transfers within this tour \u2014 Bhubaneswar to Konark (65 km), Konark to Puri (35 km) \u2014 are covered by the package vehicle.\nSee Less",
    "highlights": [
      "Full-day Bhubaneswar temple circuit \u2014 Lingaraj, Mukteshwar, Rajarani, Parshuram temples and Bindusagar Lake",
      "Khandagiri and Udayagiri rock-cut caves \u2014 2nd century BC Jain heritage site in Bhubaneswar",
      "Dhauli Stupa and Ashokan rock edicts \u2014 site of the 261 BC Kalinga War, 8 km from Bhubaneswar",
      "Pipli appliqu\u00e9 craft village \u2014 traditional Odisha textile art, en route Bhubaneswar to Konark",
      "Konark Sun Temple \u2014 13th-century UNESCO World Heritage Site; optional evening Light & Sound Show (\u20b930)",
      "Chandrabhaga Beach and Ramchandi Temple \u2014 clean, uncrowded beach stop on the way to Puri",
      "Jagannath Temple darshan, Puri \u2014 one of four Char Dhams; free entry for Hindu devotees",
      "Chilika Lake boat ride \u2014 Asia's largest brackish water lagoon; Irrawaddy dolphins and migratory birds",
      "See More"
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1: Arrival in Bhubaneswar and Temple Visits",
        "description": "Welcome to the city of Bhubaneshwar! Once you arrive, our representative will greet you at the airport or the railway station.\nNow, you\u2019ll be driven to your hotel. Check in and freshen up.\nLater, you\u2019ll be taken on a temple tour of Lingaraj Temple, Mukteswar Temple, Parshuram Temple, Rajarani Temple, and Kedargouri Temple. Also, enjoy the Bindusagar Lake.\nEnjoy an overnight stay at the hotel.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 2: Bhubaneswar \u2013 Dhauli \u2013 Pipli \u2013 Konark \u2013 Puri (70 km/2 hrs, 40 km/1 hr)",
        "description": "Have breakfast and then get ready for a sightseeing tour today.\nYou'll be taken to Dhauli, which is a peaceful Buddhist stupa. Next stop is Pipli village, which is famous for its appliqu\u00e9 work.\nNow, you\u2019ll be taken to the Konark Sun Temple, which is also known as the Black Pagoda.\nLater, you\u2019ll be driven to the Chandrabhaga beach. Enjoy a clean, vast spread of sands here!\nAfterwards, you\u2019ll be taken to Puri, with a stopover at Ramchandi temple.\nOn arrival in Puri, check into your pre-booked hotel.\nIn the evening, go for a visit to the Shri Jagannath Temple!\nCome back to the hotel and rest for the night.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 3: Visit to Chilika Lake and Golden Beach",
        "description": "Relish a delicious breakfast at the hotel.\nToday, you\u2019ll be taken on an exciting trip to the Chilika Lake. Watch a variety of migratory birds here. You can also spot dolphins in the lake.\nLater on, visit the Kalijai Temple located on Kalijai Island. This is available on a direct payment basis.\nIn the evening, you\u2019ll be taken to the Golden Beach of Puri. Soak in the gorgeous view of the sunset here!\nEnjoy a restful night of sleep at the hotel.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 4: Departure from Bhubaneswar",
        "description": "Enjoy breakfast.\nNow, you\u2019ll be dropped off at Bhubaneshwar airport or railway station, from where you can continue your further journey. This concludes your tour with us."
      }
    ],
    "faqs": []
  },
