  "rajasthan-honeymoon-tour-package": {
    "overview": "Apart from being known as the land of palaces and maharajas, Rajasthan is also one of the prime romantic destinations. With the atmosphere enveloped in colorful beauty and surreal landscapes, Rajasthan can be your next favorite exotic destination for you and your better half. Explore the many vibrant faces of Rajasthan with My Quick Trippers\u2019s, 6 days and 5 nights romantic tour of Rajasthan.\n\nRajasthan Honeymoon Tour Itinerary Package\n\n\nDay 1 :Arrival in Jaipur\n\n\nYou will be transferred to your allotted hotel upon your arrival in Jaipur. Later you will be taken on a brief sightseeing tour of the city like \u2013 Hawa Mahal (palace of winds) \u2013 one of the most prominent landmarks of the city, representing the fine craftsmanship of the city; you will also be taken to Jantar Mantar \u2013 which is one of the most well preserved observatories in the subcontinent.\nYou will finally be taken back to your hotel for an overnight stay.\n\n\n\n\nDay 2 :Jaipur Sightseeing\n\n\nPost breakfast, you will be taken on a brief excursion of Amber Fort palace \u2013 which is a classic sign of romance, and perched atop a large platform from where you can take a breathtaking view of the Jaipur city; Nahargarh fort will be your next destination which is located all along the Aravali ranges. Next stop for you will be the holy Laxmi Narayan temple \u2013 a Hindu temple dedicated to Goddess Laxmi and Lord Vishnu.\nLater in the evening, you will be made to visit the teeming colorful marketplaces of Jaipur.\nYou can shop for locally made souvenirs like \u2013 traditional blue pottery, camel leather products, lac bangles, silk quilts, Jaipur handicrafts, bandhej and many more.\nYou also have the freedom to try out some delectable cuisines like \u2013 dal baati churma, laal maas, the iconic Rajasthani thali, Kachori and a whole plethora of others.\n\n\n\n\nDay 3 :Jaipur \u2013 Pushkar\n\n\nYou will be driven to Pushkar in the morning after breakfast, which is located at a distance of 2 hours and 40 mines. Upon arriving at Pushkar you will be immediately checked in to your hotel for staying the night. After freshening up you will be taken to Brahma Mandir \u2013 one of the few temples that is dedicated to Lord Brahma. It is a common belief that the Lord had personally chosen Pushkar as the temple site making it extremely pious. You will then proceed towards the sacred Pushkar Lake \u2013 which is surrounded by 52 bathing ghats and a dip here is believed to cleanse all your sins and skin related diseases.\nAfter spending a memorable day in one of the most fascinating destinations in India, you will then be made to head back to your hotel.\n\n\n\n\nDay 4 :Pushkar \u2013 Udaipur\n\n\nEarly in the morning, you will be made to head for Udaipur, which is located at a distance of 5 hours and 10 mines. Upon arriving at this beautifully enchanting town you will be made to check in to your hotel for a night stay.\n\n\n\n\nDay 5 :Udaipur Sightseeing\n\n\nYour sightseeing tour of Udaipur will commence in the morning starting with a visit to the famous city Palace museum \u2013 a beautifully created palace complex, which has served as the resident place for numerous ruling dynasties. Jagdish Mandir will be your next destination, which is situated just outside the royal city palace and is dedicated to Lord Jagannath and is one of the major tourist attractions in Udaipur. Saheliyon ki bari will be your next destination, a beautiful garden complete with numerous fountains, lotus pools and elephant statues made of marble. You will then be taken to bhartiya lok kala mandir which is a folk art museum.\nAfter a day of exploration and fun you will be guided back to your hotel for staying the night.\n\n\n\n\nDay 6 :Udaipur (Departure to Delhi)\n\n\nAfter the completion of your breakfast, you will be transferred to the airport or railway station from where you will depart towards Delhi and onto your desired location.",
    "highlights": [
      "Explore the city of Jaipur",
      "Visit the famous Brahma Mandir in Pushkar and some local sightseeing",
      "Visit the City of lakes Udaipur with your partner",
      "Cherish your love in the most exotic places of Rajasthan for a memorable honeymoon"
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1 :Arrival in Jaipur",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 2 :Jaipur Sightseeing",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 3 :Jaipur \u2013 Pushkar",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 4 :Pushkar \u2013 Udaipur",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 5 :Udaipur Sightseeing",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 6 :Udaipur (Departure to Delhi)",
        "description": ""
