  "rajasthan-safari-tour": {
    "overview": "When considering a vacation to Rajasthan, it might be difficult to decide where to start and where to conclude because the large state has so much to offer in the way of beauty, history, and culture.\n\nThere is so much exotic variation everywhere, and every nook and cranny of the state is home to something different. Everything seems practically difficult to take it all in on a brief journey. Because of this, going on safari in Rajasthan is the ideal way to experience the best of that state. In Rajasthan, you may even go on royal safaris to step things up a notch. You will undoubtedly have an amazing experience that you will cherish for the rest of life since true Rajasthan and royal grandeur go together like peanut butter and jelly. In this 10 days / 9 nights trip all the best of Rajasthan will be covered through the safari tour.\n\nThere is so much exotic variation everywhere, and every nook and cranny of the state is home to something different. Everything seems practically difficult to take it all in on a brief journey. Because of this, going on safari in Rajasthan is the ideal way to experience the best of that state. In Rajasthan, you may even go on royal safaris to step things up a notch. You will undoubtedly have an amazing experience that you will cherish for the rest of life since true Rajasthan and royal grandeur go together like peanut butter and jelly. In this 10 days / 9 nights trip all the best of Rajasthan will be covered through the safari tour.\n\nRajasthan Safari Tour Itinerary Package\n\n\nDay 1 :Delhi \u2013 Mandawa / 256 Km- 5 HRS\n\n\nOn arrival at Delhi, My Quick Trippers Representative will greet you and Drive to Mandawa in Rajasthan. Check in at a heritage hotel for dinner and overnight stay.\nMandawa: In the heart of the Shekhawati region of Rajasthan lies the beautiful small town Mandawa, known throughout the state for its forts and Havelis. Mandawa is situated in the north Indian state of Rajasthan around 190 km from Jaipur, the capital of the state.\n\n\n\n\nDay 2 :Mandawa \u2013 Bikaner/ 193-4 HRS\n\n\nMorning After breakfast drive to Bikaner. Check in at a hotel on arrival. Later visit local sightseeing. Overnight stay.\nTour the Junagarh Fort that was built by Raja Rai Singh; see the Lalgarh Palace that was constructed by Maharaja Ganga Singh Ji. The other attractions you may tour the Camel Breeding Farm, Karni Mata Temple etc. Stay overnight at the hotel in Bikaner.\nBikaner: If ever beauty has bloomed in a desert, it has been at Bikaner. Founded in 1488 AD by Rao Bika Ji, it\u2019s located in North West part of Rajasthan state in INDIA. The imposing palaces, beautiful and richly sculptured temples of red and yellow sandstones display some of the finest creations of Rajput civilization. It\u2019s lust for \u201cdessert\u201d or affection for \u201cdesert\u201d that tickles every heart to visit Bikaner.\n\n\n\n\nDay 3 :Bikaner \u2013 Khimsar / 155 Km- 3.5 HRS\n\n\nAfter Breakfast, Drive to Khimsar. Check in at the Khimsar Fort for an overnight stay. Tour the Junagarh Fort and other attractions before retiring for the night at the Khimsar Fort. Khimsar History, leisure, desert adventure, sports, wildlife safaris and historic sightseeing tours make it a \u201ccomplete\u201d holiday destination\u201d. Perched on the edge of the Great Thar Desert in the heart of rural India lies this unique 16th-century fort that offers experience after exhilarating experience. Hundreds of years of history unfold as you glance at its battle-scarred walls and stroll down its ramparts. You are not prepared for the beauty, the grandeur, the layout or the magnificence of this castle even as you approach it through sand dunes and narrow countryside roads. It suddenly hits you on a blind corner. Come and savor the experience.\n\n\n\n\nDay 4 :Khimsar \u2013 Jaisalmer/ 288 Km- 7 HRS\n\n\nThe morning takes you to Jaisalmer via Osian \u2013 an oasis in the desert. A drive to this ancient township takes one past undulating terrain, punctuated by desert stretches and little hamlets, Osian has 15 beautifully sculpted Jain and Brahma temples. On arrival check-in at the hotel for overnight stay.\n\n\n\n\nDay 5 :Jaisalmer\n\n\nDay five, the Rajasthan Tour brings you to the desert city of Jaisalmer. Explore the stupendous Jaisalmer Fort that houses the entire township within its protective ramparts and the magnificent havelis such as Patwon-ki-haveli and Salim Singh-Ki-Haveli that are over centuries old. The evening is reserved for a visit to the Sam Sand Dunes that give you the taste of the Thar Desert at its majestic best. Enjoy camel safaris as well as cultural programmes. Overnight stay at Camp.\n\n\n\n\nDay 6 :Jaisalmer \u2013 Jodhpur/ 307 Km-8 HRS\n\n\nThe morning takes you to Jodhpur where you check in at a hotel. After lunch, visit the Mehrangarh Fort, which is set a top a 125-meter high hill. Explore the Jaswant Thada Memorial- a cluster of royal cenotaphs built in 1899 AD in memory of Maharaja Jaswant Singh II. Overnight stay at a hotel.\n\n\n\n\nDay 7 :Jodhpur \u2013 Rohet Garh\n\n\nIn the morning we drive to Rohet Garh and check-in at hotel on arrival. In the afternoon, proceed on a safari to Bishnoi Villages to explore these environmentalists\u2019 distinct way of life that hasn\u2019t been tarred with modernity. Also visit the villages of craftsmen \u2013 potters, weavers, and metal-ware. Overnight stay at the hotel.\n\n\n\n\nDay 8 :Rohet Garh \u2013 Udaipur\n\n\nMorning, after breakfast, drive towards Udaipur en-route visiting Ranakpur Jain Temples that are renowned for their exquisite carved work in marble and a center for Jain pilgrimage as well. On arrival at Udaipur, check into a hotel for overnight stay.\n\n\n\n\nDay 9 :Udaipur\n\n\nThe city of lakes- Udaipur is a fascinating city to explore. With its intriguing blend of sights, sounds and experience- Udaipur is a tourist\u2019s delight. Enjoy a boat ride on the placid waters of Lake Pichola and in the afternoon and visit the City Palace, Jagdish Temple, Sahelion-Ki-Bari and Bharatiya Lok Kala Museum as well as the island palaces of Jag Mandir and Jag Niwas. Overnight stay at the hotel.\n\n\n\n\nDay 10 :Udaipur Departure\n\n\nToday a farewell from Desert, as we will drop you at railway station/ Airport.",
    "highlights": [
      "Visit to the Mandwa city, the city of forts and havelis",
      "Enjoy the Bikaneri culture",
      "Be a part of history with a tour to the Khimsar fort",
      "Covering Jaisalmer, Jodhpur and Rohet Garh",
      "A special visit to the city of lakes Udaipur"
    ],
    "itinerary": [
