  "rameshwaram-madurai-tour": {
    "overview": "Curious to explore the beauty of Tamil Nadu? See More\n\nThe Madurai Rameshwaram Kanyakumari tour package shows you temples, beaches, beautiful landscapes and rich South Indian culture. Journey begins in Madurai famous for its Meenakshi Amman Temple. An interesting fact about this temple is that it has around 33,000 carvings and statues covering every corner..\nThis temple\u2019s architecture is truly unique - imagine how special it will feel when you visit there. The next stop is Rameshwaram. Here, the beaches look stunning and crystal clear. If you get time, don't forget to click sunset photos. You will also visit the popular Ramanathaswamy Temple, one of the 12 Jyotirlingas in India.\nAfter visiting Rameshwaram, trip continues to Kanyakumari. Here, you can see the meeting point of three oceans- the Bay of Bengal, the Arabian Sea and the Indian Ocean, which creates unforgettable memories. You will also visit the Kumari Amman Temple, a sacred Shakti Peetha. According to legend, Sati Devi\u2019s spine fell here while Lord Shiva carried her body. So get ready and experience the magic of South India on your Madurai Rameshwaram Kanyakumari trip.\nSee Less\n\nThe Madurai Rameshwaram Kanyakumari tour package shows you temples, beaches, beautiful landscapes and rich South Indian culture. Journey begins in Madurai famous for its Meenakshi Amman Temple. An interesting fact about this temple is that it has around 33,000 carvings and statues covering every corner..\n\nThis temple\u2019s architecture is truly unique - imagine how special it will feel when you visit there. The next stop is Rameshwaram. Here, the beaches look stunning and crystal clear. If you get time, don't forget to click sunset photos. You will also visit the popular Ramanathaswamy Temple, one of the 12 Jyotirlingas in India.",
    "highlights": [
      "Explore temples, beaches, and cultural landmarks across Madurai, Rameshwaram and Kanyakumari including Meenakshi Amman Temple, Ramanathaswamy Temple and Kumari Amman Temple.",
      "Take unique experiences like the holy dip at Agni Theertham, sunrise and sunset views over the oceans in Kanyakumari and Rama Setu/Adam\u2019s Bridge.",
      "Enjoy scenic beauty and architecture at Vivekananda Rock Memorial, Thiruvalluvar Statue, Thanumalayan Temple and Padmanabhapuram Palace.",
      "Make your 5 day tour stress free with comfortable hotel stays, customized plan and easy travel with transport arranged.",
      "See More"
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1: Madurai - Rameshwaram (173 km / 4 Hours Drive)",
        "description": "Our My Quick Trippers representative will meet you at Madurai Airport or Railway Station to start your tour comfortably. If you\u2019ve booked a guide, they will join the driver to help you throughout the day.\nAfter pick-up, your Madurai sightseeing tour includes:\nMeenakshi Amman Temple-\nThis temple has a unique ritual. In the past, 1,000 thousands of devotees joined Goddess Meenakshi i\u2019s wedding, and this tradition continues in cultural festivals.\nThiruparankundram Murugan Temple\nOn arrival in Rameshwaram, check in at the hotel. Later, visit:\nRamanathaswamy Temple\nAgni Theertham-\nThis holy beach is where pilgrims dip to wash away their sins.\nRamjharoka Temple\nAfter sightseeing enjoy an overnight stay in Rameshwaram.\nNote-\nAgni Theertham is best to visit early morning, when many devotees take a holy dip.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 2: In Rameswaram - Full day Sightseeing Tour",
        "description": "Early in the morning, around\n5:00 AM\n, proceed to the\nSpatika Linga Darshan,\nalso called\nMani Darshan\n, where the natural crystal Shivling (not man-made) is very important in Hinduism and looks very beautiful.\nLater you will head out for\nAgni Teertham\nto have a holy bath in the sea.\nFurther proceed to the main temple through North gate and\nTake sacred bath with holy water of the 22 wells, inside the\nRamanathaswamy Temple\nduring\nTheerth Snanam.\nThen proceed for darshan and pooja at the main temple.\nAfter the holy bath and Darshan, return to the hotel for breakfast.\nAfter breakfast, proceed for a sightseeing tour of\nRameshwaram,\nwhich covers the\nFive-faced Hanuman Temple\n(famous for floating stones from Ram Setu),\nRamar Patham, Kothandaramaswamy Temple, Gandamadana Parvatham\n(a hilltop temple with Rama\u2019s footprint and beautiful views),\nRama Setu/Adam\u2019s Bridge\n(the chain of stones said to be built by Rama\u2019s army),\nFormer President A. P. J. Abdul Kalam\u2019s House, and Dhanushkodi.\nNote- The APJ Museum opens at 7am and closes at 8pm.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 3: Rameswaram - Kanyakumari (312 km/ 7 hours)",
        "description": "Early in the morning, visit the temple again or take a\nSamudra Snanam\n(holy dip in the sea).\nAfter breakfast, leave the hotel and go to\nKanyakumari,\nwhere the\nBay of Bengal, Arabian Sea, and Indian Ocean\nmeet. It's a beautiful spot to take photos.\nKanyakumari\nis famous as the only place on earth where you can see both sunrise and sunset over the ocean.\nKanyakumari\nis famous as the only place on earth where you can see the sunrise over the Bay of Bengal and the sunset over the Arabian Sea.\nOn arrival, check into the hotel and rest. Overnight stay at the hotel.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 4: Kanyakumari - Kovalam - Thiruvananthapuram (Trivandrum) (100 Kms/3 Hr )",
        "description": "Early in the morning, you can watch the beautiful\nsunrise in Kanyakumari.\nThe calm atmosphere makes it a perfect time to take pictures.\nAfter breakfast visit the\nSwami Vivekananda Rock Memorial\nand its\nmeditation hall\nwhere you can meditate for some time. Walk over the Sea by Glass bridge to reach Thiruvalluvar Statue.\nNext, visit\nKanyakumari Mandir (Kumari Amman Temple).\nThis temple is built in\nKerala-style architecture,\nso just get ready to click photos.\nThen, see the point where the three oceans meet. Stop near\nGandhi Mandapam,\nwhere Mahatma Gandhi\u2019s ashes were once kept for public viewing. Don\u2019t forget the\nThiruvalluvar Statue,\ndedicated to the poet who wrote the\nThirukkural.\nLater drive towards\nTrivandrum\nand stop at\nThanumalayan Temple\nin\nSuchindram.\nThis temple is known for its architecture and the 22-foot-high statue of\nHanuman.\nContinue to visit the\nPadmanabhapuram Palace.\nIf time permits visit Kovalam Beach before reaching\nTrivandrum.\nOn arrival, check into your hotel and later visit the\nSri Padmanabhaswamy Temple\ndedicated to Lord Vishnu/Krishna.\nOvernight stay at\nTrivandrum.\nNote -\nSome temples, including Sri Padmanabhaswamy Temple, may have strict dress codes. Please dress modestly.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 5: Thiruvananthapuram (Trivandrum) (Departure)",
        "description": "Enjoy your morning breakfast as your\nMadurai Rameshwaram Kanyakumari package\nconcludes. You will then be transferred to Trivandrum Airport or the railway station for your onward journey."
      }
    ],
    "faqs": []
  },
