  "ranthambore-weekend": {
    "overview": "Ranthambore National Park, with its distinct class and charm, plays an important role in India\u2019s tourism industry. While Ranthambore is not the largest national park in India, it is without a doubt the most well-known. The Ranthambore forest is 1334 square kilometers in size, with 392 square kilometers designated as a national park. It is located near the Aravali Hills and the Vindhya plateau. The Ranthambore Tiger Reserve is renowned for providing a natural habitat for a large number of Royal Bengal tigers, and it is well-known among wildlife enthusiasts for its diurnal tigers, which means that tourists can easily spot a tiger during their day safari visit. With the weekend 3 days / 2 nights tour relishes the wildlife flora and fauna.\n\nRanthambore Weekend Tour Itinerary Package\n\n\nDay 1 :Sawai Madhopur to Ranthambore\n\n\nYou will be received at Sawai Madhopur railway station by the My Quick Trippers representative and assisted on your drive to Ranthambore resort. Check-in and after lunch, you can visit the Ranthambore Fort for sightseeing. It is a two-hour to and fro journey and then gets back to the resort after dusk. Freshen up for dinner and spend the night at the resort.\n\n\n\n\nDay 2 :At Ranthambore National Park\n\n\nOn day 2 get up early and drive to Ranthambore jungle with your guide or naturalist on jeep to track tigers and enjoy the wildlife thriving here. This jungle trip will last for 3 hours. Get back to the hotel for a filling breakfast and then spend some time relaxing. Post lunch you can start for game drive to the National Park again. Discover other beasts and birds living here and the vegetation growing in this region. Get back to the hotel for dinner and night stay at the resort.\n\n\n\n\nDay 3 :Sawai Madhopur to Delhi\n\n\nOn the final day enjoy a hearty breakfast and then check-out of the resort to drive back to the Sawai Madhopur railway station. The My Quick Trippers representative will drop you to the railway station for you to head homewards safely.",
    "highlights": [
      "A quick visit to the Ranthambore fort",
      "A full tour to the Ranthambore National Park",
      "Enjoy the local cuisine",
      "Bring back fresh breeze and nature\u2019s memories"
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1 :Sawai Madhopur to Ranthambore",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 2 :At Ranthambore National Park",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 3 :Sawai Madhopur to Delhi",
        "description": ""
      }
    ],
    "faqs": []
  },
