  "shimla-manali-tour": {
    "overview": "Himachal Pradesh, a beautiful hill station which is also called as \u201cQueen of Hills\u201d is adorned with mesmerizing landscapes and serene and tranquil ambiance. Book our most customized 5 nights and 6 days long Shimla Manali Tour Package and get the most possible way to explore the wonders of this hill station and also Delhi and Manali.\n\nShimla Manali Tour Itinerary Package\n\n\nDay 1 :Arrival in Delhi\n\n\nOn your arrival in Delhi, the capital city of India which represents a beautiful symbiosis of rich culture, history, art, beauty, and many more. Delhi is a city like a canvas reflecting the past pieces of evidence in present also with its gorgeous architectural grandeur and is also known for its amazing city life. Explore the beauties of fascinating and enriching travel experience and once you reach this huge city, check-into the hotel room and then go for a half-day sightseeing tour in Delhi.\nExplore the wonders of Old as well as New Delhi and especially the Red Fort which was constructed by the great Mughal Ruler Shah Jahan in the year 1648. Later on, continue your drive towards Jama Masjid which is the largest mosque in India and then drives towards Shanti Vana and Raj Ghat. After exploring these wonders of the city make your visit to Chandni Chowk, the shopping hub in Delhi. Let\u2019s get some spiritual now and visit the popular temples like Laxminarayan Temple and then drive towards President House, Connaught Place, Parliament House, and Government Secretariat Buildings.\n\n\n\n\nDay 2 :Delhi \u2013 Manali (554 km)\n\n\nPost breakfast drives towards Manali and covers a distance of 554 km by roadways. There is an interesting legend about this panoramic hill station which states that when the water stream of Great Deluge receded and then Mark Anu came to reside on the hillside. When this cascading water stream starts drying and when it dried up completely then this place looked so stunning. Since then Manali started welcoming thousands of tourists every year. Located at a huge elevation of almost 2050 meters above sea level, Manali is one of the most preferred tourist destinations in India.\n\n\n\n\nDay 3 :Manali\n\n\nPost breakfast at the hotel, proceed for a half-day sightseeing tour in Manali including Hadimba Temple which is popular because of its 4 tired Pagodas- shaped like a roof way which is adorned with beautiful paintings and symbols. After the completion of your sightseeing tour, you will be dropped back to the hotel for dinner which is then followed by a relaxing overnight stay.\n\n\n\n\nDay 4 :Manali \u2013 Shimla by Roadways (260 km)\n\n\nAfter covering a distance of 260 km drive towards Shimla and on reaching there check-into the hotel room. Shimla which was the former summer capital of British India and the capital of Himachal Pradesh, Shimla is one of the most important attractions in the state of Himachal Pradesh. This beautiful hill station is popular as a colonial aura and a major shopping hub and especially the Mall Road where one comes to buy some amazing handicrafts and woolen items. Do not forget to visit the Scandal Point which is adorned with snow-capped mountains and the iconic attraction of this hill city.\n\n\n\n\nDay 5 :Shimla\n\n\nPost breakfast drive towards Jakhoo Hill, the major landmarks and the highest point in Shimla which offers a panoramic view of the entire city, hills, and the mountain ranges which are known for offering the pictorial view of sunrise and sunset. You can also visit the Institute of Advanced Study which was constructed in the year 1888 and then visit Tara Devi Temple and Himachal Pradesh Museum.\n\n\n\n\nDay 6 :Shimla \u2013 Delhi\n\n\nAfter treating your taste buds with a relishing breakfast, drive towards the airport to board the flight for your onward journey towards home. We hope you had a great time us and you had collected many wonderful moments with us.",
    "highlights": [
      "Explore the gorgeous historical monuments including Qutub Minar, Red Fort, and India Gate.",
      "Visiting the popular pagoda-shaped Hadimba Temple.",
      "Explore the majestic Tibetan monasteries at Manali.",
      "Shop out some amazing souvenirs at the Mall Road in Shimla.",
      "Visiting the Jakhoo Hills and enjoy the eye-treating views of sunrise and sunset."
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1 :Arrival in Delhi",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 2 :Delhi \u2013 Manali (554 km)",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 3 :Manali",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 4 :Manali \u2013 Shimla by Roadways (260 km)",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 5 :Shimla",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 6 :Shimla \u2013 Delhi",
        "description": ""
      }
    ],
    "faqs": []
