  "shining-rajasthan": {
    "overview": "Rajasthan is the most trending tourist destination of Northwestern India. With its royal insight and hospitality it makes the traveler feel like the royal guests.\n\nThe rich culture, tasty food and the celebration mode of this state attracts tourists from all over the globe. Starting from the forts, the desert safari and the visits to the mysterious forts everything is exciting and fun to feel it from the heart. The 10 days / 9 nights Shining Rajasthan tour package is a once-in-a-lifetime trip not to be missed.\n\nThe rich culture, tasty food and the celebration mode of this state attracts tourists from all over the globe. Starting from the forts, the desert safari and the visits to the mysterious forts everything is exciting and fun to feel it from the heart. The 10 days / 9 nights Shining Rajasthan tour package is a once-in-a-lifetime trip not to be missed.\n\nShining Rajasthan Tour Itinerary Package\n\n\nDay 1 :Arrive Jaipur\n\n\nWelcome to you in \u2018Pink City\u2019! Arrive at Airport / Railway Station in Jaipur and transfer to your hotel. On arrival check-in into your hotel. Overnight stay at Jaipur. Rajasthan\u2019s beautiful Pink City Jaipur was the stronghold of a clan of rulers whose three hill forts and series of palaces in the city are important attractions. Known as the Pink City because of the color of the stone used exclusively in the walled city, Jaipur\u2019s bazaars sell embroidered leather shoes, blue pottery, tie and dye scarves and other exotic wares. Western Rajasthan itself forms a convenient circuit, in the heart of the Thar Desert which has shaped its history, lifestyles and architecture.\n\n\n\n\nDay 2 :Jaipur City Tour\n\n\nThis morning, after breakfast, visits the ancient capital of the Kachwaha Rajputs, Amer. One can take an elephant ride or the jeep ride upto the fort. Thereafter, enjoy a photo-stop at Hawa Mahal \u2013 the Palace of Winds. Later, visit the City Palace and the apartment housing museums with an array of textiles, costumes, arms, weapons and paintings and finally visit Jantar Mantar, the observatory built by Maharaja Jai Singh-II. The founder of Jantar Mantar is Maharaja Jai Singh II, he had built Jantar Mantar in five different locations of India, out of which Jantar Mantar at Jaipur is the largest. The observatories, or \u2018Jantar Mantar\u2019 as they are commonly known, incorporate multiple buildings of unique form, each with a specialized function for astronomical measurement. Later you are free to enjoy shopping in the local market. The market of Jaipur will delight you with the exotic blue pottery, the batik painting, block printed textiles of Sanganer and Bagru, tie and dye fabrics, Mojari \u2013 (the local shoe), sandalwood carving items, beautiful stone carvings etc.\n\n\n\n\nDay 3 :Jaipur to Bikaner (350 km/8 hrs)\n\n\nAfter breakfast proceed to Bikaner. On arrival, check in to the hotel. Evening free for shopping and overnight stay in the hotel.\n\n\n\n\nDay 4 :Bikaner to Jaisalmer (350 km/8 hrs)\n\n\nTake a full day sightseeing tour and visit Junagarh Fort, Anup Mahal, Gaj Mandir, Sheesh Mahal and Deshnok Temple. Afternoon proceeds to Jaisalmer. Overnight stay at the hotel in Jaisalmer.\n\n\n\n\nDay 5 :Jaisalmer Sightseeing\n\n\nTake a half-day sightseeing tour and visit Jaisalmer Fort, Jain temple and Havelis. Rest of the day at leisure. Take a drive to the Sam sand dunes in the evening. Back to the hotel or overnight stay in a Tent at Sam Sand Dunes.\n\n\n\n\nDay 6 :Jaisalmer \u2013 Jodhpur (295 km/8 hrs)\n\n\nFrom Jaisalmer transfer to Jodhpur and check into the hotel on arrival. Rest of the day at leisure. Overnight stay at the hotel.\n\n\n\n\nDay 7 :Jodhpur \u2013 Udaipur (295 km/8 hrs)\n\n\nJodhpur sightseeing tour visiting Umaid Bhawan Palace, Mehrangarh Fort Mandore garden and Jaswant Thada. Afternoon proceed to Udaipur and overnight stay at the hotel.\n\n\n\n\nDay 8 :Udaipur Sightseeing\n\n\nTake a full day sightseeing tour and visit the City Palace, Saheliyon ki Badi, Maharana Pratap Smarak and Pear Hill. Overnight stay at the hotel.\n\n\n\n\nDay 9 :Udaipur \u2013 Mount Abu (195 km/3 hrs)\n\n\nFrom Udaipur transfer to Mount Abu and check into the hotel on arrival. Rest of the day at leisure. Overnight stay at the hotel.\n\n\n\n\nDay 10 :Mount Abu Departure\n\n\nTake a sightseeing tour of Mount Abu visiting Dilwara Jain Temples, Prajapita Brahmakumari Ashram and University, Guru Shikhar and Nakki Lake. Afternoon drop at Abu Road Railway Station or Udaipur airport or Ahmedabad airport.",
    "highlights": [
      "City tours of Bikaner, Jaisalmer, Jodhpur, Jaipur, Udaipur and Mount Abu",
      "Visiting the top tourists spots",
      "Visiting the local markets and museums",
      "Enjoy the adventurous forts",
      "Trying out on the ethnic Rajasthani local delicacies"
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1 :Arrive Jaipur",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 2 :Jaipur City Tour",
        "description": ""
