  "special-package-for-karnataka": {
    "overview": "Karnataka attracts a considerable number of tourists each year thanks to its wealth of natural resources. Among the captivating hill towns in Karnataka are Coorg, Nandi Hills, and Chikmagalur. Its gorgeous coastline areas, like the well-known Blue Lagoon Beach and Ladies Beach in Karwar, which are both surrounded by Casuarina trees, are appreciated by beachgoers looking for unspoiled shorelines. Pattadakal and Hampi, two UNESCO World Heritage Sites in Karnataka, are excellent for heritage tourism. With the 5 days / 4 nights tour package we have planned for you, you can enjoy all the best tourists spots in the state.\n\nKarnataka Special Tour Itinerary Package\n\n\nDay 1 :Mysore Arrival\n\n\nWelcome to Mysore, You are greeted on arrival at Mysore Railway station/Bus Stand by My Quick Trippers representative and Transfer to Hotel, (standard check-in time at the hotel is 1200 hrs noon) later visit Maharaja Palace \u2013 the Palace is a splendid structure in the Indo-Saracenic style, among its many attractions, are a magnificent gold throne. Art Gallery in the Jaganmohan Palace houses an excellent collection of ceramics, sandalwood, ivory, stone, antique furniture and ancient musical instruments, St. Philomena\u2019s Church-this imposing Gothic structure with beautiful stained glass windows and lofty towers is a must see. Later in the evening visit Brindavan Garden / Krishna Raja Sagar Dam after sundown, when musical fountains and closed lights transform this place into a magical fairyland. Return to hotel and overnight.\n\n\n\n\nDay 2 :Mysore \u2013 Ooty (160 km)\n\n\nAfter the breakfast, check out the hotel and drive to Ooty, the land where green mountains, as well as azure sky, roll down to embrace quivering beds of crimson roses. En-route, visit Bandipur Wildlife Sanctuary, Mudumalai Wildlife Sanctuary along with Kalhatti Falls. On arrival at Ooty, you can check-in to the hotel and relax for some time. Later proceed for Ooty sightseeing. The major attractions of Ooty include Botanical Garden, a stylish garden bordering huge variety of flowering bushes, flowers, plants, fern house with a huge range of ferns and orchids, a clear pool are a few of the tourist attractions. Ooty Lake has an uneven L shape and extends for more than 2 km in length. Then visit to the Doddabetta Peak which is situated at an altitude of 2623 meters above sea level and it is the highest point of Nilgiris hills. Return to the hotel and overnight stay at the Hotel.\n\n\n\n\nDay 3 :Ooty \u2013 Sightseeing\n\n\nAfter the breakfast, transfer to Coonoor for sightseeing, the place surrounded by the tea plantations. The tourist attractions of Coonoor include Pasteur Institute established in 1907. Sim\u2019s Park is the place where individual tree specimens are planted all over the place, providing an extraordinary attraction to the park. Lamb\u2019s Rock is 8 km from Coonoor and on the way to Dolphin\u2019s Nose. It offers a striking view of the Coimbatore Plains. Laws Falls is an amazing picnic spot and heaven for Nature lovers, located at Coonoor-Mettupalayam road. The height of the Law falls is about 180 feet. Return to the hotel at Ooty and overnight stay at the Hotel.\n\n\n\n\nDay 4 :Ooty \u2013 Bangalore (270 kms/7 Hrs Drive)\n\n\nAfter breakfast transfer to Bangalore & proceed for sightseeing which covers Bull Temple, Cubbon Park, Tipu Palace, Lalbagh Botanical Gardens, ISKCON Temple, Vidhana Soudha (Outside view), overnight stay at hotel.\n\n\n\n\nDay 5 :Bangalore Departure\n\n\nMorning, after breakfast, transfer to Airport/ Railway/Bus Stand for Journey to onwards Destination. here tour ends with happy memories to cherished forever. (standard check out time at the hotel is 1200 hrs noon).",
    "highlights": [
      "Explore the sandal capital Mysore",
      "Be a part of the Brindaban Garden",
      "Visit to the Kriashna Raja sagar dam",
      "Enjoy a trip to the Queen of Hills, Ooty",
      "Fascinating Bangalore tour",
      "Best hotel and local meal will exhilarate your stay"
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1 :Mysore Arrival",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 2 :Mysore \u2013 Ooty (160 km)",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 3 :Ooty \u2013 Sightseeing",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 4 :Ooty \u2013 Bangalore (270 kms/7 Hrs Drive)",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 5 :Bangalore Departure",
        "description": ""
      }
    ],
    "faqs": []
  },
  "spiritual-uttar-pradesh": {
    "overview": "The state of Uttar Pradesh is dotted with a number of spiritual and pilgrimage centers. The spiritual Uttar Pradesh tour package which pans for 7 days and 6 nights will make sure that you have a mesmerizing experience. This land of immense spirituality and peace offers its pilgrims, devotees and visitors an opportunity to explore the pious state.\n\nUttar Pradesh Pilgrimage Tour Itinerary Package\n\n\nDay 1 :Arrival in Varanasi\n\n\nUpon your arrival in Varanasi, one of the oldest living holy cities in India, our tour representative will transfer you to your allotted hotel for an overnight stay. Your evening time is free for you to explore this sacred town of Varanasi which is filled with some of the most traditional creations which you can buy as souvenirs.\n\n\n\n\nDay 2 :Varanasi\n\n\nAfter completing your breakfast early in the morning your full day of temple tour sightseeing tour will commence. You will be covering spiritual centres like \u2013 Bharat Mata Mandir, Durga Mandir, Kashi Vishwanath Temple, Sankat Mochan Mandir and Tulsi Manas Mandir. All these temples are known for their immense and extreme spirituality and remains flocked by pilgrims and devotees all year long.\nIn the evening you will be assisted for a Ganga aarti on the ghats of the Ganga River before retiring back to your allotted hotel in Varanasi for an overnight stay.\n\n\n\n\nDay 3 :Varanasi \u2013 Prayagraj \u2013 Varanasi\n\n\nEarly in the morning, your 3-hour road journey of Prayagraj will commence. Once you arrive at Prayagraj your half day sightseeing tour of the city will commence where you will be taken to the following places \u2013 Allahabad Fort, Allahabad Museum, Anand Bhawan and Swaraj Bhawan. You will also be duly checked in to your allotted hotel in Varanasi where you will be spending the night.\n\n\n\n\nDay 4 :Varanasi \u2013 Bodhgaya\n\n\nFrom Varanasi, you will be made to depart towards one of the holiest town in India of Bodhgaya which is situated at a distance of 5 hours. Later on you will be made to visit the famous Lord Buddha temple. Later on you will be made to head on towards Bodhgaya for an overnight stay.\n\n\n\n\nDay 5 :Bodhgaya \u2013 Gaya \u2013 Varanasi\n\n\nSituated at a road journey distance of 12 km you will be made to head on to Gaya for a visit to the pious Vishnupad mandir. You will then be driven to Varanasi, after lunch, which is located at a distance of 7 hours. Upon your arrival in Varanasi, you will be duly checked in to your hotel for an overnight stay.\n\n\n\n\nDay 6 :Varanasi \u2013 Ayodhya\n\n\nEarly in the morning post breakfast, you will be made to depart for one of the most sacred and culturally rich destinations of Ayodhya. Here you will be made to visit Ram Janmabhoomi \u2013 Lord Rama\u2019s birthplace and the famous Sarayu River. You will then be immediately checked into your allotted hotel here for an overnight stay.\n\n\n\n\nDay 7 :Ayodhya \u2013 Varanasi\n\n\nPost breakfast you will be made to depart for the holy town of Varanasi which is situated at a distance of 5 hours. Once you reach Varanasi you will be guided to your allotted departure spot of either railway station or airport ending your tour journey with us.",
    "highlights": [
      "Tour of the holy city Varanasi",
      "Visiting to all the famous temples in this divine place",
      "Enjoying the local delicacies",
      "Visit to Prayagraj (Allahabad) to the tourist spots like the fort, museum etc.",
      "Seek some blessings at the Bodhgaya temple",
      "Visit to the Ram Janmabhoomi, Ayodhya"
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1 :Arrival in Varanasi",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 2 :Varanasi",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 3 :Varanasi \u2013 Prayagraj \u2013 Varanasi",
        "description": ""
      },
