  "sri-lanka-ramayana-tour": {
    "overview": "Sri Lanka is known all over the world for its natural beauty. It's a nature's precious gem, famous for its magnificent wildlife biodiversity and picturesque coastline! See More\n\nAlso, Sri Lanka is very tightly connected to the Ramayana story, as many places here are linked to the crucial events that happened in the mythological epic. And with our all-inclusive Sri Lanka Ramayana Tour Package, you can explore the land's cultural and religious sites with utmost comfort and ease!Also known as 'the land of ancient civilizations', Sri Lanka makes for an excellent pilgrimage destination for Hindus. The Ramayana Tour in Sri Lanka is perfect for those who want to discover the island's ancient religious sites and culture, as well as explore the scenic beauty of the country! With our tour plan, you'll see all the key places where Lord Rama, Sita, and Ravana played an important role. To know more about our packages, call us!Why Choose My Quick Trippers for the Sri Lanka Ramayana Package?We offer you an all-encompassing Sri Lanka Tour! Here are the facilities that you'll get with us:Logistics Handled: Our trip packages provide accommodation, transport charges, perfectly curated tour plans by experts, and much more.Natural Beauty and Spirituality Combined: Our Ramayana Sri Lanka Tour itinerary is carefully crafted so that the tourists can enjoy both the sightseeing and the pilgrimage aspects of the trip.Local Knowledge: We'll provide you with knowledgeable guides who will help you know the Ramayana sites on a deeper level. They will tell you stories and tales associated with the place that will enrich your experience tenfold!Safety and Reliability: We offer you licensed vehicles and vetted hotels. And with our 24x7 customer support, you can rely on us for resolving any issue should they arise during the trip.Tailor-Made Options: With our customizable Sri Lanka Ramayana Travel Package, you can go on a trip of your dreams! You can alter the trip duration, choose the car of your choice, and also control the inclusions in your trip.So wait no more, book our package today and go on a trip that is super comfortable and luxurious!Best Time to Go on Sri Lanka Ramayana TourThe best time to go on your Sri Lanka Ramayana trip is from December to March. The weather during this period is dry with little to no rainfall and therefore is highly favourable for sightseeing and other tourist activities.Also, during this time window, you can visit sites like Ravana Falls, Kandy, Nuwara Eliya, and other coastal areas - which otherwise are very difficult to reach because of rain.The temperatures around this time are warm (25\u00b0C to 30\u00b0C) with sunny weather -- which makes exploring gardens, temples, and other Ramayana-linked attractions a cakewalk.Cost of Ramayana Tour Sri LankaOur Ramayana Tour Sri Lanka Cost is INR 38,900 per person. We're currently offering you a discount of over 15%. Therefore, take advantage of this limited-time deal and go on a budget Ramayana Tour Package Sri Lanka!Our Sri Lanka Ramayana Tour Package price are really reasonable, offering the tourists a chance to see the best of Sri Lanka without spending a fortune on the trip. With this package, we'll take full care of your hotel charges, dining bills, and all your travel expenses. Book now!Best Place to Visit on the Sri Lanka Ramayana TripSri Lanka played an important role in the ancient Indian epic Ramayana. And there are multiple significant places here that are deeply connected to the Hindu mythology tale of Lord Rama, Sita, and Ravana. Include the following sites in your itinerary to see it all and have a full-fledged journey:PlaceDescription / SignificanceSeetha Amman Temple (Nuwara Eliya)According to the Ramayana, this is the place where Goddess Sita was held captive by Ravana. This temple houses Ashok Vatika where Sita spent her days in captivity. The temple also possesses a beautiful Sita idol.Ravana Falls (Kandy)This majestic waterfall is widely believed to be the place where Ravana used to take his baths. It beautifully cascades down in a number of tiers and makes for a perfect tourist spectacle. It must be included in your Sri Lanka Ramayana holiday package.Hakgala Botanical GardenThis place lies in close proximity to Ashoka Vatika. This legendary garden has a variety of plants. Tourists just love to stroll around here and reflect on the Ramayana.Manavari Temple (Anuradhapura)According to legend, Manavari is the first place where Lord Rama set foot on after coming to Sri Lanka. It is also believed to be the place where he built a shrine and performed puja of Lord Shiva after defeating Ravana.Ramboda Falls (Ramboda)This is another waterfall that is linked to Ravana. Ramboda Falls is one of the places where he had his Pushpak Viman fly over when he was taking Sita home. He did this to show her the beauty of his kingdom. Today, travellers love the cold winds blowing here and enjoy the picturesque views of lush tea plantations surrounding the area.SigiriyaSigiriya is also closely related to the Ramayana. This UNESCO World Heritage site is a rock fortress where Sita was kept as a captive by Ravana in his kingdom. Tourists love the panoramic views from the top of the rock. A must-addition to the luxury Ramayana Tour Package Sri Lanka!Divurumpola (Near Nuwara Eliya)This sacred place is where Sita underwent Agni Pariksha to prove her innocence after her rescue. Before reuniting with Rama, it is believed that Sita walked around the sacred area in Divurumpola.How to Reach Sri LankaSri Lanka is an island located in the Indian Ocean. Therefore Sri Lanka Ramayana Yatra by air is the primary route to reach here.By Air (International Flights)Sri Lanka has a number of international airports. The two main ones are:1. Bandaranaike International Airport, Colombo:This is the primary airport in Sri Lanka for all international flights. It is approximately 35 km from the capital. The majority of international flights to Sri Lanka arrive here. The airport is well-connected to Asia, Europe, the Middle East, and other continents.2. Mattala Rajapaksa International Airport, Hambantota:This airport also operates international flights. However, it is less busy than Bandaranaike International Airport. It handles flights mainly from the Middle East and some regional destinations.Things to Do on the Sri Lanka Ramayana TourHere are a few things that you must do to make the most out of your trip:Explore Iconic Ramayana SitesRavana Cave: This cave is considered to be the place where Ravana hid Sita.Ashok Vatika: Now a garden, this place was once a prison for Sita.Divurumpola: This site is where she went through the Agni Pariksha.Visit TemplesSeetha Amman Temple: Sita was believed to have spent her time in captivity here.Koneswaram Temple: Legend says Ravana used to come to worship Lord Shiva in this temple during his rule.Sita Eliya Temple: This temple is built around yet another location where Sita was kept captive. Sita River nearby is the place where she would take her baths.Manavari Temple: As per the legend, puja and rituals were performed here by Lord Rama after he had victory over Ravana. Many Sri Lanka Ramayana travel packages include a visit to the nearby ruins in this area as well.Attend Cultural Performances and Local CuisineThere are various Ramayana theme dances and devotional performances organised regularly. A must-do activity on your Ramayana Yatra to Lanka from India! Talking about food, there are delicious Sri Lankan dishes that you can gorge on, such as sweet coconut pancakes, rice noodles, Kaju Curry, etc.Marvel at Natural WondersSri Lanka is home to one of the most iconic natural attractions. While you're there, do visit the Little Adam's Peak and Ella Rock and Sigiriya Rock Fortress. Also, visit the Ram Setu Connection. Although it's mainly on the Indian side, it's still a site to behold from the Sri Lankan shores!Explore Ancient CitiesAnuradhapura and Polonnaruwa are the two ancient capitals that have a plethora of ruins deeply connected to Sri Lanka's mythology.Tips for TravellersHere are some travel tips for your Sri Lanka Ramayana Circuit Tour:While you're planning for the trip, do check the visa requirements for Sri Lanka for Indian tourists.When you're visiting the temples in the country, wear modest clothes. Also, before entering the shrines, take your shoes off.Evening can be cool in the country. Therefore, pack some warm clothes as well.Also, carry rain gear with you, such as an umbrella and a raincoat.If you have some specific food preferences, then go for a tour plan that caters to those things. You can also opt for our Ramayana Tour Package with Indian food in Sri Lanka!While you're on the trip, make sure you stay hydrated. Drink water at regular intervals of time.Respect local customs in order not to get on the bad side of the people.Book the Best Sri Lanka Ramayana Tour Package!This special Sri Lankan tour is an incredible journey that provides glimpses into Ramayana's past while also offering stunning scenery all around! This Ramayana trail Sri Lanka will offer you everything from exploring the mythology to soaking in the spirituality to enjoying the natural beauty of the island! Walk the very lands that once lord Rama and Goddess Sita set foot on! Book My Quick Trippers's Ramayana Tour Packages from India now and enjoy a comfortable trip here. To know more, give us a call!See Less",
    "highlights": [
      "Temple of Lord Shiva Established by Lord Ram after killing Raavan.",
      "Visit to the healing 7 wells.",
      "Visit to the iconic Sigiriya Rock fort which is also a UNESCO world heritage site.",
      "Complete sightseeing of Kandy and Nuwara Eliya.",
      "Visit to the place where Sita had performed her Agni Pariksha.",
      "See More"
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1: Arrival in Sri Lanka - Chilaw - Anuradhapura",
        "description": "Upon arrival, you will be assisted by our tour representative who will make you head towards Anuradhapura via Chilaw. Upon arriving at Chilaw your Ramayana tour will kick start with a visit to Manavari Temple - the spot where Lord Rama had forst established a lingam after killing Ravana. This is an extremely sacred place since there are only two Ramalingam (lingams established by Lord Rama) in the world, one of them being in Rameshwaram. You will then be taken to Munneswaram Temple - this is the exact place where Lord Rama had prayed to Lord Shiva after committing Brahmahasti (priest killing).\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 2: Anuradhapura - Trincomalee",
        "description": "Early in the morning you will be made to proceed for Trincomalee but first you will be made to take a brief tour of Anuradhapura starting with a visit to Kanniya hot water spring well - a collection of 7 wells which is believed to possess natural healing powers and the place where king Ravana is believed to have carried out the last rites for his mother.\nAfter covering a 2 hours road journey and upon arriving at Trincomalee you will be taken to visit the famous Koneswaram Hindu temple - which was built by Rishi Agastya after getting instructions from Lord Shiva who was highly impressed by King Ravana\u2019s devotion. The temple is extremely unique since it is a temple which was built by the lord for his devotee. You will be duly checked in to your hotel for spending the night.\nYour evening will end on a relaxing note at Nilaveli Beach where you will also witness the majestic sunset.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 3: Trincomalee - Kandy",
        "description": "Early in the morning you will start off your journey towards Kandy, while stopping on your way for visits to some of the most mesmerizing tourist attractions like - Sigiriya rock fortress - a UNESCO world heritage site, and popularly dubbed as the 8th wonder of the world is a triple moated defense from where a massive rock emerges to a height of 600 feet, which is complete with gardens and swimming pools on the summit.\nYou will then head on to Cobra cave - named so because of its shape and the place where Sita was held in captivity whose walls are covered in prehistoric inscriptions and artworks.\nUpon arriving at Kandy which is located at a distance of 4 hours and 5 mines you will be checked in to your hotel, after which you will be made to attend the local and traditional Kandy dance show presentation.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 4: Kandy - Nuwara Eliya",
        "description": "Early in the morning, you will be taken on a local sightseeing of Kandy, where you will be made to visit the famous temple of the tooth - a sacred 16th-century site for Sri Lankan Buddhists which houses Lord Buddha\u2019s tooth relic.\nYou will then be escorted to Shri Bhakta Hanuman Temple - where Lord Hanuman wandered looking for Sita and is visited by numerous devotees throughout the year.\nRamboda waterfalls will be your next destination - which is one of the most pristine and picturesque cascading\nwaterfalls in Sri Lanka\n.\nThe island country of Sri Lanka is popular all over the world for its high-quality tea; you will be taken for a visit to the tea factory and tea plantation estates. Here you will also have the option of buying yourself some locally produced tea.\nYour next destination for the day will be upon your arrival at Nuwara Eliya, Seetha Amman temple - a modern vibrant and attractive building which is dedicated to Lord Rama and Sita and enshrines both their statues.\nFinally, you will be taken to the colorful and lively Ashok Vatika - the place where Sita preferred to stay in captivity under the Ashoka tree, hence the name.\nYou will then be duly checked in to your hotel after a wholesome sightseeing tour, where you will be staying overnight.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 5: Nuwara Eliya - Kataragama",
        "description": "Your early morning visit will be on an extremely colorful not, where you will be made to visit Hakgala botanical garden - one of the\n5 most popular botanical gardens in Sri Lanka\nand was Ravana\u2019s favorite places where he kept a very depressed Sita.\nGayathri Amman temple at Nuwara Eliya will be your next destination - which houses numerous Swayambhu (self-created lingams). Next, you will be taken to the historic site of Divurumpola Temple - the spot where Sita had performed her Agnipariksha to prove her purity and took her oaths. Several years later the villagers still pledge their fidelity or take oaths.\nDhowa rock temple will be your next stop - it holds immense relevance since during the 1st century BC this place had served as the refuge place for King Walagamba. It also holds Buddhist importance since there is also a small stupa present inside the cave.\nThe small mountain hamlet of Ella will be your next destination which possesses this was also one of the places where Ravana was hiding Sita. The Ella cave is located at the massive Ella waterfalls (1080 feet). After exploring this glorious site you will be made to head on to Kataragama which is located at a distance of 4 hours where you will be checked in to your allotted hotel for the night.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 6: Kataragama - Colombo",
        "description": "You will be made to visit the famous Kataragama Hindu temple in the morning - the place where Lord Kartikeya had requested to proceed to the battlefield by Lord Indra during the last day of war.\nLater you will be made to proceed towards Ussangoda - the place which was one of the burnt up areas caused by Lord Hanuman\u2019s blazing tail when he was testing the might of Ravana. Galle fortress will be your next destination which was built by the Portuguese in 1588 which till present day reminds the visitors of the colonial past.\nAfter covering a road journey of 5 hours you will reach the magnificent city of Colombo - the largest city of Sri Lanka where upon arrival you will be checked in to your hotel for an overnight stay.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 7: Colombo Sightseeing",
        "description": "Early in the morning, you will be taken on a fun riverboat safari on Bentota Madu. You will also be taken to the famous turtle farms.\nYour sacred temple tour of the day will kick start with Panchamuga Anjaneyar Temple - the only temple on the island which is dedicated to the Panchamuga form (five faces) of Lord Hanuman. You will also be made to visit Kelaniya Raja Maha Vihara - a Buddhist sanctuary which is said to be visited by Lord Buddha himself. There is also a Hindu shrine present within the sanctuary.\nDepending on the availability you will also be taken on a city-wide tour of Colombo which will cover the Independence Memorial Hall, old parliament and Galle face garden.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 8: Colombo Departure",
        "description": "From Colombo, you will be made to head on to the airport which is a 1-hour journey where you will be made to board the flight heading towards your onward destination."
      }
    ],
    "faqs": []
  },
