  "srisailam-mallikarjuna-jyotirlinga-darshan": {
    "overview": "Want to go on a tour that is a reflection of culture, nature, and spirituality?See More\n\nThen, hop on this journey that will take you to the Jyotirlinga, Shakti Peeth Temple, waterfalls, the heritage museum, and so much more! Moreover, the interesting part of this amazing trip is the exploitation of the grandeur of Srisailam! From its big hills to the majestic dam to the peaceful ropeway rides, there\u2019s just so much to enjoy and explore here! To book this special trip, call us now!This two day trip is perfect for individuals who are short on time. From spirituality to natural beauty, there\u2019s a lot to enjoy on this trip. Plus, we\u2019ll also take care of a lot of things for you on the tour. From your dining to transfers to accommodation, everything will be handled by us, so that you can travel worry-free. So wait no more. Give us a call now, and we\u2019ll plan your next adventure in the south today!See Less\n\nThen, hop on this journey that will take you to the Jyotirlinga, Shakti Peeth Temple, waterfalls, the heritage museum, and so much more! Moreover, the interesting part of this amazing trip is the exploitation of the grandeur of Srisailam! From its big hills to the majestic dam to the peaceful ropeway rides, there\u2019s just so much to enjoy and explore here! To book this special trip, call us now!\n\nThis two day trip is perfect for individuals who are short on time. From spirituality to natural beauty, there\u2019s a lot to enjoy on this trip. Plus, we\u2019ll also take care of a lot of things for you on the tour. From your dining to transfers to accommodation, everything will be handled by us, so that you can travel worry-free. So wait no more. Give us a call now, and we\u2019ll plan your next adventure in the south today!",
    "highlights": [
      "Seek blessings at Mallikarjuna Swamy Temple, one of the 12 revered Jyotirlingas",
      "Darshan at Sri Bhramaramba Ammavari Temple, one of the Shakti Peethas",
      "Scenic views of Srisailam Dam",
      "Enjoy photography at the Octopus View Point",
      "Cultural visit to the Chenchu Lakshmi Tribal Museum",
      "Enjoy a ropeway ride to Pathala Ganga",
      "Experience boating on the River Krishna",
      "Visit to sacred spots like Paladhara Panchadara, Sikharam Temple, and Sakshi Ganapathi Temple",
      "Optional visit to the Statue of Equality near Hyderabad",
      "See More"
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1: : Arrival in Hyderabad \u2013 Sightseeing",
        "description": "Welcome to Hyderabad! Our tour representative will greet you with a warm welcome once you arrive at the Hyderabad airport/railway station.\nNow, you\u2019ll be comfortably driven to Srisailam (a 4 hour long drive) in your private vehicle. Along the way, we'll stop at the following sightseeing places:\nSrisailam Dam\n- Take a picture of the breathtaking, massive reservoir\nOctopus View Point\n- Watch as the Krishna river meanders through the hills and in the process, makes the shape of an octopus\nChenchu Lakshmi Tribal Museum\n- Discover the lifestyle of the people who lived in the Nallamala forests for centuries\nRopeway\n- Take this ropeway to capture click bird-eye view shots of the Krishna River\nEvening darshan of Lord Mallikarjuna Swamy Temple and Sri Bhramaramba Ammavari Shakti Peeth Temple.\nBy evening, you\u2019ll be dropped off at your pre-booked hotel. Take a restful night\u2019s sleep.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 2: Temple Visit \u2013 Srisailam Sightseeing \u2013 Departure from Hyderabad",
        "description": "Wake up early in the morning, and proceed to the Darshan of Lord Mallikarjuna Swamy Temple. After the close up with the divine, head to Sri Bhramaramba Ammavari Shakti Peeth Temple, which is housed in the same complex.\nNow, we\u2019ll take you on a sightseeing tour at:\nPaladhara and Panchadhara Waterfalls\nSikharam / Shikaresvara Temple\nSakshi Ganapathi Temple\nPatala Ganga\nYou can also enjoy a scenic boat ride on the Krishna River (on a direct payment basis).\nLastly, we\u2019ll drop you off at the Hyderabad railway station or airport. And if time permits, we\u2019ll also make a stop at the\nStatue of Equality\n(monument dedicated to Shree Ramanujacharya), which is quite close to the Hyderabad Airport.\nHope you enjoyed your trip with us!\nNote:\nTo book your Pooja, Abhishekam, Seva, and more, visit the link:-\nhttps://www.srisailadevasthanam.org/en-in/devotee-app/online-booking/pratyaksha-seva\n.\nNote:\nStatue of Equality is closed on Wednesdays. The entry tickets are as follows:\nAdults - Rs. 200/-\nChild - Rs. 125/-\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      }
    ],
    "faqs": []
  },
  "srisailam-temple-tour-from-hyderabad": {
    "overview": "The 4 Days Srisailam Mallikarjuna tour package from Hyderabad takes travellers to a destination where every spot feels special and worth exploring. See More\n\nThe main attraction here is famous Mallikarjuna Temple, one of the twelve Jyotirlingas.Many devotees feel peaceful and positive here, as if Mahadev\u2019s divine power is all around them. Along with the spiritual experience, travellers can also enjoy a ropeway ride and see the stunning view of Krishna River surrounded by green forests. This tour also covers Chowmahalla Palace, known for its beautiful gardens and royal architecture..It\u2019s a favourite spot for photographers and reel makers so don\u2019t miss it. Another popular highlight is Bhramaramba Devi Temple, which is around 2000 years old and has very interesting history. There are many places to explore but going with good planning and guidance helps you enjoy it fully. So get ready to experience Srisailam Mallikarjuna Temple Darshan!See Less\n\nThe main attraction here is famous Mallikarjuna Temple, one of the twelve Jyotirlingas.\n\nMany devotees feel peaceful and positive here, as if Mahadev\u2019s divine power is all around them. Along with the spiritual experience, travellers can also enjoy a ropeway ride and see the stunning view of Krishna River surrounded by green forests. This tour also covers Chowmahalla Palace, known for its beautiful gardens and royal architecture..\n\nIt\u2019s a favourite spot for photographers and reel makers so don\u2019t miss it. Another popular highlight is Bhramaramba Devi Temple, which is around 2000 years old and has very interesting history. There are many places to explore but going with good planning and guidance helps you enjoy it fully. So get ready to experience Srisailam Mallikarjuna Temple Darshan!",
    "highlights": [
      "Visit the famous Mallikarjuna Jyotirlinga Temple and feel peaceful, positive energy surrounded by green forests and hills.",
      "Explore other attractions like Bhramaramba Devi Temple, Sakshi Ganapathi Temple, Hatkeshwar Temple, Paladhara-Panchadhara, Pathala Ganga, and enjoy boat rides and nature.",
      "Enjoy adventure and fun with the Srisailam Ropeway, Octopus View Point and capture stunning photos of Krishna River and scenic landscapes.",
      "Experience Hyderabad sightseeing and Ramoji Film City, one of the world\u2019s largest film studios, with entertainment, shows and sightseeing included.",
      "See More"
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1- Hyderabad - Srisailam (213 Kms, 4-5 Hours Drive)",
        "description": "We\u2019ll start your Jyotirlinga trip by picking you up from your preferred location - Hyderabad Airport or Railway Station. Our driver from\nMy Quick Trippers\nwill come to pick you up and take you to Srisailam. If you\u2019ve booked a guide, he\u2019ll come with a driver and stay with you all day to assist.\nOn the way, you\u2019ll visit-\nSrisailam Dam\nBhramaramba Devi Temple\nSakshi Ganapathi Temple-\nThis temple may be small, but it is special - people believe the Pandavas visited here.\nHatkeshwar Temple\nOctopus View Point-\nEnjoy the amazing view of the Krishna River between hills. Its shape is like an octopus (a great photography spot)\nChenchu Lakshmi Tribal Museum\nPaathala Ganga-\nMany visitors come to Pathala Ganga for boating and to see its caves. It\u2019s a great spot for nature lovers.\nRopeway, Srisailam\nAfter you arrive, check in at the hotel. In the evening, visit the holy\nMallikarjuna Jyotirlinga Temple\nlocated on the Nallamala Hills. Enjoy your night\u2019s stay at Srisailam.\nNote-\nMallikarjuna Temple is open from\n4:30 AM to 3:00 PM\nand\n6:00 PM to 9:00 PM\n.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 2- Srisailam - Hyderabad (214 Kms / 4-5 Hours Drive)",
        "description": "Start your day with prayer at\nLord Mallikarjuna Swamy Temple\n.\nThen explore\nSri Bhramaramba Ammavari Shakti Peeth Temple\n, where Goddess Sati\u2019s neck is believed to have fallen.\nNow go to\nPaladhara-Panchadhara\n, a very beautiful spot surrounded by nature. If you get a chance, try camping as well.\nClimb\nSikharam Hill\nto visit\nShikaresvara Temple\n, then proceed to\nSakshi Ganapathi Temple\nand\nPathala Ganga\n, and don\u2019t forget to take a boat ride on\nKrishna River\n.\nLater, drive back to\nHyderabad\n. If time permits visit the\nStatue of Equality\nnear\nHyderabad Airport\n.\nSpend a comfortable overnight stay in\nHyderabad\n.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 3- Hyderabad Sightseeing",
        "description": "Start your day with breakfast and then explore\nRamoji Film City\n.\nRamoji Film City\nis one of the world\u2019s biggest and most famous film studios, listed in the Guinness World Records.\nEnjoy a day full of entertainment, shows, and sightseeing.\nReturn to the hotel for an overnight stay in Hyderabad.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 4- Hyderabad Sightseeing - Departure",
        "description": "After breakfast check out from the hotel and go for sightseeing. The places you visit today will depend on your departure time (optional).\nStart your day at the historic\nGolconda Fort\n. Try clapping at the entrance - the echo travels nearly a kilometer. In the past, it helped warn soldiers during attacks.\nNow proceed to\nNehru Zoological Park\n.\nThen, explore the famous\nSalar Jung Museum\n.\nNext, go to\nChowmahalla Palace\n, a beautiful place that took around 100 years to build. Its stunning design will surely impress you.\nLater, visit\nCharminar\n. Try to visit in the evening if possible; the colorful lights make it look truly beautiful.\nIn the evening, visit\nLaad Bazaar\n, famous for its bangles, pearls, and traditional Hyderabad items.\nDrive through\nHussain Sagar Lake\nand\nLumbini Park\nif time allows.\nAfter sightseeing, you\u2019ll be dropped at\nHyderabad\nAirport or Railway Station for your next journey.\nYour Srisailam Mallikarjuna travel package ends with happy memories!\nNote -\nHyderabad city sightseeing\nis not available on Fridays as many places remain closed.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      }
    ],
    "faqs": []
  },
  "srisailam-weekend-trip": {
    "overview": "Want to go on a tour that is a reflection of culture, nature, and spirituality?See More\n\nThen, hop on this journey that will take you to the Jyotirlinga, Shakti Peeth Temple, waterfalls, the heritage museum, and so much more! Moreover, the interesting part of this amazing trip is the exploitation of the grandeur of Srisailam! From its big hills to the majestic dam to the peaceful ropeway rides, there\u2019s just so much to enjoy and explore here! To book this special trip, call us now!This two day trip is perfect for individuals who are short on time. From spirituality to natural beauty, there\u2019s a lot to enjoy on this trip. Plus, we\u2019ll also take care of a lot of things for you on the tour. From your dining to transfers to accommodation, everything will be handled by us, so that you can travel worry-free. So wait no more. Give us a call now, and we\u2019ll plan your next adventure in the south today!See Less\n\nThen, hop on this journey that will take you to the Jyotirlinga, Shakti Peeth Temple, waterfalls, the heritage museum, and so much more! Moreover, the interesting part of this amazing trip is the exploitation of the grandeur of Srisailam! From its big hills to the majestic dam to the peaceful ropeway rides, there\u2019s just so much to enjoy and explore here! To book this special trip, call us now!\n\nThis two day trip is perfect for individuals who are short on time. From spirituality to natural beauty, there\u2019s a lot to enjoy on this trip. Plus, we\u2019ll also take care of a lot of things for you on the tour. From your dining to transfers to accommodation, everything will be handled by us, so that you can travel worry-free. So wait no more. Give us a call now, and we\u2019ll plan your next adventure in the south today!",
    "highlights": [
      "Seek blessings at Mallikarjuna Swamy Temple, one of the 12 revered Jyotirlingas",
      "Darshan at Sri Bhramaramba Ammavari Temple, one of the Shakti Peethas",
      "Scenic views of Srisailam Dam",
      "Enjoy photography at the Octopus View Point",
      "Cultural visit to the Chenchu Lakshmi Tribal Museum",
      "Enjoy a ropeway ride to Pathala Ganga",
      "Experience boating on the River Krishna",
      "Visit to sacred spots like Paladhara Panchadara, Sikharam Temple, and Sakshi Ganapathi Temple",
      "Optional visit to the Statue of Equality near Hyderabad",
      "See More"
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1: : Arrival in Hyderabad \u2013 Sightseeing",
        "description": "Welcome to Hyderabad! Our tour representative will greet you with a warm welcome once you arrive at the Hyderabad airport/railway station.\nNow, you\u2019ll be comfortably driven to Srisailam (a 4 hour long drive) in your private vehicle. Along the way, we'll stop at the following sightseeing places:\nSrisailam Dam\n- Take a picture of the breathtaking, massive reservoir\nOctopus View Point\n- Watch as the Krishna river meanders through the hills and in the process, makes the shape of an octopus\nChenchu Lakshmi Tribal Museum\n- Discover the lifestyle of the people who lived in the Nallamala forests for centuries\nRopeway\n- Take this ropeway to capture click bird-eye view shots of the Krishna River\nEvening darshan of Lord Mallikarjuna Swamy Temple and Sri Bhramaramba Ammavari Shakti Peeth Temple.\nBy evening, you\u2019ll be dropped off at your pre-booked hotel. Take a restful night\u2019s sleep.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 2: Temple Visit \u2013 Srisailam Sightseeing \u2013 Departure from Hyderabad",
        "description": "Wake up early in the morning, and proceed to the Darshan of Lord Mallikarjuna Swamy Temple. After the close up with the divine, head to Sri Bhramaramba Ammavari Shakti Peeth Temple, which is housed in the same complex.\nNow, we\u2019ll take you on a sightseeing tour at:\nPaladhara and Panchadhara Waterfalls\nSikharam / Shikaresvara Temple\nSakshi Ganapathi Temple\nPatala Ganga\nYou can also enjoy a scenic boat ride on the Krishna River (on a direct payment basis).\nLastly, we\u2019ll drop you off at the Hyderabad railway station or airport. And if time permits, we\u2019ll also make a stop at the\nStatue of Equality\n(monument dedicated to Shree Ramanujacharya), which is quite close to the Hyderabad Airport.\nHope you enjoyed your trip with us!\nNote:\nTo book your Pooja, Abhishekam, Seva, and more, visit the link:-\nhttps://www.srisailadevasthanam.org/en-in/devotee-app/online-booking/pratyaksha-seva\n.\nNote:\nStatue of Equality is closed on Wednesdays. The entry tickets are as follows:\nAdults - Rs. 200/-\nChild - Rs. 125/-\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      }
    ],
