  "tamil-nadu-pondicherry-tour": {
    "overview": "As you begin the Tamil Nadu and Pondicherry Tour you\u2019ll feel the magic of South India - simple, with welcoming people and full of hidden beauty. See More\n\nThe tour starts at Mahabalipuram, popular for its old temples and historical monuments, which is very different from other historical places. Every site has something unique to explore!\nPondicherry is another highlight. If time allows visit French-theme cafes that have a peaceful and luxurious vibe, a perfect spot for sipping coffee. Don't miss Auroville Matrimandir, which looks like a big golden ball where people meditate in silence. There is no puja or mantra, only peace and silence.\nRameshwaram is also an important stop, known for the famous Ramanathaswamy Temple, one of the twelve Jyotirlingas of Lord Shiva. There are many hidden gems that people often miss without guidance. Our Tamil Nadu Pondicherry package covers everything for a smooth experience. Just plan your trip with us and enjoy hassle free journey!\nSee Less\n\nThe tour starts at Mahabalipuram, popular for its old temples and historical monuments, which is very different from other historical places. Every site has something unique to explore!\n\nPondicherry is another highlight. If time allows visit French-theme cafes that have a peaceful and luxurious vibe, a perfect spot for sipping coffee. Don't miss Auroville Matrimandir, which looks like a big golden ball where people meditate in silence. There is no puja or mantra, only peace and silence.\n\nRameshwaram is also an important stop, known for the famous Ramanathaswamy Temple, one of the twelve Jyotirlingas of Lord Shiva. There are many hidden gems that people often miss without guidance. Our Tamil Nadu Pondicherry package covers everything for a smooth experience. Just plan your trip with us and enjoy hassle free journey!",
    "highlights": [
      "Explore ancient temples and UNESCO heritage sites in Mahabalipuram, Thanjavur, Chidambaram and Kumbakonam.",
      "Enjoy Pondicherry\u2019s French Quarter, Auroville, cafes and peaceful ashrams.",
      "Visit Rameshwaram with Ramanathaswamy Temple, holy dips, and Rama Setu/Adam\u2019s Bridge.",
      "See Madurai and Tiruchirappalli temples, Rockfort views, museums and local culture.",
      "Experience Kanyakumari sunrise and sunset, Samudra Snanam and meeting point of three oceans.",
      "See More"
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1: Arrive Chennai - Mahabalipuram - Pondicherry (160-170km/4-5 hours)",
        "description": "Start your\nTamil Nadu and Pondicherry trip\nwith a pick-up from your selected location in Chennai airport or railway station. Our driver will come to receive you and then you will continue the tour of Mahabalipuram. If you choose a guide, they will travel with the driver and help you on the journey.\nAfter pick-up you will start your tour and visit-\nKrishna Mandapam\n- This is a rock-cut temple made from a single rock. It has beautiful pictures that shows the stories of Lord Krishna and is a UNESCO World Heritage Site.\nArjuna\u2019s Penance\nCave Temples\n- Around 1,300 years old, these caves are peaceful and have stunning rock art \u2013 perfect spot for photography.\nPancha Rathas\nAfter covering the main sightseeing in Mahabalipuram, you will drive to Pondicherry. On arrival, check into the hotel. Overnight stay at Pondicherry.\nNote-\nKrishna Mandapam is open every day from 7 AM to 6 PM.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "DAY 2: Pondicherry - Chidambaram - Kumbakonam (Approx. 133 km / 2.5 Hours)",
        "description": "After breakfast, check out of the hotel and go to the\nAuroville Matrimandir\n, a calm place for meditation. The Matrimandir and its surrounding gardens have a stunning view, great spot for photography.\nThen, drive to the hotel and check in. Next, visit\nSri Aurobindo Ashram\none of India\u2019s most famous ashram. Around 1,200 people live here in its calm spiritual community.\nAfterward, visit\nArulmigu Manakula Vinayagar Temple\n, an ancient temple dedicated to Lord Ganesh.\nVisit the\nPuducherry Museum\n, famous for its 81 Chola metal statues, one of the largest collections in India.\nLater proceed to\nChidambaram\n, a temple town famous for the\nThillai Nataraja Temple.\nThe temple, spread over 40 acres is dedicated to Lord Shiva as Nataraja.\nExplore\nGangaikonda Cholapuram\n, popular for the\nBrihadeeswarar Temple.\nThis UNESCO World Heritage Site has one of the largest Shiva Lingas, 13 feet tall, with excellent architecture (perfect place for photos ).\nFinally drive to\nKumbakonam.\nAfter arriving, check into the hotel for an overnight stay.\nNote-\nPuducherry Museum is closed on Mondays and holidays.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "DAY 3: Kumbakonam - Thanjavur (Tanjore) - Tiruchirappalli (Trichy) (150 km/ 3.5-4 Hours)",
        "description": "After breakfast, check out and visit\nKumbakonam\n, a city filled with unique temples. On arrival, start exploring the sights.\nSee the\nAdi Kumbeswarar Temple.\nNearby is a large temple tank called\nMahamaham Tank\n, where devotees take holy dips.\nNext travel to\nDarasuram\n, a small town near\nKumbakonam\n, to visit\nAiravatesvara Temple.\nLater drive to\nThanjavur\n(Tanjore). On arrival, visit the\nBrihadeeswara Temple\nthat was built entirely without using any iron or cement.\nThen, explore\nThanjavur Palace\nwhere the\nMaratha rulers\nlived between 1674 and 1855.\nNext go to\nThanjavur Art Gallery\nfilled with beautiful metal and stone art. These works show the rich culture of Tamil history \u2013 perfect for art lovers..\nAfter sightseeing proceed to\nTiruchirappalli (Trichy)\n. Arrive, check into hotel and stay overnight.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "DAY 4: Tiruchirappalli (Trichy) - Madurai (Approx. 123 km/ 4-5 Hours)",
        "description": "Morning after breakfast, check out the hotel and proceed for sightseeing at\nTiruchirappalli.\nFirst, visit\nSri Ranganatha Swamy Temple\n, which is one of the 108 Divya Desams (holy shrines of Vishnu).\nThen proceed to the\nJambukeswarar Akilandeswari Temple\nwhere water from a small underground flow falls on the Shiva Lingam - something truly special.\nAfter that, visit\nUcchi Pillayar\nTemple, dedicated to Lord Ganesha, located on\nRockfort\n, with stunning city views from the top ( don\u2019t forget to take photos ).\nThen visit the\nGovernment Museum\nat Rani Mangammal Mahal, where you can see collections of art, history and local wildlife.\nAfter that visit the\nButterfly Park\nto see colorful butterflies, and explore Nakshatra Vanam, which has 27 trees linked to stars and zodiac signs in Indian astrology.\nAfter sightseeing, proceed to\nMadurai.\nOn arrival, check in to the hotel and enjoy an overnight stay.\nNote-\nGovernment Museum timings are 10 AM to 5 PM.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "DAY 5: Madurai - Rameshwaram (173 km/ 3-4 Hours)",
        "description": "On the fifth day of your\ntrip\n, have breakfast, check out of the hotel, and start your sightseeing tour of\nMadurai.\nVisit\nMeenakshi Sundareswarar Temple\n, a beautiful old temple near the\nVaigai River\n(looks stunning in the evening due to lights).\nThen, see\nThiruparankundram Murugan Temple.\nLater, drive to\nRameshwaram\n, located on\nPamban Island.\nAccording to mythology, Rama made a bridge here to reach Lanka and rescue Sita from Ravana.\nOn arrival, check into your hotel. Then explore\nRamanathaswamy Temple, Agnitheertham, and Ramjharoka Temple.\nStay overnight in Rameshwaram.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "DAY 6: In Rameswaram",
        "description": "Early in the morning, around\n5:00 AM\n, proceed to the\nSpatika Linga Darshan\n, also called\nMani Darshan\n, where the natural crystal Shivling (not man-made) is very important in Hinduism and looks very beautiful.\nLater you will head out for\nAgni Teertham\nto have a holy bath in the sea.\nFurther proceed to the main temple through North gate and\nTake sacred bath with holy water of the 22 wells, inside the\nRamanathaswamy Temple\nduring\nTheerth Snanam.\nThen proceed for darshan and pooja at the main temple.\nAfter checking out of the hotel, proceed to visit\nFive-faced Hanuman Temple.\nNext, explore\nRamar Patham\nand\nKothandaramaswamy Temple, Rama Setu/ Adam\u2019s Bridge\n(stones placed by Lord Rama that don\u2019t sink), and visit\nGandamadana Parvatham\n, where Lord\nRama\u2019s footprint\nis believed to be.\nAlso, explore\nA. P. J. Abdul Kalam\u2019s house\n, the home of India\u2019s famous scientist and former President.\nGo to\nDhanushkodi\n, an old town at Rameshwaram Island. If time allows, explore and enjoy the beaches.\nOn arrival, check into the hotel. Overnight stay in\nRameshwaram.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "DAY 7: Rameswaram - Kanyakumari (312 kms/ 7 Hours)",
        "description": "In the morning, visit the temple once again or take a\nSamudra Snanam\n(holy dip in the sea). Afterward, check out of the hotel and drive to\nKanyakumari\n, the point where the Bay of Bengal, the Arabian Sea, and the Indian Ocean meet.\nKanyakumari\nis famous for being the only place where you can see both the sunrise and sunset over the ocean.\nOn arrival, check into your hotel and relax for the rest of the day. Stay overnight at the hotel.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "DAY 8: Kanyakumari - Kovalam - Thiruvananthapuram (Trivandrum) (Approx. 109/ 3 Hrs)",
        "description": "Early in the morning, you can watch the beautiful\nsunrise in Kanyakumari.\nThe calm atmosphere makes it a perfect time to take pictures.\nLater return to hotel for breakfast.\nAfter breakfast visit the\nSwami Vivekananda Rock Memorial\n- a quiet place surrounded by the sea. Walk over the Sea by Glass bridge to reach Thiruvalluvar Statue.\nIf you have time, take a boat ride.\nNext move to the famous\nKanyakumari Temple\n, also known as\nKumari Amman Temple.\nThis temple is built in\nKerala-style architecture\n, so just get ready to click photos.\nYou can also visit\nTriveni Sangam\nwhere the three oceans meet, and\nGandhi Mandapam\n, built at the place where Mahatma Gandhi\u2019s ashes were kept before being put into the sea.\nDon\u2019t miss the impressive\nThiruvalluvar Statue\nbuilt in memory of the great Tamil poet and philosopher.\nLater drive towards\nTrivandrum.\nOn the way visit\nThanumalayan Temple\nat\nSuchindram\nfamous for its beautiful architecture and the 22-foot-tall statue of Lord Hanuman.\nThen continue to\nPadmanabhapuram Palace\nknown for its traditional\nKerala\n-style design. Don\u2019t forget to take some photos.\nIf time permits stop at\nKovalam Beach\nfor a short visit before heading to Trivandrum.\nOn arrival, check into the hotel and later visit\nSri Padmanabhaswamy Temple\ndedicated to Lord Vishnu.\nOvernight stay at Trivandrum.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "DAY 9: Thiruvananthapuram (Trivandrum) (Departure)",
        "description": "After breakfast, your\ntrip to Pondicherry and Tamil Nadu\nends with happy memories as you are transferred to Trivandrum Airport or railway station for your onward journey."
      }
    ],
    "faqs": []
  },
