  "tamilnadu-pilgrimage-tour": {
    "overview": "Do you believe South India is only famous for temples? See More\n\nThis Tamil Nadu pilgrimage tour Package will surprise you with its mix of heritage, seaside beauty, and rich culture. From Chennai, the trip takes you first to Mahabalipuram, famous for the Pancha Rathas, where each temple is made from a single big stone.\nIn Rameswaram, you can see Ram Setu, a line of stones in the sea. Some of them even float! People believe Lord Rama built this bridge to reach Lanka and save Sita. You will also visit Ooty. Be sure to see its popular Botanical Garden, full of rare, colorful flowers and excellent surroundings - it\u2019s truly memorable for nature lovers.\nThe trip also covers Kanchipuram, famous for its silk Sarees. Make sure to shop if you get the chance. There\u2019s much more to explore! Just get ready to discover such\nhidden gems waiting for you on this Tamil Nadu pilgrimage tour Plan.\nSee Less\n\nThis Tamil Nadu pilgrimage tour Package will surprise you with its mix of heritage, seaside beauty, and rich culture. From Chennai, the trip takes you first to Mahabalipuram, famous for the Pancha Rathas, where each temple is made from a single big stone.\n\nIn Rameswaram, you can see Ram Setu, a line of stones in the sea. Some of them even float! People believe Lord Rama built this bridge to reach Lanka and save Sita. You will also visit Ooty. Be sure to see its popular Botanical Garden, full of rare, colorful flowers and excellent surroundings - it\u2019s truly memorable for nature lovers.\n\nThe trip also covers Kanchipuram, famous for its silk Sarees. Make sure to shop if you get the chance. There\u2019s much more to explore! Just get ready to discover such\nhidden gems waiting for you on this Tamil Nadu pilgrimage tour Plan.",
    "highlights": [
      "Explore famous temples, heritage sites, and unique architecture across Tamil Nadu.",
      "Spend time near the sea, enjoy hills and see beautiful gardens at Ooty and Kodaikanal.",
      "Explore cultural spots like Kanchipuram for silk shopping and Pondicherry for peaceful experiences.",
      "Visit famous places such as Rama Setu, Brihadeeswarar Temple and Annamalaiyar Temple.",
      "See More"
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1: Arrival Chennai - Mahabalipuram - Pondicherry (250 - 280 km/ 6 - 7 hours)",
        "description": "Start your Tamil Nadu trip. Your journey begins in Chennai, where our\nMy Quick Trippers\nteam will meet you at Chennai Railway Station or airport and take you to Mahabalipuram to see the main sights. Later, continue to Pondicherry for local sightseeing. If you have a guide, they will join the driver and help you for the whole day.\nExplore These Places in Mahabalipuram\nFive Rathas-\nancient rock-cut temples, the best destination to click photos.\nCave Temple-\nA beautiful temple around\n1,200\u20131,300 years old.\nArjuna\u2019s Penance-\nIn Mahabalipuram, a huge rock shows a story from the Mahabharata. Arjuna is shown meditating to gain special powers surrounded by gods, animals and magical scenes.\nIn Pondicherry, you will visit-\nArtificial Beach-\nA man-made seaside spot.\nAuroville Ashram-\nIt is a peaceful community where people from around the world live together. Many visitors come here from far away to experience its unique meditation.\nOnce sightseeing is done, spend the night in Pondicherry.\nNote-\nCarry water, sun protection, and comfortable walking shoes. Photography is allowed at most places, but follow local rules.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 2: Pondicherry- Chidambaram- Kumbakonam (140 km/3-4 hours)",
        "description": "In the morning, go to Chidambaram and spend time at the Nataraja Temple. This temple covers an area of 40 acres. It is famous for its unique architecture and is perfect for taking pictures.\nLater, drive to\nKumbakonam\n. On arrival, in\nKumbakonam, visit Oppiliappan Koil, Thiruvenkadu,Thirunageswaram\n(oldest temple around 1,100 years),\nThirumanancheri\n(known for beautiful surroundings),\nPatteeswaram\n,\nAlangudi\n,\nSuriyanar Kovil\n(best for morning sunrise views),\nKanjanur\n,\nVaitheeswaran Temple\n,\nKeezhaperumpallam\n,\nThingalur\n,\nThirunallar\n.\nOvernight stay at the hotel.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 3: Kumbakonam-Tanjore -Trichy (95 - 100 km/2.5 -3 hours)",
        "description": "After breakfast, visit\nTanjore\nto see the\nBrihadeeswarar Temple\n, famous for one of the largest Shiva lingams in India. Next, explore\nTanjore Palace\nand its\nmuseum\n.\nLater, travel to\nTrichy\n. See the\nSri Ranganathaswamy Temple\nin\nSrirangam\n, visit\nRockfort\n(best place to click photos from the top because of city views), then also visit\nSamayapura\n, and\nThiruvanaikaval\n.\nAfter having dinner, continue to\nRameswaram\nand stay overnight there.\nNote-\nBrihadeeswarar Temple timing is\n6am -12:30pm\n,\n4pm - 8:30pm\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 4: Trichy - Rameswaram (228 Kms/ 6-7 hours)",
        "description": "After breakfast, travel to Rameswaram.\nEnjoy sightseeing in\nRameswaram\nand visit\nPamban Bridge\n(famous sea bridge with amazing views),\nRamanatha Swamy Temple\n,\nRamar Patham\n(believed footprints of Lord Rama),\nKothandaramaswamy Temple\n,\nAgni Theertham\n(holy water for ritual baths),\nDhanushkodi\n(scenic beaches to click photos),\nHanuman Temple\nand\nfloating stonenear Hanuman ji temple\n(sacred stone that floats on water called Ram Setu).\nThen, return to the hotel, enjoy dinner, and stay overnight.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 5: Rameshwaram - Madurai - Kodaikanal (Distance approx, 313 km/ 6-7 hours)",
        "description": "Early in the morning, start with\nSpatika Lingam Darshan\nat the\nRamanathaswamy Temple\nin\nRameswaram\n. After that, proceed to\nMadurai\n. Visit the\nMeenakshi Amman Temple\nand enjoy its stunning design. This temple has\n14 colorful towers\n, which makes it more unique than many other temples.\nAfter sightseeing in\nMadurai\n, drive to\nKodaikanal\n. On arrival, check into the hotel. Overnight stay at Kodaikanal.\nNote-\nMeenakshi Amman Temple is closed during lunch hours (around\n12:00pm\n-\n4:30pm\n), so plan your visit accordingly.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 6: Kodaikanal Sightseeing",
        "description": "After breakfast start sightseeing in\nKodaikanal\n. Enjoy beautiful hills and fresh mountain air.\nIn\nKodaikanal\n, visit\nBryant Park\n(a beautiful garden with colorful flowers),\nCoakers Walk\n,\nPillar Rock\n,\nSuicide Point\n(breathtaking views of valleys and forests for photos),\nSilver Falls\n(180 feet waterfall hidden in the forest),\nBear Shola Falls\n,\nKurinji Andavar Temple\n(special Kurinji flowers bloom here once every 12 years) and\nKodaikanal Lake\n( perfect for boating and relaxing ).\nReturn to the hotel for relaxation after a day full of sightseeing. Overnight stay at\nKodaikanal\n.\nNote-\nKodaikanal is at a high altitude, so the weather can be cool even during the day. Carry warm clothes.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 7: Kodaikanal - Palani - Ooty",
        "description": "After breakfast, drive to\nOoty\n. Stop at\nPalani\nto visit the\nMurugan Temple\n(famous for its 600+ stairs going up the hill) and visit Coonoor to enjoy the beautiful tea gardens and hill views.\nAfter arriving in\nOoty\n, check into the hotel.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 8: Ooty - Tiruvannamala",
        "description": "After breakfast proceed for Ooty sightseeing. Explore the key attractions and enjoy the natural beauty of this hill station.\nIn Ooty, visit\nBotanical Gardens\n,\nRose Garden\n(India\u2019s largest with 2,000+ rose varieties),\nOoty Lake\n(boating and horse rides),\nDoddabetta Peak\n(known for the highest Nilgiri peak with valley views),\nGovernment Museum\n,\nPykara Falls\n(scenic waterfall for photography),\nChocolate Factory\n,\nGolf Course\nand\nLady Canning\u2019s Seat\n.\nHave dinner after sightseeing and continue your night journey to\nTiruvannamalai\n.\nNote-\nSince it\u2019s a hilly area, download maps before you start.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 9: Tiruvannamalai Sightseeing",
        "description": "Check into the hotel in\nTiruvannamalai\n. After that, proceed for sightseeing. Have Darshan of Lord Annamalaiyar at the famous\nAnnamalaiyar Temple\n. Unlike most temples, Annamalaiyar Temple has a special ritual called Girivalam, where devotees walk around the Arunachala Hill at night on full moon days for spiritual blessings.\nOvernight stay at the hotel in\nTiruvannamalai\n.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 10: Tiruvannamalai - Kanchipuram - Thiruttani (Approx. 195 km/ 5.5 hours )",
        "description": "Start your day with a road trip to\nKanchipuram\n. Once you arrive visit the famous\nEkambareswarar Temple\n, dedicated to Lord Shiva, which has the 6th-tallest Gopuram (towered entrance) in the world.\nNext stop at the\nKailasanathar Temple\n, an ancient temple made of sandstone. Unlike many temples that are painted, its stone designs are left natural, which gives the temple its unique charm.\nAfter Darshan, you will travel by road to\nThiruthani\n. When you reach, check into the hotel for an overnight stay.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 11: Thiruthani Departure",
        "description": "After breakfast, your\nTamil Nadu pilgrimage tour package\nends, and you will be taken to your departure location for your home."
      }
    ],
    "faqs": []
  },
  "tamilnadu-tour": {
    "overview": "Tamilnadu, inarguably one of those wonderful states where you can witness the vivid cultures and traditions.  See More\n\nThis gorgeous state in India is a magnificent delight for travel enthusiasts and also for the devotees looking for a wonderful religious tour as there are several temples located in the city that were constructed several centuries ago and are still holding the same significance and importance in Hinduism and also the tourism rate of this southern state. Kanchipuram, Rameshwaram, Madurai, and Mahabalipuram are the major sites where tourists love visiting and spending time with their loved ones. Being located on the Western Ghats, the city is also studded with incredible greenery found all around and the dense forests serve habitat to various wildlife species.\nAlso, if you are tired of bearing the scorching heat of the sunrays then move towards Ooty and Kodaikanal, the two gorgeous hill stations that are adorned with panoramic landscapes and witness pleasant climate to make it an ideal holiday destination. Check out this beautifully crafted best of Tamil Nadu tour itinerary and plan your next holiday here.\nSee Less\n\nThis gorgeous state in India is a magnificent delight for travel enthusiasts and also for the devotees looking for a wonderful religious tour as there are several temples located in the city that were constructed several centuries ago and are still holding the same significance and importance in Hinduism and also the tourism rate of this southern state. Kanchipuram, Rameshwaram, Madurai, and Mahabalipuram are the major sites where tourists love visiting and spending time with their loved ones. Being located on the Western Ghats, the city is also studded with incredible greenery found all around and the dense forests serve habitat to various wildlife species.",
    "highlights": [
      "Visit to Kapaleeswarar Temple, Ashtalakshmi Temple.",
      "Visit to the UNESCO world heritage temple of the shore temples.",
      "Exploration of heritage sites like Pancha Ratha, Varaha Cave Temple, Balancing Rock, Krishna Mandapam, Arjuna\u2019s penance etc.",
      "Tanjore sightseeing to places like Nandi Temple, royal palace complex etc.",
      "Exploration of Trichy en route Madurai to places like Rock Fort Temple, Jambukeswarar Temple.",
      "Visit of marvellous tourist attractions in Madurai including visit to places like Meenakshi Amman Temple, Gandhi Museum etc.",
      "Scenic drive up to Rameshwaram.",
      "Sightseeing in Rameshwaram including visit to places like Ram Jharokha Temple and Rameshwaram Temple (a Char Dham Temple).",
      "Checking out the incredible Triveni Sangam of Arabian Sea, Bay of Bengal and Indian Ocean.",
      "Visit some of the most famous tourist attractions in Kanyakumari to places like Vivekananda Rock Memorial Suchindram Temple, Kanyakumari Temple etc.",
      "See More"
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1: Chennai Arrival",
        "description": "Arrival at the Chennai airport. Our representative meets and welcomes you on your arrival to Chennai Railway station/Airport. Later our representative assists you to transfer to Cochin Hotel. Later visit Kapaleeswarar Temple and Ashtalakshmi Temple, evening free to Explore the beaches, overnight stay at hotel.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 2: Chennai - Mahabalipuram",
        "description": "Morning, after breakfast drive to Mahabalipuram visit Crocodile Farm and Dakshinachitra (Craft village). Visit Shore Temple (UNESCO World Heritage site) and other heritage sites (Pancha Ratha, Varaha Cave Temple, Tiger Cave, Krishna Mandapam, Balancing rock, Arjuna\u2019s Penance, all within 1-2 km radius) in the evening. Overnight in Mahabalipuram.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 3: Mahabalipuram - Tanjore",
        "description": "After breakfast drive to Tanjore, Upon arrival, check in at pre-booked hotel then explore the local tourist attractions which include Brihadeeswara temple, Nandi temple and the Royal Palace complex. Overnight in Tanjore.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 4: Tanjore - Trichy - Madurai",
        "description": "Morning Proceed to Madurai on the way visit Trichy where you see the Rock Fort Temple, Jambukeswarar Temple and Srirangam Temple. Now proceed to Madurai. On arrival check in at hotel. Later explore the marvelous temples and other attractions of this city. The famous places you will visit here include Meenakshi Amman Temple, Gandhi Museum and Thirumalai Nayak Palace. Drive back to hotel. Overnight in Madurai.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 5: Madurai - Rameshwaram",
        "description": "After breakfast at hotel. Drive towards Rameshwaram. On arrival check in at pre-booked hotel then go for city tour covering the sightseeing of the most famous attraction of this place is Rameshwaram temple, a prominent Jyotirlinga of Lord Shiva. Other temples you will visit here include Ramjharoka Temple, Kothandaramaswamy Temple and Ramanathaswamy Temple. Stay overnight at the hotel in Rameshwar.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 6: Rameshwaram - Kanyakumari",
        "description": "Today, after breakfast at hotel leave for Kanyakumari, it is the city where you can witness the confluence of three mighty water bodies- Arabian Sea, Indian Ocean and the Bay of Bengal. The famous places you will visit here include Vivekananda Rock Memorial, Suchindram Temple, Kanyakumari Temple and the Gandhi Mandapam. Enjoy Sunset of Kanyakumari from the tip of India, overnight at Hotel.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 7: Kanyakumari - Trivandrum",
        "description": "Departure Early morning enjoy the sunrise on the beach. After breakfast transfer to Kanyakumari Trivandrum Airport/ Railway Station for Journey to onwards Destination. Thank you for your patronage and looks forward to serving you again in the near future."
      }
    ],
