  "tiger-trail-tours-india": {
    "overview": "The tour takes you to two well-known reserves in India, both of which have unrivalled wildlife. Kanha National Park is often called \u2018Tigerland\u2019 and Bandhavgarh National Park is known as white tiger country. Have fun seeing the big cat on the elephant\u2019s back. The tour can also be customized to meet your specific requirements. Madhya Pradesh is India\u2019s heritage heartland. It is India\u2019s central province, is endowed with natural beauty, frequented by wild animals, steeped in history, and teeming with wildlife. Here vacations are a treat for those who want to live life to the fullest and go above and beyond to explore the best of the jungles. Madhya Pradesh is home to a diverse range of wild animals, including deer, wild boar, and tigers. In this 14 days / 13 nights tour will cover the 3 best wildlife sanctuaries of the region.\n\nTiger Trail Tour Itinerary Package\n\n\nDay 1 :Delhi Arrival\n\n\nThe My Quick Trippers representative will receive you at the Delhi airport/ railway station and take you safely to the hotel booked in advance for you. Rest for the day and spend the night at the hotel.\n\n\n\n\nDay 2 :New Delhi to Jabalpur\n\n\nWill start with breakfast post which you will be taken to Jabalpur by flight. As you arrive in Jabalpur you will be taken to the hotel where you will check-in and rest for lunch. In the evening you can indulge in excursion to the Bhedaghat marble rocks which lie at both banks of the Narmada River. Opt for a boat ride on this river and go to the Dhuandhar Falls for a scenic beauty. The night will be spent in the Jabalpur hotel.\n\n\n\n\nDay 3 :Jabalpur to Kanha National Park\n\n\nOn day 3, start with early breakfast and then move on to the Kanha National Park. As you arrive here check-in and rest for lunch. Post lunch hop into the jeep for a safari of the jungle where you can view the tigers. Return in the evening for a delicious dinner and night stay.\n\n\n\n\nDay 4 :At Kanha National Park\n\n\nDay 4 starts with morning safari to the jungle followed by breakfast at the hotel. To enjoy the Tiger show you can opt for elephant ride in the afternoon. Enjoy the serene atmosphere of the jungle till the evening and get back to the hotel for dinner and overnight stay.\n\n\n\n\nDay 5 :Kanha National Park Continued\n\n\nOpt for an early morning safari on day 5. Return to the hotel for breakfast and get geared up again for going deep into the jungle to see the single-horned rhinos and other animals dwelling in this place. Dinner and night stay at the hotel in Kanha.\n\n\n\n\nDay 6 :Kanha to Bandhavgarh National Park\n\n\nOn day 6, start with morning safari of the jungle and then head back to the hotel for breakfast. Freshen up and leave for Bandhavgarh National Park. Once in Bandhavgarh, check into the hotel booked for you and rest for the day. Night stay will be at the hotel.\n\n\n\n\nDay 7 :At Bandhavgarh National Park\n\n\nDay 7 will start with hearty breakfast followed by jeep safari to the National Park to view the tigers and various other beasts housed in this place. Discover the habitat of these creatures and return to the hotel for lunch. Post lunch get back on the jeep for another ride into the jungle and learn more about the wild beasts of this region. In the evening get back to the hotel for dinner and night stay.\n\n\n\n\nDay 8 :Bandhavgarh National Park Continued\n\n\nStart day 8 with early breakfast followed by morning trip to the jungle to check out the ambiance of this place in the morning time. You can also enjoy elephant rides to encounter tigers. Post lunch start out again for this National Park and get deeper into the jungle to explore the vegetation and wildlife of the region. Get back to the hotel in the evening for a sumptuous dinner and overnight stay.\n\n\n\n\nDay 9 :Bandhavgarh to Panna National Park\n\n\nOn day 9, after a filling breakfast leave for Panna National Park. After arriving here check into the hotel booked for you. Post lunch opt for a jungle safari and enjoy the flora and fauna of this place. Get back to the hotel for dinner and night rest.\n\n\n\n\nDay 10 :At Panna National Park\n\n\nDay 10 will include both morning and evening jungle safari. After an early breakfast explore the geographic richness of the region of this Panna National Park. After an exciting day with the wildlife here return to the hotel for night stay.\n\n\n\n\nDay 11 :Panna to Khajuraho\n\n\nPost breakfast on day 11 you will be taken to Khajuraho and after arrival here you will check into the hotel here. After freshening up leave for sightseeing the historically significant temples of both Eastern and Western groups. View the amazing architecture and return to the hotel in the evening for rest and night stay.\n\n\n\n\nDay 12 :Khajuraho to Delhi\n\n\nAfter a hearty breakfast on day 12, you will leave Khajuraho for Delhi. As you reach Delhi you will be checked into the hotel booked for you previously. Take rest for the day and overnight stay at the hotel.\n\n\n\n\nDay 13 :At Delhi\n\n\nPost breakfast on day 13 you will start for sightseeing which will include Old as well as New Delhi that will cover Jama Masjid, Chandni Chowk, Qutub Minar, Humayun\u2019s Tomb, India Gate, Raj Ghat, Parliament and President House. Return to the hotel for night stay.\n\n\n\n\nDay 14 :Leaving Delhi\n\n\nAfter breakfast on the final day, the My Quick Trippers representative will escort you to the Delhi airport/railway station to get back home safely.",
    "highlights": [
      "Visit the famous Jabalpur Bhedaghat marble rocks on the sides of Narmada River",
      "Be a part of the Kanha Wildlife Sanctuary",
      "Be with the majestic cats at the Bandhavgarh Wildlife Sanctuary",
      "Understand history at the Khajuraho Temple",
      "Also visit to the Panna Wildlife Sanctuary"
    ],
