  "tirupati-rameshwaram-kanyakumari-madurai-tour": {
    "overview": "Experience the best that Andhra Pradesh and Tamil Nadu have to offer with our handcrafted packages, including visits to Tirupati, Thanjavur, Rameshwaram, Kanyakumari, and Madurai. These packages are an amalgamation of the best experiences, spiritual tours, adventure activities, and lip-smacking meals. Our guide will accompany you throughout the tour, ensuring you get to have the best experience of your life. With amenities like top-notch accommodation, tasty meals, and guided sightseeing, you're bound to have an extraordinary tour.\n\nTour Gallery\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nTour Name\nTirupati Thanjavur Rameshwaram Kanyakumari Madurai Tour Package\n\n\nTour Duration\n8 Days / 7 Nights\n\n\nMeals\nBreakfast\n\n\nVehicle Type\nPrivate AC Car\n\n\nStarting & Ending Point\nChennai / Thiruvananthapuram\n\n\nDestination Covered\nTirupati \u279d Thanjavur \u279d Rameshwaram \u279d Kanyakumari \u279d Madurai\n\n\nPickup Time\nDepend on your Flight Timing\n\n\n Tour Benefits\nBest price & enjoyable travel guarantee",
    "highlights": [
      "Seek the blessings of Lord Venkateswara at Tirumala Hills.",
      "Sightseeing tour of Tiruchirapalli.",
      "Tirupati Darshan.",
      "Visit the Government Museum.",
      "Visit the famous attractions of Madurai.",
      "Take a dip in the sacred water of Agni Theertham.",
      "Enjoy the sunrise view in Kanyakumari.",
      "Absorb the sacred aura of the Sri Padmanabhaswamy temple.",
      "See More"
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "DAY 01: Arrival - Chennai - Tirupati (3 hrs/140 kms)",
        "description": "Arrive at Chennai and meet our representative at Chennai Railway Station/Airport.\nOur representative will make all the arrangements to transfer you to Tirupati, which is dotted with cultural and historical treasures.\nThis is a famous pilgrimage town in Andhra Pradesh, home to the Vaishnavite shrine of Tirumala Venkateswara Temple.\nAfter reaching Tirupati, you will check into your hotel and relax for some time.\nYou will then head to the Tirumala Hills, that is known to be the sacred abode of Lord Venkateshwara.\nThe Tirumala hills are a group of seven peaks, namely Anjanadri, Vrushabadri, Narayanadri, Seshadri, Neeladri, Garudadri, and Venkatadri.\nPlease Note:-\nWithout a darshan ticket, you won't be able to have darshan at Tirupati. You can opt for Sarva Darshanam.\nYou can choose from two options. Without or with a token, Sarva Darshanam will take more time for darshan. 12-18 hours on weekends, 8-12 hours on regular days, and 12-36 hours on festival days.\nWithout a Darshan Ticket, you may be able to visit Tirumala, but you won't be able to have Darshan at the Main Temple.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 02: Tirupati Darshan-(3 Hrs/110 Kms)- Vellore -(2Hrs/95 Kms)-Tiruvannamalai",
        "description": "Have a delicious breakfast in the morning, and then you will head to Kanipakam and Srinivasa Mangapuram.\nLater, you will head to Vellore, which houses the Golden Temple.\nAfter arriving at Vellore, you will visit the Golden Temple that is situated at Sripuram and built in honor of goddess Lakshmi. The temple's architecture is star-shaped, and the goddess has been placed in the middle of the star.\nThen you will head to Tiruvannamalai, a renowned pilgrimage center situated at the foothills of Annamalai hills.\nOnce you have arrived, you will check into your pre-booked hotel and visit the main temple. Tiruvannamalai houses Annamalaiyar Temple, which is dedicated to Shiva and worshiped as Annamalaiyar or Arunachalesvara. It is one of the largest temples in India that houses four gateway towers. The Shiva Lingam here has an association with the Pancha Bhoota, specifically the element of Fire.\nAfter the darshan, you will head back to your hotel and have an overnight stay.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 03: Tiruvannamalai - (220 Kms/ 5 Hrs)- Thanjavur (Tanjore) - (75 Kms/ 2 Hrs)-Tiruchirappalli (Trichy)",
        "description": "Relish a delicious breakfast in the morning, and then you will check out of your hotel and get ready for sightseeing in Thanjavur.\nYou will visit the famous attractions, including the Brihadeeswara Temple, a UNESCO World Heritage Site and the biggest temple in the region. This architectural marvel was built by Raja Raja Chola during the 11th century.\nYou will then visit Thanjavur Palace, a historical structure in Thanjavur. It was the Maratha rulers' official residence from 1674 to 1855.\nThen you will visit the Thanjavur Art Gallery, where you will see a treasured collection of stone sculptures, bronze icons, and other artifacts, which testify to the golden age in Tamil history.\nYou will then embark on a drive to Tiruchirappalli, renowned for its historical attractions.\nAfter arriving in Tiruchirappalli, you will check into your hotel and have an overnight stay.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 04: Tiruchirappalli - Madurai- (3 hrs/140 km)",
        "description": "Relish a tasty breakfast in the morning, and then you will check out of your hotel.\nYou will get ready for a sightseeing tour of Tiruchirapalli.\nYou will visit the Sri Ranganatha Swamy temple, which is dedicated to Lord Ranganatha Swamy and is considered to be the most important of the one hundred and eight main Vishnu temples.\nYou will then visit the Jambukeswarar Akilandeswari Temple, which is built in honor of Lord Shiva and Goddess Parvathi. The temple has an association with the Pancha Bhoota, specifically the element of Water (Jala).\nThen you will get ready to visit Ucchi Pillayar Temple. This seventh-century Hindu temple is situated at the top of Rockfort and is dedicated to Lord Ganesha.\nYou will also visit the Government Museum, which is located in Bharathidasan San town at Rani Mangammal Mahal. The museum comprises a wide range of exhibits related to anthropology, epigraphy, geology, zoology, paintings, and history.\nYou will then head to Tropical Butterfly Conservatory Campus, the Tropical Butterfly Conservatory. Then you will drive to Madurai.\nAfter arriving at Madurai, you will check into your hotel and have an overnight stay.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 05: Madurai - Rameshwaram (3 hrs/180 km)",
        "description": "Post breakfast, you will check out of the hotel and head out for a sightseeing tour of Madurai.\nYou will visit the famous attractions such as the Meenakshi Sundareswarar Temple, which is situated on the southern banks of the river Vaigai. The complex has twelve gateway towers, ranging in height from 45-50 m.\nThen you will head to Thiruparankundram Murugan Temple, one of the six abodes of Lord Murugan.\nYou will then head to Rameshwaram, which is situated on Pamban Island and is separated by the Pamban channel from mainland India. According to legend, Rameshwaram is considered to be the spot from where Rama built a bridge to rescue his consort Sita from Ravana.\nYou will then head to Rameshwaram and check into your hotel.\nYou will then visit Ramanathaswamy Temple, Ramjharoka Temple, and Agnitheertham and have an overnight stay at your hotel in Rameshwaram.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 06: Rameswaram - Kanyakumari - (6 hrs/310 km)",
        "description": "Early morning, you will take a dip in the sacred water of Agni Theertham, and then you will go for Sphatik Lingam Darshan.\nAfter the darshan and holy bath, you will head back to your hotel and have a tasty breakfast.\nYou will then head out for a sightseeing tour of Rameshwaram, which includes Ramar Patham, Five-faced Hanuman Temple, Gandamadana Parvatham/ Lord Rama footprint, Kothandaramaswamy Temple, Former President A. P. J. Abdul Kalam House, Rama Setu/ Adam's Bridge, and Dhanushkodi.\nYou will then head to Kanyakumari -the Indian Peninsula's southernmost point and the confluence of three oceans - the Arabian Sea, the Bay of Bengal, and the Indian Ocean.\nAfter arriving at Kanyakumari, you will check into your hotel and have an overnight stay.\nDhanushkodi:\nAdam's Bridge is the main attraction of Dhanushkodi. You can reach this place by hiring a jeep (4-wheel drive). It is a tip of the island where normal cars don't go.\nKothandaraman Temple:\nThis is the sacred site where Vibhishana surrendered to Lord Rama. In this temple, Rama, the main idol, has been depicted with a bow and arrow.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 07: Kanyakumari - Kovalam - Thiruvananthapuram (Trivandrum) (2 Hrs/100 Kms)",
        "description": "Early in the morning, you will head out for a sunrise view in Kanyakumari.\nYou will then head back to your hotel and have a Scrumptious breakfast.\nYou will then head out to visit the Swami Vivekananda Rock Memorial, the meditation hall, and the Smarak. You will then head to Kanyakumari mandir, one of the 51 Shakti Peethas.\nOther attractions that you will visit include Gandhi Mandapam, which has been built on the place where the urn containing the ashes of Mahatma Gandhi was kept before immersion for public viewing.\nYou will also see the Thiruvalluvar Statue, and then you will drive to Trivandrum.\nOn the way to \"Suchindram\", you will visit the Thanumalayan temple, known for its splendid architecture. Later, you will visit the \"Padmanabhapuram Palace,\" a sixteenth-century wooden palace where the Travancore king resided.\nIf you have time, you can visit Kovalam beach, and then you will head to Trivandrum.\nAfter arriving at Trivandrum, you will check into your hotel.\nAfter relaxing for some time, you will visit the Sri Padmanabhaswamy temple, which is dedicated to Visnu/Krishna.\nYou will then have an overnight stay at your hotel in Trivandrum.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 08: Thiruvananthapuram (Trivandrum) (Departure)",
        "description": "Savour a lip-smacking breakfast, and then you will check out of your hotel.\nYou will be transferred to Trivandrum railway station or the Airport from where you will continue your journey to your hometown.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      }
    ],
    "faqs": []
  },
  "tirupati-thanjavur-kanyakumari-madurai-tour": {
    "overview": "On the Tirupati Thanjavur Rameshwaram Kanyakumari Madurai Tour, each city welcomes you with its own charm, rich history and cultural heritage. The journey begins from Tirupati. Don't miss its popular Venkateswara Temple. According to The Times of India around 50,000 people visit this temple every day.See More\n\nAnother great destination is Thanjavur famous for its royal palaces, old temples and unique paintings. Our guests will also visit Rameshwaram, the place where Lord Rama is believed to have built a bridge to Sri Lanka.\nNext stop is Kanyakumari. If you have time, visit the glass bridge - you can clearly see ocean right below, which feels amazing. After that next stop is Madurai, known for the Meenakshi Sundareswarar Temple. Its beautiful architecture and amazing stories impress every visitor. So book your Tirupati Thanjavur Rameshwaram Kanyakumari Madurai trip to experience more.\nSee Less\n\nAnother great destination is Thanjavur famous for its royal palaces, old temples and unique paintings. Our guests will also visit Rameshwaram, the place where Lord Rama is believed to have built a bridge to Sri Lanka.\n\nNext stop is Kanyakumari. If you have time, visit the glass bridge - you can clearly see ocean right below, which feels amazing. After that next stop is Madurai, known for the Meenakshi Sundareswarar Temple. Its beautiful architecture and amazing stories impress every visitor. So book your Tirupati Thanjavur Rameshwaram Kanyakumari Madurai trip to experience more.\n\nTour Gallery\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nTour Name\nTirupati Thanjavur Kanyakumari Madurai Tour Package\n\n\nTour Duration\n9 Days / 8 Nights\n\n\nMeals\nBreakfast\n\n\nVehicle Type\nPrivate AC Car\n\n\nStarting & Ending Point\nChennai / Thiruvananthapuram\n\n\nDestination Covered\nTirupati \u279d Thanjavur \u279d Rameshwaram \u279d Kanyakumari \u279d Madurai\n\n\nPickup Time\nDepend on your Flight Timing\n\n\n Tour Benefits\nBest price & enjoyable travel guarantee",
    "highlights": [
      "Visit top spiritual sites like Tirupati Balaji, Brihadeeswara Temple, Meenakshi Temple and Ramanathaswamy Temple.",
      "Enjoy peaceful moments near Kaveri River, scenic roads between Rameshwaram and Kanyakumari, and calm beaches.",
      "Explore royal palaces, colorful markets, butterfly parks and gardens filled with South Indian culture and history.",
      "Experience the beauty of both sunrise and sunset over the ocean at Kanyakumari - a perfect end to your trip."
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "DAY 01- Chennai - Tirupati (152 km/ 3 hrs)",
        "description": "We'll start your tour by picking you up from your selected spot in Chennai, whether it's the airport or railway station. Our representative from\nMy Quick Trippers\nwill meet you and take you to\nTirupati\n. If a guide is included, he'll travel with you and provide support during the tour.\nWhen you reach Tirupati, you'll explore its sites such as-\nTirumala Hills -\nHere you'll see seven beautiful peaks - Seshadri, Neeladri, Garudadri, Anjanadri, Vrushabadri, Narayanadri, and Venkatadri. The cool air and peaceful view make you feel fresh and happy.\nVarahaswamy Temple\nSri Venkateswara Temple-\nIt is believed that Lord Vishnu stayed in this temple. You'll also notice locals make colorful Rangolis here, which look beautiful, and the whole atmosphere is amazing.\nWhen the Darshan is done, come back to Tirupati and rest at your hotel. Enjoy a comfortable night stay in Tirupati.\nNote-\nTo skip the crowd, book\n\u20b9300\nspecial Darshan tickets on the TTD website (\nhttps://tirupatibalaji.ap.gov.in/#/login\n) for the Venkateswara Temple.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 02- Tirupati - Vellore -Tiruvannamalai (210 Kms/ 4-4.5Hrs)",
        "description": "Morning after breakfast, proceed to visit\nSrinivasa Mangapuram\nand\nKanipakam.\nLater, drive to\nVellore,\nknown for its\nGolden Temple.\nOn arrival, go to the\nGolden Temple\nat\nSripuram.\nThe gold-plated temple shines beautifully in the sunlight - a great spot for photography.\nAfter the visit, proceed to\nTiruvannamalai.\nOn reaching, check in at the hotel then explore\nAnnamalaiyar Temple\n, where Lord Shiva is worshiped as\nArunachalesvara\nor\nAnnamalaiyar\n. This temple is one of the largest in India located at the base of\nAnnamalai Hill.\nReturn to the hotel. Overnight stay at\nTiruvannamalai.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 03- Tiruvannamalai - Thanjavur (Tanjore) -Tiruchirappalli (Trichy) (Approx. 296 Kms/ 6 Hrs)",
        "description": "Morning after breakfast, check out from the hotel and proceed to\nThanjavur\nfor sightseeing. Visit the famous\nBrihadeeswara Temple\n. Inside, you can see old paintings on the walls that attract every visitor.\nLater, visit\nThanjavur Palace.\nThe Kaveri River flows near the palace, and the view is lovely. It feels so calm when you sit there.\nThen travel to the\nThanjavur Art Gallery,\nwhere you can see the real history of\nTamil Nadu\nin an interesting way.\nAfter sightseeing, drive to\nTiruchirappalli\n(Trichy). On arrival, check into the hotel. Overnight stay at Trichy.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 04- Tiruchirappalli - Madurai (135 km/ 2-2.5 hrs)",
        "description": "After breakfast, check out from the hotel and proceed for sightseeing in\nTiruchirappalli.\nExplore\nSri Ranganatha Swamy Temple\nat\nSrirangam,\nwhich is also one of the largest temple spread over\n156 acres,\nwhere every corner is worth seeing.\nNext, visit\nJambukeswarar Akilandeswari Temple\n, dedicated to Lord Shiva and Goddess Parvati.\nThen, proceed to\nUcchi Pillayar Temple\n, dedicated to\nLord Ganesha\n, located on the top of\nRockfort.\nYou can see beautiful, amazing views of the entire city (don't miss the evening view if time allows).\nContinue your trip to the\nGovernment Museum\n, built within the\nRani Mangammal Mahal.\nNow, travel to the\nButterfly Park\nfilled with colorful butterflies, and later visit\nNakshatra Vanam,\na peaceful garden nearby and a perfect spot for a picnic.\nAfter sightseeing, drive to\nMadurai\n.\nOnce you reach, check into the hotel. Overnight stay in\nMadurai.\nNote-\nWear comfortable footwear as you'll walk a lot while exploring temples and forts.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 05- Madurai - Rameshwaram (173 km/ 3-4 hrs )",
        "description": "After breakfast check out of the hotel and explore the beautiful city of\nMadurai.\nVisit\nMeenakshi Sundareswarar Temple\npopular worldwide for its amazing architecture and interesting facts. As you enter, fragrance of Agarbatti (incense) and the positive atmosphere give a truly amazing feeling.\nLater, go to\nThiruparankundram Murugan Temple.\nAfter exploring the city, get ready to travel to\nRameshwaram.\nOn arrival, check into the hotel. Later, proceed to\nRamanathaswamy Temple, Agnitheertham\n( a holy bathing spot )\nand Ramjharoka Temple.\nRelax and spend the night at your hotel in\nRameshwaram.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 06- In Rameswaram",
        "description": "Start early at\n5:00 am\nwith a holy dip at\nAgni Theertham.\nNext, visit\nSphatik Lingam Darshan,\nalso known as\nMani Darshan\n. The shining crystal lingam here looks truly beautiful and the interesting thing is that it is not man-made.\nAfter that, take a holy bath in the\n22 wells\ninside the Ramanathaswamy Temple, known as\nTheerth Snanam.\nOnce you finish the holy bath and Darshan, return to the hotel for a nice breakfast.\nAfter that, go for a local sightseeing tour in\nRameswaram\nand visit places like the\nFive-faced Hanuman Temple, Ramar Patham, Kothandaramaswamy Temple, Gandamadana Parvatham\n(famous for Lord Rama's footprint),\nRama Setu, Dr. A. P. J. Abdul Kalam's House, and Dhanushkodi.\nOvernight stay at\nRameswaram.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 07- Rameswaram - Kanyakumari (312 km/ 7 hrs)",
        "description": "In the morning, you can visit the Ramanathaswamy Temple again or take a holy dip in the sea, known as\nSamudra Snanam.\nAfter that, check out of the hotel and drive to\nKanyakumari\n, the meeting point of three oceans - the Bay of Bengal, the Arabian Sea, and the Indian Ocean.\nKanyakumari\nis the only place where you can enjoy both sunrise and sunset over the sea.\nAfter reaching Kanyakumari, check into the hotel. Check into the hotel and get some rest. Overnight stay in Kanyakumari.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 08- Kanyakumari - Thiruvananthapuram (Trivandrum) (91 Kms / 2 Hours Drive)",
        "description": "Start your morning with a peaceful sea view and some fresh cool air and have breakfast.\nAfter breakfast, proceed to visit the\nSwami Vivekananda Rock Memorial.\nThe ocean view around the rock looks truly beautiful - even Prime Minister Narendra Modi also meditated here.\nExplore the\nKumari Amman Temple\n, one of the\n51\nsacred\nShakti Peethas\n. It is believed that the spine of Goddess Sati fell here, which makes this temple a very holy place.\nAfter that, travel to the\nTriveni Sangam\n, the point where the three oceans meet, and then proceed to\nGandhi Mandapam\n, the place where Gandhi's ashes were kept before being placed in the sea.\nVisit the\nThiruvalluvar Statue,\nwhich is dedicated to the well-known Tamil poet. The statue is about\n133 feet\ntall.\nOn the way to\nTrivandrum\n, go to the\nThanumalayan Temple\nat\nSuchindram\n, known for its\n22-ft Hanuman statue\nand stunning architecture (best photography spot).\nAs you reach the\nPadmanabhapuram Palace\n, you'll be surprised by its wooden work and traditional\nKerala-style\ndesign.\nIf time permits, visit\nKovalam Beach\nbefore reaching Trivandrum.\nAfter reaching\nTrivandrum\n, check into the hotel. In the evening, visit the\nSri Padmanabhaswamy Temple\n, which is dedicated to Lord Vishnu. Stay overnight in\nTrivandrum\n.\nNote-\nKeep some cash with you because small shops or temple counters might not take online payments.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 09- Thiruvananthapuram (Trivandrum) (Departure)",
        "description": "After breakfast, your\ntrip\nends with sweet memories. You'll be dropped at Trivandrum Airport or railway station for your home.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      }
    ],
    "faqs": []
  },
