  "uttar-pradesh-darshan-tour": {
    "overview": "Experience the best that Uttar Pradesh has to offer with our tour package See More\n\nthat offers the perfect combination of culture, history, and spirituality. With this package, you will get to explore the famous destinations of Uttar Pradesh, including Varanasi, Prayagraj, Ayodhya, and Sarnath. Our packages are well-curated and come with all the important amenities.\nWhether you're travelling for the first time or have visited Uttar Pradesh before, we promise to offer a once-in-a-lifetime experience. With this package, you can enjoy various amenities such as top-notch accommodations, private transportation, and a guided sightseeing tour.\nSee Less\n\nthat offers the perfect combination of culture, history, and spirituality. With this package, you will get to explore the famous destinations of Uttar Pradesh, including Varanasi, Prayagraj, Ayodhya, and Sarnath. Our packages are well-curated and come with all the important amenities.\n\nWhether you're travelling for the first time or have visited Uttar Pradesh before, we promise to offer a once-in-a-lifetime experience. With this package, you can enjoy various amenities such as top-notch accommodations, private transportation, and a guided sightseeing tour.\n\nTour Gallery\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nTour Name\nUttar Pradesh Darshan Tour\n\n\nTour Duration\n05 Days / 04 Nights\n\n\nMeals\nBreakfast\n\n\nVehicle Type\nSedan / SUV\n\n\nStarting & Ending Point\nVaranasi\n\n\nDestination Covered\nVaranasi - Prayagraj - Ayodhya - Naimisharanya \n\n\nPickup Time\nDepend on your Flight Timing \n\n\n Tour Benefits\nBest price & enjoyable travel guarantee",
    "highlights": [
      "Visit the famous attractions of Varanasi.",
      "Explore the famous attractions of Sarnath.",
      "Sightseeing tour of Prayagraj.",
      "Take a dip in the Saryu River.",
      "Pay homage to Lord Rama at Ram Janmabhoomi.",
      "See More"
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1: Arrive at Varanasi",
        "description": "Your Uttar Pradesh Darshan tour will start as you arrive at Varanasi and meet our courteous representative, who will brief you about the rest of the tour and ensure you have a smooth Yatra.\nYou will check in at your pre-reserved hotel in Varanasi and freshen up. After some time, you\u2019ll go on a sightseeing tour and\nVisit the famous attractions, including\nVishwanath temple, Annapurna Temple, Kashi Vishalakhi, Manas Mandir, Durga Mandir, Birla Mandir, and Sankat Mochan Mandir.\nLater, you will embark on a picturesque drive to\nSarnath\n- the site where\nGautam Buddha\ndelivered his first sermon.\nAfter reaching\nSarnath,\nyou will visit the famous attractions such as the\nBuddha temples,\nChaukhandi Stupa, the Dhamek Stupa,\nand the\narcheological museum.\nIn the evening, you will enjoy a boat cruise on the river Ganga.\nYou will also attend the Ganga Aarti ceremony. You will have an overnight stay in your Varanasi hotel.\nVishwanath Temple\nDarshan Timing: 04:00 AM to 11:00 AM\nEvening/Noon Slots: 12:00 PM to 07:00 PM and 08:30 PM to 09:00 PM\nSapta Rishi Aarti: 07:00 PM to 08:30 PM\nPlease Note:\nSugam Darshan, Pooja, and Aarti can be booked online\nDuring the Sawan month, the Kanwar Yatra may impact the tour, which can cause route diversion or heavy traffic.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 2: Varanasi - Vindhyachal \u2013 Prayagraj (130 km/3hrs)",
        "description": "You will relish a delicious breakfast in the morning, and then you\u2019ll head out on a scenic drive to\nPrayagraj.\nOn the way, you will visit\nSitamarhi\n, which is believed to be the place where Mata Sita went inside the earth.\nHave a Darshan of Mata Sita at\nJanki Temple\n, and then you will head out on a drive to Prayagraj.\nNext, go to\nPrayagraj\n, and visit\nTriveni Sangam\n, where the Ganga, Yamuna, and Saraswati rivers meet. Take a holy dip and enjoy a boat ride.\nThen travel to\nBade Hanuman Mandir.\nPeople believe that Hanuman Ji stopped here to rest after burning Lanka.\nVisit the\nAkshayavat Temple\nand Tree at\nPatalpuri Temple\nin\nPrayagraj Fort\n, believed to be the spot where Ram, Lakshman, and Sita rested. People pray here to wash away sins.\nNow proceed to\nPrayagraj Fort\n, also called\nAllahabad Fort\nbuilt by Akbar in 1583 beside the Yamuna River near where it joins the Ganga (Great photo spot).\nStop at\nAlopi Devi Temple\n, a well-known holy Shaktipeeth.\nOptional:\nif time allows, visit\nLalita Devi Temple, Shri Nagvasuki Temple\nwhere people pray for blessings. Then, explore ,\nAnand Bhavan,\nthe Nehru family\u2019s home.\nAfter the sightseeing tour, you will have an overnight stay in your hotel.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 3: Prayagraj - Ayodhya (4 hr/167 km)",
        "description": "After a delicious breakfast, you will head out on a drive to Ayodhya.\nAfter arriving at Ayodhya, you will visit\nRama Janmabhumi\n, which is considered to be the birthplace of lord Rama.\nLater, you will visit\nDasharath Bhavan, Kanak Bhavan, and Hanuman Garhi.\nIn the evening, you will visit the\nSaryu River.\nBy taking a dip in this river, you can get rid of the sins you have committed in your past and present life.\nYou will have an overnight stay in your pre-reserved hotel.\nHanuman Garhi\nDarshan Timing\n05:30 am to 10:00 pm\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 4: Ayodhya - Lucknow (4 hrs/140 km)",
        "description": "Have a yummy breakfast in the morning, and then you will drive to\nLucknow.\nYou will visit the\nGomti river front, Bada Imambara (Bhulbhulliya) Ambedkar Park, and Hazratganj market.\nIn the evening, you will return to your hotel and have an overnight stay.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 5: Lucknow - Naimisharanya (2hr/93 km) - Lucknow",
        "description": "Post breakfast, you will head out on a drive to\nNaimisharanya.\nThe main attraction of this place is the\nNaimisaranya Temple\n, a sacred destination for Hindus.\nYou will then visit other popular attractions, including\nChakra Teerth, Vyas Gaddi, Dadhichi Kund, Swayambhu Manu, Suth Gaddi, Pandav Kila, Satrupa, and Hanuman Gaddi.\nLater, you will head back to\nLucknow.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      }
    ],
    "faqs": []
  },
