  "uttar-pradesh-tour": {
    "overview": "Are you planning a trip where you can attain the spiritual, adventurous, and heritage-rich experience? If yes, then browse our beautifully designed Best of Uttar Pradesh Tour Package. This 12 nights and 13 days long tour let you explore each and every beauty of the state and helps you enjoy the wonders of the place to the utmost level.\n\nBest of Uttar Pradesh Tour Itinerary Package\n\n\nDay 1 :Delhi \u2013 Varanasi\n\n\nUpon arrival in Delhi, our tour representative will greet you and then escort you to the airport to catch the flight to Varanasi. Upon your arrival at the Varanasi Airport, the representative will pick you and assist you in transferring to the pre-listed hotels. Later in the afternoon, get ready and come out of the hotel to explore some of the most important and famous temples in Varanasi. Today you will be visiting the popular temples like Tulsi Birla Manas Temple, Mother India Temple, Hanuman Temple, Sankat Mochan Temple, and also the newly built Vishwanath Temple. Also, participate in the grand evening Ganga Aarti ceremony at the popular Dashashwamedh Ghat. This is all for today so return to the hotel for dinner and then overnight stay.\n\n\n\n\nDay 2 :Varanasi\n\n\nWake up little early today and get ready for enjoying the boat ride in the holy River the Ganges and then proceed towards exploring all the bathing Ghats. Walk through the narrow lanes of the city and also perform the special puja rituals organized at the ghats. Varanasi Ghats are pretty popular for organizing Pind Daan performed to pay respect to your forefathers. After performing the puja rituals return to the hotel for the morning meal. After enjoying the scrumptious breakfast, proceed towards Sarnath. After the completion of a fun-filled day excursion, return to the hotel for the delectable night meal which will then be followed by a relaxing overnight stay.\n\n\n\n\nDay 3 :Varanasi \u2013 Vindhyachal \u2013 Prayagraj\n\n\nPost breakfast, you will drive towards Prayagraj and on the way to Prayagraj, make a halt at Vindhyachal. After reaching the destination, take a holy dip into the Sangam and explore those places popular for religious and historical significance. After exploring the places, you will be transferred to the pre-booked hotel in Prayagraj for a relaxing overnight stay.\n\n\n\n\nDay 4 :Prayagraj \u2013 Chitrakoot \u2013 Prayagraj\n\n\nAfter enjoying the breakfast, set out of the hotel and move towards the next destination of the trip, Chitrakoot. On reaching Chitrakoot, explore the popular places of the city and then drive back to Prayagraj from where you will depart for Lucknow. By the time you reach Lucknow, it will be dark so you will be transferred to the hotel for dinner and then overnight stay.\n\n\n\n\nDay 5 :Lucknow\n\n\nAfter coming out of the hotel, set out of the hotel for enjoying the sightseeing tour in new as well as ancient Varanasi. Explore Chhota Imambara, Bada Imambara, Constantia House, Residency, Rumi Darwaza, Hazrat Ganj, Ambedkar Park, and Chattar Manzil. Later completing the day exploration, return to the hotel for the scrumptious night meal which is then followed by an overnight stay.\n\n\n\n\nDay 6 :Lucknow \u2013 Dewa Sharif \u2013 Ayodhya \u2013 Lucknow\n\n\nAfter savoring yourself with the hearty breakfast, drive towards Ayodhya. On the way to Ayodhya, visit Dewa Sharif which represents the beautiful symbiosis of love and brotherhood. After this, continue driving towards Ayodhya and after reaching the religious destination, head towards Sri Ram Janm Bhoomi \u2013 where the great Hindu Lord Rama took birth. Also, visit the famous Sarayu ghats and Hanuman Garhi. After visiting the place, drive back to Lucknow in the evening for dinner and overnight halt in the hotel.\n\n\n\n\nDay 7 :Lucknow \u2013 Naimisharanya \u2013 Dudhwa National Park\n\n\nPost enjoying the hearty breakfast at the hotel in Lucknow, drive towards Naimisharanya which is the next destination of your journey. After paying homage at the shrines of Naimisharanya, hit the road towards Dudhwa National Park. This huge national park is home to exotic species of animals including tigers, crocodiles, wild elephants, rhinos, and approx.. 450 species of birds. After exploring this gorgeous national park, drive towards the hotel to enjoy the night meal followed by an overnight stay.\n\n\n\n\nDay 8 :Dudhwa National Park\n\n\nStart your little morning as you will be exploring the huge Dudhwa National Park and enjoy the jungle elephant ride. Spot various wildlife species and also track the various species of tigers here and then drive back to the guest house for enjoying the morning and then the afternoon meal. Also, enjoy walking along with the atmosphere or bird watch and then drive back to the jungle and witness the rhinos from the giant watchtower. Return to the guest house for dinner and a relaxing overnight halt.\n\n\n\n\nDay 9 :Katarniaghat Wildlife Sanctuary\n\n\nAfter enjoying the breakfast, get ready to complete a 2 hrs. driving distance and almost 110 kilometers. Upon arrival at this gigantic wildlife sanctuary, enjoy the boat ride and spot the Gangetic Dolphin, birds, Gharials, and crocodiles. After exploring the beauty of this wildlife sanctuary, drive towards your pre-booked hotel and stay there for the whole night.\n\n\n\n\nDay 10 :Katarniaghat Wildlife Sanctuary \u2013 Lucknow\n\n\nPost enjoying the mouth-watering morning meal, drive towards Lucknow. You will be reaching there by afternoon and on reaching there you will be transferred to the pre-booked hotel. Check-into the hotel, enjoy the lunch and then relax for a few hours. Later in the evening, go out for shopping in Aminabad for Chicken market. After completing your shopping, return to the hotel for dinner followed by a relaxing overnight stay.\n\n\n\n\nDay 11 :Lucknow \u2013 Agra\n\n\nAfter savoring yourself with the scrumptious morning meal, come out of the hotel and drive towards Agra. On reaching there, check into the pre-booked hotel and stay there for an overnight stay.\n\n\n\n\nDay 12 :Agra\n\n\nAfter completing your breakfast you will be taken for the complete sightseeing trip. Today you will be exploring Taj Mahal one of the seven wonders of the world and also the popular Agra Fort. Later in the afternoon, drive towards Fatehpur Sikri to explore the popular Buland Darwaza and then after completing the fun-filled day return to the hotel for a night halt.\n\n\n\n\nDay 13 :Agra \u2013 Mathura \u2013 Vrindavan \u2013 Delhi\n\n\nOn the final day of your journey, drive towards Mathura and Vrindavan and visit the popular Braj Bhoomi. After exploring the popular leftover destinations of the trip, head towards Delhi and spend your overnight stay in Delhi or you can also opt to fly back towards your home. This is how your heritage and adventure tour of Uttar Pradesh ends here with plenty of unforgettable memories.",
    "highlights": [
      "The Varanasi tour start with exploring the Tulsi Birwa Manas Temple, Mother India Temple, Hanuman Temple, Sankat Mochan Temple, and Vishwanath Temple",
      "Be in sync with river Ganges with the grand evening Ganga Aarti ceremony at the popular Dashashwamedh Ghat",
      "Early morning boat ride on river Ganga and a holy dip will fulfill your soul for the next whole day",
      "At Prayagraj enjoy the holy dip into the Sangam and explore those places popular for religious and historical significance",
      "After visiting the shrines of Naimisharanya, hit the road towards Dudhwa National Park",
      "At Katarniaghat Wildlife Sanctuary enjoy the boat ride and spot the Gangetic Dolphin, Birds, Gharials, and crocodiles",
      "At Vrindavan be in sync with the divine, the birth place of Lord Krishna"
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1 :Delhi \u2013 Varanasi",
