  "uttarakhand-bird-watching-tour": {
    "overview": "The Valley of flowers and the Devbhoomi not only gives the travelers the extreme divine feeling but the beautiful greenery and forests have other exciting activities hidden in it. One of the most marvelous tourist activities is the Uttarakhand bird watching, and based on that this tour package is designed. Bird watchers are very keen and they visit the Devbhoomi all around the globe during the peak season. This 5 Days / 4 Nights tour package will cover all the necessary bird-watching activities adding peace and serenity for the travelers.\n\nUttarakhand Bird Watching Tour Itinerary Package\n\n\nDay 1 :Delhi to Corbett National Park (270 Kms)\n\n\nThe My Quick Trippers representative will receive you at Delhi airport/ railway station and drive you to Corbett National Park. In the final two hours, you will stop for bird watching activity and enjoy the wildlife of this region. Arrive at the resort and check-in after which you can rest and explore the forest in the evening time. Spend the night at the hotel.\n\n\n\n\nDay 2 :At Corbett National Park\n\n\nWill start with breakfast after which you will be taken for a walk on the side of the Ramganga River to view the water birds including the mergansers, waders and river lapwings among other birds. Next, you can opt for an elephant ride to get closer to the birds of the jungle. It is more like a \u2018watchtower\u2019 giving you the utmost possibility of clear bird view. You can see birds like Blue Winged Minla, Lammergeier, White-rumped Shama and Puff-Throated Babbler along with other beasts of the jungle. Return to the hotel for night stay.\n\n\n\n\nDay 3 :Corbett National Park to Pangot (50 Kms)\n\n\nEarly morning on day 3 leave Corbett to reach Pangot in Nainital. It is 2-3 hours journey and as you reach this village on the north-western side of Nainital, you will check into a wildlife cottage. Start with the bird watching activity which will include viewing the Himalayan species of birds like the Himalayan Griffon, Rufous-Bellied Woodpecker, Blue-winged Minla, Lammergeier, Slaty \u2013 Backed and Spotted Fork Tail. Take some rest and then stroll in the evening along the forest line. Spend the night in the Pangot cottage.\n\n\n\n\nDay 4 :Pangot to Sat Tal (45 Kms)\n\n\nOn the morning of day 5, start with breakfast and then start for Sat Tal. On way spot all the bird species of this amazing region. The drive will take you to the Cheena Peak Range through Kilbury and Snow View Point. After reaching Sat Tal check into the hotel booked for you. Bird watching activity can take place along the Sat Tal region. Spend the night at the hotel.\n\n\n\n\nDay 5 :Sat Tal to Nainital\n\n\nOn the final day start with early breakfast and move forward to Nainital. On the way you can stop for bird watching activity and when you reach Nainital go for shopping at local bazaar. Leave Nainital after lunch and the My Quick Trippers representative will drop you at Delhi airport/ railway station to head homewards with \u2018birds\u2019 on your mind.",
    "highlights": [
      "Visiting all the bird-watching spots in the valley",
      "Exciting travel through the flora and fauna",
      "Enjoying the delicious local food",
      "Best traveling vehicles offered"
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1 :Delhi to Corbett National Park (270 Kms)",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 2 :At Corbett National Park",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 3 :Corbett National Park to Pangot (50 Kms)",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 4 :Pangot to Sat Tal (45 Kms)",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 5 :Sat Tal to Nainital",
        "description": ""
      }
    ],
    "faqs": []
  },
  "uttarakhand-delights-tour": {
    "overview": "Uttarakhand is the most divine place on earth with the innumerable temples and divine shrines, making it the best spot for pilgrimage. Also it is a natural paradise giving the travelers around the globe a reason to visit it once in a lifetime. This 8 days / 7 nights tour will cover all the best places with immense flora and fauna, with the visit to the wildlife of the region with Jim Corbett National park tour.\n\nUttarakhand Delights Tour Itinerary Package\n\n\nDay 1 :Arrive Delhi \u2013 Nainital (330 kms / 9 hrs)\n\n\nWelcome to New Delhi, You are greeted on arrival at Delhi Airport / Railway station by My Quick Trippers representative and Proceed on a picturesque drive to the charming hill station of Nainital. On arrival, check into your hotel. The evening is at leisure, Night stay at Hotel.\n\n\n\n\nDay 2 :In Nainital\n\n\nThis morning, enjoy an excursion to the lakes which includes Sat Tal, a group of seven lakes including the famous jade green Garud Lake, the bigger Bhimtal and Naukuchiatal. Rest of the evening, enjoy a walk on the Mall road and shop for the famous wax candles or you can enjoy a boat ride on Naini Lake (on direct payment basis), Night stay at Hotel.\n\n\n\n\nDay 3 :In Nainital\n\n\nToday, you will proceed on a local tour of Nainital visiting the Naina Devi Temple and Hanuman Garhi. Rest of the day is free to enjoy a boat ride on the Naini Lake (boats can be hired directly) or take the ropeway to enjoy the best view of snow-capped peaks (on direct payment basis). Or can enjoy pony ride up to Naina peak (provides a bird\u2019s eye view of Nainital and snow-clad peak of mighty Himalaya), Night stay at Hotel.\n\n\n\n\nDay 4 :Nainital \u2013 Ranikhet (80 kms / 3 hrs)\n\n\nThis morning, you will drive to the popular hill station Ranikhet. On arrival, check into your hotel. In the afternoon, explore the temples and the wonderful sights in Ranikhet like as 9-hole golf course at Upat, a Government Fruit Garden and Research Station at Chaubatia and the fascinating temples in Dwarahat, Night stay at Hotel.\n\n\n\n\nDay 5 :Ranikhet \u2013 Corbett (125 kms / 4 hrs)\n\n\nToday your drive continues to the wild tropical jungles to Corbett. On arrival, check into your hotel. In afternoon enjoy a jeep safari to spot a variety of wildlife. (The park is open from November to June) Night stay at Hotel.\n\n\n\n\nDay 6 :Corbett \u2013 Mussoorie (287 kms/ 7 hrs)\n\n\nThis morning you will drive to the picturesque town of Mussoorie, spread along a horseshoe-shaped ridge overlooking the Doon Valley. On arrival, you will check into your hotel. The evening is at leisure, Night stay at Hotel.\n\n\n\n\nDay 7 :In Mussoorie\n\n\nAfter breakfast, go on a full-day sightseeing tour of Mussoorie. Visit Gun Hill, Kempty Fall (a popular picnic spot) and stroll on the Mall Road in the evening. overnight stay in the hotel. (You can also enjoy the thrills of ropeway up to Gun Hill).\n\n\n\n\nDay 8 :Mussoorie \u2013 Delhi (270 kms / 7 hrs)\n\n\nReturn home with sweet memories.",
    "highlights": [
      "Well planned morning excursions",
      "Deluxe and comfortable vehicles provided for travel",
      "Covering the best places namely Nainital, Ranikhet, Jim Corbett and Mussoorie",
      "Shopping from the local markets",
      "Enjoying the local cuisine"
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1 :Arrive Delhi \u2013 Nainital (330 kms / 9 hrs)",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 2 :In Nainital",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 3 :In Nainital",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 4 :Nainital \u2013 Ranikhet (80 kms / 3 hrs)",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
