  "vaishno-devi-tour": {
    "overview": "One of the most revered pilgrimage sites in India, the Vaishno Devi Temple nestles in the serene Trikuta Hills of Jammu and Kashmir. Dedicated to Goddess Vaishno Devi\u2014an incarnation of Durga\u2014this sacred shrine draws millions of devotees yearly seeking divine blessings. The pilgrimage journey blends devotion, natural beauty, and spiritual fulfilment.\n\nOur Vaishno Devi tour package from Delhi perfectly suit both first-time pilgrims and seasoned travellers. My Quick Trippers offers a specialised, budget-friendly package starting from Delhi\u2014complete with sightseeing, meals, and accommodation. This hassle-free experience maximises your sacred journey while saving time and money.\n\nOur Vaishno Devi tour package from Delhi perfectly suit both first-time pilgrims and seasoned travellers. My Quick Trippers offers a specialised, budget-friendly package starting from Delhi\u2014complete with sightseeing, meals, and accommodation. This hassle-free experience maximises your sacred journey while saving time and money.\n\nVaishno Devi Yatra Tour Itinerary Package\n\n\nDay 1 :Arrive Delhi On to Jammu\n\n\nFirst arrive in Delhi, where our My Quick Trippers Executive will welcome you to our Vaishno Devi Yatra.\nOur travel executive will accompany you to Delhi's famous locations and narrate every important detail about the same.\n\nRed Fort\nJama Masjid\nIndia Gate\nChandni Chowk (optional food tour)\nLotus Temple\n\nLater in the evening, you will leave for Jammu through your preferred means of transport.\n(Flight: 1.5 hours/train: overnight journey).\n\n\n\n\nDay 2 :Jammu to Katra (48 Kilometers)\n\n\nUpon your arrival in Jammu, you will be served delicious local cuisine, and then you will be ready for local sightseeing\n\nBahu Fort-an ancient fort with the temple of Goddess Kali\nMubarak Mandi Mahal, a historic royal palace\nAmar Mahal, a museum with art collections\nPanch Peer -sacred Sufi shrine\nRaghunath Temple-the largest temple complex in North India\nJammu Museum - History and artefacts\n\nAfter local sightseeing, you will be transferred to the Katra hotel (48 km, coverable in 1.5 hours), where you will rest for the day and thus end day 2 of your Vaishno Devi Yatra.\n\n\n\n\nDay 3 :Katra to Mata Vaishno Devi and Back to Katra\n\n\nThe next day, you will be served a piping hot breakfast, and thus your day starts for the 13 km trek and Darshan. Remember to collect the Yatra slip near the Katra bus stop before the Yatra. (There are also options for a Palki (palanquin), a horse ride, and ponies available all along the route.)\nEn route to your trek, you will have many places to see, like\n\nArdhkuwari Cave (6 km)-where Mata meditated for 9 months\nSanjichhat (9.5 km)-resting point with tea/snack stalls\nBhawan, the final destination for Darshan\n\nAfter Darshan, descend back to your hotel and relax for the day, thus marking the end of day 3 of your Yatra.\n\n\n\n\nDay 4 :Jammu to Delhi\n\n\nHave breakfast and depart for Jammu (48 km in 1.5 hours) and later board your preferred mode of transport for your return to your destination.\nIf you have extra time, you may visit these nearby locations on your own -\n\nBagh-e-Bahu Park\nRailway station market (souvenirs)\nRaghunath Bazaar (religious items)",
    "highlights": [
      "Delhi sightseeing - Red Fort, Jama Masjid, India Gate, Chandni Chowk (optional food tour), and Lotus Temple.",
      "Jammu sightseeing: Mubarak Mandi palace, Amar Mahal, Bahu Fort, and Raghunath Temple.",
      "Mata Vaishno Devi Darshan and En route places like Ardhkuwari cave, Bhawan (shrine cave with Mahakali, Mahalakshmi, and Maha Saraswati); Tulip viewpoint (seasonal); and Holy Charan Paduka (footprint of Mata).",
      "Guided tour along with stays with included breakfast and dinner"
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1 :Arrive Delhi On to Jammu",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 2 :Jammu to Katra (48 Kilometers)",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 3 :Katra to Mata Vaishno Devi and Back to Katra",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 4 :Jammu to Delhi",
        "description": ""
      }
    ],
    "faqs": []
  },
