  "valley-of-flowers-tour": {
    "overview": "Valley of flowers is a situated in Bhyundar Valley at an elevation of 3250 Mts above sea level. The valley of flowers was declared as the National Park of India in the year 1982 and it is now a world heritage site.\n\nThe virgin beauty of this mystical valley has always lured botanists, nature lovers and adventure lovers. Many a legend is associated with this vibrant and eye-catching Valley and is often in the epics of the Ramayana and Mahabharata. Best time to visit valley of flowers from mid-July to mid-August because the bloom starts immediately after the melting of snow.\nYou can reach the valley of flowers from Haridwar to Joshimath then Govindghat and trek to Ghangaria. It is the last place where you can find hotels, lodges, etc. Govindghat is the point from where the trek is started. Ghangaria is situated at a height of 10,500 feet. The charming beauty of the place is increased more with the long deodar trees. The cold is enough. Hemkund is 06 Km on the left bridle path from Ghangaria. Hemkund is surrounding the place are 07 snow-clad peaks of lofty mountains. The beautiful lake of clear and sweet water is full of lotus flowers in the center and the sweet blooming variety of grassy fields all around the lake, despite an unrivaled sublime beauty of magnificent grandeur.\n\nThe virgin beauty of this mystical valley has always lured botanists, nature lovers and adventure lovers. Many a legend is associated with this vibrant and eye-catching Valley and is often in the epics of the Ramayana and Mahabharata. Best time to visit valley of flowers from mid-July to mid-August because the bloom starts immediately after the melting of snow.",
    "highlights": [
      "Exciting trekking at Govind Ghat",
      "Be at the mesmerizing Valley Of Flowers at Ghangaria",
      "Hemkund Sahib Visit",
      "City tour at Joshimath"
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1 :Haridwar \u2013 Joshimath",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 2 :Joshimath \u2013 Govindghat \u2013 Ghangaria/14 Km Trek",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 3 :Ghangaria \u2013 Valley of Flower/05 Km Trek",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 4 :Ghangaria \u2013 Hemkund Sahib/06 Km Trek",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 5 :Ghangaria \u2013 Joshimath",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 6 :Joshimath \u2013 Haridwar",
        "description": ""
      }
    ],
    "faqs": []
  },
  "varanasi-allahabad-ayodhya-naimisharanya-tour": {
    "overview": "Ready to explore a state full of rich history and colorful culture? The Varanasi Prayagraj Ayodhya Naimisharanya Tour lets you experience it all. See More\n\nStart with Varanasi, India\u2019s oldest city, with over 80 Ghats that attract many tourists. Besides temples and Ghats not many people know that this holy place is also used for TV shoots because of its beautiful surroundings. Don\u2019t miss a boat ride on the Ganga for unforgettable memories.\nNow the journey continues to Prayagraj, where you will visit the famous Prayagraj Fort near the Yamuna River, built by Mughal King Akbar. One interesting thing is the underground Patalpuri Temple in the fort, which few people can visit. Next, the tour moves to Ayodhya, the birthplace of Lord Rama. The special thing about Ram Ji\u2019s temple is that, even without cement or iron, it is strong. Every person gets inner peace here.\nFinally, the journey ends in Lucknow, the city of Nawabs. Visit the Bada Imambara famous for its beautiful architecture and the thrilling Bhool Bhulaiyaa maze inside. There is a lot to explore; just plan your Varanasi Prayagraj Ayodhya Naimisharanya trip for a better experience.\nSee Less\n\nStart with Varanasi, India\u2019s oldest city, with over 80 Ghats that attract many tourists. Besides temples and Ghats not many people know that this holy place is also used for TV shoots because of its beautiful surroundings. Don\u2019t miss a boat ride on the Ganga for unforgettable memories.\n\nNow the journey continues to Prayagraj, where you will visit the famous Prayagraj Fort near the Yamuna River, built by Mughal King Akbar. One interesting thing is the underground Patalpuri Temple in the fort, which few people can visit. Next, the tour moves to Ayodhya, the birthplace of Lord Rama. The special thing about Ram Ji\u2019s temple is that, even without cement or iron, it is strong. Every person gets inner peace here.",
    "highlights": [
      "Explore Varanasi\u2019s ancient Ghats, temples and enjoy peaceful boat ride on the sacred Ganga River.",
      "Explore Prayagraj\u2019s Prayagraj Fort, Vindhyachal Devi Temple and other special spots.",
      "Experience Ayodhya\u2019s Ram Janmabhoomi, Hanuman Garhi, Kanak Bhavan and holy Saryu River rituals.",
      "In Lucknow, enjoy Bara Imambara, Ambedkar Park and Hazratganj Market and later explore Vishnu temples of Naimisharanya.",
      "See More"
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1: Arrival Varanasi",
        "description": "Start your\nTravel Plan\nwith a convenient pick-up from your selected location in Varanasi, either airport or railway station, where our\nMy Quick Trippers\nteam will receive you and take you comfortably to your hotel. If you choose a guide, they will join the driver to help you all day.\nAfter check-in, proceed for sightseeing in Varanasi-\nDurga Mandir\nMana Temple\nSankat Mochan Mandir\nBirla Mandir\nIn the evening, attend the famous\nGanga Aarti\nat the Ghats, or enjoy it from a boat for a spiritual experience. You will stay overnight at a hotel in Varanasi.\nNote-\nTiming of Ganga Aarti can change with the season.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 2: Varanasi - Morning Boat Ride, Sarnath Visit (10 km/31 min), and Temple Tour",
        "description": "Enjoy a calm\nmorning boat ride\non the sacred Ganges Ghats as the sun rises. You may also take a bath at your hotel or in the holy\nGanga River.\nNext, visit\nAnnapurna Mandir, Vishalakshi Mandir, Vishwanath Temple,\none of the 12 Jyotirlingas. It\u2019s also a wonderful place for taking memorable photos.\nThen go to\nSarnath,\nthe sacred place where Lord Buddha gave his first teaching.\nLater, visit other famous sites in Sarnath such as the\nBuddhist temples, Dhamek Stupa, Chaukhandi Stupa\nand the\narcheological museum.\nIn the evening enjoy some free time to shop in\nVaranasi\non your own (optional).\nRelax and stay overnight at the hotel.\nNote-\nPooja, Aarti, and Sugam Darshan can be booked online only.\nWeblink:\nhttps://shrikashivishwanath.org\nNote:\nIn the month of Sawan, the Kanwar Yatra may cause heavy traffic.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 3: Varanasi - Vindhyachal - Prayagraj (155 km/ 3 hrs)",
        "description": "Have breakfast and then continue your journey to\nPrayagraj.\nEnroute visit\nVindhyachal Devi\nfor a Darshan at Shaktipeeth. Later visit\nSitamarhi\n, the temple where Mother Sita went into the earth.\nNext, go to\nPrayagraj,\nand visit\nTriveni Sangam\n, where the Ganga, Yamuna, and Saraswati rivers meet. Take a holy dip and enjoy a boat ride.\nThen travel to\nBade Hanuman Mandir\n. People believe that Hanuman Ji stopped here to rest after burning Lanka.\nVisit the\nAkshayavat Temple\nand Tree at\nPatalpuri Temple\nin\nPrayagraj Fort,\nbelieved to be the spot where Ram, Lakshman, and Sita rested. People pray here to wash away sins.\nNow proceed to\nPrayagraj Fort\n, also called\nAllahabad Fort\nbuilt by Akbar in 1583 beside the Yamuna River near where it joins the Ganga (Great photo spot).\nStop at\nAlopi Devi Temple\n, a well-known holy Shaktipeeth.\nOptional:\nIf time allows, visit\nLalita Devi Temple, Shri Nagvasuki Temple\nwhere people pray for blessings. Then, explore\nAnand Bhavan,\nthe Nehru family\u2019s home.\nSpend the night at your hotel in Prayagraj and take some rest.\nNote-\nTimings of Vindhyachal Temple 5\u201310PM, Prayagraj Fort 9AM\u20136PM, Museum 10AM\u20135PM, Anand & Swaraj Bhawan 9:30\u20135 PM.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 4: Prayagraj  - Ayodhya (166 km/ Approx. 4 hr 20 minutes)",
        "description": "After breakfast, drive to\nAyodhya\nand visit\nRam Janmabhoomi\nto light Diyas, join rituals and feel the spiritual peace there.\nLater, explore\nHanuman Garhi, Dasharath Bhavan\n(Lord Rama\u2019s father palace) and\nKanak Bhavan\n(temple dedicated to Sita and Rama).\nVisit the\nSaryu River\nin the evening, where bathing is believed to remove all sins. If time allows, also enjoy boating (optional).\nReturn to the hotel for overnight stay in Ayodhya.\nNote-\nHanuman Garhi Temple is open from 5AM to 11PM.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 5: Ayodhya - Lucknow (135 km/3 hrs)",
        "description": "After breakfast start your journey to Lucknow.\nVisit\nBara Imambara (Bhool Bhulaiyaa)\nand explore it\u2019s fascinating maze. Don't forget to take photos of this beautiful spot.\nNext visit\nAmbedkar Park\nand then proceed to the\nGomti Riverfront.\nLater, explore\nHazratganj Market\nfor shopping and local experiences.\nReach the hotel, check in and spend the night in\nLucknow.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 6: Lucknow - Naimisharanya - Lucknow (180 km/ 3 to 4 hours)",
        "description": "Drive to\nNaimisharanya\nafter breakfast, a sacred Lord Vishnu temple.\nStart your tour to the\nLord Vishnu Temple\nand continue sightseeing in\nNaimisharanya\n, including\nChakra Teerth, Dadhichi Kund, Vyas Gaddi, Sut Gaddi, Swayambhu Manu, Satrupa, Hanuman Gaddi\nand\nPandav Kila.\nAfter sightseeing, return to Lucknow and then proceed the airport or railway station for your next journey.\nThe spiritual journey ends here. You will carry beautiful memories of Naimisharanya, and this\nUP tour package\nwill be truly unforgettable.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      }
    ],
    "faqs": []
  },
