  "varanasi-bodhgaya-chitrakoot-trip": {
    "overview": "India is known for being the spiritual destination of the world with being home to some of the most religious destinations. The Varanasi and Bodhgaya with Chitrakoot Holiday Package will evoke extreme spiritualism in the visitor\u2019s heart and mind. For 7 Days and 6 Nights, you will be made to experience the rich plethora of vibrant and age-old culture of this pious and one of the oldest living towns in the world.\n\nVaranasi Bodhgaya Chitrakoot Tour Itinerary\n\n\nDay 1 :Arrival in Varanasi\n\n\nYou will be welcomed into this holy land by our tour representative who will guide and transfer you to your allotted hotel here. After freshening up you will be taken for visit to some of the most highly revered temples here, starting with Kashi Vishwanath Temple (golden temple) which is one of the most popular shrines of Lord Shiva since it is also home to one out of the 12 Jyotirlingas in India. Later you will be taken to Durga Mandir, a bright red temple which was constructed in 18th-century and dedicated to Maa Durga. Finally, you will be taken to Tulsi Manas Mandir, the place where the historical Hindu epic Ramcharitmanas was written by Goswami Tulsidas. During sunset you will be taken for the evening Ganga Aarti on the Dashashwamedh Ghat which is not only beautiful to look at but it also works in spiritually uplifting your soul.\nFinally you will head on towards your hotel for the night.\n\n\n\n\nDay 2 :Varanasi \u2013 Bodhgaya\n\n\nYour morning will commence by witnessing a glorious sunrise on a boat ride on the holy River Ganga. You will then be taken to Bodhgaya, which will be a 5 hours road journey. Upon arriving at Bodhgaya you will be duly checked in to your hotel after which you will be made to visit the famous site for Buddhist pilgrimage tourism and one of the cardinal points in Varanasi, Mahabodhi temple \u2013 which houses a descendant of the Bodhi tree under which Buddha had attained his enlightenment. After spending some time here you will be taken back to your hotel for staying the night.\n\n\n\n\nDay 3 :Bodhgaya to Varanasi\n\n\nEarly in the morning, you will be made to proceed towards the city of Gaya which is located at a distance of 5 hours from the main town of Bodhgaya. Here you will be made to visit the temple which houses the footprints of Lord Vishnu himself \u2013 Vishnupad temple.\nYour journey towards Varanasi will then commence which will take 5 hours and upon your arrival there you will be transferred to your allotted hotel here for spending the night.\nYour evening will be free for you to explore the neighboring market places and shop for local souvenirs like, Banarasi silk, wooden toys, Gulabi Meenakari, Rudraksh mala and much more. you can also gorge on some locally prepared delicacies like, Chena Dahi Vada, Kachori Sabzi, Malaiyyo, Choor Matar and so much more.\n\n\n\n\nDay 4 :Varanasi \u2013 Vindhyachal \u2013 Prayagraj\n\n\nEarly morning after breakfast you will be transferred to Prayagraj while stopping en route at Vindhyachal where you will be made to visit Maa Vindhyavasini Mandir which is dedicated to goddess Durga.\nYou will then head on towards Prayagraj which will be a 2 hour journey, where upon arrival you will be checked into your hotel and later proceed towards the famous confluence of the three rivers Ganga, Yamuna and Saraswati \u2013 Triveni Sangam. You will be made to take a holy dip at this highly sacred point and offer your Pooja rituals. You will also be made to visit Prayagraj fort from where you will be able to view the ravishing setting sun and browse through the Prayagraj museum filled with ancient weaponry and other interesting artifacts.\nBefore heading back to your hotel you will be taken to Swaraj Bhawan or popularly also known as Anand Bhawan will be your next stop which is a large mansion formerly owned by Motilal Nehru and had served as the Nehru family\u2019s residence.\n\n\n\n\nDay 5 :Prayagraj \u2013 Ayodhya \u2013 Lucknow\n\n\nEarly in the morning, you will be taken to the birthplace of Lord Rama \u2013 Ayodhya. Upon your arrival here and after getting you checked in you will be taken for a brief sightseeing tour of the city kick starting with, Hanuman Garhi Temple dedicated to Lord Hanuman where the custom remains that before visiting Lord Rama\u2019s temple you will have to visit Lord Hanuman temple first.\nYou will then be taken to Dashrath Bhawan \u2013 which is located at the center of the town and is known for being the palace of Dashrath in the initial years and Lord Rama along with his siblings is said to have spent his childhood and youth here.\nFinally, you will be made to proceed towards Lucknow which is a 2.5 hours long road journey. You will be spending the night here in your allotted hotel.\n\n\n\n\nDay 6 :Lucknow \u2013 Naimisharanya \u2013 Lucknow\n\n\nAfter breakfast, you will be driven to Naimisharanya or popularly known as Neemsar which is located on the banks of the River Gomti (a tributary of River Ganga). A dip in this river is said to be an extremely sacred ritual. It will take 2 hours to reach Naimisharanya the place where Ved Vyas is said to have written the epic Hindu mythology Mahabharata.\nYou will be made to visit Chakratirth Mandir which holds great relevance to Hindus. Later you will be made to proceed towards Lalita Devi Temple which is one of the most important Shakti Peeths in India.\nLater after a wholesome tour of the city you will be transferred back to Lucknow for the night.\n\n\n\n\nDay 7 :Lucknow Sightseeing \u2013 Departure\n\n\nPost breakfast early in the morning you will be taken for a local sightseeing tour of the city starting with a visit to Bara and Chota Imambara \u2013 which are the sacred complexes built in 17th century consisting of imposing structures. Rumi Darwaza will be your next stop which is a towering gateway which was built by Asaf-ud-Daula in 1784.\nFinally, after an insightful day you will then be headed towards your departure destination from where you will head on to your onward destination.",
    "highlights": [
      "Have a divine tour in the city of temples Varanasi",
      "Have a boat ride early morning welcoming the sun",
      "Tour to Bodhgaya",
      "On the way to Allahabad visit to the Maa Vindhyavasini Mandir in Vindhyachal",
      "Visit to the Triveni Sangam",
      "Ayodhya Darshan with Hanuman Mandir and Dashrath Mahal",
      "Visit the city of Nawabs Lucknow and enjoy the Nawabi cuisine",
      "Visit Naimisharanya, also known as Neemsar, which is located on the banks of the River Gomti.",
      "Lalitha Devi Temple visit, another Shaktipeeth",
      "Lucknow sightseeing"
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1 :Arrival in Varanasi",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 2 :Varanasi \u2013 Bodhgaya",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 3 :Bodhgaya to Varanasi",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 4 :Varanasi \u2013 Vindhyachal \u2013 Prayagraj",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 5 :Prayagraj \u2013 Ayodhya \u2013 Lucknow",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 6 :Lucknow \u2013 Naimisharanya \u2013 Lucknow",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 7 :Lucknow Sightseeing \u2013 Departure",
        "description": ""
      }
    ],
    "faqs": []
  },
  "varanasi-bodhgaya-prayagraj-package": {
    "overview": "Have you ever thought why so many tourists travel to Varanasi and Bodhgaya every year? See More\n\nOur Varanasi Bodhgaya Prayagraj Tour Package gives you a complete experience of both cities. First, we will explore Varanasi, known for its colorful and attractive culture that people from different countries specially come here to see its beautiful temples, old traditions, local music, Ghats, and the peaceful Ganges River.\nThis city has around 2,000 temples, but don't miss Kashi Vishwanath temple, the main attraction, and one of the 12th Jyotirlingas. Many rulers destroyed it, but devoted people rebuilt it each time. Those who visit this temple feel deep peace in their heart, that\u2019s why everyone should see it. After Varanasi, our journey continues to Bodhgaya.\nIt is a beautiful site full of Buddhist culture, located in Bihar. This is where Lord Buddha meditated under the Bodhi Tree, and since then, it has become a famous spiritual destination. You will see Monks from many countries wear red or maroon robes. They meditate and chant, and the place has a very spiritual vibe. During Buddha Jayanti, visitors can enjoy unique activities and colorful celebrations at the Mahabodhi Temple, which you shouldn't miss! Get ready for Varanasi to Bodhgaya Prayagraj tour! \nSee Less\n\nOur Varanasi Bodhgaya Prayagraj Tour Package gives you a complete experience of both cities. First, we will explore Varanasi, known for its colorful and attractive culture that people from different countries specially come here to see its beautiful temples, old traditions, local music, Ghats, and the peaceful Ganges River.",
    "highlights": [
      "Visit the famous temples and Ghats of Varanasi, see the Kashi Vishwanath Temple, and enjoy a peaceful boat ride on the Ganga.",
      "Visit Sarnath where Lord Buddha gave his first teaching and see the Dhamekha Stupa and other Buddhist sites.",
      "Experience Bodhgaya\u2019s charm with the Mahabodhi Temple, the sacred Bodhi tree and monasteries.",
      "The package includes visits with guide, temple rituals, sightseeing, hotel stays and pickup/drop transport for your comfort.",
      "See More"
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1: Arrive in Varanasi",
        "description": "Your\nVaranasi Bodhgaya Prayagraj trip\nbegins when our My Quick Trippers team welcomes you at the airport or railway station and takes you to your hotel. If you add a guide, they will come with the driver and help you during the whole day.\nAfter you check in, visit these places in Varanasi-\nVishwanath Temple\nAnnapurna Mandir\nVishalakshi Mandir\nKal Bhairava\nDurga Mandir\nMana Mandir\nSankat Mochan Mandir\nBirla Mandir\nGanga Ghats (River Front)\n- Watch the famous Ganga Aarti, and you can also enjoy it from a boat (Optional). After exploring the main attractions in Varanasi, stay overnight at your hotel in Varanasi.\nNote:\nPooja, Aarti, and Sugam Darshan can be booked online only. \nWeblink:\nhttps://shrikashivishwanath.org\nVishwanath Temple-\nMorning Darshan- 4:00 AM to 11:00 AM\nAfternoon Darshan- 12:00 PM to 7:00 PM\nEvening Darshan- 8:30 PM to 9:00 PM\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 2: Varanasi - Bodhgaya (248 km/5hr)",
        "description": "After breakfast, start your journey to\nBodhgaya\nvisit the\nMahabodhi Temple\n, a UNESCO World Heritage site built by Emperor Ashoka. Explore here beautiful gardens, old stone artwork, and the holy Bodhi tree where Buddha meditated.\nLater, explore other important sites like\nAnimesh Lochana Temple\n(over 2,300 years old),\nBuddhist Dharma Chakra\n(Buddhist monument),\nLotus Tank, Archaeological Museum, Thai Temple, Indosan Nipponji Temple, Gelugpa Tibetan Monastery\nand the\nGiant Buddha Statue\n(about 80 feet tall).\nOvernight stay in Bodhgaya.\nNote\n- Some temples and museums don\u2019t allow photos so please follow the rules.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 3: Bodhgaya \u2013 Gaya (15 km/35 min) \u2013 Varanasi (257 km/ 6hr)",
        "description": "In the morning visit the\nVishnu Pad Temple\n, famous for the sacred footprint of Lord Vishnu known as Dharmasila. A 40 cm long footprint of Lord Vishnu is in solid rock and covered with a silver plate.\nPerform\nPind Daan\n(offerings and prayers for your ancestors) at this holy place. It is believed to help your ancestors\u2019 souls rest in peace and bring you happiness and good luck.\nFirst, do prayers at\nBrahma and Gayatri Ghat,\nthen at\nPita Maheshwar,\nand lastly at\nPretshila.\nAfter the rituals, proceed for the drive to\nVaranasi,\nwhich takes around 6 hours.\nOn arrival, check in to the hotel and enjoy an overnight stay in\nVaranasi.\nNote-\nVishnupad Temple timings are 5:00 am to 12:30 pm and 2:00 pm to 11:00 pm.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 4: Varanasi - Prayagraj \u2013 Varanasi (240 km/ Approx. 6 hours)",
        "description": "After breakfast, continue the journey to\nPrayagraj\nand visit\nTriveni Sangam,\nwhere Ganga, Yamuna, and the invisible Saraswati meet. Take a dip and pray there.\nAfter the holy ritual, take a half-day tour of\nPrayagraj\nand visit\nAllahabad Fort\n(a historic fort with great views of the river),\nAllahabad Museum, Anand Bhawan\n(the home of the Nehru family), and\nSwaraj Bhawan\n(where freedom leaders once stayed).\nStop at\nAlopi Devi Temple,\na well-known holy Shaktipeeth.\nNext, return to Varanasi and check into your hotel for an overnight stay.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 5: Varanasi - Morning Ganga Boat Ride, Sarnath Visit, Temple Tour & Departure",
        "description": "Total distance-\n30 to 40 Approx.\nExperience the morning in\nVaranasi\nwith a sunrise boat ride on the Ganges. See people performing prayers and rituals on the Ghats. You can bathe at your hotel or take a holy dip in the river.\nAfter that, visit the\nVishwanath Temple,\na very sacred temple in India. Then go to\nSarnath,\nwhere Lord Buddha gave his first teaching. Be sure to see the\nDhamek Stupa,\na tall and beautiful Stupa that\u2019s great for photos. You can also see the\nBuddha temples, Chaukhandi Stupa and Archaeological Museum.\nAfter sightseeing your\nVaranasi Bodhgaya Prayagraj tour\nends as you are transferred to Varanasi Railway Station/ Airport for your next journey.\nNote\n- Varanasi needs a lot of walking around temples and Ghats. Wear comfortable shoes.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      }
    ],
    "faqs": []
  },
  "varanasi-city-tour": {
    "overview": "Visiting Varanasi transports one to a different era altogether. It is as if the sacred city exists in an entirely different realm! Nowhere else would you find death so openly intermingling with life?\n\nEnjoy a romantic boat ride along the serene waves of Ganga. The myriad pictures of Varanasi city from the boat-ride would appear as if they have been lifted straight out of a nostalgic film of yesteryears. And when it gets to describing the magnificent Ganga Aarti, we find our words retreating away shyly. The grandeur and numinosity evoked by the Aarti has to be experienced to be known!\nCombine the diverse wonders of Varanasi with a visit to Sarnath, the holy site that witnessed the first sermon by Lord Buddha. Enjoy two-day long immersion in the religious, spiritual, cultural and aesthetic environ of Varanasi.\n\nEnjoy a romantic boat ride along the serene waves of Ganga. The myriad pictures of Varanasi city from the boat-ride would appear as if they have been lifted straight out of a nostalgic film of yesteryears. And when it gets to describing the magnificent Ganga Aarti, we find our words retreating away shyly. The grandeur and numinosity evoked by the Aarti has to be experienced to be known!\n\nCombine the diverse wonders of Varanasi with a visit to Sarnath, the holy site that witnessed the first sermon by Lord Buddha. Enjoy two-day long immersion in the religious, spiritual, cultural and aesthetic environ of Varanasi.\n\nVaranasi Sightseeing Tour Itinerary Package\n\n\nDay 1 :Arrival Varanasi\n\n\nWelcome to the magical city of Varanasi! Our Representative would welcome you warmly and initiate you into the trip. First, you would be transferred to the Hotel. After freshening up, let us proceed to visit the many wonders of Varanasi. The sights of Varanasi know no limits! It is as if every nook and corner, curve and twist in the city\u2019s terrain has a story of its own.\nThe holiest of all cities are lined with millions of temples. Some of the more prominent of them include Kashi Vishwanath Temple, Sankat Mochan Temple, Bharat Mata Mandir, Gauri Mata Mandir, Kaal Bhairav Temple and Durga Temple. The city of temples also has a hundred Ghats that lead one into the waters of holy Ganga. Some of the more famous of the Ghats include Panchganga Ghat, Manikarnika Ghat, Dasaswamedh Ghat, Harishchandra Ghat, Assi Ghat and Kedar Ghat.\nAfter letting your senses soak in the myriad hues of Varanasi, immerse them in the sacred atmosphere the Ganga Aarti evokes. The resounding sound of a hundred cymbals, bells and drums against the ritualized chanting of sacred Sanskrit mantras provide the perfect musical ambience to the myriads of lamps worshipping the holiest of holy Rivers. Enjoying the holy Ganga Aarti from a boat amplifies the visual aesthetic effect of the entire experience.\nAfterward, enjoy your overnight stay at the hotel room.\n\n\n\n\nDay 2 :Varanasi \u2013 Sarnath\n\n\nBeing in Varanasi, one cannot afford to witness how the city wakes up to a new day. It is as if the morning rays of the Sun casts a sublimely beautiful shade to everything it touches! A cruise about the waters of Ganga enjoying the morning views at the Ghats where people offer their morning prayers to Sun God and Maa Ganga is truly delightful! You may begin the auspicious day by taking a holy dip in the sacred waters of Ganga as well. Also, pay visit to one of the many beautiful Temples, or the prime Kashi Vishwanath temple itself! You may join in to perform religious rites for your ancestors at the Ghats of Ganga River. Afterward, retire shortly to the hotel for a sumptuous breakfast.\nThe latter part of the day is allotted to sightseeing of Sarnath. Situated 10 km north-east of Varanasi, Sarnath is the land that saw the origins of Buddhism. Visit its deer park famed to be the spot in which Lord Buddha gave his first sermon on Buddhism. In short, Sarnath is to Buddhists what Varanasi is to Hindus! While at Sarnath, enjoy visiting the Dhamek Stupa, the Chaukhandi Stupa marking the site where Buddha received his first disciples, the pre- Ashokan stupa of Dharmarajika Stupa, Ashoka Pillar and Sarnath Archeological Museum.\nAfterward, you may enjoy shopping in the many alleys of Varanasi and purchase for yourself souvenirs of having visited the spectacularly magical city of Varanasi.",
    "highlights": [
      "The city of temples Varanasi will welcome worth open hands.",
      "Visit the famous temples namely Kashi Vishwanath Temple, Sankat Mochan Temple, Bharat Mata Mandir, Gauri Mata Mandir, Kaal Bhairav Temple and Durga Temple.",
      "Explore through the numerous Ghats like Panchganga Ghat, Manikarnika Ghat, Dasaswamedh Ghat, Harishchandra Ghat, Assi Ghat and Kedar Ghat.",
      "Enjoy the early morning boat cruise on river Ganga enjoying the sunrise and in the evening the sunset and the evening Aarti.",
      "At Sarnath visit the Dhamek Stupa, the Chaukhandi Stupa marking the site where Buddha received his first disciples, the pre- Ashokan Stupa of Dharmarajika Stupa, Ashoka Pillar and Sarnath Archeological Museum, all are unique in their own way.",
      "Also enjoy the local cuisine of Varanasi."
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1 :Arrival Varanasi",
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 2 :Varanasi \u2013 Sarnath",
        "description": ""
      }
    ],
    "faqs": []
  },
  "varanasi-prayagraj-ayodhya-vindhyachal-tour": {
    "overview": "Explore India\u2019s 4 famous cities where you will see hidden gems, rituals, and hear local stories that make every place special. See More\n\nOur Varanasi Prayagraj Ayodhya Vindhyachal tour package is designed with proper guidance for every visitor. Start your trip in Varanasi, one of the oldest city.\nThe journey feels incomplete without visiting the Shri Kashi Vishwanath temple, one of the 12 Jyotirlingas. People believe visiting this temple brings moksha (salvation). Apart from this, you\u2019ll also explore many other exciting places listed in the itinerary that will give lasting memories. Your next destination is Prayagraj, famous for its Bade Hanuman Mandir.\nThis temple is very old, around 700 years and has a 20 foot statue of Lord Hanuman that travelers love to see. It is located near Triveni Sangam. Now, the tour continues to Ayodhya, the birthplace of Lord Rama. Here you will visit Ram Janmabhoomi temple known for its impressive design and visited by many tourists not only from India but also abroad for its mythological importance. So make memories on a special Kashi Vindhyachal Prayagraj Ayodhya trip.\nSee Less\n\nOur Varanasi Prayagraj Ayodhya Vindhyachal tour package is designed with proper guidance for every visitor. Start your trip in Varanasi, one of the oldest city.\n\nThe journey feels incomplete without visiting the Shri Kashi Vishwanath temple, one of the 12 Jyotirlingas. People believe visiting this temple brings moksha (salvation). Apart from this, you\u2019ll also explore many other exciting places listed in the itinerary that will give lasting memories. Your next destination is Prayagraj, famous for its Bade Hanuman Mandir.",
    "highlights": [
      "Explore the holy cities of Varanasi, Prayagraj and Ayodhya, visiting famous temples, Ghats and historic places with rich cultural experiences.",
      "At Triveni Sangam in Prayagraj see Ganga Aarti, where the Ganga, Yamuna, and Saraswati meet and enjoy a peaceful boat ride.",
      "Visit Hanuman Garhi Temple on hill (perfect for photos), Ram Janmabhoomi, Kanak Bhavan and other temples with beautiful architecture.",
      "Travel in comfort with a private AC car, enjoy festivals and cool weather from October to March and make special memories on this 4-day trip.",
      "See More"
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1: Arrive in Varanasi",
        "description": "Our\nMy Quick Trippers\nteam will meet you at Varanasi Airport or Railway Station to start your tour and transfer you to the hotel for check-in and a comfortable rest. If you choose a guide, they will travel with the driver to help you during the tour.\nStart exploring the famous sights of\nVaranasi-\nShri Kashi Vishwanath Temple\nAnnapurna Temple\nVishalakshi Temple\nBaba Kal Bhairav Temple\nSankat Mochan Hanuman Temple\nDurga Mandir\nTulsi Manas Temple\nNew Vishwanath Temple\nExplore the Banaras Hindu University (BHU) campus.\nIn the evening, take a relaxing\nboat ride on the Ganges,\nsee the popular Ghats of Varanasi, and experience the spiritual vibe of the city (optional, extra cost). Later, attend the world-famous\nGanga Aarti at Dashashwamedh Ghat\n- watch it from the Ghat or on a private boat. This beautiful ceremony shows the amazing traditions of Varanasi (don't forget to click photos). Stay overnight in Varanasi.\nNote-\nNot many tourists know that they can ride a hot air balloon in Varanasi - try it if time allows.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 2: Varanasi - Vindhyachal - Prayagraj (155-160 km / 4 hours)",
        "description": "Morning after breakfast, drive towards Prayagraj. Enroute visit\nVindhyachal Devi\nfor a Darshan at Shaktipeeth. Later visit\nSitamarhi,\nthe temple where Mother Sita went into the earth.\nNext, go to\nPrayagraj,\nand visit\nTriveni Sangam,\nwhere the Ganga, Yamuna, and Saraswati rivers meet. Take a holy dip and enjoy a boat ride.\nThen travel to\nBade Hanuman Mandir.\nPeople believe that Hanuman Ji stopped here to rest after burning Lanka.\nVisit the\nAkshayavat Temple\nand Tree at\nPatalpuri Temple\nin\nPrayagraj Fort,\nbelieved to be the spot where Ram, Lakshman, and Sita rested. People pray here to wash away sins.\nNow proceed to\nPrayagraj Fort,\nalso called\nAllahabad Fort\nbuilt by Akbar in 1583 beside the Yamuna River near where it joins the Ganga (Great photo spot).\nStop at\nAlopi Devi Temple,\na well-known holy Shaktipeeth.\nOptional:\nif time allows, visit\nLalita Devi Temple, Shri Nagvasuki Temple\nwhere people pray for blessings. Then, explore\nAnand Bhavan,\nthe Nehru family\u2019s home.\nSpend the night at your hotel in Prayagraj and take some rest.\nNote-\nAllahabad Fort timings are 10 a.m. to 6 p.m.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 3: Prayagraj - Ayodhya (166 km / 4 hours)",
        "description": "Start your day with breakfast and then drive to\nAyodhya.\nOnce you arrive see\nRam Janmabhoomi Temple\nwhere Lord Rama was born.\nNext visit\nHanuman Garhi Temple,\na famous temple dedicated to Lord Hanuman, built on a hill - perfect for taking beautiful photos. Later, see\nKanak Bhavan Temple,\nfamous for its golden domes.\nDashrath Mahal\n- It is a popular Siddha Peetha, and divine abode of King Dasharatha, (father of Lord Rama).\nExplore\nRam ji ki Paidi\nand\nDashrath Mahal\nwhere Dasharatha Lord Rama\u2019s father, once lived.\nIn the evening enjoy the\nSaryu River Aarti\nat\nNaya Ghat\nand go for peaceful walk along the river. After a day of spiritual experiences, return to your hotel in\nAyodhya\nfor the night..\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 4: Ayodhya - Varanasi Departure",
        "description": "Morning after breakfast, we will drop you to the\nVaranasi airport\nor railway station to catch your next flight or train.\nThe\ntrip to Ayodhya, Varanasi and Prayagraj\nends with blissful memories."
      }
    ],
    "faqs": []
  },
  "varanasi-prayagraj-bodhgaya-ayodhya-tour": {
    "overview": "Our Varanasi tour package with Prayagraj, Gaya, Bodhgaya, and Ayodhya takes you on a sacred journey to Uttar Pradesh and Bihar's famous attractions. See More\n\nYou get to explore famous destinations like Prayagraj, Ayodhya, Gaya, Varanasi, and Bodhgaya. Our expert guide will be there to assist you throughout the journey. The highlight of the trip is that you will get a chance to visit the iconic temples of Varanasi and Bodhgaya. You will take a dip at the Triveni Sangam.\nBook our Varanasi tour package now to have the most fulfilling and spiritually enchanting journey of your life.\nSee Less\n\nYou get to explore famous destinations like Prayagraj, Ayodhya, Gaya, Varanasi, and Bodhgaya. Our expert guide will be there to assist you throughout the journey. The highlight of the trip is that you will get a chance to visit the iconic temples of Varanasi and Bodhgaya. You will take a dip at the Triveni Sangam.\n\nBook our Varanasi tour package now to have the most fulfilling and spiritually enchanting journey of your life.\n\nTour Gallery\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nTour Name\nVaranasi Prayagraj Bodhgaya Ayodhya Tour\n\n\nTour Duration\n07 Days / 06 Nights\n\n\nMeals\nBreakfast\n\n\nVehicle Type\nSedan / SUV\n\n\nStarting & Ending Point\nVaranasi\n\n\nDestination Covered\nVaranasi - Prayagraj - Ayodhya - Bodhgaya \n\n\nPickup Time\nDepend on your Flight Timing \n\n\n Tour Benefits\nBest price & enjoyable travel guarantee",
    "highlights": [
      "Explore the popular attractions of Bodhgaya.",
      "Exploration of Varanasi\u2019s famous sites.",
      "Visit Triveni Sangam and have a boat ride.",
      "Spiritual exploration of Ayodhya.",
      "See More"
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1: Arrive at Varanasi",
        "description": "Today you will arrive at Varanasi. After arriving at Varanasi Railway Station/ Airport, you will be greeted by one of our representatives who will transfer you to your pre-booked hotel, where you\u2019ll check in and relax for some time.\nLater, you\u2019ll head out for Kashi sightseeing\nVisit famous temples, including the\nShri Kashi Vishwanath Temple.\nVisit\nVishalakshi Temple\nDarshan at\nAnnapurna Temple\nDarshan of Baba Kal Kalbhairav at\nBaba Kal Kal Bhairav Temple\nEvening: In the evening, you will embark on a boat cruise on the River Ganges. You will explore the famous Ghats of Varanasi and experience the city\u2019s sacred vibes (For this, you will have to pay an additional cost). Later, you will attend the Ganga Aarti at Dashashwamedh Ghat. You can do this either during a private boat ride or from the Ghat itself.\nHave an Overnight Stay in Varanasi\nVishwanath Temple\nDarshan timing - 04:00 am to 11:00 am\n08:30 pm to 09:00 pm and 12:00 pm to 7:00 pm\nSapta rishi 07:00 pm to 08:30 pm\nPlease note:\nYou can book Sugam Darshan, Pooja, and Aarti online.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 2: Varanasi \u2013 Bodhgaya (250 km/6hr)",
        "description": "Relish a tasty breakfast, and then you\u2019ll head to\nBodhgaya\n, the site of Lord Buddha\u2019s enlightenment. After arriving at Bodhgaya, you will check into your pre-reserved hotel.\nYou will begin your sightseeing tour by visiting the\nMahabodhi Temple\n, one of the most famous Buddhist temples in the world. It is considered to be the site where Buddha attained enlightenment under the\nMaha Bodhi Tree\n, which is considered to be the original Peepal tree\u2019s descendant.\nExplore the other popular attractions, such as\nBuddhist Dharma Chakra\nAnimesh Lochana Temple\nLotus tank\nThai Temple\nArchaeological Museum\nGelugpa Tibetan Monastery\nIndosan Nipponji Temple\nGiant statue of Buddha\nYou can meditate or explore the surreal surroundings of\nBodhgaya\nin the evening.\nYou will have an overnight stay at your hotel in Bodh Gaya.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 3: Bodhgaya \u2013 Gaya (35 min/12 km) \u2013 Varanasi (7hr/250 km)",
        "description": "Early in the morning, you will be transferred to\nVishnupad Temple\n, which houses Lord Vishnu\u2019s sacred footprint. It is the site where Pind Daan is performed by people to liberate their ancestors from the endless cycle of birth and death.\nSituated on the banks of the River Phalgu, Vishnupad Temple is one of the most famous Hindu temples in Gaya, Bihar, India. It\u2019s a major pilgrimage center for those who want to attain salvation.\nYou will then visit\nMaa Sarva Mangala Gauri Shakti Peeth\nand head to\nPretshila.\nLater, you will head back to Varanasi, and you will check into your pre-booked hotel. You can spend the evening as you want. You can attend Ganga Aarti at the sacred Ghats.\nYou will have an overnight stay in Varanasi.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 4: Varanasi \u2013 Sarnath Sightseeing",
        "description": "Early Morning:\nYou will start your day with a boat ride on the River Ganges. You can explore the sacred Ghats such as\nHarishchandra Ghat, Assi Ghat, and Manikarnika Ghat.\nIf you have time, you can visit the\nKashi Vishwanath Temple.\nLater in the Morning\nYou will head to the famous temples of Varanasi:\nDurga Mandir\nNew Vishwanath Temple\nSankat Mochan Hanuman Temple\nTulsi Manas Temple\nExplore the Bharat Kala Bhawan Museum and the Banaras Hindu University (BHU) campus.\nAfternoon\nIn the afternoon, you will embark on a drive to Sarnath. You will also explore:\nChaukhandi Stupa\nDhamek Stupa\nBuddhist Temples\nEvening\nBoat ride on the Ganga River at\nDashashwamedh Ghat.\nHave an overnight stay in Varanasi.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 5: Varanasi - Vidhyanchal - Prayagraj(4hrs/140 km)",
        "description": "Morning:\nRelish a tasty breakfast in the morning, and then you will head out on a drive to Prayagraj. On the way, you will visit the\nVindhyachal Devi Temple\nand seek Mother Divine Shakti\u2019s blessings. You will then visit\nSitamarhi\n, where Mother Sita entered the earth. You will then head to\nPrayagraj\nand explore famous sites, including\nAnand Bhavan.\nVisit Lalita Devi Temple: One of the 51 sacred Shakti Peeth.\nVisit Alopi Devi Temple\nSeek spiritual bliss at Shri Nagvasuki Temple\nEvening Aarti at Ghat\nHave an overnight stay in Prayagraj.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 6: Prayagraj - Ayodhya (4 hr/167 km)",
        "description": "Early Morning:\nYou will visit Triveni Sangam\u2014the confluence of the mythical Saraswati, Ganga, and Yamuna rivers, where you can take a holy dip.\nHoly bath and boat ride in Sangam:\nEnjoy a boat ride on the Sangam & Yamuna River.\nBade Hanuman Mandir:\nSeek blessings at the Hanuman Mandir.\nVisit Akshayavat Tree and Temple:\nWithin the Patalpuri temple in Prayagraj Fort, the sacred fig tree is worshiped as Akshayavat. Devotees believe that Sita, Ram, and Lakshman rested under this tree.\nVisit Prayagraj Fort:\nBuilt in 1583 by Akbar at the confluence of the Yamuna and Ganges Rivers.\nLater, you will head out on a drive to Ayodhya.\nOnce you have arrived, you will check into your pre-booked hotel and relax, and later you will have the sightseeing tour of Ayodhya.\nEvening:\nAt\nRam ki Paidi\n, you will witness the divine Sarayu Aarti.\nStroll by the Ram ki\nPaidi Ghats.\nIf you have time, you can visit\nRam Janmabhoomi Temple.\nOvernight stay at your hotel in\nAyodhya.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 7: Spiritual and Cultural Exploration of Ayodhya & Departure",
        "description": "Visit the Saryu River:\nYou will take a dip in the Saryu River.\nVisit Ram Janmabhoomi Temple\n, the birthplace of Lord Rama.\nAbsorb the sacred vibes of\nHanuman Garhi Temple\n, which is dedicated to Lord Hanuman.\nExplore the\nKanak Bhavan Temple\n, which is renowned for its gold-plated domes.\nVisit\nNageshwarnath Temple\n, which is dedicated to Lord Shiva.\nExplore\nDashrath Mahal\n, King Dashrath\u2019s residence.\nIf you have time, you can\nVisit\nValmiki Ramayana Bhawan\n, where you can see illustrated depictions of the Ramayana epic.\nYou will visit\nTreta Ke Thakur Temple.\nEvening:\nYou will depart from Ayodhya. Our driver will drop you at your preferred location.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      }
    ],
    "faqs": []
  },
  "varanasi-sarnath-tour": {
    "overview": "Witness the world where time stops to behold the divine in its most beautiful forms. See More\n\nVaranasi captures the heartbeat of spiritual India and Sarnath offers a sanctuary of eternal peace and sacred drops of wisdom from the life of Lord Buddha. In our 2 Day Varanasi Tour with Sarnath Sightseeing, you will find delight in the chaotic energy of eternal Varanasi and serene solitude in Sarnath where every moment is a step ahead to Nirvana.\nFrom the divine moksha of Varanasi to the light of enlightenment in Sarnath, My Quick Trippers offers best pilgrimage tour experiences to the travellers. You don\u2019t have to worry about travel logistics with us in your 2 Day Varanasi with Sarnath Tour. We will handle all the transportation, meals, VIP Darshans, Hotels and guide arrangements. So, leave all your worries and pack your bags to embark on a divine journey to find your soul at Varanasi and Sarnath. Book your trip now at best price.\nSee Less\n\nVaranasi captures the heartbeat of spiritual India and Sarnath offers a sanctuary of eternal peace and sacred drops of wisdom from the life of Lord Buddha. In our 2 Day Varanasi Tour with Sarnath Sightseeing, you will find delight in the chaotic energy of eternal Varanasi and serene solitude in Sarnath where every moment is a step ahead to Nirvana.\n\nFrom the divine moksha of Varanasi to the light of enlightenment in Sarnath, My Quick Trippers offers best pilgrimage tour experiences to the travellers. You don\u2019t have to worry about travel logistics with us in your 2 Day Varanasi with Sarnath Tour. We will handle all the transportation, meals, VIP Darshans, Hotels and guide arrangements. So, leave all your worries and pack your bags to embark on a divine journey to find your soul at Varanasi and Sarnath. Book your trip now at best price.",
    "highlights": [
      "Dive deep into the spiritual whirlwind by visiting Kashi Vishwanath Temple.",
      "Seek divine blessings at Durga Mandir/ Durga Kund Temple. It is dedicated to goddess Durga who represents strength and power.",
      "Stand in awe before Lord Hanuman at Sankat Mochan Temple.",
      "Seek solace and blessings at Birla Temple in BHU dedicated to Lord Shiva. It is also known as Kashi Vishwanath Temple. We will also visit Baba Kal Bhairav Temple, Annapurna Temple and Vishalakshi Temple.",
      "Discover the serenity and bliss by witness the sacred Ganga Aarti in evening and enjoy the boat ride on ganga river. Explore the sacred Ghats such as Assi Ghat, Manikarnika Ghat and Harishchandra Ghat.",
      "Nurture your mind by visiting the spiritually enriching city of Sarnath. It is a place where LORD Buddha delivered his first sermon.",
      "See famous places connected to Lord Buddha like Dhamek Stupa, Chaukhandi Stupa and archeological museum.",
      "See More"
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1: Arrival at Varanasi \u2013 The city of Liberation",
        "description": "After your arrival at Varanasi, our tour representative will pick you up from airport/ railway station and transfer you to your pre-booked hotel.\nAfter check-in, take some rest and unpack. Later we will start our Varanasi tour and see many iconic places like Kashi Vishwanath Temple, Annapurna Temple, Vishalakshi Temple, Baba Kal Bhairav Temple, Sankat Mochan Mandir & Birla Mandir.\nEvening- In the evening, we will enjoy a scenic boat ride in the blissful ganga river. You will be mesmerized to see the Varanasi from the holy Ghats. If you wish to explore the holy city of Varanasi completely then extra charges will be required.\nAlso, immerse in the spiritual rhythm of Ganga Aarti at the Dashashwamedh Ghat either from Ghat or from a scenic boat ride.\nAfter the tour, get back to your hotel room for overnight stay.\nImportant Timings to Note\nVishwanath Temple\nDarshan timing - 04:00 am to 11:00 am\n12:00 pm to 7:00 pm and 08:30 pm to 09:00 pm\nSaptarishi - 07:00 pm to 08:30 pm\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 2: Varanasi (Kashi)\u2013 Sarnath Sightseeing (11 kms/20-25 minutes)",
        "description": "We will start the day by exploring the beauty of Varanasi by enjoying a sunrise boat\ncruise at Ganga River.\nIt is optional whether you want to take a holy dip in ganga or bath in the hotel room.\nWe will enjoy the vibrant life on the sacred Ghats such as Assi Ghat, Manikarnika Ghat and Harishchandra Ghat.\nLater, visit to Kashi Vishwanath Temple, the divine sanctuary of Lord Shiva to seek blessings. (Optional).\nAfter sometime, visit the sacred temple of Varanasi such as Sankat Mochan Temple, Durga Mandir, Tulsi Manas Temple, New Vishwanath temple, BHU campus and Bharat Kala Museum.\nThereafter in the afternoon, visit Sarnath, a place where Lord Buddha delivered his first sermon. Witness some famous places connected to lord Buddha\u2019 life and times like Dhamek Stupa, Chaukhandi Stupa and other Buddhist temples nearby.\nThe tour ends and you will be driven back to airport/ railway station for further journey.\nNote \u2013\nBook all your Pooja, Aarti and Sugam Darshan online only, Weblink-\nhttps://shrikashivishwanath.org\nIf you are planning to visit in Sawan Month, your tour will be impacted by Kanwar yatra, which can cause heavy traffic or route diversion.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      }
    ],
