  "yamuna-pushkaralu-tour-from-delhi": {
    "overview": "The Yamuna Pushkaralu Tour from Delhi is a 4 Days / 3 Nights trip. See More\n\nIt is designed for pilgrims who want to seek the blessing of the goddess Yamuna on the auspicious event of Pushkaralu which takes place only once every 12 years. It is marked by the special astrological event when Jupiter enters Cancer. This holy tour will take you to the revered Yamunotri Temple from Delhi via Haridwar, Dehradun, Mussoorie, Barkot, and Janki Chatti.\nSignificance\nIt is believed that attending this special event and performing rituals cleanses sins and removes negative karmas. In addition, it grants relief from Pitru Dosha and other planetary afflictions. Pilgrims who come here perform the holy rituals such as Pushkara Snanam, ancestral rituals, and special pujas.\nThis tour brings together spirituality with natural beauty \u2013 giving you a once-in-a-lifetime opportunity for memorable experiences.\nSee Less\n\nIt is designed for pilgrims who want to seek the blessing of the goddess Yamuna on the auspicious event of Pushkaralu which takes place only once every 12 years. It is marked by the special astrological event when Jupiter enters Cancer. This holy tour will take you to the revered Yamunotri Temple from Delhi via Haridwar, Dehradun, Mussoorie, Barkot, and Janki Chatti.",
    "highlights": [
      "Visit to Yamunotri Temple, dedicated to Goddess Yamuna",
      "Holy participation in Yamuna Pushkaralu, a spiritual festival held once every 12 years",
      "Sacred Pushkara Snanam in the icy waters of River Yamuna",
      "Get relief from Pitru Dosha, Naga Dosha, and long-pending karmic obstacles",
      "Gain spiritual merit through ancestral rites, such as Pinda Pradan & Tarpan",
      "Perform rituals at Surya Kund (cook rice as sacred Prasadam with other devotees)",
      "Worship at Divya Shila, the sacred rock believed to be Yamuna\u2019s point of origin",
      "Attend evening Ganga Aarti at Har Ki Pauri",
      "Soak in the scenic Himalayan drive via Dehradun and Mussoorie",
      "Enjoy a brief picnic at Kempty Falls",
      "Opportunity to perform special Pujas, Homas, Deep-Daan, and Yamuna Aarti",
      "See More"
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1: Arrive Delhi \u2013 Haridwar (220 km/5 Hrs)",
        "description": "Once you arrive at the New Delhi Airport/Railway Station, you\u2019ll be warmly greeted and assisted by our tour representative.\nNow, you\u2019ll be driven to Haridwar. Enjoy the scenic drive all along.\nOnce you reach the holy city, check into your hotel and relax for a while.\nIn the evening, head to\nHar Ki Pauri\nfor bathing on the sacred banks of the River Ganges.\nAlso, attend the evening\nGanga Aarti\n.\nVisit\nBrahma Kund\n, too. This is believed to be the very spot where drops of Amrit (nectar) fell.\nIf time permits, also visit the Manasa Devi Temple.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 2: Haridwar \u2013 Dehradun \u2013 Barkot / Janki Chatti (240 kms / 9 Hrs)",
        "description": "After breakfast in the morning, set out for a morning drive to Barkot via Dehradun & Mussoorie.\nAlong the way, we\u2019ll make a stop at the\nKempty Falls\n. Enjoy the scenic Himalayan views here.\nContinue your drive to\nBarkot\n.\nOnce you get there, check into your hotel and enjoy an overnight stay.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 3: Barkot - Yamunotri Snan \u2013 Barkot (45 Kms road / 6 kms Trek)",
        "description": "Start your day early and drive towards\nJanki Chatti\n(trek starting point) in the morning.\nWhen you get there, begin your trek or hire a pony/Doli (on a direct payment basis).\nOnce you arrive at Yamunotri, take a holy dip in the waters of the River Yamuna.\nAt\nSurya Kund\n, cook rice in the hot spring. This is the Prasadam that you can also take home.\nAlso, offer your prayers at the\nDivya Shila\nand seek blessings.\nAfter your Darshan, trek back to Janki Chatti.\nNow, you\u2019ll be driven back to Barkot for an overnight stay.\nYamunotri Temple\n: The temple is dedicated to Goddess Yamuna who is believed to be daughter of Lord Surya and sister of Yamraj.\nSurya Kund:\nThere are a number of thermal springs close to the temple, which flows into numerous pools. The most important of these is \u201cSurya Kund\u201d and is dedicated to Lord Surya.\nDivya Shila:\nAccording to mythology, river Yamuna came out for the very first time from \u201cDivya Shila\u201d. This is the worship place of Yamuna Mata.\nTrek Options:\nBy Walk: 6 Kms / 2-3 Hrs one way\nHorse: \u20b93,000 per person (Approx)\nPalki: \u20b98,000 to 10,000 per person (Approx)\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 4: Barkot \u2013 Delhi (350 kms / 10 Hrs)",
        "description": "In the morning, you\u2019ll head back to Delhi after breakfast.\nEnjoy the scenic views along the way. We\u2019ll also take a few comfort breaks as required.\nOnce we arrive in\nDelhi\n, you\u2019ll be dropped off at Delhi Airport/Railway Station.\nHope you have a memorable trip full of beautiful memories.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      }
    ],
    "faqs": []
  },
  "yamuna-pushkaralu-yatra-from-dehradun": {
    "overview": "Get a once-in-a-lifetime opportunity to attend Yamuna Pushkaralu, one of the most revered Hindu festivals that is celebrated once every twelve years when Jupiter enters Gemini. This year it will be held from June 2, 2026, to June 13, 2026. It is believed that if you take a dip in the Yamuna River during this period, your soul gets purified and you get to seek divine blessings. See More\n\nYamuna Pushkaralu Tour from Dehradun includes lodging, food, transportation, and guided sightseeing. The divine journey will start from Dehradun and take you to Dakpatthar, a serene hill town situated on the banks of the River Yamuna and an important spiritual and scenic destination. Connect with the rich heritage of India by embarking on this holy pilgrimage. \nSee Less\n\nYamuna Pushkaralu Tour from Dehradun includes lodging, food, transportation, and guided sightseeing. The divine journey will start from Dehradun and take you to Dakpatthar, a serene hill town situated on the banks of the River Yamuna and an important spiritual and scenic destination. Connect with the rich heritage of India by embarking on this holy pilgrimage.\n\nTour Gallery\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nTour Name\nYamuna Pushkaralu Yatra to Dakpatthar\n\n\nTour Duration\n3 Days / 2 Nights\n\n\nMeals\nBreakfast\n\n\nVehicle Type\nSedan / SUV\n\n\nStarting & Ending Point\nDehradun\n\n\nDestination Covered\nDehradun \u2013 Haridwar \u2013 Dakpatthar \u2013 Yamuna Snan\n\n\nPickup Time\nDepend on your Flight / Train Timing\n\n\n Tour Benefits\nHoly Yamuna Snan \u2022 Ganga Aarti \u2022 Spiritual Purification",
    "highlights": [
      "Take part in a holy bathing ritual in the water of the River Yamuna.",
      "Perform special poojas and rituals on the riverbank of the Yamuna.",
      "Attend the evening aarti at Har Ki Pauri.",
      "Visit Brahma Kund, where drops of Amrit fell.",
      "Visit Robber\u2019s Cave and Tapkeshwar Temple.",
      "See More"
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 01: Arrival at Dehradun and Local Sightseeing",
        "description": "You begin your journey by arriving at\nDehradun Airport or Railway Station\n, where a tour representative receives you and helps with the transfer. The drive itself is short, but traffic around Dehradun and Haridwar can sometimes slow things down, especially during pilgrimage seasons.\nAfter checking into your\npre-booked hotel\n, it\u2019s advisable to rest for a while. The terrain and climate here are different from the plains, and even light travel fatigue can show up early.\nLater in the day, you visit two well-known local attractions:\nRobber\u2019s Cave, a narrow river cave that requires a short walk on uneven ground\nTapkeshwar Temple, a naturally formed cave temple where water continuously drips over the Shivling\nBoth places are popular, so expect crowds in the afternoon. Comfortable footwear is important here.\nThe evening is kept light. You return to the hotel and settle in for an overnight stay, allowing your body to adjust before the next day\u2019s rituals.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 02: Dakpatthar Visit and Yamuna Pushkaralu Rituals",
        "description": "This is the most spiritually significant day of the tour and also the most physically engaging.\nAfter an early start, you drive towards\nDakpatthar\n, a quiet stretch along the River Yamuna. The area is calmer than Haridwar, but during Yamuna Pushkaralu, the ghats can still become crowded at peak ritual hours.\nHere, you take a holy dip in the Yamuna, followed by participation in the\nYamuna Pushkaralu\nrituals. These rituals often take time, depending on priest availability and crowd flow, so patience is important. Elderly travellers or those with mobility concerns should move cautiously, as river steps can be slippery.\nPost rituals, you return to Haridwar by afternoon.\nIn the evening, the focus shifts to the River Ganga:\nA sacred dip at\nHar Ki Pauri\n, where crowd density is usually high\nAttendance at the evening\nGanga Aarti\n, which is spiritually uplifting but involves standing for a long duration\nA visit to\nBrahma Kund\n, traditionally believed to be the spot where drops of Amrit fell\nAfter a long but fulfilling day, you return to the hotel for a\nquiet overnight stay\n.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 03: Departure from Haridwar / Dehradun",
        "description": "The final day is intentionally kept simple.\nAfter breakfast, you check out from the hotel and proceed towards\nDehradun Airport or the railway station\n, depending on your onward journey. Morning departures are usually smoother, while afternoon travel may face traffic near Haridwar.\nWith this, the\nYamuna Pushkaralu 2026 journey concludes\n. The experience is less about sightseeing and more about participation, patience, and spiritual intent\u2014something that tends to stay with travellers long after they return.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      }
    ],
    "faqs": []
  },
  "yamuna-pushkaralu-yatra-packages": {
    "overview": "",
    "highlights": [],
    "itinerary": [],
    "faqs": []
  },
  "yamuna-pushkaralu-yatra-to-kashi-ayodhya": {
    "overview": "The Yamuna Pushkaralu Spiritual Tour offers you a trip of divine purification during the auspicious Yamuna Pushkaram. See More\n\nThis event falls only once in 12 years, when Jupiter enters Cancer. Enjoy this spiritual journey with visits to the eternally holy cities of Varanasi, Prayagraj, and Ayodhya. You\u2019ll also be visiting the \u2018City of Tehzeeb\u2019 \u2013 Lucknow.\nOn this tour, you\u2019ll be performing ancestral rituals (Pitru Tarpan & Pinda Pradan), visiting temples, taking holy dips, and witnessing river Aarti. All in all, this journey blends faith and tradition \u2013 all in a span of four days!\nSpiritual Significance of Yamuna Pushkaralu\nIt is believed that during the 12-day period of Yamuna Pushkaralu, Goddess Yamuna grants special boon to her devotees. In addition, taking holy dips in this period is said to cleanse the sins of past lives and purifies negative karmas. You also get freed from Pitru Dosha, Naga Dosha, and planetary afflictions.\nOverall, this tour brings spiritual upliftment to devotees as well as peace to their ancestors. \nSee Less\n\nThis event falls only once in 12 years, when Jupiter enters Cancer. Enjoy this spiritual journey with visits to the eternally holy cities of Varanasi, Prayagraj, and Ayodhya. You\u2019ll also be visiting the \u2018City of Tehzeeb\u2019 \u2013 Lucknow.\n\nOn this tour, you\u2019ll be performing ancestral rituals (Pitru Tarpan & Pinda Pradan), visiting temples, taking holy dips, and witnessing river Aarti. All in all, this journey blends faith and tradition \u2013 all in a span of four days!",
    "highlights": [
      "Participation in the rare Yamuna Pushkaralu (once in 12 years)",
      "Performance of Pitru Tarpan, Pinda Pradaan, Pujas, and Homas",
      "Darshan at Shri Kashi Vishwanath Temple in Varanasi",
      "Witness the world-famous Ganga Aarti at Dashashwamedh Ghat",
      "Take a holy bath at Triveni Sangam \u2013 confluence of Ganga, Yamuna & Saraswati",
      "Visit to Akshayavat, Bade Hanuman Mandir, and Prayagraj Fort",
      "Enjoy Darshan at Ram Janmabhoomi Temple in Ayodhya",
      "Attend the evening Saryu River Aarti at Naya Ghat in Ayodhya",
      "Exciting sightseeing in Lucknow: Bara Imambara and Rumi Darwaza",
      "See More"
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1: Arrive Varanasi Sightseeing",
        "description": "Once you arrive at Varanasi Airport/Railway Station, you will be warmly greeted and assisted by our representative.\nYou\u2019ll be taken to your hotel now. Check in and relax for a while.\nAfter this, you\u2019ll be taken for a sightseeing tour of:\nShri Kashi Vishwanath temple\nAnnapurna Temple\nVishalakshi Temple\nBaba Kal Bhairav Temple\nIn the evening, you\u2019ll be taken for\nboat cruise on the river Ganga\n.\nAlso, explore\nhistoric Ghats of Varanasi\nand soak in the spiritual aura of the holy city.\nLater, be a part of the mesmerizing\nGanga Aarti at Dashashwamedh Ghat\n.\nReturn to the hotel for an overnight stay.\nKey Notes:\nVishwanath Temple\nDarshan timing\n- 4:00 AM to 11:00 AM & 12:00 PM to 7:00 PM, 8:30 PM to 10:00PM\nAarti Timings\n- Mangla Aarti - 3:00 AM, Sapta Rishi Aarti - 7:00 PM to 8:30 PM, Shayan Aarti 10:30 PM\nDarshan Booking\n- Devotees book their Sugam Darshan tickets online:\nhttps://shrikashivishwanath.org\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 2: Varanasi \u2013 Prayagraj (130 kms / 4 Hrs)",
        "description": "In the morning, you\u2019ll be driven to Prayagraj.\nOn arrival, check into your hotel.\nLater, you\u2019ll be taken to the Triveni Sangam \u2013 confluence of Ganga, Yamuna, and Saraswati rivers. Take a holy dip here and perform other sacred rituals.\nAfter this, take a boat ride in Sangam.\nNow, you\u2019ll be taken to the following places:\nBade Hanuman Mandir:\nSeek Darshan of Lord Hanuman.\nAkshayavat Temple and Tree:\nThis sacred fig tree is believed to be the one under which Ram, Lakshman, and Sita rested. As per the ancient Hindu texts, it\u2019s believed that whoever worships Akshayavat gets freed from sins.\nPrayagraj Fort (Allahabad Fort):\nThis was built by Akbar in 1583. Its vicinity to the sacred Yamuna River gives it a spiritual touch.\nAlopi Devi Temple:\nThis is also a Shaktipith temple.\nLalita Devi Temple:\nIt is revered as Madhaveswari Devi in scriptures. It is believed that the fingers of Maa Sati\u2019s hand fell here.\nShri Nagvasuki Temple:\nDevotees believe that worshipping here removes obstacles, protects from snake afflictions (Sarpa Dosh), and brings peace and prosperity.\nYour overnight stay will be in Prayagraj.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 3: Prayagraj - Ayodhya (167 km / 4 hr)",
        "description": "After breakfast, you\u2019ll be driven to Ayodhya.\nEnjoy a sightseeing tour of the following places:\nRam Janmabhoomi Temple:\nThis is the birthplace of Lord Rama.\nHanuman Garhi Temple:\nIt\u2019s a temple dedicated to Lord Hanuman.\nKanak Bhavan Temple:\nIt\u2019s known for its gold-plated domes.\nRam ki Paidi:\nThis is yet another temple dedicated to Lord Rama.\nDashrath Mahal:\nThis was the residence of Lord Ram's father, King Dashrath.\nIn the evening, you\u2019ll be taken to attend the Saryu River Aarti at Naya Ghat. Also, take this time to stroll around the Saryu River banks.\nYour overnight stay will be in Ayodhya.\nKey Notes:\nSri Ram Janmabhoomi Temple timings:\nDarshan Timing\n- 7:00 AM to 12:00 PM & 1:00 PM to 7:00 PM\nAarti Timings\n- Mangla Aarti - 4:00 AM, Shringar Aarti - 6:00 AM, Shayan Aarti 10:00 PM\nOther Temples timing:\nHanuman Garhi Temple\n- 4:30 AM to 12:00PM - Bhog Time - 12:30 PM to 9:00 PM\nKanak Bhavan Temple\n- 8:00 AM to 11.30 AM & 4:00 PM to 8:00 PM\nDashrath Mahal\n- 8:00 AM to 12.30 PM & 4:00 PM to 8:00 PM\nDarshan Booking:\nDevotees book their Sugam Darshan tickets online at:\nhttps://online.srjbtkshetra.org/#/mobileVerification\n.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 4: Ayodhya / Varanasi Departure",
        "description": "In the morning after breakfast, you\u2019ll be taken to Ayodhya airport, Lucknow or Varanasi (depending on the return flight).\nIf you visit Lucknow, you\u2019ll be taken on a sightseeing tour of:\nBada Imambara\n(6:00 AM \u2013 5:00 PM, Fridays 3:00 PM \u2013 5:00 PM, Closed on Mondays)\nRumi Darwaza\nResidency Complex\n(10:00 AM \u2013 5:00 PM)\nAfter this, you\u2019ll be transferred to the airport. And this concludes your trip with us.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      }
    ],
    "faqs": []
  },
  "yamuna-pushkaralu-yatra-to-yamunotri": {
    "overview": "The Yamuna Pushkaralu Tour from Dehradun is of 4 Days 3 Nights. See More\n\nThis holy tour will take you to the sacred Yamunotri. You also get to visit other holy towns, such as Haridwar and Barkot. We will also be making stops at Dehradun and Mussoorie. The Yamuna Pushkaram is a holy sacred event that takes place only once every 12 years. Visiting Yamunotri and taking a ritualistic bath during this period is highly auspicious.\nSpiritual Significance \nYamuna Pushkaralu is a 12 day event that is marked by the special astronomical alignment of Jupiter entering Cancer. It\u2019s believed that taking a bath in the river Yamuna cleanses the pilgrims from their accumulated sins from past lives. Negative karma are also purified. Pitru Dosha and Naga Dosha are also relieved. Enjoy the special spiritual enlightenment through Pushkara Snanam.\nSee Less\n\nThis holy tour will take you to the sacred Yamunotri. You also get to visit other holy towns, such as Haridwar and Barkot. We will also be making stops at Dehradun and Mussoorie. The Yamuna Pushkaram is a holy sacred event that takes place only once every 12 years. Visiting Yamunotri and taking a ritualistic bath during this period is highly auspicious.",
    "highlights": [
      "Participation in Yamuna Pushkaralu, held every 12 years",
      "Take holy dip in the sacred waters of River Yamuna",
      "Performance rituals and rites like Pitru Tarpan, Pinda Pradan, Pujas, and Homas",
      "Visit to Yamunotri Temple, dedicated to Goddess Yamuna",
      "Sacred rituals at Surya Kund",
      "Worship at Divya Shila",
      "Evening Ganga Aarti at Har Ki Pauri, Haridwar",
      "Visit to Brahma Kund",
      "Scenic Himalayan drive via Dehradun, Mussoorie, and Kempty Falls",
      "See More"
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1: Arrive Dehradun \u2013 Haridwar (40 kms/1 Hrs)",
        "description": "Once you arrive in Dehradun, you will be warmly greeted by our representative at Dehradun Airport/Haridwar Railway Station.\nAfter this, you\u2019ll be driven to Haridwar.\nOnce you get there, check into your hotel and relax for a while.\nIn the evening, go for the ritualistic bathing on the sacred banks of the River Ganges.\nAlso, attend the Ganga Aarti at Har Ki Pauri, one of the most sacred Ghats in Haridwar.\nTake a tour to Brahma Kund as well. It\u2019s believed that drops of Amrit (nectar) fell here.\nIf time permits, visit Mansa Devi Temple, too.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 2: Haridwar \u2013 Dehradun \u2013 Barkot /Jankichatti (240kms/ 9 Hrs)",
        "description": "After breakfast in the morning, you\u2019ll be taken for a morning drive to Barkot via Dehradun and Mussoorie.\nAlong the way, we\u2019ll be making a stop at Kempty Falls. Also, enjoy scenic Himalayan views during your journey.\nContinue your drive to Barkot.\nYour overnight stay will be at Barkot.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 3: Barkot - Yamunotri Shan \u2013 Barkot (45 Kms road/ 6 kms Trek)",
        "description": "In the early morning, you\u2019ll be driven to Jankichatti \u2013 the starting point of the trek.\nOnce you get there, trek to Yamunotri (6 km). You can do that either by foot or take the service of pony/Doli (on a direct payment basis).\nTake a holy dip in the waters of River Yamuna. This is especially auspicious during Yamuna Pushkar.\nAt Surya Kund, cook rice in the hot spring and take this home as Prasadam.\nAt Divya Shila, offer your prayers and seek blessings of Mata Yamuna.\nOnce you reach the Yamunotri temple, complete your Darshan and Poojan. Goddess Yamuna is believed to be daughter of Lord Surya and sister of Yamraj.\nTrek back to Jankichatti.\nAfter this, you\u2019ll be driven back to Barkot for an overnight stay.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 4: Barkot - Dehradun (150 kms / 5 Hrs)",
        "description": "In the morning, head back to Dehradun.\nAlong the way, enjoy scenic views\nOnce you get to Dehradun, you\u2019ll be transferred to Dehradun Airport/Railway Station.\nThis concludes your tour. Hope you return home with happy memories.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      }
    ],
    "faqs": []
  },
  "yamuna-pushkaralu-yatra-with-kurukshetra-haridwar": {
    "overview": "Attend the Yamuna Pushkaralu festival and get ready to experience the divine power of the River Yamuna.  See More\n\nThe Yamuna Nadi Pushkaralu 2026 will arrive this year in June, offering you a rare opportunity to connect with the divine. Our Yamuna Pushkaralu Tour from Dehradun package comes with the best amenities and an unforgettable travel experience.\nWe ensure complete care, comfort, and a truly unforgettable spiritual journey for you. Our packages come with well-planned itineraries, fuss-free transportation options, and top-notch accommodation. \nSee Less\n\nThe Yamuna Nadi Pushkaralu 2026 will arrive this year in June, offering you a rare opportunity to connect with the divine. Our Yamuna Pushkaralu Tour from Dehradun package comes with the best amenities and an unforgettable travel experience.\n\nWe ensure complete care, comfort, and a truly unforgettable spiritual journey for you. Our packages come with well-planned itineraries, fuss-free transportation options, and top-notch accommodation.\n\nTour Gallery\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nTour Name\nYamuna Pushkaralu Yatra with Kurukshetra Haridwar\n\n\nTour Duration\n3 Days / 2 Nights\n\n\nMeals\nBreakfast\n\n\nVehicle Type\nSedan / SUV\n\n\nStarting & Ending Point\nDelhi\n\n\nDestination Covered\nDelhi - Kurukshetra - Yamuna Snan - Haridwar\n\n\nPickup Time\nDepend on your Flight Timing \n\n\n Tour Benefits\nBest price & enjoyable travel guarantee",
    "highlights": [
      "A sightseeing tour of Kurukshetra.",
      "Take a dip in the water of the River Yamuna.",
      "Perform sacred rituals such as Special Poojas, Tarpanam, and Pindapradanam at the River Yamuna.",
      "Attend the Ganga aarti at Har Ki Pauri.",
      "Visit Brahma Kund.",
      "Visit the sacred attractions of Haridwar, such as Manasa Devi Temple, Bharat Mata Temple, and the Daksha Mahadev Temple.",
      "See More"
    ],
    "itinerary": [
      {
        "title": "Day 1: Arrive Delhi - Kurukshetra (5 Hrs/230 kms)",
        "description": "As you arrive in\nDelhi\n, you will be greeted by one of our\ncourteous representatives\nwho will welcome you with open arms.\nYou will then head to\nKurukshetra\n.\nYou can enjoy a\nsightseeing\ntour\nof the\nlocal attractions\n.\nLater, you will head out on a drive to\nYamuna Nagar\nand have an\novernight stay\n.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 2: In Yamuna Snan - Haridwar (140 kms/4 Hrs)",
        "description": "You'll head to the\nRiver Yamuna\nin the\nmorning\n.\nTake a\nholy dip\nin its water.\nBesides this, you can perform\nsacred rituals\nsuch as\nSpecial Poojas\n,\nTarpanam\n, and\nPindapradanam\n.\nIt is believed that if you take a dip in the\nRiver Yamuna\nduring this time, you can\npurify your soul\n.\nLater, you will head to\nHaridwar\n.\nYou'll take a\nholy dip\nin the\nRiver Yamuna's water\nin the\nevening\n.\nAt\nHar Ki Pauri\n, you will attend\nGanga Aarti\n.\nYou will also visit\nBrahma Kund\n, which is believed to be the place where\ndrops of Amrit fell\n.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
      },
      {
        "title": "Day 3: Haridwar - Delhi (6 Hrs/230 Kms)",
        "description": "Enjoy a\ntasty breakfast\nin the\nmorning\n.\nYou will be taken to\nManasa Devi Temple\n, one of the\nfive pilgrimage sites\nin Haridwar.\nIt is also known as the\n\"Panch Tirths.\"\nYou will also visit\nBharat Mata Temple\n.\nYou will then head to the\nDaksha Mahadev Temple\n.\nAfter the\nspiritual tour\n, you will head back to\nDelhi\n.\nYou will be transferred to\nDelhi Railway Station or Airport\n, from where you will continue your\nfurther journey\n.\nPlaces You\u2019ll See"
